essor/Associate Professor/Professor", "description": "Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor - Academic Breast Surgical Oncologist Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor - Academic Breast Surgical Oncologist Date Posted: 10/16/2026 Closing Date: 12/18/2026 , 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50531 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Surgery Hospital Affiliation: Sinai Health System Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Sinai Health System (SHS) and the Department of Surgery at the University of Toronto are currently\u00a0seeking a full-time Academic Breast Surgical Oncologist to join the Division of General Surgery. The effective date of this appointment is flexible and is between March 1, 2027 and July 1, 2027. Division of General Surgery at SHS consists of 12 fellowship trained surgical oncologists and colorectal surgeons who work in a collaborative clinical practice with full integration of education and research.\u00a0The successful candidate will also work in the Marvelle Koffler Breast Centre with a team of breast and plastic surgeons, oncologists, radiologists and pathologists to provide multi-disciplinary breast cancer care across the full spectrum of breast cancer car, including prevention, treatment and survivorship. The successful candidate will provide the full scope of breast cancer surgery services, including consultations, surgical procedures, and follow up. The successful candidate will have an academic focus in basic, clinical or education research, quality improvement or another relevant area of focused academic expertise. Evidence of excellence in teaching, research, and clinical care is required. With the completion of its new Cancer Centre and Operating Room, SHS is looking to continue to be an international leader in critical thinking and innovative approaches to the delivery of surgical care.\u00a0The SHS team is deeply committed to providing the highest possible care for patients and working in partnership with them to educate the future generation of surgeons and discovery of life-saving surgical treatments. The successful candidate: Must be a fellowship-trained breast or general surgical oncologist and must be a Fellow of the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada, or have comparable qualifications, with completion of a postgraduate degree program (e.g. MSc, MPH, PhD). The candidate should also be eligible for licensure with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario, and for appointment at the Surgery and Oncology Program at Sinai Health at Mount Sinai Hospital. Must be eligible for an academic appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor/Associate Professor or Professor in the Department of Surgery, Temerty Faculty of Medicine at the University of Toronto. Academic rank will be commensurate with the candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience. Will be eligible for a cross-appointment at other University of Toronto institutions based on clinical need. Sinai Health System (SHS) is a full affiliate of the University of Toronto, is an academic hospital comprised of Mount Sinai Hospital, Hennick Bridgepoint, Lunenfeld-Tannenbaum Research Institute and Circle of Care \u2013 working together to create a premier exemplar of an integrated health system, SHS combines acute care, complex and rehabilitative care, primary care and other community based services to create an innovative and integrated continuum of care, with the goal to achieve the best outcomes and experiences and outcomes for our patients. The rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The salary range of this position exceeds $200,000 CAD per annum. This estimate is based on fee for service billings. Applications will be accepted until December 18, 2026, or until the position is filled. Interviews for short-listed candidates are planned for late January/early February 2027. Please submit an up-to-date curriculum vitae, names and email addresses of three references, and a two-page expression of interest to: Dr. Erin Kennedy, Deputy Surgeon-in-Chief Mount Sinai Hospital 600 University Avenue, Room 449 Toronto, Ontario M5G 1X5 Email: erin.kennedy@sinaihealth.ca Phone: 416-586-4800 x 6872 For more information about the Department of Surgery at Sinai Health and the Temerty Faculty of Medicine/Department of Surgery , please visit our website at: https://www.sinaihealth.ca/areas-of-care/surgery and http://surgery.utoronto.ca CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Oncology, Pathology, Rehabilitation, General Surgery, Academic, Healthcare, Education Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-Anesthesiology-&-Pain-Medicine-Unity-Health-St_-Mike&apos;s-ON/607092717/": {"title": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor", "description": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor | Anesthesiology & Pain Medicine | Unity Health - St. Mike's Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant / Associate / Full Professor | Anesthesiology & Pain Medicine | Unity Health - St. Mike's Date Posted: 10/15/2026 Req ID: 50559 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Anesthesiology & Pain Medicine Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: [[positionNumber]] Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Department of Anesthesiology & Pain Medicine, Temerty Faculty of Medicine at the University of Toronto, and Unity Health Toronto - St. Michael\u2019s Hospital are seeking an academic anesthesiologist to fulfill a strategic role within the Department of Anesthesia at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. The anticipated start date will be July 1, 2027, or one which is mutually agreed upon. The successful candidate will provide anesthetic care throughout the hospital programs including supervision and teaching of students, residents, and fellows. On-call services will be provided in rotation. Participation in formal in-house and University teaching programs, as well as hospital administrative duties, will be expected. Academic opportunities for research and teaching are available. Academic time is assigned according to an objective assessment of requirements. The incumbent will have major clinical responsibilities and in addition to their own academic activities, will facilitate the research, teaching, and education by others. Teaching may be done concurrently with clinical care and/or in organized educational programs. Strategic needs currently include, among others, cardiovascular anesthesia and cardiovascular critical care, interventional pain, obstetric anesthesia, and educational leadership. The successful candidate must have a medical degree, postgraduate fellowship training, Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada certification in Anesthesia, or international equivalent, and be eligible for licensure with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario. The successful candidate must have proven clinical skills at a high level, evidence of demonstrated excellence in research and/or education and/or quality improvement, and a commitment to teaching students, residents, and fellows. Scholarly excellence will be assessed using University of Toronto, Temerty Faculty of Medicine guidelines. St. Michael\u2019s Hospital is part of Unity Health Toronto, which includes Providence, St. Joseph\u2019s, and St. Michael\u2019s. St. Michael\u2019s is one of Canada\u2019s leading academic health sciences centres and is fully affiliated with the University of Toronto. Located in downtown Toronto, it provides secondary, tertiary, and quaternary care services for Toronto, southern Ontario, and beyond. The Hospital is organized in a programmatic fashion with an emphasis on Heart & Vascular Disease, Trauma and Neurosurgery, Neuromusculoskeletal Disorders, Oncology, Specialized Services, Inner City Health, and Diabetes Comprehensive Care. The Hospital services more than 77,000 patients annually in our emergency department, 520,000 ambulatory visits, and over 25,000 inpatients, with more than 450 inpatient beds and 25 operating rooms. The Department of Anesthesia at St. Michael\u2019s is known for its clinical excellence and dedication to quality improvement, research, and education. A new patient care tower opened in 2020 that includes modernized operating rooms and critical care areas. Compensation for clinical activities and academic rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience and within the usual range for an academic anesthetist in the Province of Ontario ($350,000 \u2013 550,000 per annum). Applications will be accepted until November 30, 2026, or until the position is filled. Applicants should submit a letter of interest, a copy of their curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information of three referees to: Dr. Nick Lo Interim Chief, Department of Anesthesia Unity Health Toronto - St. Michael\u2019s Hospital, Toronto Nick.Lo@unityhealth.to For more information about the Department of Anesthesia at the University of Toronto, please visit our website at http://www.anesthesia.utoronto.ca/ CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above\u00a0for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position . Closing Date: 11/30/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: [[custEmployeeSubgroup]] Appointment Type : [[custApptmentType]] Schedule: [[custFullPartTime]] Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: [[custPayScaleGrpHiringRate]] Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Divisional HR Office Email: [[custDivisionalHREmail]] Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Medical, Neurology, Oncology, Anesthesia, ICU, Healthcare Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Professor-Occupational-Psychiatrist-Investigator-and-Medical-Head-ON/607099217/": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "Assistant Professor - Occupational Psychiatrist - Investigator and Medical Head Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant Professor - Occupational Psychiatrist - Investigator and Medical Head Date Posted: 10/16/2026 Closing Date: 11/26/2026 , 11:59PM ET, Open Until Filled Req ID: 50571 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Psychiatry Hospital Affiliation: Centre for Addiction & Mental Health Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Description: Assistant Professor - Occupational Psychiatrist - Investigator and Medical Head The Centre for Addiction and Mental Health (CAMH) is seeking to recruit a Scientist \u2013 Academic Psychiatrist, to build a program of clinical, research and creative professional activities specifically in the area of Occupational Psychiatry in the Work Stress and Health (WSH) Clinic, as well as to provide clinical care in the General Adult Psychiatry and Health Systems Division.\u00a0 The anticipated start date is February 1, 2027 or mutually agreed start date. As a Medical Head of the WSH clinic, the candidate will be expected to lead a clinic focused on the assessment and treatment of patients with workplace injuries within CAMH and the surrounding community.\u00a0 The clinic will employ a team-based care approach and utilize measurement in the delivery of care. A main focus of the role will be working with the senior manager and director on operational efficiency and ensuring deliverables for contracts with external funders are on track and to contribute to the submission of proposals for new contracts.\u00a0 As an investigator, the successful candidate will be required to establish local, national, and international collaborations, provide practical supervision of undergraduate, graduate, post-doctoral research trainees, and technical staff.\u00a0 The successful candidate will be expected to lead research activities, maintain an active publication record, and secure extramural funding sources for those activities. They will also disseminate research results through presentations at academic meetings and conferences and communicate ideas to key decision makers. Participation in leadership advisory groups at CAMH and externally is expected. \u00a0There are also teaching opportunities with undergraduate and post graduate students, elective residents and fellows.\u00a0 The successful candidate will be required to have an MD and PhD and will have an academic position description of Clinician Investigator and must be eligible for a full-time clinical academic appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor at the University of Toronto. CAMH\u00a0is Canada\u2019s premier addiction and mental health facility and a world leader in the diagnosis and care of patients with addiction and mental disorders, offering a wide spectrum of care, from treatment for the first episode to care for the severely and persistently mentally ill. It is fully affiliated with the University of Toronto, the largest and most prestigious research-intensive university in Canada. The General Adult Psychiatry and Health Systems Division is one of the largest outpatient programs in Ontario receiving more than 25,000 referrals each year.\u00a0 The outpatient program is highly interconnected with other the emergency and inpatient units as well as specialized services throughout the hospital. The successful applicant must hold an MD and PhD degree and be eligible for a Clinical Full-Time appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor at the University of Toronto. They must have, or be eligible for, certification in Psychiatry with the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada, as well as licensure with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario. The successful candidate must have a track record of publications in the area of occupational psychiatry.\u00a0 The successful candidate is required to have graduate training in research pertaining to occupational psychiatry.\u00a0 Training in quality improvement is an asset and if the candidate does not have formal training it will be expected that they participate in more formal QI training through the Faculty of Medicine.\u00a0 Applicants must be eligible for certification with the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada and for licensure with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario.\u00a0 As a full-time staff member at CAMH, the candidate will provide on-call services as part of their clinical responsibilities. Remuneration will consist of a combination of OHIP billings, third party billings through the WSH clinic, administrative stipend for the medical head role and 1.5 protected days for research, commensurate with qualifications and experience. The salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The salary range of this position exceeds $200,000 CAD per annum. CAMH, strives to be an equitable and inclusive employer. Our commitment to equity is grounded in an institution-wide commitment to achieving a working, teaching, and learning environment that is free of discrimination and harassment.\u00a0 CAMH actively seeks candidates from First Nations, M\u00e9tis and Inuit, racialized and LGBTQ2S+ communities, women, and people with disabilities (including people who have experienced mental health and substance use challenges).\u00a0 We encourage people from all backgrounds to apply to our positions. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should send a letter of interest, a copy of their curriculum vitae and the names of three references via email to: Dr. Daniel Blumberger Chief, General Adult Psychiatry and Health Systems Division Centre for Addiction & Mental Health 1025 Queen Street West, Toronto, ON, M6J 1H4 Daniel.Blumberger@camh.ca For more information on the University of Toronto, Department of Psychiatry, please visit http://www.psychiatry.utoronto.ca . For more information about the Centre for Addiction and Mental Health, please visit https://www.camh.ca. CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Investigation, Psychology, Counseling, Research Scientist, Clinical Research, Healthcare, Legal, Science Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-LecturerAssistantAssociateFull-Professor-Academic-Psychiatrist-Integrated-Day-Treatment-ON/607099317/": {"title": "Lecturer/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor", "description": "Lecturer/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Academic Psychiatrist - Integrated Day Treatment Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Lecturer/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Academic Psychiatrist - Integrated Day Treatment Date Posted: 10/16/2026 Closing Date: 11/26/2026 , 11:59PM ET, Open Until Filled Req ID: 50573 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Psychiatry Hospital Affiliation: Centre for Addiction & Mental Health Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Description: Lecturer/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Academic Psychiatrist \u2013 General Adult Psychiatry and Health Systems Division \u2013 Integrated Day Treatment and Borderline Personality Disorder Clinics and Outpatient Services The Centre for Addiction and Mental Health (CAMH) is seeking a full-time psychiatrist in the General Adult Psychiatry and Health Systems Division.\u00a0 The successful candidate must be eligible for a full-time clinical academic appointment at the rank of Lecturer, Assistant, Associate or Full Professor at the University of Toronto. Effective start date is July 1, 2027 or shortly thereafter. CAMH is Canada\u2019s premier addiction and mental health facility and a world leader in the diagnosis and care of patients with addiction and mental disorder, offering a wide spectrum of care from treatment for\u00a0first episode to care for the severely and persistently mentally ill. It is fully affiliated with the University of Toronto, the largest and most prestigious research-intensive University in Canada. CAMH, together with the Department of Psychiatry at the University of Toronto, has a strong tradition in the integration of clinical, teaching and research activities.\u00a0 The successful candidate will provide exemplary team-based psychiatric care for people with mood, anxiety and trauma related disorders and overall general adult psychiatry assessment.\u00a0\u00a0 The candidate will also be expected to participate in the undergraduate and postgraduate teaching programs of the University of Toronto Department of Psychiatry. The applicant will have a desire to work in and contribute to an active academic environment, with a commitment and experience in teaching at the undergraduate and postgraduate level. The candidate will have demonstrated experience working with patients with complex trauma and borderline personality disorder and training or willingness to be trained in dialectical behaviour therapy.\u00a0 Duties will include working 4 - 5 days per week in the integrated day treatment program and borderline personality disorder clinics and 0-1 days per week in other general adult psychiatry outpatient settings.\u00a0 The academic role will focus on teaching and supervision of medical students and psychiatry residents and developing quality improvement. Applicants must hold a Doctor of Medicine (MD) and be certified (or eligible for certification) by the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada, and must be licensed (or eligible for licensure) with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario. The successful must be eligible for academic appointment in the Department of Psychiatry, at the University of Toronto. Academic rank will be commensurate with the qualifications and experience of the successful candidate. English language proficiency is required. This is a full-time position with estimated remuneration in the range of $250,000 - 350,000 per annum based on a combination of clinical stipends, fees for service, funding through Academic and Educational Trust Funds, and on-call stipends. Benefits are not included. This position is located at 1025 Queen Street West, Toronto, ON, M6J 1H4. At CAMH, we strive to be an equitable and inclusive employer. Our commitment to equity is grounded in an institution-wide commitment to achieving a working, teaching, and learning environment that is free of discrimination and harassment.\u00a0 CAMH actively seeks candidates from First Nations, M\u00e9tis and Inuit, racialized and LGBTQ2+ communities, women, and people with disabilities (including people who have experienced mental health and substance use challenges). We encourage people from all backgrounds to apply to our positions. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should send a letter of interest, a copy of their curriculum vitae and the names of three references via email to: Dr. Daniel Blumberger Chief, General Adult Psychiatry and Health Systems Division Centre for Addiction & Mental Health 1025 Queen Street West, Toronto, ON, M6J 1H4 Daniel.Blumberger@camh.ca For more information on the University of Toronto, Department of Psychiatry, please visit http://www.psychiatry.utoronto.ca . For more information about the Centre for Addiction and Mental Health, please visit https://www.camh.ca. CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Psychology, Counseling, Academic, Behavioral Health, Substance Abuse, Healthcare, Education Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-LecturerAssistant-Professor-Academic-Psychiatrist-InOut-patient-Services%2C-Bridging-Transitions-ON/607099617/": {"title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor", "description": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor - Academic Psychiatrist - In/Out-patient Services, Bridging Transitions Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Lecturer/Assistant Professor - Academic Psychiatrist - In/Out-patient Services, Bridging Transitions Date Posted: 10/16/2026 Closing Date: 11/26/2026 , 11:59PM ET, Open Until Filled Req ID: 50575 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Psychiatry Hospital Affiliation: Centre for Addiction & Mental Health Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Description: Lecturer/Assistant Professor - Academic Psychiatrist \u2013 General Adult Psychiatry and Health Systems Division \u2013 Inpatient Services, Bridging Transitions, and Outpatient Services The Centre for Addiction and Mental Health (CAMH) is seeking a full-time psychiatrist in the General Adult Psychiatry and Health Systems Division.\u00a0 The successful candidate must be eligible for a full-time clinical academic appointment at the rank of Lecturer or Assistant Professor at the University of Toronto. Effective start date is July 1, 2027 or shortly thereafter. CAMH is Canada\u2019s premier addiction and mental health facility and a world leader in the diagnosis and care of patients with addiction and mental disorders, offering a wide spectrum of care from treatment for\u00a0first episode to care for the severely and persistently mentally ill. It is fully affiliated with the University of Toronto, the largest and most prestigious research-intensive University in Canada. CAMH, together with the Department of Psychiatry at the University of Toronto, has a strong tradition in the integration of clinical, teaching and research activities.\u00a0 The successful candidate will provide exemplary team-based psychiatric care for people admitted to general psychiatry inpatient units. The applicant will have a desire to work in and contribute to the active academic environment at CAMH, with a commitment to teaching at the undergraduate and postgraduate level. The candidate will also be expected to participate in the undergraduate and postgraduate teaching programs associated with the University of Toronto Department of Psychiatry. Alternatively, for candidates with an academic interest in quality improvement, they will contribute to clinical quality initiatives, teaching and scholarship at CAMH and be involved in the quality improvement faculty community associated with the University of Toronto Department of Psychiatry.\u00a0 Clinical duties will include providing care for patients admitted to general psychiatry inpatient services, Bridging Transitions Clinic, and outpatient services (two \u00bd days each week.) The academic role will focus on teaching and supervision of medical students and psychiatry residents or developing and leading quality improvement initiatives to enhance clinical services in the General Adult Psychiatry and Health Systems Division. Applicants must hold a Doctor of Medicine (MD) and be certified (or eligible for certification) by the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada, and must be licensed (or eligible for licensure) with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario. The successful candidate must also be eligible for academic appointment in the Department of Psychiatry, at the University of Toronto at the rank of Lecturer or Assistant Professor. English language proficiency is required. This is a full-time position with estimated remuneration in the range of $350,00 - 400,000 per annum based on a combination of clinical stipends, fees for clinical service, funding through Academic and Educational Trust Funds, and on-call stipends. Benefits are not included. This position is located at 1025 Queen Street West, Toronto, ON, M6J 1H4. At CAMH, we strive to be an equitable and inclusive employer. Our commitment to equity is grounded in an institution-wide commitment to achieving a working, teaching, and learning environment that is free of discrimination and harassment. CAMH actively seeks candidates from First Nations, M\u00e9tis and Inuit, racialized and LGBTQ2+ communities, women, and people with disabilities (including people who have experienced mental health and substance use challenges). We encourage people from all backgrounds to apply to our positions. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should send a letter of interest, a copy of their curriculum vitae and the names of three references via email to: Dr. Daniel Blumberger Chief, General Adult Psychiatry and Health Systems Division Centre for Addiction & Mental Health 1025 Queen Street West, Toronto, ON, M6J 1H4 Daniel.Blumberger@camh.ca For more information on the University of Toronto, Department of Psychiatry, please visit http://www.psychiatry.utoronto.ca . For more information about the Centre for Addiction and Mental Health, please visit https://www.camh.ca. CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Psychology, Counseling, Academic, Behavioral Health, Substance Abuse, Healthcare, Education Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-LecturerAssistantAssociateFull-Professor-Academic-Psychiatrist-OCD-and-Anxiety-Clinic-ON/607099517/": {"title": "Lecturer/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor", "description": "Lecturer/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Academic Psychiatrist - OCD and Anxiety Clinic Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Emp