neral Adult Psychiatry and Health Systems Division.\u00a0 The successful candidate must be eligible for a full-time clinical academic appointment at the rank of Lecturer, Assistant, Associate or Full Professor at the University of Toronto. Effective start date is July 1, 2027 or shortly thereafter. CAMH is Canada\u2019s premier addiction and mental health facility and a world leader in the diagnosis and care of patients with addiction and mental disorder, offering a wide spectrum of care from treatment for\u00a0first episode to care for the severely and persistently mentally ill. It is fully affiliated with the University of Toronto, the largest and most prestigious research-intensive University in Canada. CAMH, together with the Department of Psychiatry at the University of Toronto, has a strong tradition in the integration of clinical, teaching and research activities.\u00a0 The successful candidate will provide exemplary team-based psychiatric care for people with mood, anxiety and trauma related disorders and overall general adult psychiatry assessment.\u00a0\u00a0 The candidate will also be expected to participate in the undergraduate and postgraduate teaching programs of the University of Toronto Department of Psychiatry. The applicant will have a desire to work in and contribute to an active academic environment, with a commitment and experience in teaching at the undergraduate and postgraduate level. The candidate will have demonstrated experience working with patients with OCD and anxiety disorders. \u00a0\u00a0Duties will include working 3 days per week in the OCD and anxiety clinic and 2 days per week in other general adult psychiatry outpatient or emergency department settings.\u00a0 The academic role will focus on teaching and supervision of medical students and psychiatry residents, developing quality improvement. Applicants must hold a Doctor of Medicine (MD) and be certified (or eligible for certification) by the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada, and must be licensed (or eligible for licensure) with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario. The successful must be eligible for academic appointment in the Department of Psychiatry, at the University of Toronto. Academic rank will be commensurate with the qualifications and experience of the successful candidate. English language proficiency is required. This is a full-time position with estimated remuneration in the range of $250,00 - 350,000 per annum based on a combination of clinical stipends, fees for service, funding through Academic and Educational Trust Funds, and on-call stipends. Benefits are not included. This position is located at 1025 Queen Street West, Toronto, ON, M6J 1H4. At CAMH, we strive to be an equitable and inclusive employer. Our commitment to equity is grounded in an institution-wide commitment to achieving a working, teaching, and learning environment that is free of discrimination and harassment.\u00a0 CAMH actively seeks candidates from First Nations, M\u00e9tis and Inuit, racialized and LGBTQ2+ communities, women, and people with disabilities (including people who have experienced mental health and substance use challenges). We encourage people from all backgrounds to apply to our positions. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should send a letter of interest, a copy of their curriculum vitae and the names of three references via email to: Dr. Daniel Blumberger Chief, General Adult Psychiatry and Health Systems Division Centre for Addiction & Mental Health 1025 Queen Street West, Toronto, ON, M6J 1H4 Daniel.Blumberger@camh.ca For more information on the University of Toronto, Department of Psychiatry, please visit http://www.psychiatry.utoronto.ca . For more information about the Centre for Addiction and Mental Health, please visit https://www.camh.ca. CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Clinic, Psychology, Counseling, Emergency Medicine, Academic, Healthcare, Education Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-Cardiothoracic-Radiology-St_-Michael&apos;s-Hospital-ON/607105717/": {"title": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor Cardiothoracic Radiology", "description": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor Cardiothoracic Radiology - St. Michael's Hospital Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant / Associate / Full Professor Cardiothoracic Radiology - St. Michael's Hospital The Department of Medical Imaging at St. Michael\u2019s Hospital (SMH) and the University of Toronto are recruiting a full-time, fellowship-trained, academic radiologist into their Cardiothoracic and Abdominal Divisions.\u00a0The successful candidate will be assigned an academic position description based on their teaching or research strengths and must be eligible for a full-time clinical academic appointment at the rank of Assistant / Associate / Full Professor. The anticipated start date is January 1, 2027. SMH is a member of the Unity Health Toronto network, and is a busy, 463-bed quaternary care academic centre, and one of four principal teaching hospitals of the University of Toronto.\u00a0 Within the University of Toronto, the Department of Medical Imaging has distinguished itself with recognized excellence in undergraduate, graduate, and postgraduate teaching, as well as research.\u00a0 The successful candidate will join a collegial and subspecialty academic practice which supports our mission of excellent patient care, delivered in a positive and constructive work environment, with close multidisciplinary collaboration across cardiology, cardiovascular surgery, respirology, general surgery, gastroenterology, urology, gynecology and other clinical programs. The role offers excellent compensation and opportunities for professional and career growth. This is the ideal role for a self-starter and a team player and will offer the opportunity to excel in interaction with patients, colleagues, staff, and management, and excel in a high-volume environment with a commitment to high-quality patient and family centered care, continuous quality improvement, research and teaching. This recruitment is for a hybrid role within both the Cardiothoracic and Abdominal Imaging divisions, but expected to be predominant in the Cardiothoracic division. In this role, the successful candidate will report all types of cardiothoracic and abdominal imaging studies performed at SMH. The Cardiothoracic Imaging practice encompasses Cardiac CT (Coronary CTA, Structural Heart CT [including CT for transcatheter aortic,\u00a0 mitral, and tricuspid intervention], CT for Minimally Invasive Cardiac Surgery), Cardiac MRI (including tissue mapping and adenosine stress perfusion), and Chest CT (supporting the Division of Respirology, which includes the largest outpatient TB clinic in Toronto, The National Cystic Fibrosis Centre [largest program in North America],\u00a0 the HHT program [largest Canadian centre], and other subspecialty clinics). Unity Health Toronto, including SMH, is now an official participant site in the Ontario Lung Cancer Screening Program and we have an active lung cancer screening CT program as well. The Abdominal Imaging practice encompasses high-acuity and complex abdominal and pelvic CT and MRI, including oncologic, hepatobiliary, gastrointestinal, genitourinary, postoperative, emergency and trauma imaging; advanced gynecologic and pelvic MRI, including pelvic floor imaging; and a broad range of abdominal and pelvic ultrasound, including advanced doppler and gynecologic ultrasound. There are 3 dedicated IR suites and 2 dedicated neurointerventional suites, 9 ultrasound units, 4 CT scanners (2 dual-energy whole heart volume CT scanners), 4 MRI scanners (all with cardiac imaging packages), and 1 PET-CT scanner (already operational with Ontario Health approval for both cardiac and oncologic applications) at SMH. The hospital houses the Li Ka Shing Knowledge Institute and the Keenan Research Centre that provides excellent research support and affords many opportunities for radiologists to engage in inter-departmental, collaborative translational research in Medical Imaging. There are significant resources in support of the Department of Medical Imaging\u2019s internationally recognized AI research work. The position includes a significant opportunity for advancement in clinical leadership and research in Cardiothoracic and Abdominal Imaging, both at the University of Toronto and at SMH. The successful applicant must hold an MD or equivalent and will have completed residency training in Diagnostic Radiology and fellowships in both Cardiothoracic Imaging and Abdominal Imaging. The successful candidate will join the Divisions of Cardiothoracic and Abdominal Radiology in the Department of Medical Imaging at SMH, and participate in the on-call roster covering these specialties. They will be expected to participate in radiology resident rounds and in multi-disciplinary team meetings/rounds including Structural Heart Rounds. They will supervise trainees at the undergraduate, graduate and post-graduate levels in their area of formal fellowship training, including but not limited to the dedicated clinical Cardiothoracic and Abdominal Fellowship programs at SMH each year. They must be eligible for medical licensure with the College of Physicians and Surgeons in Ontario and for certification with the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada, or have comparable qualifications. Evidence of excellence in teaching and research is required. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with the candidate's qualifications and experience. The salary range of this position exceeds $200,000 CAD per annum. Qualified candidates should send a cover letter, CV, and list of 3 potential references to Dr. Anish Kirpalani, Chief, Department of Medical Imaging, St. Michael\u2019s Hospital to: Anish.Kirpalani@unityhealth.to by November 19, 2026. The position will remain open until filled. Review of applications will begin immediately. For more information about the Department of Medical Imaging at the University of Toronto, please visit our home page at https://medical-imaging.utoronto.ca/ For more information about the Department of Medical Imaging at SMH, please visit our practice\u2019s home page at https://radiology.to/ . CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Cardiac, Gastroenterology, Neurology, Oncology, General Surgery, Healthcare Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Website-Design-and-Digital-Storytelling-Officer-%28TERM%29-ON/607100917/": {"title": "Website Design and Digital Storytelling Officer (TERM) Job Details", "description": "Website Design and Digital Storytelling Officer (TERM) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Website Design and Digital Storytelling Officer (TERM) Date Posted: 10/16/2026 Req ID: 50576 Faculty/Division: Henry N.R. Jackman Faculty of Law Department: Henry N.R. Jackman Faculty of Law Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00059635 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Henry N.R. Jackman Faculty of Law is one of the oldest professional faculties at the University of Toronto. Today, it is one of the world's great law schools. The Faculty's rich academic programs are complemented by its many legal clinics and public interest programs. Jackman Law is housed in the elegant, state-of-the-art Jackman Law Building, alongside two historic buildings, Flavelle House and Falconer Hall, on the St. George Campus in downtown Toronto. Your opportunity: Jackman Law is home to a vibrant community of scholars, students, alumni and staff whose work and impact extend well beyond the Faculty. Our digital platforms play an important role in telling those stories, connecting with our communities, and showcasing the Faculty's teaching, research, people, programs and contributions to the legal profession and society. Under the general direction of the Head of Strategy and Transformation & Senior Advisor to the Dean, the Website Design and Digital Storytelling Officer will play a central role in shaping and strengthening the Faculty's digital presence. Combining strong web, design and technical skills with excellent editorial judgment and a creative approach to storytelling, the incumbent will support the development and enhancement of the Faculty's websites, create engaging digital and multimedia content, and support digital communications initiatives that advance the Faculty's strategic priorities and strengthen engagement with key audiences. Your responsibilities will include: Creating, editing and enhancing the Faculty's websites and digital platforms Creating compelling digital stories and content that showcase the Faculty's people, programs, research and impact Advising on website design, content and digital communications strategies to advance Faculty priorities Developing and Implementing digital communication plans across multiple channels Creating and coordinating digital and visual assets, including determining the effective presentation of video, audio and photography, and developing graphic designs and layouts Ensuring the Faculty's web and digital content meets University requirements and recognized standards for accessibility, usability, brand identity and style Building strong working relationships with faculty, staff and other internal and external partners, by providing advice and support on web and digital communications Using web, campaign and audience analytics to evaluate the effectiveness of digital initiatives, identify opportunities for improvement, and recommend emerging technologies, tools and approaches Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or an acceptable combination of equivalent education and experience Minimum four years of relevant experience in website management, digital communications, digital content creation, and marketing communications, preferably within a higher education or similarly complex organization. Demonstrated experience managing and maintaining websites using a content management system, including creating and editing webpages and interactive content. Experience troubleshooting website issues and working effectively with technical teams, vendors or service providers to resolve problems and implement improvements. Demonstrated experience contributing to and implementing digital communications initiatives across multiple channels. Demonstrated experience developing digital stories and translating academic research, professional education or other complex subject matter into accessible and compelling content. Experience creating and producing multimedia content, including creating and editing photographs, videos, audio, graphics, and other digital assets. Experience with digital layout, including demonstrated ability to develop visually engaging materials aligned with organizational objectives and brand standards. Experience using web and digital analytics to assess audience behaviour and the effectiveness of digital content, campaigns or programs. Exceptional writing, editing and proofreading skills, with demonstrated ability to create engaging digital content for a range of audiences and purposes. High level of proficiency with MS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), CMS (Drupal, WordPress), HTML, Adobe Creative Suite (Illustrator, Photoshop, Lightroom, Premiere Pro, After Effect), Canva, Mailchimp, web analytics (Google Analytics). Demonstrated knowledge of digital accessibility standards and experience applying accessibility requirements to web and digital content. Demonstrated knowledge of contemporary web design, usability and user experience practices. Knowledge of search engine optimization principles and techniques. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple digital and communications projects simultaneously, including coordinating contributors, production requirements and deadlines. Strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills, with demonstrated ability to advise and collaborate effectively with a wide range of colleagues, clients and stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to exercise excellent judgment and translate client or stakeholder objectives into effective digital communications solutions. Strong organizational and problem-solving skills and demonstrated ability to work effectively in a fast-paced environment with changing priorities and urgent assignments. Demonstrated commitment to staying current with emerging technologies, digital communications practices and trends. Assets (Nonessential): Experience working in a university, professional school or other complex academic environment. Knowledge and understanding of the legal community and profession. To be successful in this role you will be: Adaptable Discerning Meticulous Motivated self-learner Organized Proactive Resourceful Team player Closing Date: 10/27/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 11 -- $79,640 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $101,845. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Communication/Media/Public Relations Divisional HR Office Email: pfhr@utoronto.ca Note: This opportunity is for a one year term Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Photography, Proofreading, Copy Editor, SEO, Web Design, Creative, Marketing Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Associate-Director%2C-Undergraduate-Awards-%28Term%29-ON/607100817/": {"title": "Associate Director, Undergraduate Awards (Term)", "description": "Associate Director, Undergraduate Awards (Term) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Associate Director, Undergraduate Awards (Term) Date Posted: 10/16/2026 Req ID: 50588 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: Faculty Registrar Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00043101 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Faculty of Arts & Science is the heart of Canada\u2019s leading university and one of the most comprehensive and diverse academic divisions in the world. The strength of Arts & Science derives from our combined teaching and research excellence in the humanities, sciences and social sciences across 29 departments, seven colleges and 46 interdisciplinary centres, institutes and programs. We can only realize our mission with the dedication and excellence of engaged staff and faculty. The diversity of opportunities and perspectives within the Faculty reflect the local and global landscape and the need for curiosity, innovative thinking and collaboration. At Arts & Science, we take pride in our legacy of innovation and discovery that has changed the way we think about the world. Your opportunity: Reporting to the Associate Faculty Registrar & Director, Operations & Project Management, this position supports the administration of student awards and scholarships in the Faculty of Arts & Science. The role is responsible for managing the assessment of award eligibility, managing scholarship funds and financial records, conducting financial audits, and providing guidance to students on scholarship options and related matters. The incumbent analyzes financial and statistical information, prepares reports, and makes recommendations on funding allocations. The position also collaborates with committees, donors, and internal stakeholders, promotes student programs and services, and supports students facing complex challenges. In addition, the role provides oversight and direction to support staff. Your responsibilities will include: Facilitating educational workshops and seminars Analyzing complex statistical reports and/or financial information for management decision-making Implementing plans for awards programs and related objectives Producing complex statistical and/or financial reports Planning and implementing components of registrarial projects Collaborating on cost estimates Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum of five (5) years of recent and related experience in administering student awards, scholarships, bursaries, financial aid programs, or related student services within a post-secondary environment. Experience interpreting and applying policies, procedures, and eligibility criteria related to awards, scholarships, funding programs, and student support services. Demonstrated experience managing financial records, budgets, scholarship funds, reconciliations, and financial reporting. Experience with developing and interpreting financial reports. Proven awards administration experience, including advising prospective and current students on award programs and assessing scholarship and grant applications for eligibility. Experience preparing statistical analyses, reports, and making recommendations for management. Experience working collaboratively with donors, committees, faculty, staff, and other internal and external stakeholders. Demonstrated experience supervising, coordinating, or providing direction to administrative or support staff. Experience with Financial Information System (FIS), Arbor and/or Development Information System (DIS), and ROSI. Experience working with payment cycles, criteria-based awards as they relate to provincial matching program guidelines. Experience and demonstrated knowledge and application of accounting principles. Advanced financial analysis and data management skills with a high degree of accuracy and attention to detail. Strong verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to prepare reports, correspondence, and presentations. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, and experience working with student information systems, databases, and reporting tools. Strong analytical, organizational, research, strategic thinking and planning skills. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to assess complex information and make sound recommendations. Exceptional interpersonal and relationship-building skills, with the ability to work effectively with students, faculty, donors, committees, and senior administrators. Assets (Nonessential): MBA and/or CPA designation is considered an asset. To be successful in this role you will be: Approachable Communicator Multi-tasker Organized Problem solver Resourceful Self-directed Team player Please note:\u00a0 This is a term position until November 2027. Closing Date: 10/27/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 15 -- $101,242 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $129,471. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Divisional HR Office Email: adminhr.artsci@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Data Management, Information Systems, Project Manager, Equity, Data, Technology, Finance, Research Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Professor%2C-Teaching-Stream-Engineering-Design-ON/607102817/": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream", "description": "Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream - Engineering Design Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream - Engineering Design Date Posted: 10/16/2026 Closing Date: 12/08/2026, 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50211 Job Category: Faculty - Teaching Stream (continuing) Faculty/Division: Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering Department: Department of Mechanical and Industrial Engineering Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes POSITION DESCRIPTION The Department of Mechanical and Industrial Engineering (MIE) and the Division of Engineering Science (EngSci) in the Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering at the University of Toronto invite applications for a full-time teaching stream position in engineering design. This will be a joint appointment between MIE (51%) and EngSci (49%). The appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. REQUIREMENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS Applicants must have earned a PhD degree in engineering or a related area by the time of appointment, or shortly thereafter, with a demonstrated record of excellence in teaching in engineering design. We seek candidates whose teaching interests complement and enhance our existing departmental strengths . The successful candidate will be jointly appointed to the Department of Mechanical & Industrial Engineering (MIE) and the Division of Engineering Science (EngSci); however, a background in mechanical or industrial engineering is not required as the position considers engineering design broadly across all engineering disciplines aligned with EngSci\u2019s nine interdisciplinary majors. The successful candidate will teach introductory and advanced courses in these areas to undergraduate students in EngSci and beyond. Candidates must be registered, or eligible for registration, as a Professional Engineer. This is important as faculty members teaching design courses to undergraduate students must be Professional Engineers for program accreditation as set out by the Canadian Engineering Accreditation Board. For more information on registering as a Professional Engineer in Ontario, follow this link . Candidates must have teaching experience in a degree-granting program, including lecture preparation and delivery, curriculum development, and development of online material/lectures. Additionally, candidates must possess a demonstrated commitment to excellent pedagogical inquiry and a demonstrated interest in teaching-related scholarly activities. Evidence of excellence in teaching and a commitment to excellent pedagogical inquiry will be demonstrated through teaching accomplishments, awards and accolades, presentations at significant conferences, the teaching dossier (including the required materials outlined below), and strong letters of reference. RESPONSIBILITIES The successful candidate will be assigned a teaching and service load with the following responsibilities: Deliver an innovative, hands-on, theoretically grounded, rigorous engineering design curriculum. Teach engineering design courses throughout the curriculum. Engineering Science program currently has three one-term, cornerstone design courses in the foundation curriculum (years 1 and 2) as well as capstone design courses in each of its nine Majors (years 3 and 4). Redefine, reshape, and continuously improve the Engineering Science design curriculum, and hence, the candidate should be comfortable with a wide variety of design pedagogies, as demonstrated through the application materials. Collaborate with other members of the faculty to blend engineering design education with communication and teamwork. Serve as the Division\u2019s representative on various faculty and divisional committee/s as required. HIRING SALARY RANGE The salary range is $125,000-$160,000 CAD per annum, depending on experience. Negotiations beyond this salary range will be considered for exceptionally qualified candidates. ABOUT US About the Division of Engineering Science Engineering Science is an undergraduate program within the Faculty of Applied Science and Engineering at the University of Toronto that leads to the degree of Bachelor of Applied Science in Engineering Science. The program attracts bright and capable students from across Canada and around the world, making for an excellent and inspiring community of learners, many of whom go on to post-graduate studies in engineering, science, business, medicine, and law. The Division of Engineering Science is the administrative unit within the Faculty that is responsible for this program. Except for this faculty appointment and three others in the Division of Engineering Science, the majority of teaching resources for the program are drawn from departments across the Faculty and outside the Faculty. The program has a world-renowned reputation for innovative engineering pedagogy that integrates a strong foundation in theory with practice. The curriculum consists of two years of common foundation, followed by two years of specialization in one of nine Majors. For more information about the Engineering Science program, please visit: engsci.utoronto.ca . About the Faculty The Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering offers opportunities for collaborative and interdisciplinary research and teaching, and the excitement of working with a diverse student population. Established in 1873, the Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering has earned an international reputation for excellence in education and knowledge creation and is known as a forward-thinking resource to address global concerns. As the economic and intellectual hub of Canada, Toronto provides access to leading policy and decision makers at all levels, and is a vibrant, cosmopolitan, and safe city. For more information about the Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering, please visit: engineering.utoronto.ca . For more information on working at the University of Toronto, please visit https://www.utoronto.ca/research-innovation/working-at-uoft . APPLICATION PROCESS All application materials, including recent reference letters, must be received by December 8, 2026. All qualified candidates are invited to apply online by clicking the link below. Your CV and cover letter should be uploaded into the dedicated fields. Please combine additional application materials into one or two files in PDF/MS Word format. Applicants must submit the following materials: a cover letter; a current curriculum vitae; a recent writing sample; a complete teaching dossier, including: a teaching statement, sample syllabi and course materials, evidence of design practice, and teaching evaluations; and the name and contact information of three references. At least one reference letter must primarily address the candidate\u2019s teaching. The University of Toronto\u2019s recruiting tool will automatically solicit and collect letters of reference from each referee within 48 hours of an application being submitted. Applicants remain responsible for ensuring that references submit recent letters (on letterhead, dated and signed) by the closing date. Submission guidelines and details on the automatic reference letter collection, including timelines, are available in the candidate FAQ . If you have any questions about this position, please contact Diane Giang, Manager of Finance and Administration at director.engsci@utoronto.ca . All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Industrial Engineer, Curriculum Development, Engineer, Design Engineer, Engineering, Education, Research Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Faculty Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Manager%2C-Information-Security-ON/607109817/": {"title": "Manager, Information Security Job Details", "description": "Manager, Information Security Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Manager, Information Security Date Posted: 10/16/2026 Req ID: 50591 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: Information and Instructional Technology Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00055831 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About Us The Faculty of Arts & Science is the heart of Canada\u2019s leading university and one of the world's most comprehensive and diverse academic divisions. The strength of Arts & Science derives from our combined teaching and research excellence in the humanities, sciences and social sciences across 29 departments, seven colleges and 46 interdisciplinary centres, institutes and programs. We can only realize our mission with the dedication and excellence of engaged staff and faculty. The faculty\u2019s diversity of opportunities and perspectives reflects the local and global landscape and the need for curiosity, innovative thinking, and collaboration. At Arts & Science, we take pride in our legacy of innovation and discovery that has changed how we think about the world. The Faculty\u2019s divisional IT team, Information & Instructional Technology (IIT) provides divisional IT services and support across the Faculty including day to day computing and infrastructure fulfillment as well as data centre and public web services and application development. Working collaboratively with central University IT and local departmental IT teams, IIT supports teaching, research, and administrative operations through secure, reliable, and modern technology solutions. Your Opportunity Reporting to the Executive Director, Information & Instructional Technology, and with a dotted-line relationship to the University's Chief Information Security & Digital Trust Officer (CISDTO), the Manager, Information Security provides strategic and operational leadership for the Faculty's information security and IT risk management programs. The Manager, Information Security is responsible for developing, implementing, and advancing a coordinated, division-wide approach to information security and technology risk. Working collaboratively with institutional security leadership, divisional IT, and departmental IT teams, the incumbent strengthens the Faculty's security posture while supporting the diverse needs of teaching, research, and administration. The role combines strategic planning, security program development, risk assessment and program management, technical expertise, incident coordination, and stakeholder engagement. It also supports the responsible adoption of emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence, automation, and cloud services, in alignment with University policies, standards, and governance requirements. As a member of the Faculty's IT leadership team, the Manager, Information Security fosters a proactive, collaborative, and risk-aware security culture while balancing security requirements with academic and operational priorities. Key Responsibilities Information Security Strategy and Risk Management Lead the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of divisional information security and IT risk management programs. Establish security priorities, assess vulnerabilities, identify risks, and recommend appropriate controls and remediation strategies. Support the adoption and implementation of University information security policies, standards, governance requirements, and industry best practices. Develop security reporting, risk assessments, performance measures, and recommendations to support informed leadership decisions. Advise on security and risk considerations associated with emerging technologies, including AI, automation, cloud platforms, and digital innovation. Security Operations and Incident Management Coordinate divisional security incident response, investigations, escalation, and remediation in collaboration with institutional security teams and departmental IT. Support security assessments, technical investigations, vulnerability management, and risk reduction initiatives. Collaborate with functional IT Managers and teams to strengthen operational resilience, security controls, and business continuity readiness. Review proposed technology solutions and projects to identify security risks and recommend appropriate safeguards. Leadership and Program Delivery Lead and manage assigned security personnel, resources, priorities, projects, and operational activities. Develop and oversee security initiatives, including planning, budgeting, procurement, vendor management, implementation, and performance reporting. Collaboration, Governance and Security Awareness Build strong working relationships with Faculty leadership, departmental IT teams, institutional security teams, and other stakeholders. Promote a consistent and collaborative approach to information security and risk management across the Faculty. Provide expert security advice to academic and administrative units on technology initiatives, risk mitigation, and compliance requirements. Support security awareness, education, and engagement initiatives for faculty, staff, and students. Required Qualifications Education University degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Information Technology, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. Graduate degree and professional certifications such as CISSP, CISM, CISA, CRISC, PMP, or equivalent are considered assets. Experience Information Security and Risk Management Minimum eight (8) years of progressively responsible experience in information technology, with significant experience in information security, IT risk management, and security program development. Demonstrated experience developing, implementing, and improving information security policies, standards, controls, and risk management practices. Strong experience assessing security risks across enterprise technology environments, including endpoints, servers, networks, cloud services, applications, vendor solutions and identity systems. Experience coordinating security incidents, investigations, vulnerability assessments, and remediation activities. Experience with security monitoring, threat detection, defense-in-depth strategies, and security assessment tools. Experience supporting compliance reviews, security audits, and the implementation of security governance requirements. Technology and Infrastructure Minimum eight (8) years of experience in an IT operations, infrastructure, or technology support environment. Strong understanding of enterprise IT architecture, networking, cloud platforms, infrastructure security, and business-critical applications. Experience with Microsoft enterprise technologies, including Azure, Microsoft Entra ID, and associated security and identity management capabilities. Knowledge of change management, configuration management, and technology lifecycle practices. Familiarity with the security and governance considerations associated with artificial intelligence, automation, and emerging technologies. Leadership and Management Minimum eight (8) years of experience in a formal people management or technology leadership role. Demonstrated success leading and mentoring technical teams, managing competing priorities, and delivering complex initiatives. Experience with project and program management, financial planning, budgeting, procurement, vendor management, and contract oversight. Proven ability to collaborate with diverse stakeholders and influence outcomes across decentralized or complex organizational environments. Skills and Competencies Strong strategic thinking, leadership, organizational, and decision-making abilities. Excellent interpersonal, relationship management, and communication skills. Ability to translate complex technical and security issues into clear, practical recommendations for senior leadership and non-technical stakeholders. Strong analytical, problem-solving, risk assessment, and incident management capabilities. Ability to manage multiple priorities, respond effectively to urgent issues, and exercise sound judgment under pressure. Strong commitment to collaboration, confidentiality, professionalism, and service excellence. Ability to navigate complex organizational structures, build consensus, and escalate issues appropriately. Demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity, and inclusion. Additional Assets Experience working in a large, decentralized organization, preferably within higher education or a research-intensive environment. Familiarity with IT Service Management and ITIL practices, including platforms such as ServiceNow. Familiarity with AI security governance, cloud security assessments, and enterprise technology risk management. LEAN, Six Sigma, or related process improvement experience. Other Requirements Availability to respond to critical security incidents outside regular working hours, when required. Ability to manage sensitive and confidential information with discretion and integrity. Closing Date: 11/06/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 5 -- Hiring Zone: $125,319 - $146,206 -- Broadband Salary Range: $125,319  - $208,864 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Information Technology, IT Manager, Information Security, Risk Management, Program Manager, Technology, Finance, Management Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Indigenous-Student-Life-Coordinator-ON/607109417/": {"title": "Indigenous Student Life Coordinator", "description": "Indigenous Student Life Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Indigenous Student Life Coordinator Date Posted: 10/16/2026 Req ID: 50577 Faculty/Division: Vice-Provost, Students Department: Indigenous Student Services Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00011468 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Student Life connects life to learning. We believe every student should have the opportunity to participate in university life actively and find connection and community while discovering new ways of thinking and being in the world. We provide resources, support and engagement opportunities that are inclusive and accessible, ensuring every student can build experiences that set them up for a lifetime of success. Within the Division of Student Life, the cluster of Student Life Programs and Services, supports students as they achieve personal, academic, career and civic goals. We engage students throughout their learning and development with the following units: Accessibility Services, Career Exploration & Education, Centre for Learning Strategy Support, Clubs & Leadership Development, Indigenous Student Services, Mentorship & Peer Programs, Multi-faith Centre, Orientation, Student Success, Transition & Engagement and TCard Services. Together with staff, faculty, students, alumni, employers and community partners, we provide an integrated and coherent path to success that reflects our students' diversity. In support of U of T\u2019s vision, Student Life Programs and Services is committed to creating diverse, accessible, inclusive and welcoming spaces of opportunity that foster deepened engagement, learning, personal growth, and identity development for all students. We are committed to embedding these principles into all the work we do, reducing barriers so that students from all backgrounds and lived experiences can feel a sense of belonging in the communities they find here. To align with our strategic priorities, and the specificities of this role, we encourage individuals from Indigenous communities to apply. Your opportunity: Under the direction of the Director of the Office of Indigenous Student Services, the incumbent will be responsible for the development, implementation and/or coordination of activities that encourage student development. To achieve this, the Indigenous Student Life Coordinator, working with other offices at the Indigenous Student Services/First Nations House (e.g. Elders in Residence) will assist in the organization of programming that supports personal, leadership and spiritual growth for students. In addition, the Indigenous Student Life Coordinator is responsible for coordinating the promotion of First Nations House within the institution (e.g. studentfairs, orientations, divisional activities); and support the Indigenous Recruitment Officer in the implementation of coordinating outreach activities at the University (e.g. Summer Mentorship Program, Jr. Deep, SOAR). The Indigenous Student Life Coordinator is also responsible for the coordination of annual department events (e.g. Indigenous Education Week, Fall Gathering potluck). The incumbent will refer students to the appropriate resources upon request; develop and maintain a volunteer list; and as necessary, develop and maintain student records. The incumbent will be responsible for all communications for the department, including but not limited to the maintaining the departmental website and listserv; oversee departmental social media outlets, development of promotional material (print and digital) and interacting with the appropriate communication network within the university (e.g. Strategic Communications, Student Life). The Indigenous Student Life Coordinator oversees work-study students, either directly supervising or supporting student staff; is the liaison to the Indigenous Students\u2019 Association and other student bodies. Your responsibilities will include: Planning and implementing components of curricular and/or co-curricular programs and activities Planning and overseeing the implementation of an evaluation framework for programs and initiatives Conducting detailed analysis on program efficiency and student learning outcomes to inform program planning activities Implementing plans and process improvements for program and service activities Promoting experiential learning opportunities Facilitating educational workshops and seminars Screening and making referrals to academic advising and learning skills programs and other resources or services Developing strategies that maximize outreach to students Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or an acceptable equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum four years related experience working with Indigenous communities/agencies and peoples in a community and/or life skills development role. Minimum two years in a student life programming role preferably in a post-secondary setting. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to create, compose, edit written materials. Excellent presentation, interpersonal and organizational skills. Excellent program development and implementation skills and excellent relationship building skills. Working knowledge of Word, PowerPoint, Excel, Outlook, web software (e.g. Dreamweaver) and design software (e.g. Creative Suite). A good degree of social media experience is required. Tact and diplomacy; ability to work in a team environment; build partnerships and collaborate across the University. Strong knowledge of the diverse Indigenous traditions, values and cultural protocols; along with an understanding of services and resources available in the Greater Toronto Area. Knowledge of educational issues/barriers (e.g. educational history, funding access) and wider community concerns (i.e. housing, family concerns, economic). Assets (Nonessential): Experience making effective referrals. Aptitude in an Indigenous language. To be successful in this role you will be: Approachable Communicator Multi-tasker Organized Resourceful Team player Closing Date: 10/30/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 12 -- $84,564 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $108,145. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Divisional HR Office Email: cahrs.hr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Equity, Intern, Finance, Entry Level Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Operating-Engineer-B-%283rd-Class%29-Building-Shift-Operations-ON/604395517/": {"title": "Operating Engineer B (3rd Class)", "description": "Operating Engineer B (3rd Class) - Building Shift Operations Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Operating Engineer B (3rd Class) - Building Shift Operations Date Posted: 10/14/2026 Req ID: 49231 Faculty/Division: Asst VP - Operations & Services Department: F.&S. Utilities -06 Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: General Description of Class: Under the direction of the Chief Operating Engineer and/or the Assistant Chief Engineer, the incumbent is responsible for building shift operations governed by TSSA regulations. The shift engineer is responsible for the safe and economical operation and maintenance of all mechanical and associated equipment and services in their area of responsibility. Typical Duties: The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required and the extent of responsibility involved in this job; they in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated: Regular rounds to check mechanical equipment and perform needed mechanical service; Ensures continuous efficiency of all mechanical equipment services and faculty equipment; Provides running maintenance by checking lube levels of compressors and adjustments to all equipment and controls; Answers and reacts promptly to all trouble calls or alarms from buildings during off hour and weekend shifts; Reviews computer printouts and alarms and takes appropriate action; Co-ordinates and/or assists outside contractors and University of Toronto Trades Services when work is performed during shift; Housekeeping: painting, sweeping floors, cleaning piping, boilers and equipment; Responds to off duty calls to correct emergency situations and problems; and Maintains daily log sheets on operating equipment and records all important events that occur during shift and Communicates with relief shift engineer on event issues. Education: High School graduate or equivalent combination of education and experience plus a Third (3rd) Class Operating Engineer Certification valid in the Province of Ontario. Experience: Minimum of one\u00a0(1) year\u00a0experience as an operating engineer. Must have a good working knowledge ofthe operation and maintenance of mechanical equipment, including refrigeration, heating (e.g.boilers) and air handling systems, and ability to comprehend and apply environmental control principles. Must have: basic electrical knowledge and trouble-shooting skills, basic profi ciency in standard office computer applications (e.g.Microsoft Word, Excel, Windows OS) and familiarity with computerized Building Automation Systems or other computerized control systems. Other: Must have: good diagnostic and record keeping skills, the ability to communicate effectively (both orally and written), strong customer service skills and the ability to work collaboratively with others. Building Environmental Systems Certificate an asset. This position is not eligible for the Operating QET for TSSA OE certification Work Schedule: Must be available for day, afternoon and night shifts (including weekends and statutory holidays). Rotating shifts, 40hrs/week. Please note: This vacancy is for 2 positions. Closing Date: 10/28/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: Unifor FT L2003 Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: $43.13/hr Job Category: Engineering / Technical Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: HVAC, Housekeeping, Electrical, Engineer, Operations, Healthcare, Engineering, Hospitality Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Sport-Facility-Operator-ON/607039017/": {"title": "Note: This position requires outdoor work during all seasons of the year.", "description": "Sport Facility Operator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Sport Facility Operator Date Posted: 10/15/2026 Req ID: 50557 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Kinesiology & Physl Ed. Department: Faculty of Kinesiology & Physl Ed Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Description: Under general supervision, operates and maintains a number of motorized vehicles and specialized equipment; performs maintenance functions. Typical Duties The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required, and the extent of responsibility involved in this job. They in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated. Flexibility of the employee to perform a wide variety of functions is necessary in successfully fulfilling the requirements of this position. The degree to which each employee performs each of the following tasks listed below will vary according to where and when the employee is scheduled to work. drives and operates a pick-up truck, ice flooding machine, field grooming machine, ice edging machine, snow blower and outdoor vacuum, golf cart and other motorized vehicles as required; maintain sport playing surfaces including, natural grass, AstroTurf, ice surfaces, courts (basketball and volleyball); facility upkeep including identifying and troubleshooting deficiencies in the facility including identifying defective vehicles and equipment and may perform minor facility maintenance on vehicles and equipment; set-up and maintain vehicles and sporting equipment for faculty, university and external customer events; while continuously projecting a positive professional image of the faculty in dress and behaviour at all times while on duty; shovels snow, sweeps garbage, mops floors, marks fields and erects temporary fixtures, cleans locker rooms, paints and performs minor maintenance duties; opens and locks doors of designated areas used by authorized personnel; requests unauthorized personnel to leave premises; escalating as required; prepares laundry for washing, maintains and operates equipment according to standard operating procedures; maintains inventory of supplies. Notifies supervisor when supplies are low; ensures equipment and materials are moved and stored in an orderly and appropriate manner, moves furniture and equipment as required; performs seasonal locker clean outs, cutting locks as directed; removes belongings, records and stores items removed in the designated area for pick up; provides guidance and assistance to casual staff and others as directed; other related duties as required. Note: This position requires outdoor work during all seasons of the year. Qualifications Minimum Requirements: Education: Completion of Grade 12 or equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience: A minimum of three years of related sport facility operator experience. A minimum of one year of experience with an ice resurfacer is required. Experience maintaining sport playing surfaces is considered an asset. Must have considerable front line customer service experience. Other: Must have the ability to perform the essential physical functional requirements of the position, including lifting and moving heavy equipment up to 25kgs. Must possess excellent communication skills including the demonstrated ability to follow written and oral instructions. Must demonstrate diplomacy, tact and conflict management skills; must be able to deal calmly with angry or upset individuals, to exercise good judgment and to take initiative; must be able to resolve problems and to participate effectively within a team. Must have an understanding of diversity and equity issues. Must possess a Provincial Class \"G\" driver's license to operate motorized vehicles. Must successfully complete a current First Aid, AED and CPR certificate within the probationary period (90 working days). Certifications must be kept current and must be updated annually. Completion of the ORFA Ice Maintenance course is a strong asset. Closing Date: 10/25/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Monday to Friday: 3:00 p.m. to 11:30 p.m. Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: Job Rate: $28.24/hr Job Category: Athletics Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Facilities, Fitness, Equity, Temporary, Operations, Hospitality, Finance, Contract Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Lab-Coordinator-%28term%29-ON/607060717/": {"title": "Lab Coordinator (term)", "description": "Lab Coordinator (term) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Lab Coordinator (term) Date Posted: 10/15/2026 Req ID: 50550 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: Dept of Psychology Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00057207 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Faculty of Arts & Science is the heart of Canada\u2019s leading university and one of the most comprehensive and diverse academic divisions in the world. The strength of Arts & Science derives from our combined teaching and research excellence in the humanities, sciences and social sciences across 29 departments, seven colleges and 46 interdisciplinary centres, institutes and programs. We can only realize our mission with the dedication and excellence of engaged staff and faculty. The diversity of opportunities and perspectives within The Faculty reflect the local and global landscape and the need for curiosity, innovative thinking and collaboration. At Arts & Science, we take pride in our legacy of innovation and discovery that has changed the way we think about the world. Established in 1927, the Department of Psychology has for more than a century been a top choice for those pursuing a career in psychological research. The combined expertise of our faculty spans all major areas of psychology and reflects a wide range of approaches to the study of mind, brain and behaviour. Our department comprises a diverse and internationally recognized faculty, first-rate laboratory facilities and a tradition of cutting-edge, collaborative research in an inspiring intellectual atmosphere. Your opportunity: Under close supervision of the Principal Investigators, the Lab Coordinator is responsible for coordinating all aspects of research for various cognitive studies with both children and adults. Duties include but are not limited to proofing and posting adverts to recruit participants; following rules and procedural instructions when administering research study test materials, testing participants and collating data; and scheduling and keeping track of participants\u2019 appointments and participant fees. The Lab Coordinator applies established standards when cleaning and maintaining the research lab, ensuring supplies are adequate stocked; maintains filing and website information. Due to various events and other lab activities, the Lab Coordinator role may include some hours worked in the evenings and/or on the weekends as needed. Note: this is a one year grant-funded term opportunity. Your responsibilities will include: Proofing and posting adverts to recruit applicants Following rules and procedural instructions when administering research studies Recording and tabulating experiment results Preparing consent forms using templates Providing some care to prevent physical or emotional injury or harm Recording or verifying transactions on a single account Providing orientation to others, including workstudy students, on work procedures and practices Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in Psychology, a related field, or an acceptable combination of equivalent education and experience. Minimum one (1) year of relevant experience working in a developmental psychology or cognitive neuroscience lab. Some experience working with children participating in research studies. Demonstrated interest in and exposure to research in cognition, particularly learning and memory, and their relation to the brain. Must be comfortable working with children and families, and have strong interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated time management and organizational skills with proven ability to prioritize work and meet firm deadlines. Strong attention to detail, demonstrated ability to follow rules and procedural instructions when administering research studies. Demonstrated ability to workas a team player. Working knowledge of software such as Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and R statistical software to record and tabulate experiment results and code quantitative research data. To be successful in this role you will be: Accountable Communicator Courteous Multi-tasker Organized Problem solver Closing Date: 10/26/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Grant - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 05 -- $55,563 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $71,056. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Research Administration & Teaching Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Testing, Neurology, Laboratory, Equity, Technology, Healthcare, Science, Research, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Mississauga-Landscape-Technician-I-Temp-ON/607070117/": {"title": "Landscape Technician I", "description": "Landscape Technician I -  Temp Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Landscape Technician I -  Temp Date Posted: 10/15/2026 Req ID: 50566 Faculty/Division: UofT Mississauga Department: UTM: Facilities, Management & Planning Campus: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Entry level of the Landscape Technician series, under direct supervision performs standard landscape duties. Typical Duties: The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required and the extent of the responsibility involved in this position. They in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated. Flexibility of the employee to perform a wide variety of functions is necessary in successfully fulfilling the requirements of this position. The degree to which each employee performs each of the following tasks listed below will vary according to where and when the employee is\u00a0scheduled to work. trims, cuts and waters grass and flowers, rakes and collects leaves, lays sod; plants flowers, shrubs and trees; maintains soft landscaping by aerating, weeding, cultivating, fertilizing, etc.; drives and operates a variety of landscape and snow removal vehicles and equipment such as equipment used in tree maintenance, turf care, chainsaws, sod cutters, riding vacuums, snow maintenance vehicles, tractors (front and back-end loaders) and skid steers; sets up vehicles and equipment for use, and performs simple adjustments; loads and unloads equipment onto vehicles; works on cleaning details using appropriate vehicles and equipment; includes the removal of graffiti, posters and abandoned or illegally locked bicycles; works on snow and ice removal details using appropriate vehicles and equipment; works on moving details using appropriate vehicles and equipment; maintain landscape irrigation and other landscape related systems; and provides instruction to Service Worker \u2013 Grounds staff in performing assigned tasks; other related duties as required. Qualifications Minimum Requirements: Education: Completion of Grade 12 or equivalent combination of education and experience. Completion of some related landscape courses are an asset. Experience: Three years of related experience. Other: Possession of valid Provincial Class \"G\" driver's license, physical ability to perform required duties, demonstrated ability to communicate effectively in English (oral and written), ability to work under all weather conditions and may be required to work long and varied hours. PLEASE NOTE: THIS POSITION IS TEMPORARY FOR 120 DAYS ONLY Shift Details: May-October: Monday-Friday,10:30AM \u2013 7:00PM November-April: Monday-Friday, 12:00PM \u2013 8:30PM NOTE : Must be available to be On Call during the winter months for snow removal operations in accordance with the Collective Agreement. Closing Date: 10/26/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: CUPE Tmp L3261 Appointment Type : Budget - Temp Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: Job Rate -- $25.66 Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Landscaping, Temporary, Technician, Entry Level, Operations, Contract, Technology Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Research-Associate-%282-Year-Term%29-Materials-ON/607037117/": {"title": "Research Associate (2 Year Term)", "description": "Research Associate (2 Year Term) - Materials Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Research Associate (2 Year Term) - Materials Date Posted: 10/15/2026 Req ID: 50555 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering Department: Dept of Civil and Mineral Engineering Campus : St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The University of Toronto\u2019s Department of Civil & Mineral Engineering offers a dynamic compendium of research and academic programs with a mandate that spans a wide range of applications in professional practice, encompassing the built environment and its infrastructure, transportation engineering and planning, structural engineering, environmental engineering, mining and geomechanics. Our department seeks to uphold and strengthen its position as a preeminent leader in education and research, and to continue to develop sustainable solutions for the global community across the spectrum from mineral engineering to urban infrastructure. The Structural Materials group in the Department of Civil and Mineral Engineering carries out research in the areas of concrete and other structural materials, durability, sustainability and corrosion. The Research Associate will work directly under the supervision of Professor Karl Peterson, and also conduct research supervised by Professors Daman Panesar, Ibrahim Ogunsanya and Professor Emeritus Doug Hooton. Responsibilities: Developing and executing\u00a0a research vision with PIs to achieve research goals Leading research activities on cement and concrete samples using SEM/EDX, TGA/DTA/DSC, XRD, isothermal calorimetry, and optical microscopy Training graduate students and other researchers on safe laboratory operations, material handling and equipment use\u00a0(including the analytical methods mentioned in the point above) Assisting graduate students, undergraduate students, and other researchers with their experimental testing program related to cement, concrete and other construction materials Providing technical leadership in the delivery of specialized research services, including experimental design, data analysis, interpretation of results, and communication of findings to stakeholders Maintaining laboratory equipment and ensure compliance with safety, quality, and operational protocols Writing grant and funding applications Preparing manuscripts, patents, technical reports, and reports to sponsors Presenting and publishing results at conferences and in journals. Quali\ufb01cations: Ph.D. in Civil\u00a0Engineering with specialization in concrete materials, or acceptable combination of equivalent experience Area of specialization must be in cementitious materials At least 4 years of post-PhD laboratory experience Evidence of research collaboration, teaching and training HQP Knowledge of lab safety protocols and ability to provide awareness and adherence of protocols to lab users Excellent verbal and written communication skills Demonstrated excellent leadership/organization as a team leader in R&D projects. Demonstrated research excellence, preferably with a strong publication record. Able to lift 20 kg to chest height Required Documents: Candidates are requested to submit a comprehensive cover letter that summarizes the research experience of the applicant and a CV. Note: This is a two year position with possibility of renewal. Closing Date: 10/23/2026,11:59PM ET Employee Group: Research Associate Personnel Subarea: Research Assoc Appointment Type : Grant - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: R01 -- Research Associates (Limited Term):  $55,661 - $104,364 Job Category: Engineering / Technical Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Civil Engineer, Structural Engineer, Environmental Engineering, Engineer, Data Analyst, Engineering, Data Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Mississauga-Landscape-Technician-I-Temp-ON/607070617/": {"title": "Landscape Technician I", "description": "Landscape Technician I - Temp Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Landscape Technician I - Temp Date Posted: 10/15/2026 Req ID: 50565 Faculty/Division: UofT Mississauga Department: UTM: Facilities, Management & Planning Campus: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Entry level of the Landscape Technician series, under direct supervision performs standard landscape duties. Typical Duties: The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required and the extent of the responsibility involved in this position. They in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated. Flexibility of the employee to perform a wide variety of functions is necessary in successfully fulfilling the requirements of this position. The degree to which each employee performs each of the following tasks listed below will vary according to where and when the employee is\u00a0scheduled to work. trims, cuts and waters grass and flowers, rakes and collects leaves, lays sod; plants flowers, shrubs and trees; maintains soft landscaping by aerating, weeding, cultivating, fertilizing, etc.; drives and operates a variety of landscape and snow removal vehicles and equipment such as equipment used in tree maintenance, turf care, chainsaws, sod cutters, riding vacuums, snow maintenance vehicles, tractors (front and back-end loaders) and skid steers; sets up vehicles and equipment for use, and performs simple adjustments; loads and unloads equipment onto vehicles; works on cleaning details using appropriate vehicles and equipment; includes the removal of graffiti, posters and abandoned or illegally locked bicycles; works on snow and ice removal details using appropriate vehicles and equipment; works on moving details using appropriate vehicles and equipment; maintain landscape irrigation and other landscape related systems; and provides instruction to Service Worker \u2013 Grounds staff in performing assigned tasks; other related duties as required. Qualifications Minimum Requirements: Education: Completion of Grade 12 or equivalent combination of education and experience. Completion of some related landscape courses an asset. Experience: Three years of related experience. Other: Possession of valid Provincial Class \"G\" driver's license, physical ability to perform required duties, demonstrated ability to communicate effectively in English (oral and written), ability to work under all weather conditions and may be required to work long and varied hours. **** THERE ARE THREE (3) POSITIONS AVAILABLE FOR THIS POSTING **** THESE POSITIONS ARE TEMPORARY FOR 120 DAYS ONLY Shift Details: Monday \u2013 Friday, 6:00AM \u2013 2:30PM NOTE : Must be available to be On Call during the winter months for snow removal operations in accordance with the Collective Agreement. Closing Date: 10/26/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: CUPE Tmp L3261 Appointment Type : Budget - Temp Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: Job Rate -- $25.66 Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Landscaping, Technician, Temporary, Entry Level, Operations, Technology, Contract Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-ProfessorClinician-Scientist-Academic-Geriatrician-ON/606991117/": {"title": "Assistant Professor/Clinician Scientist", "description": "Assistant Professor/Clinician Scientist - Academic Geriatrician Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant Professor/Clinician Scientist - Academic Geriatrician Date Posted: 10/13/2026 Closing Date: 11/17/2026 , 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50521 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Medicine Hospital Affiliation: University Health Network (UHN) & Sinai Health System (SHS) Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Department of Medicine, Temerty Faculty of Medicine, University of Toronto and the Division of General Internal Medicine & Geriatrics, Department of Medicine, University Health Network (UHN)/Sinai Health System (SHS) are inviting applications for the position of an Academic Geriatrician. This full-time appointment will be eligible for an academic appointment at the University of Toronto with a position description as a Clinician Scientist at the rank of Assistant Professor. It is expected that the position will be approximately 25% clinical and 75% related to research for a Clinician Scientist. Expected start date is April 1, 2027, or another mutually agreeable date. We are seeking a geriatrician Clinician Scientist who will advance excellence in academic geriatric medicine at UHN and Sinai, with expertise in health services research, aging, delirium, and equity. The successful candidate will lead an innovative research program focused on improving care and outcomes for older adults, informing health system policy and practice, and addressing inequities in access to and delivery of care. Research excellence will be assessed by the presence of research grants, publications in leading journals, invited presentations at conferences, awards, and other related accomplishments. The successful candidate will join the Division of General Internal Medicine & Geriatrics. The successful candidate will be expected to participate in geriatric medicine clinical activities in both the inpatient and outpatient settings. They will also be expected to participate in the educational and relevant administrative activities of the Division. The successful candidate must hold both MD and PhD degrees and be certified, or eligible for certification in Geriatric Medicine by the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canadaor have comparable qualifications. The candidate must also hold, or be eligible for, licensure with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario. Applicants must demonstrate an established record of scholarly achievement and excellence in research. Academic rank, salary and contractual arrangements will be commensurate with the qualifications and experience of the successful candidates. Compensation will be within the usual income range for an academic geriatrician in the Province of Ontario (estimated range is $300,000-$350,000 per year), achieved through a combination of fee for service and stipends for weekly work and call shifts. Applications will be accepted until November 17th, 2026 or until the position is filled. Interested individuals should submit their letter of intent, curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for three references, to: c/o Tracy Watkins ( tracy.watkins@sinaihealth.ca ) Dr. Nathan Stall Site Lead Geriatrics, Sinai Health Division of General Internal Medicine and Geriatrics, Sinai Health System and University Health Network Dr. Richard Norman Site Lead Geriatrics, University Health Network Division of General Internal Medicine and Geriatrics, Sinai Health System and University Health Network For more information about the Department of Medicine at the University of Toronto, please visit our website at www.deptmedicine.utoronto.ca . The Department of Medicine\u2019s academic position descriptions can be viewed here , under the position Academic Clinician. CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Clinic, Geriatric, Scientific, Research Scientist, Internal Medicine, Healthcare, Engineering, Science Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Professor%2C-Teaching-St-Italian-Language-Teaching-and-Applied-Second-Language-Acquisition-ON/607007617/": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Teaching St", "description": "Assistant Professor, Teaching St - Italian Language Teaching and Applied Second Language Acquisition Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant Professor, Teaching St - Italian Language Teaching and Applied Second Language Acquisition Date Posted: 10/14/2026 Closing Date: 12/01/2026, 11:59PM ET Req ID: 48725 Job Category: Faculty - Teaching Stream (continuing) Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: Department of Italian, Spanish, Portuguese and Latin American Studies Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes POSITION DESCRIPTION The Department of Italian, Spanish, Portuguese and Latin American Studies in the Faculty of Arts and Science at the University of Toronto invites applications for a full-time teaching stream position in Italian Language Teaching; Applied Second Language Acquisition . The appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. This search aligns with the University\u2019s commitment to strategically and proactively promote diversity among our community members ( Statement on Equity, Diversity & Excellence ). Recognizing that Black, Indigenous, and other Racialized communities have experienced inequities that have developed historically and are ongoing, we strongly welcome and encourage candidates from those communities to apply. REQUIREMENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS Applicants must have earned a PhD degree in Italian Studies, Italian Applied Linguistics or a related area by the time of appointment, or shortly thereafter, with a demonstrated record of excellence in teaching in Italian Language. Native or near-native fluency in Italian is required, together with an excellent command of English. We seek candidates whose teaching interests complement and enhance our existing departmental strengths . Candidates must have teaching experience in a degree-granting Italian Language program, including lecture preparation and delivery, curriculum development, and development of online material/lectures. Additionally, candidates must possess a demonstrated commitment to excellent pedagogical inquiry, a demonstrated interest in teaching-related scholarly activities. E xpertise in language assessment, experience in language program development and/or coordination, and the ability to support other departmental programs are highly desirable. Evidence of excellence in teaching and a commitment to excellent pedagogical inquiry will be demonstrated through teaching accomplishments, awards and accolades, presentations at significant conferences, the teaching dossier (including the required materials outlined below), and strong letters of reference. RESPONSIBILITIES The successful candidate will be assigned a teaching and service load. The responsibilities of the role include: Teaching of Italian language courses and coordination of multi-section courses. Participation in unit-level language teacher training, including teaching a practical teaching/foreign language pedagogy course Participation in curricular development within the Italian Language Program Supporting and organizing community-oriented departmental events Development of experiential learning courses HIRING SALARY RANGE The salary range is $113,300 to $130,000 CAD per annum, depending on experience. Negotiations beyond this salary range will be considered for exceptionally qualified candidates. ABOUT US The Department of Italian, Spanish, Portuguese & Latin American Studies at the University of Toronto houses four undergraduate programs (Spanish, Italian, Portuguese and Latin American Studies), and two graduate programs (Spanish and Italian). Our enthusiastic faculty and staff are a key ingredient to our department\u2019s success. In addition to instruction in the three languages, our programs explore the literature and cultures of the Hispanic, Lusophone and Italophone worlds. The study of Hispanic, Italian and Portuguese linguistics offers a special focus on the structure and diversity of these languages. As part of the University of Toronto, one of the world\u2019s top teaching and research universities, our department is an ideal place to work, research and make an impact in higher education. Research activity in the Department spans textual, cultural and linguistic scholarship. For more information on working at the University of Toronto, please visit https://www.utoronto.ca/research-innovation/working-at-uoft . APPLICATION PROCESS All application materials, inclu ding recent reference letters, must be received by December 1, 2026. All qualified candidates are invited to apply online by clicking the link below. Your CV and cover letter should be uploaded into the dedicated fields. Please combine additional application materials into one or two files in PDF/MS Word format. Applicants must submit the following materials: a cover letter; a current curriculum vitae; a recent writing sample; a complete teaching dossier, including a teaching statement, sample syllabi and course materials, and teaching evaluations and the name and contact information of three references. At least one reference letter must primarily address the candidate\u2019s teaching. Equity, diversity and inclusion are essential to academic excellence as articulated in University of Toronto\u2019s Statement on Equity, Diversity and Excellence . We seek candidates who share these values and who demonstrate throughout the application materials their commitment and efforts to advance equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment. The University of Toronto\u2019s recruiting tool will automatically solicit and collect letters of reference from each referee within 48 hours of an application being submitted. Applicants remain responsible for ensuring that references submit recent letters (on letterhead, dated and signed) by the closing date. Submission guidelines and details on the automatic reference letter collection, including timelines, are available in the candidate FAQ . If you have any questions about this position, please contact Sueli de Almeida at sueli.dealmeida@utoronto.ca All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Curriculum Development, Equity, Teacher, Drafting, Education, Finance, Research, Engineering Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Faculty Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-LecturerAssistantAssociate-or-Full-Professor-Academic-Hepatologist-ON/607015717/": {"title": "Lecturer/Assistant/Associate or Full Professor", "description": "Lecturer/Assistant/Associate or Full Professor - Academic Hepatologist Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Lecturer/Assistant/Associate or Full Professor - Academic Hepatologist Date Posted: 10/14/2026 Closing Date: 12/01/2026 , 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50541 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Medicine Hospital Affiliation: University Health Network (UHN) & Sinai Health System (SHS) Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Temerty Faculty of Medicine at the University of Toronto, together with the Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology at University Health Network (UHN) and Sinai Health invite applications for the position of Academic Hepatologist within the Toronto Centre for Liver Disease at Toronto General Hospital, UHN. The anticipated start date is February 1, 2027, or as mutually agreed. The successful candidate will be an accomplished physician holding an MD degree or equivalent, with residency and subspecialty training in hepatology and demonstrated expertise in the management of acute and chronic liver disease. A subspecialty interest in autoimmune liver disease would be preferred, based on current clinical needs. The candidate will bring a compelling vision for advancing and expanding UHN\u2019s dynamic, high-volume liver disease program, with a strong commitment to clinical excellence and academic advancement. Applicants must be certified by the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada, or hold equivalent qualifications permitting eligibility for practice in Ontario, and must hold or be eligible for licensure with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario. The successful candidate will join the full-time academic faculty as a Clinician Teacher, Clinician Quality Improvement or Clinician Investigator at UHN and will provide comprehensive care to both ambulatory and hospitalized patients with liver disease, as well as providing outpatient endoscopy for hepatology patients. In addition to clinical responsibilities, the candidate will hold a graduate degree (Master Teacher Program, MSc, PhD, or equivalent) with experience in medical education, quality improvement and/or research in liver disease. The successful candidate will complement existing strengths within the Toronto Centre for Liver Disease and/or develop emerging areas of academic excellence. With preference for expertise in autoimmune liver disease, opportunities exist to contribute to educational initiatives, quality improvement activities, and clinical trials. Academic rank, compensation, and contractual arrangements will be commensurate with the successful candidate's qualifications, experience, and scholarly accomplishments. The position offers a minimum annual income of CAD $300,000, derived primarily from fee-for-service clinical practice and other components of the UHN Department of Medicine Practice Plan. Compensation will be highly competitive and consistent with that of academic hepatologists in Ontario. Proficiency in English is required. Applications will be accepted until December 1st, 2026 or until the position is filled. Interested individuals should submit\u00a0a one-page statement of interest,\u00a0a current curriculum vitae, and\u00a0the names and contact information of three referees to: Jordan J. Feld MD MPH Director of the Toronto Centre for Liver Disease, UHN Toronto General Hospital 200 Elizabeth Street Eaton Building 9th floor Room 234 (9 EB 234) Toronto ON M5G 2C4 email: jordan.feld@uhn.ca admin : eliverta.bicja@uhn.ca CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. More information about the Department of Medicine\u2019s academic position descriptions can be found on this webpage. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Gastroenterology, Academic, CAD, Drafting, Surgery, Healthcare, Education, Engineering Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Mississauga-Student-Development-Officer-ON/606996517/": {"title": "Student Development Officer Job Details", "description": "Student Development Officer Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Student Development Officer Date Posted: 10/14/2026 Req ID: 50545 Faculty/Division: UofT Mississauga Department: UTM: Office of the Vice-Principal Academic & Dean Campus: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Position Number: 00056620 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: U of T Mississauga\u2014the second largest campus of Canada\u2019s top-ranked university and the only research university in Ontario\u2019s booming Peel Region\u2014is one of the world\u2019s great catalysts of human potential. Our employee community hums with the energy of 3,400 faculty, librarians and staff, who power our campus with curiosity, connection and care. We work together to spark life-changing research and innovation, make an indelible mark on the world by building equitable cities and societies, enable healthy lives, create a sustainable future and ignite entrepreneurship. Above all, we prioritize student success, and seek to give our 16,500 students the lift of a lifetime through learning and discovery. We love to open opportunities available nowhere else for our community to achieve their ambitions and make their unique contributions to Canada and the world. This work all comes together on a spectacularly green campus, alongside the Missinihe-ziibi (Trusting Creek or Credit River), where we seek to honour truth, reciprocity and reconciliation on the traditional land of the Huron-Wendat, Seneca and the Mississaugas of the Credit First Nation. We\u2019re thrilled to welcome those who want to learn more about us and to be part of what we do. Your opportunity: The Experiential Education Unit (EEU) in the Office of the Vice-Principal Academic and Dean (OVPAD), UTM, aims to enrich the undergraduate education experience by promoting and nurturing unique opportunities and approaches to learning both within and outside of the classroom. General areas of responsibilities of the OVPAD include: academic programs, academic HR; academic policy and planning; academic experience; academic integrity; academic appeals; experiential education; teaching and learning support; strategic leadership; divisional research and data analysis; graduate affairs; tri-campus affairs; and more. As the Student Development Officer, you will support and advance the mission of the EEU by supporting the new UTM Co-op Internship Program (UTMCIP). You will be responsible for a variety of tasks including advising students on university\u2019s policies and procedures; overseeing the delivery of pre-work mandatory professional development modules; tracking student progress and helping them to meet program milestones, timelines, and deliverables; advising students on career-related skills development; coaching students on career decision-making and job search strategies; serving as a point of contact between employers and students to troubleshoot any issues that may arise during the work term; and supporting overall student learning and development to prepare them for success in their work terms and future careers. The Student Development Officer will further support the business development of the UTMCIP by monitoring industry trends; researching and evaluating potential employers for work-integrated learning opportunities; fostering and maintaining relationships with potential and existing employers; responding to inquiries within the defined scope of the role and redirecting as appropriate; reviewing and assessing feedback from employers; organizing and participating in student, faculty, and employer-facing events; and promoting the program through social media and other channels. The ideal candidate will be a motivated self-starter with impeccable organizational and planning skills and great enthusiasm for work-integrated learning. The Student Development Officer will report to the Associate Director, Student Learning & Professional Development and work closely with the Director, Experiential Education & Community Engagement; the Associate Dean, Academic Experience; and other internal and external stakeholders. You will work as part of a team to ensure student success within the program and develop relationships with stakeholders within and outside the university, as well as external organizations within our local and international communities. Your responsibilities will include: Advising students on job search, industry research and networking strategies including cover letter, resume and interview preparation. Advising and coaching students on the selection of appropriate work-integrated learning opportunities. Implementing plans that support the development of work-integrated learning opportunities for students. Evaluating job prospects in alignment with student academic goals. Promoting employer opportunities to students and encouraging them to submit applications. Gathering information on student performance from employers. Keeping well-informed on policies, rules, regulations and guidelines. Implementing plans that support the development of work-integrated learning opportunities for students Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum five years of relevant experience providing direct support to students in an experiential learning environment. Thorough knowledge and understanding of best practices in advising, career coaching, job search skills and presentation skills. Experience developing and maintaining employer or industry partnerships. Experience working with a range of eLearning authoring tools and learning management systems, such as Quercus (Canvas). Experience in program development and evaluation. Must have strong computer skills, including the use of Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Adobe Acrobat, and email software, as well as an ability to adapt to and learn new technologies. Familiarity with database management systems and ROSI. Excellent oral and written communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to understand and apply complex community and university policies and regulations. Ability to positively represent UTM in the community and to all members of the University community. Ability to effectively manage multiple deadlines and priorities, and appreciate and interact well with diverse personalities and cultural backgrounds. Assets (Nonessential): Experience working in a university environment in the area of co-op and/or internship programs. To be successful in this role you will be: Approachable Diplomatic Efficient Motivated self-learner Possess a positive attitude Team player Please note that one continuing position is available. Closing Date: 10/22/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 12 -- $84,564 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $108,145. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Divisional HR Office Email: hrserv.utm@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Developer, Data Analyst, Intern, Sustainability, Database, Technology, Data, Entry Level, Energy Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Manager%2C-Active-Healthy-Living-Clubs-%28TERM%29-ON/607016217/": {"title": "Assistant Manager, Active Healthy Living Clubs (TERM)", "description": "Assistant Manager, Active Healthy Living Clubs (TERM) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant Manager, Active Healthy Living Clubs (TERM) Date Posted: October 14, 2026 Req ID: 50532 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Kinesiology and Physl Ed. Department: Faculty of Kinesiology and Physl Ed. Campus: St. George (downtown) campus Position Number: 59814 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The University of Toronto\u2019s Faculty of Kinesiology and Physical Education is globally recognized for developing and advancing knowledge about the interactions of physical activity and health through outstanding undergraduate and graduate education programs, cutting-edge research and the delivery of sport, recreation and high-performance athletic opportunities for students, staff, faculty and community members across the three campuses. In achieving this vision, the Faculty is guided by values of integrity, respect, equity and diversity https://kpe.utoronto.ca/. Your opportunity: Under the direction of the Director, Active Healthy Living, the incumbent provides professional and dynamic leadership to the Faculty\u2019s Active Healthy Living Clubs program with an emphasis in the areas of recreational sport and physical activity clubs. Key duties include the direct management of 10 FKPE Active Healthy Living club programs; supervision of a large staff primarily composed of part time coaches, USW casuals, student leaders and contracted volunteers; creating and managing a large scheduling portfolio across multiple facilities; the financial management of one largeprogram including one FKPE budget and multiple Restricted Spending Plan budgets; the implementation of event management protocols; and the human resource management of 50+ staff including annual contracts, payroll processes, training and orientation. Your responsibilities will include: Create all practice and competition schedules across 12 facilities for 28 programs in intercollegiate and FKPE clubs. In collaboration with the Manager of Intercollegiate Sport, manage the Ontario University Sport (OUA) and U Sports requirements primarily for the Blue and White Division of the intercollegiate program. Advocating on behalf of students with internal and external contacts/agencies Design a promotion plan for athlete recruitment for all programs working with departmental colleagues, assist in the coordination of student athlete awards and recognition programs. Manage all travel requirements within IC and club travel policies \u2013 includes type of transportation within budget allocation, accommodation, travel rosters, coaches expenses; meals; therapy, reimbursements of expenses, parking, mileage, officials travel. Recruit, hire, orient and train of 80+ USW casuals, contracted volunteers, coaches, instructors and work study students. As a member of the Events Management team for intercollegiate games and events, attends games and/or events to ensure staff performs their assigned duties and to solve any problems that may arise pre, during, or post event, based on an assigned portfolio. Create Game/Event Day action plans for all games and events within the Blue and White division of the IC program, the club program and the tri campus intramural program Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in sport management, physical education or kinesiology or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum four years in recreation and sport management preferably in a post-secondary recreation and sport setting. Experience in managing budgets and supervising unionized and non-unionized staff Demonstrated event management and sport scheduling experience Experience in university or college recreation and sport across a continuum of programming \u2013 intramurals, clubs, interuniversity, high performance. Demonstrated oral and written skills Demonstrated conflict resolution skills Proficiency in the Microsoft OfficeSuite Assets (Nonessential): Experience in web site management and FUSION recreation management software is an asset. To be successful in this role you will be: Accountable Communicator Organized Problem solver Self-directed Tactful Closing Date: October 23, 2026 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget- term Schedule: Full-time, some evening and weekend work. Term ending January 2028 Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 13 -- $89,794. with an annual step progression to a maximum of $114,832. Pay\u00a0scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay\u00a0Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Athletics Divisional HR Office Email: kpe.hr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Payroll, Medical, Equity, Assistant Manager, Manager, Finance, Healthcare, Management Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Co-op-Coordinator%2C-Student-Development-ON/606994217/": {"title": "Co-op Coordinator, Student Development", "description": "Co-op Coordinator, Student Development Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Co-op Coordinator, Student Development Date Posted: 10/14/2026 Req ID: 50530 Faculty/Division: UofT Scarborough Department: UTSC:Arts & Science Co-op Programs Campus: University of Toronto Scarborough (UTSC) Position Number: 00056886 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The University of Toronto Scarborough is a place of energy, enthusiasm and passion. Our commitment to inclusive excellence attracts the brightest learners, scholars and employees from around the globe. Our success has been made possible by the opportunity given to us by our Indigenous hosts to operate on their territory, and we cherish our continuing partnerships with these communities. The University of Toronto Scarborough is an exciting campus with unlimited potential. Join us on our journey. The University of Toronto Scarborough has been a leader in Co-operative education, combining academic study with alternating work terms, for 50 years. Co-operative education gives students an opportunity to test skills learned in the classroom, and to expand their knowledge through related work experience. The Arts and Science Co-op O\ufb03ce is responsible for preparing students in over 35 unique program areas to compete for paid co-op work opportunities. The O\ufb03ce also is responsible for engaging industry partners who provide these work terms. A coordinated e\ufb00ort among the stakeholders of student, employer, and university Co-op programming contributes to the development of well-quali\ufb01ed graduates who are prepared to assume a productive role in society. With a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion, the department works closely with campus and employer partners to support students as they work to achieve their academic and Co-op aspirations. This search aligns with the University\u2019s commitment to strategically and proactively promote diversity among our community members ( Statement on Equity, Diversity & Excellence ). Recognizing that Black, Indigenous, and other Racialized communities have experienced inequities that have developed historically and are ongoing, we strongly welcome and encourage candidates from those communities to apply. Your opportunity: Working under the direction of the Assistant Director, Student Services, the incumbent works with a team of dedicated student development sta\ufb00 to prepare students to successfully compete for co-op work opportunities. Student Development Coordinators work with \ufb01rst and second year students across the Arts & Science disciplines who are preparing to search for their \ufb01rst co-op work term position. This includes developing and delivering content for in-person or online instructional workshops as well as supporting students one-on-one through advising and coaching regarding job search cycles, process and strategies, creating e\ufb00ective job search documents, preparing and conducting interviews, and preparing to compete for a \ufb01rst co-op work term. Your responsibilities will include: Advising and coaching students on work search strategies and skills Advising students on techniques to improve their interviewing skills Providing regular feedback to students on progress, assessments and assignments Advising students on how to conduct job searches, cover letter and resume development Developing content for instructional workshops Conducting detailed analysis on program efficiency and student learning outcomes to inform program planning activities Updating and maintaining records Providing proactive support to individuals in distress and making referrals to specific university services Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Certi\ufb01cation in career development, career counselling, human resources, adult learning and development, or a graduate degree in a relevant area will be considered a strong asset. Minimum three years working in direct support of undergraduate students in a co-op environment supporting co-op job search and employment and career exploration Experience with in person and online facilitation, and use of educational technologies to support facilitation and student engagement Experience in student professional development, knowledge of workplace standards, recruitment and hiring practices, and performance management techniques gained through a role in a cooperative education or internship program Excellent written and oral communication skills Strong presentation and public speaking skills Strong computer skills, including Microsoft O\ufb03ce Broad knowledge of trends in employer hiring practices, occupations, current labour market conditions and a strong understanding of student and career development theories and job search strategies for youth Knowledge of adult learning principles including facilitation, use of digital/social media, online learning concepts, and learning outcomes Self-motivated learner Demonstrated integrity, initiative, \ufb02exibility and creative problem solving Ability to manage con\ufb02icting demands and work well under pressure Strong attention to detail Applicants are also expected to show evidence of a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment Assets (Nonessential): Exposure to customized relationship databases such as Simplicity or Orbis Experience or knowledge of user experience design To be successful in this role you will be: Approachable Communicator Multi-tasker Persuasive Resourceful Team player Note s: Please note that this is a shared office environment and a term opportunity to April 2028. Regular working hours are between 8:45 AM - 5:00 P. with occasional evenings and weekends. This role is currently eligible for a hybrid work arrangement, pursuant to University policies and guidelines, including but not limited to the University of Toronto\u2019s Alternative Work Arrangements Guideline . Closing Date: 10/22/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 11 -- $79,640 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $101,845. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Divisional HR Office Email: humanresources.utsc@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Equity, Intern, Performance Management, User Experience, Finance, Entry Level, Human Resources, Technology Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Scarborough-Maintenance-Technician-ON/606995517/": {"title": "Maintenance Technician", "description": "Maintenance Technician Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Maintenance Technician Date Posted: 10/14/2026 Req ID: 50534 Faculty/Division: UofT Scarborough Department: UTSC:Facilities Management Campus : University of Toronto Scarborough (UTSC) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The University of Toronto Scarborough is a place of energy, enthusiasm and passion. Our commitment to inclusive excellence attracts the brightest learners, scholars and employees from around the globe. Our success has been made possible by the opportunity given to us by Indigenous hosts to operate on their territory, and we cherish our continuing partnerships with these communities. The University of Toronto Scarborough is an exciting campus with unlimited potential. Join us on our journey. This search aligns with the University\u2019s commitment to strategically and proactively promote diversity among our community members ( Statement on Equity, Diversity & Excellence ). Recognizing that Black, Indigenous, and other Racialized communities have experienced inequities that have developed historically and are ongoing, we strongly welcome and encourage candidates from those communities to apply. General Description: Under direction, the Maintenance Technician performs minor repairs and maintenance duties on a regular basis and some caretaking duties in a number of buildings of the University. Typical Duties: The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required, and the extent of responsibility involved in this job. They in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated. Flexibility of the employee to perform a wide variety of functions is necessary in successfully fulfilling the requirements of this position. The degree to which each employee performs each of the following tasks listed below will vary according to where and when the employee is scheduled to work. a) Performs maintenance duties to ensure the building, fixtures and equipment are maintained to standard and are in good working order such as repairing/replacing and adjusting equipment, fixtures, furniture and appliances, minor carpentry/woodwork, hardware replacement and repair; light replacement; switch and receptacle face plate replacement/installation; tightening screws; hanging pictures, signs and banners; key cutting; rod/ bracket installations and repair; change locks; replace screens, windows, tap washers; unplug toilets and bathroom/kitchen fixture adjustments; visually inspecting drains; following basic floor plans; vacuuming water; locating water problems: moving heavy items and completing room set ups. b) General maintenance of lights, equipment, and building fixtures (general building maintenance such as springs, appliances, closures, washers, seals, flooring/ceiling tile repair/replacement, caulking, basic wall repair, minor residential painting). c) Responsible for maintaining internal signage. d) Inspects, maintains and repairs all Ving card hardware; troubleshoots malfunctioning equipment as required. e) Maintains all accessibility operators in good working order. f) Performs visual inspection of building, equipment, fixtures and appliances performing maintenance or reporting as needed. g) Clears entranceways to buildings and residences of snow and ice, lays salt. h) Performs preventative maintenance. i) Checks fire and safety equipment \u2013 reporting items requiring specialized repair. j) Observes, corrects and/or reports any health and safety concerns (e.g. broken, defective or missing fire/safety equipment). k) Follows established protocol during fire alarms including checking alarm panel, communication with Fire Department, making announcements to building occupants and resetting fire pull stations/fire panel/elevator based on established rules and/or instruction; replaces smoke detector and security alarm batteries on a regular schedule. l) Reports on damaged and defective equipment; advises supervisor on repairs required and follows up to ensure repairs are completed;(e.g. building heater; pull station cover; security equipment). m) Cleans and mops floors; cleans residences and related buildings, equipment and surrounding areas; removes garbage. n) Liaises with the appropriate supervisors, such as Building Managers, Supervisors, Deans, Directors, Managers and Chairs as well as administrative staff and students to ensure Work Order Requests; maintenance and cleanliness are executed to local and University Building Standards and Health and Safety standards in a timely and safe fashion and to keep others informed of facility issues. o) Responds to requests of building occupants and contractors; informs them of required information; provides supplies or services related to building maintenance; accompanies and directs parties as needed. p) Properly stores and maintains an inventory of materials and equipment; and orders supplies as applicable. q) Maintains accurate and timely records of work completed. r) Completes work orders and special projects. s) Other related duties as required or assigned. Qualifications: Minimum Requirements for Selection: Education: Completion of Grade 12 or equivalent; technical training is desirable. Experience: Three years of related work experience, and technical training may be substituted for experience. Other: Demonstrated mechanical aptitude and experience performing a variety of building maintenance tasks. Knowledge and experience of building maintenance and repair practices demonstrated the ability to become familiar with building operations, floor plans, equipment and related health, safety and cleanliness standards. Proven ability to effectively and safely use and operate small hand tools, power tools, ladders and elevated platforms. Demonstrated physical and technical ability to perform required duties. Familiar with the Occupational Health and Safety Act and regulations that apply to this work. Ability to communicate effectively in English (oral and written); ability to communicate effectively using tools such as cell phone, pager, and radio; tact, courtesy and patience dealing with clients and staff; Computer skills required. Demonstrated ability to work independently. Ability to work outdoors in inclement weather conditions. Applicants are also expected to show evidence of a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment. Note: The hours of work for this position are Monday to Friday from 12:30 pm - 9:00 pm. Closing Date: 10/22/2026,11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: CUPE F/T L3261 Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: Job Rate: $28.07/hr Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Facilities, Kitchen, Inspector, Technician, Equity, Operations, Hospitality, Quality, Technology, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Engagement-and-Events-Planner-ON/607026117/": {"title": "Engagement and Events Planner Job Details", "description": "Engagement and Events Planner Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Engagement and Events Planner Date Posted: 10/14/2026 Req ID: 50548 Faculty/Division: Office of the President Department: Bicentennial Secretariat Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Position Summary: Under the overall direction of the Bicentennial Chair, Senior Advisor to the President, and Chief of Protocol, and reporting to the Director of Operations, Bicentennial Secretariat, the Engagement and Events Planner is responsible for the successful development and execution of University-wide engagement programs related to the University\u2019s Bicentennial. The incumbent will oversee the planning and delivery of Bicentennial events and initiatives, including but not limited to: the co-branding of Divisional, Faculty, and Departmental celebrations with the Bicentennial program; Bicentennial Secretariat\u2013initiated events and town halls; and additional initiatives or events arising from the Bicentennial committees. The incumbent promotes a positive and collaborative organizational culture and plays a lead role in the creation and implementation of institutional engagement initiatives. Working closely with the Bicentennial Secretariat leadership team, the incumbent provides strategic direction and consultation on the design, development, and execution of Bicentennial programs and strategies in alignment with institutional priorities. The position further involves coordinating various special projects, including tracking documentation and activities, creating project milestones and timelines, monitoring progress, escalating issues as required, and managing event budgets. The incumbent organizes project meetings, prepares records and follow-ups, and ensures effective communication across stakeholders. Success in this role requires strong project management skills, sound judgment, and the ability to operate in a complex environment with a high degree of discretion, sensitivity, and responsiveness. Qualifications Required: Education: Bachelor\u2019s degree and/or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience: Minimum five (5) years of progressive experience and related experience. Proven successful project management experience and experience conducting research. Experience with event management. Strong writing and editorial skills. Demonstrated experience using data to develop engagement strategies. Skills: Computer skills, including MS Office (Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Experience designing promotional materials, such as invitations and posters. Working knowledge of design software (e.g. In Design, Photoshop,\u00a0Illustrator; Project management software. Other: Demonstrated strong oral and written communication skills. Strong customer service orientation. Excellent organizational, interpersonal and time-management skills, meticulous attention to detail. High degree of judgement, diplomacy and tact. Ability to work with extremely confidential and sensitive material. Ability to work under pressure and manage multiple priorities to meet deadlines. Demonstrated initiative, creativity and flexibility. Ability to assimilate and interpret significant amount of information. Aility to react to brief instructions in relation to sensitive matters. Ability to work both independently and within a team environment. Note: This is a term position ending in December 2027. Closing Date: 10/28/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Term; ending in December 2027. Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 3 -- Hiring Zone: $97,336 - $113,558 -- Broadband Salary Range: $97,336 - $162,224 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Project Manager, Branding, Graphic Design, Event Planning, Technology, Marketing, Creative, Hospitality, Research Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Events-&-Communications-Coordinator-ON/607018317/": {"title": "Events & Communications Coordinator", "description": "Events & Communications Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Events & Communications Coordinator Date Posted: 10/14/2026 Req ID: 50542 Faculty/Division: Vice-Provost, Students Department: Career Centre Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00050116 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Student Life connects life to learning. We believe every student should have the opportunity to participate in university life actively and find connection and community while discovering new ways of thinking and being in the world. We provide resources, support and engagement opportunities that are inclusive and accessible, ensuring every student can build experiences that set them up for a lifetime of success. Within Student Life, the cluster of Student Life Programs and Services supports students as they achieve personal, academic, career and civic goals. We engage students throughout their learning and development with the following units: Accessibility Services, Career Exploration & Education, Centre for Learning Strategy Support, Co-Curricular Community-Engaged Learning, Clubs & Leadership Development, First Nations House-Indigenous Student Services, Mentorship & Peer Programs, Multi-faith Centre, Orientation, Student Success, Transition & Engagement and TCard Services. Together with staff, faculty, students, alumni, employers and community partners, we provide an integrated and coherent path to success that reflects our students' Diversity. In support of U of T\u2019s mission, StudentLife Programs and Services is committed to creating diverse, accessible, inclusive and welcoming spaces of opportunity that foster deepened engagement, learning, personal growth, and identity development for all students. We are committed to embedding these principles into all the work we do, reducing barriers so that students from all backgrounds and lived experiences can feel a sense of belonging in the\u00a0communities they find here. This role contributes to Career Exploration & Education, the central career services unit at the St. George campus. Career Exploration & Education creates curricular and co-curricular career learning experiences at the intersection of career, equity, and wellbeing in partnership with students, recent graduates, tri-campus partners, and alumni and employer communities. Taking an ecosystem approach, we work intentionally to design and deliver career learning experiences that align with student needs and ensure graduates are future-ready and able to thrive in their careers. We are motivated by the vision that University of Toronto students and graduates will contribute to a more equitable and just world of work. In this work we strive to live the values of justice & belonging; reconciliation; learning; community; and curiosity. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion, and we strive to hire and invest in candidates that reflect and support the diverse perspectives, experiences and identities of our students and our communities. We encourage individuals who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups to apply. Your opportunity: Reporting to the Assistant Director, Career Exploration & Employer Engagement and supervised by the Lead Coordinator, Employer Recruitment & Engagement, the Events & Communications Coordinator collaborates with career services colleagues to plan, deliver, evaluate, and continuously improve events and programs that support the career exploration, employment, and industry engagement needs of University of Toronto students and recent graduates. The Coordinator leads the end-to-end management of virtual and in-person events, including conferences, career fairs, information sessions, recruitment initiatives, and special programs. Responsibilities include event planning and execution, scheduling, registration management, vendor coordination, budget tracking, catering, room bookings, audiovisual arrangements, and issue resolution. The Coordinator develops and distributes event communications and promotional materials, maintains event information across digital platforms and websites, and manages correspondence with participants, registrants, vendors, and stakeholders. They also prepare presentations, onboarding resources, event materials, and briefing documents for staff, volunteers, committees, and leadership. The role includes monitoring event performance, conducting needs assessments and post-event evaluations, analyzing results, generating reports, and recommending enhancements to improve future programming and stakeholder experiences. The Coordinator maintains strong relationships with vendors and partners, ensuring clear communication regarding requirements, timelines, expectations, and feedback. Drawing on experience supporting large-scale and complex events, the incumbent contributes to Career Exploration & Education's mission of helping students and recent graduates navigate their career journeys. Your responsibilities will include: Conceptualizing, organizing and executing event activities using work back plans and critical paths. Overseeing the implementation of event plans and activities. Building and strengthening relationships with stakeholders and partners of strategic importance. Analyzing client needs and making recommendations on event logistics and options. Handling expenses for events. Coordinating the schedule for program and event calendars. Determining operations and logistics \u2013 detail and implementation activities, for organizing events and programming across the unit. Organizing materials for workshops, conferences and/or events. Creating and editing documents and communication materials. Coordinating the preparation and distribution of promotional/outreach materials. Determining changes to an event based on unusual and/or unexpected circumstances. Liaising with clients and vendors to resolve minor complaints and address issues. Resolving issues that may occur during events and escalating problems as required. Conducting post-event evaluation, analysis and recommendations for changes. Documenting and maintaining standard operating procedures. Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or an acceptable equivalent combination of education and experience. An event planning certification an asset. Minimum three (3) years relevant experience; events coordination and planning; proven successful experience with special events, managing volunteers and committees. Experience with conceptualizing, implementing and managing event plans from beginning to end, including preparing event communication and promotional material. Demonstrated experience planning and organizing numerous multi-day events that will be delivered concurrently and within high peak seasons. Experience with common tools such as Zoom, Microsoft Teams, Word, Excel and PowerPoint as well as extensive experience with databases. Experience planning and hosting engaging virtual events, webinars,and online meetings using platforms like Zoom and Microsoft Teams, ensuring smooth execution and high attendee satisfaction. Strong computer skills with sound working knowledge of PC platforms; high level of proficiency with word processing, spreadsheets, e-mail, internet, and presentation software. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Windows XP) and other Social Media Platforms. Strong written and verbal communication skills; ability to relate well with staff, volunteers and vendors. Demonstrated ability to apply a high degree of tact and sensitivity to daily activities and operate effectively in a multi-stakeholder environment. Excellent customer service skills are essential. Ability to communicate event concepts and ideas and prepare proposals. Strong organizational and time management and multi-tasking skills required. Proven ability to work independently and co-operatively on a team. Flexibility and the ability to adapt to changing circumstances, with on-the-fly thinking. Strong administrative skills; accuracy and attention to detail. Experience tracking expenses against a budget. Ability to build surveys, analyze findings and prepare reports. Ability to lead work teams and collaborate with colleagues to achieve event outcomes, including timely and ongoing communication and progress updates. Strong track record of building and maintaining partnerships cross-functionally and with external organizations. Ability to synthesize and analyze data; attention to detail. Proven ability to prioritize a large volume of work in a fast-paced, high-performance team environment. To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Goal oriented Multi-tasker Organized Problem solver Team player Closing Date: 10/29/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 09 -- $70,633 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $90,329. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Divisional HR Office Email: cahrs.hr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Event Planning, Communications, Equity, Audio Visual, Hospitality, Marketing, Finance, Creative Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Administrative-&-Project-Coordinator-ON/607013717/": {"title": "Administrative & Project Coordinator", "description": "Administrative & Project Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Administrative & Project Coordinator Date Posted: 10/14/2026 Req ID: 50549 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: Dept of Computer Science Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00058832 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Faculty of Arts & Science is the heart of Canada\u2019s leading university and one of the most comprehensive and diverse academic divisions in the world. The strength of Arts & Science derives from our combined teaching and research excellence in the humanities, sciences and social sciences across 29 departments, seven colleges and 46 interdisciplinary centres, institutes and programs. We can only realize our mission with the dedication and excellence of engaged staff and faculty. The diversity of opportunities and perspectives within the Faculty reflect the local and global landscape and the need for curiosity, innovative thinking and collaboration. At Arts & Science, we take pride in our legacy of innovation and discovery that has changed the way we think about the world. Established in 1964, the Department of Computer Science in the Faculty of Arts and Science is a tech innovation powerhouse and continues to rank among the world\u2019s top computer science departments. Our esteemed faculty boasts accolades such as two Turing Awards, along with many other national and international honours. We provide diverse programs and research opportunities while consistently producing high-impact research that is driving the future of tech in the country. Your opportunity: The strategic initiatives group in the Department of Computer Science\u00a0leads the department\u2019s largest partnerships and priority initiatives, connecting industry, government, and academia to accelerate cutting-edge research, translate discovery into real-world impact, and advance national innovation goals. A collaboration with the Department of Computer Science provides our partners access to exceptional talent, globally recognized research expertise, and innovation capabilities that help accelerate technology development, strengthen competitiveness, and create long-term business value. At any given time, the Strategics Initiatives team is engaging with senior internal and external stakeholders to advance existing and new initiatives and partnerships. The Administrative and Project Coordinator plays a pivotal role in supporting the Department's strategic initiatives and serves as the frontline representative for engagement with senior internal and external stakeholders. As one of the first points of contact for partners, executives, government officials, and senior academic leaders, the incumbent helps foster strong relationships, facilitate communications, and ensure initiatives progress smoothly through the development process. Within a highly professional, collaborative, and supportive team, the Administrative and Project Coordinator coordinates project activities, supports senior staff, and provides the operational leadership required to keep multiple initiatives moving forward successfully. Your responsibilities will include: Coordinating projects strategic initiatives involving senior internal and external stakeholders Building trusted relationships and engaging with stakeholders using sound judgment, diplomacy, discretion, and tact Coordinating meetings, briefing materials, action items, and follow-up activities in support of strategic priorities Monitoring project progress, managing competing priorities, and escalating issues as appropriate Analyzing processes and recommending changes to enhance operational effectiveness and stakeholder engagement Determining logistical details and activities for high-profile meetings, events, and strategic initiatives Essential Qualifications: Advanced College Diploma (3 years) or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum five (5) years of relevant and progressive project coordination and administrative experience supporting large-scale projects in a corporate and/or academic environment, with some experience supporting initiatives involving senior internal and external stakeholders. Proven experience effectively communicating and engaging in-person, by phone and e-mail with multiple internal and external stakeholders, including government officials, C-Suite Executives, and senior academic leadership. Extensive experience coordinating complex schedules, meetings, agendas, and travel Strong ability to manage multiple projects/tasks of varying complexities, meet deadlines and work well under pressure. Strong project coordination experience involving multiple stakeholders, including process development, setting up and monitoring organizational systems, developing schedules and tracking milestones, implementation, and evaluation. Experience drafting, editing, verifying content for, and formatting professional correspondence to a variety of stakeholders, with the proven ability to consolidate, organize and summarize information appropriately. Experience organizing logistics of events/meetings with the ability to perform set up and close off Extensive experience using online meeting tools and platforms (Calendly, Zoom, Google Meet, etc.) used for scheduling and hosting meetings and events. Success working in a complex environment that requires a high degree of sensitivity, tact, responsiveness, and a need to maintain absolute confidentiality. Demonstrated ability to employ a high degree of initiative and creativity as a strategic thinker and the ability to work in a diverse team environment. Extensive experience using the MS Office 365 suite such as Word, Excel, PowerPoint, OneDrive, SharePoint and Teams Superior organizational skills and advanced diagnostics and data handling skills Demonstrated commitment to accuracy and attention to detail; ability to work well as a member of a project team. Ability to take initiative, anticipate needs, and work proactively, with demonstrated experience recommending process and workflow improvements. Assets (Nonessential): Project Management Certificate and experience of working with corporate stakeholders is an asset. To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Efficient Meticulous Organized Problem solver Team player This role may be eligible for an Alternative Work Arrangement in accordance with the University of Toronto\u2019s Alternative Work Arrangements Guideline . Closing Date: 10/28/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 10 -- $75,004 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $95,915. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Computer Science, Project Manager, Sharepoint, Developer, Administrative Assistant, Technology, Administrative Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Mississauga-Indigenous-Inclusion-Programmer-ON/606992217/": {"title": "Indigenous Inclusion Programmer Job Details", "description": "Indigenous Inclusion Programmer Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Indigenous Inclusion Programmer Date Posted: 10/14/2026 Req ID: 50536 Faculty/Division: UofT Mississauga Department: UTM:Ctr Std Engagemt Campus: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Position Number: 00060180 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: U of T Mississauga\u2014the second largest campus of Canada\u2019s top-ranked university and the only research university in Ontario\u2019s booming Peel Region\u2014is one of the world\u2019s great catalysts of human potential. Our employee community hums with the energy of 3,400 faculty, librarians and staff, who power our campus with curiosity, connection and care. We work together to spark life-changing research and innovation, make an indelible mark on the world by building equitable cities and societies, enable healthy lives, create a sustainable future and ignite entrepreneurship. Above all, we prioritize student success, and seek to give our 16,500 students the lift of a lifetime through learning anddiscovery. We love to open opportunities available nowhere else for our community to achieve their ambitions and make their unique contributions to Canada and the world. This work all comes together on a spectacularly green campus, alongside theMissinihe-ziibi (Trusting Creek or Credit River), where we seek to honour truth, reciprocity and reconciliation on the traditional land of the Huron-Wendat, Seneca and the Mississaugas of the Credit First Nation. We\u2019re thrilled to welcome those whowant to learn more about us and to be part of what we do. Your opportunity: The Centre for Student Engagement at the University of Toronto Mississauga is committed to creating inclusive learning environments to cultivate holistic student development. Built through meaningful collaboration and informed by research and assessment our campus & community-based programs, services and resources promote access to post-secondary education, support transition into andretention through university and encourages student engagement and community-engaged learning. With over 180 opportunities led by 130 student leaders and professional staff, the Centre for Student Engagement believes that student involvement is a powerful tool to support an individual\u2019s navigation of the post-secondary environment and to feel empowered to contribute and make an impact within their community. The Indigenous Inclusion Programmer will work to develop and implement Indigenouscohort streams in some of CSE\u2019s Access Programs including Ohahi:yoh, the Indigenous Transition Program, and Indigenous Orientation. CSE\u2019s access and inclusion programs work to address systemic barriers by centering the communities we work with from the development through the implementation process of our programs in collaboration with Indigenous students and communities. To do this work, we build authentic, transparent, and reciprocal relationships with community. This role will work closely with internal and external partners to expand and enhance these programs that support indigenous students. Working closely in partnership with the Office of Indigenous Initiatives at UTM, this position also plays a pivotal role on behalf of the Student Affairs and Services in Answering the Call: Wecheehetowin the University of Toronto Response to the Truth and Reconciliation Commission of Canada. This will include working with the Office of Indigenous Initiatives to engage in relationship building with Knowledge Keepers, Indigenous and non-Indigenous faculty, scholars, staff, students, and external Indigenous communities and organizations. This role is Monday-Friday 8:45am-5:00pm, four (4) days onsite. Your responsibilities will include: Determining\u00a0logistical details and activities for events and/or programming Fostering cooperative working relationships with a wide variety of internal and external contacts Conducting post-event evaluation, analysis and recommendations for changes Facilitating educational workshops and seminars Assigning and checking the work of work-study students Training and coaching student life staff and student leaders Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum three (3) years related experience in student services (combination of professional and para-professional experience is acceptable) at the post-secondary level and/or Indigenous (First Nations, Inuit or Metis) communities/agencies. Demonstrated experience implementing large components of projects and events. Knowledge of Indigenous, equity, inclusion, and social justice approaches to inform programming. Knowledge of Indigenous educational issues and barriers, the Truth and Reconciliation Commission Final Report, the Royal Commission on Aboriginal Peoples (RCAP), and other resources pertaining to Indigenous communities. Proven leadership and supervisory experience. Strong facilitation, presentation, research, and analytical skills. Excellent judgement, diplomacy, tact, and discretion in developing partnerships and collaborating on program planning. Proven organizational and time-management skills required Experience designing surveys, interviews and other research tools for program evaluation. To be successful in this role you will be: Approachable Organized Resourceful Self-directed Team player Closing Date: 11/02/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 10 -- $75,004 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $95,915. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Sustainability, Programmer, Information Technology, Developer, Diversity, Energy, Technology, Human Resources Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Lead-Coordinator%2C-Co-curricular-Community-Engaged-Learning-ON/607019117/": {"title": "Lead Coordinator, Co-curricular Community Engaged Learning", "description": "Lead Coordinator, Co-curricular Community Engaged Learning Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Lead Coordinator, Co-curricular Community Engaged Learning Date Posted: 10/14/2026 Req ID: 50543 Faculty/Division: Vice-Provost, Students Department: Centre for Community Partnerships Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00051963 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Student Life connects life to learning. We believe every student should have the opportunity to participate in university life actively and find connection and community while discovering new ways of thinking and being in the world. We provide resources, support and engagement opportunities that are inclusive and accessible, ensuring every student can build experiences that set them up for a lifetime of success. Within the Division of Student Life, the cluster of Student Life Programs and Services, supports students as they achieve personal, academic, career and civic goals. We engage students throughout their learning and development with the following units: Academic Success, Accessibility Services, Career Exploration & Education, Co-curricular Community Engaged Learning, Clubs & Leadership Development, Housing, Indigenous Student Services, Mentorship & Peer Programs, Multi-faith Centre, Orientation, Student Success, Transition & Engagement and TCard Services. Together with staff, faculty, students, alumni, employers and community partners, we provide an integrated and coherent path to success that reflects our students' diversity. In support of U of T\u2019s vision, Student Life Programs and Services is committed to creating diverse, accessible, inclusive and welcoming spaces of opportunity that foster deepened engagement, learning, personal growth, and identity development for all students. We are committed to embedding these principles into all the work we do, reducing barriers so that students from all backgrounds and lived experiences can feel a sense of belonging in the communities they find here. To align with our strategic priorities, we encourage individuals from Black, Indigenous, and racialized communities to apply. Your opportunity: Under the direction of the Director, Student Belonging & Engagement, the Lead Coordinator, Co-curricular Community Engaged Learning (Lead Coordinator) oversees a team that is responsible for coordinating co-curricular community-engaged learning programs for students. In leading the Co-curricular Community Engaged Learning team, including strategic and annual planning, program and project development and evaluation, the Lead Coordinator supervises the work of USW staff, as well as casual staff and work-study students. The Lead Coordinator is also responsible for developing, coordinating and evaluating their own suite of programs, services and resources for co-curricular community-engaged learning. The Lead Coordinator identifies opportunities for community-engaged learning; explores student and community partner needs/interests; promotes opportunities to students, on-campus partners and community partners; coordinates program offerings; monitors progress and assesses student-learning outcomes. The Lead Coordinator is the main contact point for co-curricular collaborations units across the University and works closely with members of the Student Life staff, with academic and co-curricular partners in the University, and with partners in the wider Greater Toronto Area community. The Lead Coordinator works actively to promote a culture of community engagement at the University, devising programs that attend to access and inclusion and that are rooted in anti-oppressive and assets-based approaches to community engagement. Your responsibilities will include: Developing components of programs and initiatives that advance program objectives Building and strengthening relationships with stakeholders and partners of strategic importance Planning and overseeing the implementation of an evaluation framework for programs and initiatives Conducting detailed analysis on program efficiency and student learning outcomes to inform program planning activities Developing learning outcomes for workshops and/or services Facilitating educational workshopsand seminars Developing outreach strategies that promote programs to students and the broader community Directing the activities of a group of staff-appointed employees all performing a similar function Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree (Master's preferred) or an acceptable equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum five years in program development, delivery and evaluation, including significant work experience in a non-profit organization. At least two years of supervisory experience. Advanced program planning and evaluation expertise including designing learning outcomes. Experience in volunteer recruitment, coordination, and orientation. Demonstrated experience designing and delivering training for students or volunteers, including from anti-oppressive and assets-based foundations. Experience in programming for youth or post-secondary student populations. Demonstrated experience leading the management of large events. Experience working on collaborative initiatives with multiple partners, including community organizations. Experience planning and promoting events in a university setting. Computer skills: MS Teams, PowerPoint, Word, Excel, Outlook. Excellent communication, presentation, and problem-solving skills. Demonstrated exceptional relationship-building and stewardship skills. Demonstrated understanding of the principles and practices of community-engaged learning. Demonstrated commitment to anti-oppressive and anti-racist practice. Demonstrated understanding of experiential learning strategies including but, not limited to, experiential program design, reflection and assessment. Able to work collaboratively and collegially. To be successful in this role you will be: Diplomatic Motivated self-learner Proactive Resourceful Team player NOTE: This position is 100% in person, on campus. Some weekend work with advance notice. Closing Date: 11/11/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 14 -- $95,344 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $121,932. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Divisional HR Office Email: cahrs.hr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Training, Learning, Volunteer Coordinator, Equity, Fundraising, Education, Human Resources, Nonprofit, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Scarborough-Maintenance-Worker-II-ON/606995617/": {"title": "Maintenance Worker II Job Details", "description": "Maintenance Worker II Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Maintenance Worker II Date Posted: 10/14/2026 Req ID: 50533 Faculty/Division: UofT Scarborough Department: UTSC:FM-Maintenance Campus : University of Toronto Scarborough (UTSC) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The University of Toronto Scarborough is a place of energy, enthusiasm and passion. Our commitment to inclusive excellence attracts the brightest learners, scholars and employees from around the globe. Our success has been made possible by the opportunity given to us by Indigenous hosts to operate on their territory, and we cherish our continuing partnerships with these communities. The University of Toronto Scarborough is an exciting campus with unlimited potential. Join us on our journey. This search aligns with the University\u2019s commitment to strategically and proactively promote diversity among our community members ( Statement on Equity, Diversity & Excellence ). Recognizing that Black, Indigenous, and other Racialized communities have experienced inequities that have developed historically and are ongoing, we strongly welcome and encourage candidates from those communities to apply. General Description: Under general supervision, the Maintenance Worker performs heavy cleaning and custodial duties, moves and sets up furniture and equipment on a routine basis and for special events. Typical Duties: The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required, and the extent of responsibility involved in this job. They in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated. Flexibility of the employee to perform a wide variety of functions is necessary in successfully fulfilling the requirements of this position. The degree to which each employee performs each of the following tasks listed below will vary according to where and when the employee is scheduled to work. cleans and scrubs floors and washrooms using appropriate equipment including automatic floor cleaning machines, electric buffers, mops and vacuum cleaners; performs cleaning and dusting at elevated heights, using ladder and lifting devices as required; sets up cleaning equipment for use; maintains cleaning equipment; reconditions floors, repairs and cleans grout, using appropriate equipment; performs routine and special room set ups which entails: following work orders, room diagrams and verbal instructions; moving and setting up of furniture and equipment according to plan and schedule; opens and locks doors to assigned rooms; may assisting setting out academic examination booklets; clears furniture and equipment as requested and stores in appropriate areas. disassembles/reassembles furniture for the purpose of moving; performs maintenance functions such as changing lights and adjustments to furniture and equipment; other related duties as required. Minimum Requirements for Selection Education: Completion of Grade 10 or equivalent; technical training is desirable. Experience: One year of related work experience, education may be substituted for experience. Other: Physical ability to perform required duties, including heavy lifting and pushing of furniture and equipment, considerable walking and stair climbing; ability to communicate effectively in English (oral and written), ability to follow written instructions; awareness of building security and fire procedures; tact and diplomacy in dealing with others; ability to work at varying heights and to operate and use safety ladders and lifts. Applicants are also expected to show evidence of a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment. Note: The hours of work for this position are Monday to Friday from 12:30 pm - 9:00 pm. Closing Date: 10/22/2026,11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: CUPE F/T L3261 Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: Job Rate: $25.96/hr Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Event Planning, Hospitality Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Stewardship-Coordinator-ON/607012417/": {"title": "Stewardship Coordinator", "description": "Stewardship Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Stewardship Coordinator Date Posted: 10/14/2026 Req ID: 50546 Faculty/Division: VP - Division of University Advancement Department: Campaign and Marketing Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00052897 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Division of University Advancement (DUA) aims to sustain and enhance the University of Toronto\u2019s academic mission, leadership, and worldwide impact, by engaging alumni and private sector constituents meaningfully in the mission of the University, building mutually beneficial relationships of increasing value and satisfaction over time. DUA at the University of Toronto is engaged in a transformative agenda deeply rooted in the University\u2019s vision for growth and innovation. We are focus on growing fundraising efforts\u037e enhancing the effectiveness and satisfaction of alumni engagement and programs\u037e building advancement talent capacity within and across divisions; creating an organization and culture that fosters diversity and inclusiveness. Your opportunity: The Stewardship team at DUA promotes stewardship and donor relations best practices across the university and develops and delivers best-in-class programs that recognize donor generosity, demonstrate impact, and strengthen donors\u2019 connections to the University. Within the Stewardship team, the Stewardship Coordinator provides operational and administrative support for activities related to principal gift implementation, stewardship and donor relations, while also contributing to broader stewardship team priorities as they evolve. The role supports the planning, coordination, tracking, and follow-through required to deliver stewardship activities connected to gift agreement deliverables, donor communications, events, meetings, and reporting. The coordinator plays an important role in supporting the coordinated stewardship activity required to deliver on donor commitments, support strong relationships with principal gift donors and divisional partners and helping ensure the effective operations of the Stewardship team. Your responsibilities will include: Fostering positive relationships with prospective and existing donors Drafting donor acknowledgment and recognition communications Providing detailed information for the development of donor relations and stewardship programs Coordinating meeting schedules, agendas, materials, action and follow-up items Identifying and resolving individual data anomalies and discrepancies Updating and maintaining database records Monitoring accounts for a project and/or program Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum three years of related professional experience is required, experience with direct stewardship, donor relations, fundraising, marketing, or specials events experience preferred Experience drafting communications. Experience coordinating meeting and/or events in collaboration with other staff, volunteers and external vendors. Demonstrated writing experience and excellent writing, editing, and proofreading skills Excellent computer skills; proficiency in using advanced functions of word processing, Excel spreadsheets and CRM databases. Demonstrated ability to adhere to a high level of customer service, tact and confidentiality. Ability to manage multiple priorities concurrently; able to execute existing work while managing and responding to urgent opportunities. Detail-oriented person with an appreciation for accuracy and thoroughness. Ability to work effectively with a diverse population of staff, volunteers, donors and external contacts with tact and diplomacy to build and maintain successful relationships Demonstrated ability to adhere to high level of ethical standards in utilizing donor information and to confidentiality requirements. Assets (Nonessential): Demonstrated knowledge and understanding of fundraising and donor relations concepts, principles, procedures and techniques an asset To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Diplomatic Efficient Organized Proactive Closing Date: 11/03/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 10 -- $75,004 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $95,915. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Divisional HR Office Email: cahrs.hr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Copy Editor, Proofreading, Writing, Administrative Assistant, Fundraising, Creative, Administrative, Nonprofit Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Information-Services-Representative-ON/606955117/": {"title": "Information Services Representative Job Details", "description": "Information Services Representative Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Information Services Representative Date Posted: 10/13/2026 Req ID: 50524 Faculty/Division: VP & Provost Department: Hart House Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00060176 Existing Vacancy: No About us: Hart House is a centre for experiential education outside the classroom at the University of Toronto. Since it opened in 1919, Hart House functions as a place where students, faculty, staff, alumni and members of the broader community connect with each other and the world. Through an array of co-curricular programming in the arts, dialogue and wellness, Hart House works with local and international partners to foster community and to create innovative learning opportunities for students. Hart House operates from a historic facility on the St. George campus, as well as a 150-acre farm in Caledon, Ontario, offering a wide range of services through a social enterprise model that generates revenue to support its student-focused programming on all three University of Toronto campuses. The Information Services Desk is a dynamic focal point within Hart House where administrative functions related to a wide range of services and sales \u2013 e.g., registration for classes, memberships and other service offerings for Hart House, ticket sales for Hart House Theatre, reservations for the Hart House Fitness Centre \u2013 as well as providing general information about Hart House and the university, are performed. The Information Services Desk provides our diverse community an open door, welcoming them to enjoy a multitude of activities and services at Hart House. Your opportunity: The Information Services Representative is directly supervised by the Manager, Information & Customer Service and plays a role in supporting the Information Services team. The incumbent will work in close collaboration with the Information Services Associates and Fitness, Wellness and Recreation team to this end with a focus on the facilitation of strong customer service at service points within the building. They will also be responsible to support and provide guidance to non-appointed staff. The incumbent will act as the first point of contact for general inquiries and will be providing routine and detailed information on programs and events. They will direct information to visitors on eligibility requirements, procedures, and policies for Hart House facilities. The incumbent will be responsible for collating and organizing materials, maintaining emergency contact lists, booking rooms, ensuring responsiveness to inquiries, and maintaining daily reports. They will also handle incoming and outgoing mail and deliveries and liaise with facilities or caretaking staff to address any building issues. This role will be responsible for following rules and procedural instructions when opening and/or closing the Information Services Desk. Your responsibilities will include: Acting as the first point of contact for general enquiries, providing routine information on programs, events, and eligibility requirements Applying established standards when responding to emergencies and redirecting inquiries as appropriate Booking rooms and arranging accommodations, ensuring efficient and appropriate use of spaces Resolving minor complaints within the scope of the role and referring larger issues to the appropriate channels Checking eligibility of students to access the facility and maintaining control over the distribution of access to designated University spaces Supporting the Information Services team in providing information on programs and services to internal and external contacts Assisting with registrations, maintaining databases, generating reports, conducting regular checks and balancing financial transactions against sales Serving as a resource to others by providing (non-supervisory) administrative guidance Essential Qualifications: High School Diploma or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum of two years of experience in customer service Minimum of one year of experience in a high-volume, multi-service customer service environment involving cash/point-of-sale transactions, scheduling/reservations, and in person conflict resolution Demonstrated experience with providing job-related guidance to others Demonstrated experience de-escalating conflict with members of the public, including handling complaints, denying access/service when policy requires it, and managing frustrated or distressed patrons Excellent personal and human relation skills Computer skills required: Microsoft Office Suite. Keyboarding skills. Familiarity with or ability to quickly learn Fusion software to maintain membership database and online registrations is essential Must be able to work collaboratively and professionally as part of a team while also being capable to work independently when required An energetic individual who enjoys the challenge of work in a dynamic environment Excellent customer service, interpersonal skills, good judgment and initiative Strong sales orientation Accuracy along with the ability to multi-task is essential Demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion in all work responsibilities and in collaborative workplace practices Fluent in written and spoken English Ability to work under pressure First Aid/CPR Training is required and will be provided Assets (Nonessential): Experience with Fusion and/or Audience View a notable asset Experience with POS equipment Experience in a higher education context is preferred Fluency in second or more languages would be an asset Experience or knowledge in fitness, health or recreation promotion Knowledge and experience of for the University of Toronto and/or Hart House programs and services To be successful in this role you will be: Accountable Adaptable Patient Possess a positive attitude Self-directed Team player Notes: Hours of work: Sunday and Monday from 7:00 AM to 3:30 PM, Tuesday and Wednesday from 7:00 AM to 3:30 PM, Thursday from 7:00 AM to 3:15 PM A cover letter is required with your application. There is a second vacancy for this role with different hours of work . If interested, please visit the job posting for Information Services Representative (50523) . To be considered for both positions, candidates must apply for each role respectively. Closing Date: 10/21/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 04 -- $52,327 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $66,919. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Divisional HR Office Email: cahrs.hr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Customer Service Representative, Facilities, Database, Equity, Customer Service, Operations, Technology, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Cafeteria-Worker-Casual-%288-Vacancies%29-ON/606981917/": {"title": "Cafeteria Worker", "description": "Cafeteria Worker - Casual (8 Vacancies) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Cafeteria Worker - Casual (8 Vacancies) Date Posted: 10/13/2026 Req ID: 50538 Faculty/Division: Spaces & Experiences Department: Food Services Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Description: Under general supervision, assembles, prepares and serves food and beverage products and maintains cleanliness of the cafeteria area. May operates a cash register, receive and issue cash. Typical Duties The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required and the extent of the responsibility involved in this position. \u00a0They in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated. Flexibility of the employee to perform a wide variety of functions is necessary in successfully fulfilling the requirements of this position. \u00a0The degree to which each employee performs each of the following tasks listed below will vary according to where and when the employee is scheduled to work. (a)\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0assembles work station with appropriate products and equipment; (b)\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0assembles, prepares, and serves food and beverage products; (c)\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0cooks stir fry and grill display cooking, may cook some other items; (d)\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0prepares sandwiches, salads and bakes premixed food products; (e)\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0advises and provides information to customers such as ingredients, pricing, portion size; (f)\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0collects dishes and tableware used by customers and places them in appropriate areas for washing; (g)\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0cleans table tops, counters and furniture in cafeteria and surrounding area; (h)\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0maintains adequate supplies of dishes, utensils and food and paper products in various receptacles for use by customers; (i)\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0removes soiled tableware and garbage to specific locations, sorts recyclable materials; (j)\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0scrubs pots and pans; and washes dishes (k) \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0cleans floors; staff locker rooms and washrooms; (l)\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0receives and stores food and supplies; checks receiving slips for accuracy; (m)\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0sets up and prepares cash register, receives cash float and sets up cash appropriately; keys menu prices into cash register if required. (n) \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0prepares reports at the end of each shift; (o) \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0writes special menus and their prices on menu board; (p)\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0prepares condiment and dessert counters; (q) \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0balances cash at the end of the shift, delivers cash to accountant or locks in safe; (r) \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0may keep records of stores on hand; and (s)\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0other related duties as required. Minimum Requirements for Selection Education:\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Completion of Grade 12 or equivalent. Experience:\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0One year of related working experience. Other:\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Physical ability to perform required duties, ability to communicate effectively in English (oral and written), considerable public relations skills (courtesy and tact) and may be required to complete a University of Toronto server training program. Knowledge of food safety. Ability to work well in a team setting. Ability to handle figures rapidly. Closing Date: 10/21/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly, CUPE 3261 Casual Appointment Type : Casual Part-Time Schedule: Flexible schedule required, which may include morning, evening and weekend hours Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: $25.96 per hour Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Cashier, PR, Food Safety, Accounting, Hospitality, Marketing, Quality, Finance, Part Time Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Information-Services-Representative-ON/606955017/": {"title": "Information Services Representative Job Details", "description": "Information Services Representative Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Oppo