er community connect with each other and the world. Through an array of co-curricular programming in the arts, dialogue and wellness, Hart House works with local and international partners to foster community and to create innovative learning opportunities for students. Hart House operates from a historic facility on the St. George campus, as well as a 150-acre farm in Caledon, Ontario, offering a wide range of services through a social enterprise model that generates revenue to support its student-focused programming on all three University of Toronto campuses. The Information Services Desk is a dynamic focal point within Hart House where administrative functions related to a wide range of services and sales \u2013 e.g., registration for classes, memberships and other service offerings for Hart House, ticket sales for Hart House Theatre, reservations for the Hart House Fitness Centre \u2013 as well as providing general information about Hart House and the university, are performed. The Information Services Desk provides our diverse community an open door, welcoming them to enjoy a multitude of activities and services at Hart House. Your opportunity: The Information Services Representative is directly supervised by the Manager, Information & Customer Service and plays a role in supporting the Information Services team. The incumbent will work in close collaboration with the Information Services Associates and Fitness, Wellness and Recreation team to this end with a focus on the facilitation of strong customer service at service points within the building. They will also be responsible to support and provide guidance to non-appointed staff. The incumbent will act as the first point of contact for general inquiries and will be providing routine and detailed information on programs and events. They will direct information to visitors on eligibility requirements, procedures, and policies for Hart House facilities. The incumbent will be responsible for collating and organizing materials, maintaining emergency contact lists, booking rooms, ensuring responsiveness to inquiries, and maintaining daily reports. They will also handle incoming and outgoing mail and deliveries and liaise with facilities or caretaking staff to address any building issues. This role will be responsible for following rules and procedural instructions when opening and/or closing the Information Services Desk. Your responsibilities will include: Acting as the first point of contact for general inquiries, providing routine information on programs, events, and eligibility requirements Applying established standards when responding to emergencies and redirecting inquiries as appropriate Booking rooms and arranging accommodations, ensuring efficient and appropriate use of spaces Resolving minor complaints within the scope of the role and referring larger issues to the appropriate channels Checking eligibility of students to access the facility and maintaining control over the distribution of access to designated University spaces Supporting the Information Services team in providing information on programs and services to internal and external contacts Assisting with registrations, maintaining databases, generating reports, conducting regular checks and balancing financial transactions against sales Serving as a resource to others by providing (non-supervisory) administrative guidance Essential Qualifications: High School Diploma or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum of two years of experience in customer service Minimum of one year of experience in a high-volume, multi-service customer service environment involving cash/point-of-sale transactions, scheduling/reservations, and in person conflict resolution Demonstrated experience with providing job-related guidance to others Demonstrated experience de-escalating conflict with members of the public, including handling complaints, denying access/service when policy requires it, and managing frustrated or distressed patrons Excellent personal and human relation skills Computer skills required: Microsoft Office Suite. Keyboarding skills. Familiarity with or ability to quickly learn Fusion software to maintain membership database and online registrations is essential Must be able to work collaboratively and professionally as part of a team while also being capable to work independently when required An energetic individual who enjoys the challenge of work in a dynamic environment Excellent customer service, interpersonal skills, good judgment and initiative Strong sales orientation Accuracy along with the ability to multi-task is essential Demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion in all work responsibilities and in collaborative workplace practices Fluent in written and spoken English Ability to work under pressure First Aid/CPR Training is required and will be provided Assets (Nonessential): Experience with Fusion and/or Audience View a notable asset Experience with POS equipment Experience in a higher education context is preferred Fluency in second or more languages would be an asset Experience or knowledge in fitness, health or recreation promotion Knowledge and experience of for the University of Toronto and/or Hart House programs and services To be successful in this role you will be: Accountable Adaptable Patient Possess a positive attitude Self-directed Team player Notes: Hours of work: Sunday through Thursday from 2:45 PM to 11:00 PM A cover letter is required with your application. There is a second vacancy for this role with different hours of work . If interested, please visit the job posting for Information Services Representative (50524 ) . To be considered for both positions, candidates must apply for each role respectively. Closing Date: 10/21/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 04 -- $52,327 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $66,919. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Divisional HR Office Email: cahrs.hr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Customer Service Representative, Facilities, Database, Equity, Customer Service, Operations, Technology, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Cafeteria-Worker-Sessional-%281-vacancy%29-ON/606984417/": {"title": "Cafeteria Worker", "description": "Cafeteria Worker - Sessional (1 vacancy) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Cafeteria Worker - Sessional (1 vacancy) Date Posted: 10/13/2026 Req ID: 50539 Faculty/Division: VP-Facilities & Real Estate Department: Food Services Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Under general supervision, assembles, prepares and serves food and beverage products and maintains cleanliness of the cafeteria area. May operate a cash register, receive and issue cash. Typical Duties The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required and the extent of the responsibility involved in this position. \u00a0They in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated. Flexibility of the employee to perform a wide variety of functions is necessary in successfully fulfilling the requirements of this position. The degree to which each employee performs each of the following tasks listed below will vary according to where and when the employee is scheduled to work. (a)\u00a0 \u00a0 assembles work station with appropriate products and equipment; (b)\u00a0 \u00a0 assembles, prepares, and serves food and beverage products; (c)\u00a0 \u00a0 cooks stir fry and grill display cooking, may cook some other items; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0prepares sandwiches, salads and bakes premixed food products; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0advises and provides information to customers such as ingredients, pricing, portion size; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0collects dishes and tableware used by customers and places them in appropriate areas for washing; (g) \u00a0 \u00a0cleans table tops, counters and furniture in cafeteria and surrounding area; (h) \u00a0 \u00a0maintains adequate supplies of dishes, utensils and food and paper products in various receptacles for use by customers; (i)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0removes soiled tableware and garbage to specific locations, sorts recyclable materials; (j)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0scrubs pots and pans; and washes dishes (k)\u00a0 \u00a0 cleans floors; staff locker rooms and washrooms; (l)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0receives and stores food and supplies; checks receiving slips for accuracy; (m)\u00a0 \u00a0sets up and prepares cash register, receives cash float and sets up cash appropriately; keys menu prices into cash register if required. (n)\u00a0 \u00a0 prepares reports at the end of each shift; (o)\u00a0 \u00a0 writes special menus and their prices on menu board; (p)\u00a0 \u00a0 prepares condiment and dessert counters; (q)\u00a0 \u00a0 balances cash at the end of the shift, delivers cash to accountant or locks in safe; (r) \u00a0 \u00a0 may keep records of stores on hand; and (s) \u00a0 \u00a0other related duties as required. Minimum Requirements for Selection: Education: Completion of Grade 12 or equivalent. Experience: One year of related working experience. Other: Physical ability to perform required duties, ability to communicate effectively in English (oral and written), considerable public relations skills (courtesy and tact) and may be required to complete a University of Toronto server training program. Knowledge of food safety. Ability to work well in a team setting. Ability to handle figures rapidly. Previous barista/Starbucks experience is an asset. Shift Details: Sunday Monday Tuesday Wednesday Thursday Friday Saturday Off Off 2:00pm to 10:30pm 2:00pm to 10:30pm 2:00pm to 10:30pm 2:00pm to 10:30pm 11:00am to 7:30pm Closing Date: 10/28/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: CUPE F/T L3261 Appointment Type : Ancillary Operations Schedule: Full-Time, shift details outlined above. Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: Job Rate: $25.96/hr Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Cashier, Food Safety, PR, Accounting, Hospitality, Marketing, Quality, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Associate-Professor-Gastrointestinal-Pathology-ON/606909817/": {"title": "Assistant/ Associate/ Professor", "description": "Assistant/ Associate/ Professor - Gastrointestinal Pathology Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant/ Associate/ Professor - Gastrointestinal Pathology Date Posted: 10/09/2026 Closing Date: 11/13/2026 , 11:59PM ET Open until Filled Req ID: 50492 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Lab. Medicine & Pathobiology Hospital Affiliation: Sinai Health System Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at Mount Sinai Hospital is seeking a faculty member at the Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Level with diagnostic and academic expertise in gastrointestinal pathology. The anticipated start will on January 1, 2027 or a mutually agreeable date. We are seeking an individual who values working in a collegial environment with superb clinical material and collaborations with dedicated clinical colleagues. The successful candidate will join an academic faculty with diverse diagnostic expertise, teaching responsibilities and research activities. Mount Sinai Hospital has internationally renowned and expanding clinical and pathology programs in gastrointestinal disease (both inflammatory and neoplastic), including a pathology consultation service that is highly subscribed to by centres throughout the country. We utilize leading-edge diagnostic technologies and candidates with molecular pathology interest and/or experience would be desirable, but is not mandatory. The candidate\u2019s responsibilities will include clinical practice in GI pathology, research, and teaching as well as administrative responsibilities as necessary. Candidates must have a medical degree and hold Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada certification in Anatomical Pathology, or equivalent, and be eligible for licensure by the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario. Fellowship training or experience in GI pathology is required. The preferred candidate must be an excellent diagnostician with a demonstrated interest in teaching and a track record in clinical or translational research. In addition, the candidate should be eligible for an academic appointment in the Department of Laboratory Medicine and Pathobiology, University of Toronto. Rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Uniform Minimum Level of Compensation (UMLC) in the Province of Ontario which is currently $418,920. The UMLC program, instituted by the Ministry of Health, ensures that your total compensation package is equal to that of other Laboratory Physicians in the Province. Benefits will be provided. Evaluation of applications will be ongoing and will continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 Interested applicants should send their curriculum vitae, a brief statement of their academic plans, and the names of three references by November 13, 2026 to: Dr. James Conner Section Head, Surgical Pathology Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Mount Sinai Hospital 600 University Avenue Toronto, ON M5G 1X5 Email: james.conner@sinaihealth.ca Only applicants who are shortlisted will be contacted. CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. As one of the largest departments of its kind, the Department of Laboratory Medicine and Pathobiology (LMP) has more than 400 faculty including basic scientists, pathologists, laboratory physicians and scientists.\u00a0 By combining research with clinical practice, we are uniquely positioned to translate new findings into reality.\u00a0 As a result, we are known as leaders in diagnosing and treating patients and populations, making an impact locally, nationally and internationally.\u00a0 For more information about the Department of Laboratory Medicine and Pathobiology, University of Toronto please visit our website at www.lmp.utoronto.ca All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Gastroenterology, Pathology, Laboratory, Academic, Healthcare, Science, Research, Education Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-LecturerAssistantAssociateProfessor-Academic-Psychiatrist-Geriatric-Mental-Health-ON/606916517/": {"title": "Lecturer/Assistant/Associate/Professor", "description": "Lecturer/Assistant/Associate/Professor - Academic Psychiatrist - Geriatric Mental Health Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Lecturer/Assistant/Associate/Professor - Academic Psychiatrist - Geriatric Mental Health Date Posted: 10/09/2026 Closing Date: 11/20/2026 , 11:59PM ET, Open Until Filled Req ID: 50498 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Psychiatry Hospital Affiliation: Sinai Health System Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Description: Lecturer/Assistant/Associate/Professor - Academic Psychiatrist \u2013 Geriatric Mental Health Outpatient Services, Sinai Health The Department of Psychiatry, Faculty of Medicine at the University of Toronto and the Mental Health and Addictions Program at Sinai Health are seeking to recruit a geriatric psychiatrist. The successful candidate will qualify for an academic position as a Clinician-Teacher, Clinician-Investigator, Clinician-Educator, or Clinician in Quality, Innovation and Safety and must be eligible for a full-time clinical academic appointment at the rank of Lecturer, Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor at the University of Toronto.\u00a0 The anticipated start date is January 1, 2027 or a mutually agreeable date. Sinai Health is a leading academic health sciences centre fully affiliated with the University of Toronto.\u00a0It includes Mount Sinai Hospital, Hennick Bridgepoint Hospital, the Lunenfeld-Tanenbaum Research Institute, and our system partner Circle of Care, united in the mission to deliver compassionate, integrated care across acute, rehabilitative, and complex continuing care settings. The successful candidate will provide outpatient psychiatric consultations and ongoing care to older adults (over the age of 65). That individual may also provide consultation-liaison care to medical and surgical inpatients at Mount Sinai Hospital. Additional duties will include teaching and supervision of medical students, psychiatry residents, and geriatric psychiatry residents, and collaboration in research and other academic activities. The successful applicant must hold an MD degree, must be Royal College/Board Certified or Royal College/Board Eligible in Psychiatry and must be eligible for medical licensure with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario. Preference will be given to candidates who hold an FRCPC in Geriatric Psychiatry or an equivalent qualification. The candidate should have a track record of excellence in teaching, education, research, QI, or other academic endeavors. Remuneration is in accordance with the compensation of a psychiatrist in the province of Ontario. Estimated remuneration will be in the range of $300,000 to $350,000 per annum, commensurate with academic rank, qualifications, and experience.\u00a0All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply by October 31, 2026. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Should you be interested in this opportunity, please forward a one-page statement of interest, curriculum vitae, and three referees via email to: Dr. David Gratzer Psychiatrist-in-Chief and Medical Program Director Sinai Health 600 University Ave. Toronto, ON, M5G 1X5 416-586-8888 Email: david.gratzer@sinaihealth.ca For more information on the University of Toronto, Department of Psychiatry, please visit http://www.psychiatry.utoronto.ca . For more information about Sinai Health, please visit https://www.sinaihealth.ca/ . CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Geriatric, Medical, Psychology, Rehabilitation, Counseling, Healthcare Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Senior-Financial-Advisor-ON/606898817/": {"title": "Senior Financial Advisor Job Details", "description": "Senior Financial Advisor Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Senior Financial Advisor Date Posted: 10/09/2026 Req ID: 50284 Faculty/Division: VP - University Operations Department: FRE Financial Strategy & Services Dept Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Operations of Facilities & Real Estate \u00a0(FRE) is the largest shared service division at the University of Toronto, providing a wide range of services to the University and serving three campuses. FRE is responsible for several key portfolios within the University, including Facilities and Services, University Planning Design & Construction, and Spaces & Experiences. We also provided Financial Services to Information Technology Division. We strive to provide efficient and effective services that support the University\u2019s mission of knowledge creation, educational program delivery and community service. FRE Financial Strategy and Services Department works closely with other departments, as well as internal and external stakeholders, to manage FRE\u2019s \u00a0financial resources, enhance operational efficiency, and improve financial management capacity. The Finance Department ensures compliance, provides strategic advice, enhances support for the decision-making process, manages risks, optimizes financial processes, adopts new technologies, improves existing systems, and promotes best practices. Your Opportunity: This position is responsible for developing, analysing, allocating and aligning budgets and managing financial resources for the portfolio departments in FRE, which serves three campuses in the University. The Advisor monitors financial performance and position, provides in-depth financial analysis, conducts forecasting and reporting on the monthly, quarterly and annual basis; ensures financial controls and accuracy are maintained; reviews funding requests; and performs year end reporting. This role plays a critical part in the financial planning, budgeting process, business and operational analysis, accounting, financial modeling, helping to shape and inform strategic decisions and ensure efficient utilization of business resources. The incumbent will serve as a strategic advisor to department heads by providing financial and accounting advice on complex financial matters to both financial and non-financial stakeholders at various levels, support compliance and audit activities, and contribute to system development and maintenance. To do this effectively the Senior Financial Advisor will be required analyze, synthesize, and present on highly confidential information and data, including decisions related to staffing levels and in-depth financial Analysis to support recommendations and detailed implementation plans. Essential Qualifications: EDUCATION: A University degree in Finance, Accounting, Business Administration, or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of education and experience.\u00a0 Professional accounting designation (e.g. CPA, CA, CMA, CGA). EXPERIENCE: Minimum of five (5) years of experience in financial planning and analysis or a similar role. Experience with major ERP systems, financial software and Knowledge of SAP or the University's Administrative Management System (AMS) is required. SKILLS: Strong knowledge of building and managing large financial database. Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities. Advanced proficiency with spreadsheet and word-processing software.\u00a0 Proficient in Excel formulas and advanced functions. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Strong working knowledge of customer service principles and practices, ability to perform with minimum supervision and make decisions independently. Ability to multi-task, effectively prioritize workload, meet hard and fast deadline. Must possess strong analytical skills. Detail-oriented with multiple tasks, information organization. OTHER : Integrity and political acumen. Demonstrated ability to prioritize multiple tasks and projects with sensitive deadlines. Superior planning and organizational skills.\u00a0 Demonstrated high level of service to a large group of stakeholders.\u00a0 \u00a0Direct operational exposure to or comprehensive knowledge of best practices within construction, facilities management and information technology industries. Closing Date: 10/30/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 3 -- Hiring Zone: $97,336 - $113,558 -- Broadband Salary Range: $ 97,336 - $162,224 Job Category: Finance/Budget/Planning/Audit Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Financial, Financial Advisor, Financial Planner, Accounting, CPA, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Arts-&-Science-Internship-Program-Coordinator-%28term%29-ON/606908217/": {"title": "Arts & Science Internship Program Coordinator (term)", "description": "Arts & Science Internship Program Coordinator (term) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Arts & Science Internship Program Coordinator (term) Date Posted: 10/09/2026 Req ID: 50505 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: Experiential Learning & Outreach Support Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00049721 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Faculty of Arts & Science is the heart of Canada\u2019s leading university and one of the most comprehensive and diverse academic divisions in the world. The strength of Arts & Science derives from our combined teaching and research excellence in the humanities, sciences and social sciences across 29 departments, seven colleges and 46 interdisciplinary centres, institutes and programs. We can only realize our mission with the dedication and excellence of engaged staff and faculty. The diversity of opportunities and perspectives within the Faculty reflect the local and global landscape and the need for curiosity, innovative thinking and collaboration. At Arts & Science, we take pride in our legacy of innovation and discovery that has changed the way we think about the world. Your opportunity: The Experiential Learning and Outreach Support office in the Faculty of Arts & Science has a mandate to grow quality experiential learning opportunities for Arts & Science students, including work-integrated learning, career-engaged learning, community-engaged learning, research, and international opportunities. The Faculty has been moving forward with an ambitious plan to expand experiential learning opportunities available to undergraduate students across all Arts & Science disciplines. The Faculty is committed to preparing students for lifelong success in the labour market, deepening relationships with local partners in the public, private and non-profit sectors and increasing opportunities for international student mobility. As part of our expansion of experiential learning, we launched the Arts & Science Internship Program (ASIP) in Fall 2021.The program provides specialized professional development training and paid work-integrated learning opportunities for Arts & Science students across 79 different academic programs, with plans for continued growth. Participation in the ASIP stream allows students to explore career options, apply their academic learning in a professional context, gain valuable work experience, and build a professional network. We are committed to equity, diversity and inclusion and to designing programming that allows allstudents to meet their academic and career goals. Reporting to the Associate Director, Employer Relations & Operations, the Arts & Science Internship Program (ASIP) Coordinator is an integral part of the Employer Relations team and serves as a bridge between employers and students. The ASIP Coordinator: \u2022 Works closely with students in their assigned program(s) and/or industries/sectors to identify potential employers and connect students to meaningful employment opportunities. \u2022 Cultivates new employers (locally, nationally, and internationally) and maintains strong relationships with existing employers, working to ensure each employer\u2019s holistic recruiting needs are met. \u2022 Together with the Student Services team, coaches and provides guidance to students through the recruitment cycle and while on a work term, ensuring employment targets are met or exceeded with a high level of employer and student satisfaction. \u2022 In partnership with the Employer Relations team, ensures a seamless recruiting and hiring experience for employer partners. \u2022 Is an energetic, creative, outside-of-the-box thinker who develops innovative ways for employers from diverse industries/sectors to engage with U of T\u2019s Arts & Science students. \u2022 This ASIP Coordinator position will be responsible for supporting the Humanities and Social Sciences portfolio. \u2022 This position will be responsible for engaging with employers which includes government, not for profits, arts & entertainment, consulting, educational services, professional services, heritage institutions and research and development services in social sciences and humanities. Note: this is a term opportunity to January 2028. Your responsibilities will include: Identifying, fostering and maintaining relationships with potential and existing employers Promoting programming, student needs and interests to employers and industry contacts Researching and analyzing potential employers and recommending student placement opportunities Promoting programs at recruitment events Conducting detailed labour market analysis to inform program and partnership development Implementing plans that support the development of work-integrated learning opportunities for students Advising and coaching students on the selection of appropriate work-integrated learning opportunities Advising students on work related recruitment processes and practices Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum five (5) years of experience in employer development, relationship management, sales, marketing, and/or business development, with some experience in a targets-driven environment In depth knowledge of the post-secondary sector, the entry-level labour market, and employment trends Understanding of career pathways, opportunities and possibilities for students in Humanities & Social Sciences programs Proven successful track record of building and maintaining strong, effective relationships with potential and existing employers, alumni, and partners within a target driven environment Experience working with Customer Relationship Management tools (e.g. Salesforce) to track individual performance and outcomes Experience working with Experiential Learning Management Software (e.g. ORBIS, Symplicity) Knowledge of cooperative education and work-integrated learning programming, career advising, employment standards and workplace rights Experience providing direct support to students, new graduates, or individuals in the areas of career, skill development, and/or career transition Ability to work with a diverse client group across multiple sectors Highly driven to meet targets, proactive, persuasive, and diplomatic Demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion Excellent marketing and account management, sales, and public relations skills Ability to show sound judgement in dealing with confidential information Highly developed sense of accountability, tact, diplomacy, and professionalism Excellent communication skills and strong relationship building, interpersonal and negotiation skills Strong presentation and facilitation skills Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects or priorities simultaneously with strong organizational skills Demonstrated proficiency with Microsoft Office 365 programs and strong IT fluency Valid driver\u2019s license and/or willingness to travel within the GTA Ability to work in and comfort within a fast-paced student services environment juggling many activities simultaneously Assets (Nonessential): Established partnerships with the industry sectors listed above International work experience and international program knowledge is an asset. To be successful in this role you will be: Accountable Articulate Diplomatic Organized Resourceful Responsible Self-directed Team player Closing Date: 10/25/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 12 -- $84,564 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $108,145. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: CRM, Relationship Manager, Intern, Program Manager, Technology, Customer Service, Entry Level, Management Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-M365-Solutions-Specialist-ON/606931317/": {"title": "M365 Solutions Specialist", "description": "M365 Solutions Specialist Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb M365 Solutions Specialist Date Posted: 10/09/2026 Req ID: 50510 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: MedIT Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00057577 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Home to over 40 departments and institutes, the University of Toronto's Temerty Faculty of Medicine lies at the heart of the Toronto Academic Health Science Network and is a global leader in ground-breaking research and education, spanning clinical medicine, basic science and the rehabilitation sciences sectors. Your opportunity: MedIT provides information technology support for the Temerty Faculty of Medicine. Ourmission is to partner and collaborate with clients, University, and third parties to determine value based, sustainable technology solutions that enable the Faculty to achieve its academic mission. Working under the guidance and supervision of the M365 Lead Architect, the M365 Solutions Specialist will play a key role in optimizing workflows within Temerty Medicine using the Microsoft 365 suite. You\u2019ll work alongside clients and M365 Solution Architects to design and implement tailored, user-friendly solutions while providing hands-on programming support. This role offers a unique opportunity to deepen your expertise in M365 products and leverage that knowledge to enhance efficiency and innovation across the Faculty. Your responsibilities will include: Assessing client system requirements, business processes, and user needs, and proposing effective solutions using the Microsoft 365 (M365) suite Analyzing the performance and efficiency of current client systems (e.g., SharePoint), developing technical improvements, and ensuring system security and integrity. Gathering requirements from clients and working closely with M365 Solution Architects to create and implement user-friendly solutions that streamline workflows and improve client processes. Collaborating with M365 Solution Architects to develop and implement Enterprise offerings, rollout, and implementation across Temerty Medicine Developing, testing, and modifying programming code within the M365 suite based on client needs. Evaluating new M365 tools and updates to assess risks and/or opportunities Addressing client service requests for M365, troubleshoot issues, update documentation, and train end-users on M365 features and best practices. Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience Minimum four years of experience with M365 development and administration, ideally in a higher education environment Strong understanding of Microsoft 365 suite, including SharePoint, Teams, and Office applications Possesses knowledge of related technologies such as SQL server, MS Windows Server, Azure, Microsoft 365, and Active Directory Proven experience with Power Platform, including PowerApps, Power Automate, and Power BI Demonstrated development experience, with the ability to do custom development for M365 products Experience in working in an Agile environment Strong communications skills (both oral and written) to communicate effectively with both highly-technical and non-technical users Strong interpersonal to effectively work with a wide range of faculty, staff, and students Ability to work well as a team member in multi-professional environment and as an individual contributor Assets (Nonessential): Work experience in a university, government, or healthcare setting Certifications such as Microsoft 365 Fundamentals, Microsoft Certified Solutions Associate (MCSA), Microsoft Certified Solutions Expert (MCSE), and Microsoft Certified Solutions Developer (MCSD), or Microsoft Certified: Information Protection Administrator To be successful in this role you will be: Adaptable Communicator Multi-tasker Organized Problem solver Resourceful Team player Closing Date: 10/30/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 12 -- $84,564 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $108,145. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Information Technology (IT) Divisional HR Office Email: medhr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: System Administrator, Information Security, Rehabilitation, Sharepoint, Developer, Technology, Healthcare Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Financial-&-Administrative-Coordinator-ON/606927617/": {"title": "Financial & Administrative Coordinator", "description": "Financial & Administrative Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Financial & Administrative Coordinator Date Posted: 10/09/2026 Req ID: 50512 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Department of Molecular Genetics Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00053750 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Home to over 40 departments and institutes, the University of Toronto's Temerty Faculty of Medicine lies at the heart of the Toronto Academic Health Science Network and is a global leader in ground-breaking research and education, spanning clinical medicine, basic science and the rehabilitation sciences sectors. Your opportunity: The Department of Molecular Genetics holds a leadership position in Canada and internationally as a premier venue for biomedical and life sciences research and education. We have over 100 faculty members. Our dynamic community of over 350 graduate students is engaged in M.Sc. and Ph.D. Program in Molecular Genetics. We offer a professional M.Sc. in Genetic Counseling as well as M.H.Sc. in Medical Genomics. Furthermore, the department provides a rigorous undergraduate specialist and major in Molecular Genetics and Microbiology. Our faculty, fellows, and students are highly acclaimed for pioneering phenomenal advances in some of the most exciting areas of modern science with a profound impact on human health. As Financial & Administrative Coordinator, you will work as part of a dynamic team to support the financial and business operations of our department. You will be responsible for processing financial and payroll transactions, analyzing discrepancies and preparing financial reports to help advance our research goals and objectives. You will additionally support space planning and facilities management including, supporting logistical details for office/lab renovations. Your extensive financial background combined with your solid organizational, analytical and critical thinking skills will be key to your success in this role. Your responsibilities will include: Monitoring multiple budgets to ensure expenditures remain within budgeted allocations Identifying and analyzing data discrepancies and taking necessary actions to correct errors Processing financial and payroll transactions Monitoring, recording, reconciling and/or reporting on funding accounts for grants and contracts Distributing incoming and outgoing mail and deliveries Booking rooms and arranging catering Determining logistical details required for office/lab renovations and moves including applying established standards to control the distribution of access to designated University spaces Troubleshooting routine equipment repairs and maintaining an inventory of furniture and equipment Essential Qualifications: Advanced College Diploma (3 years) or acceptable combination of equivalent experience Minimum three years' related finance experience preferably in a university administrative setting Demonstrated experience processing high volumes of financial and payroll transactions in a fast-paced environment and balancing multiple, time-sensitive deliverables Experience monitoring, recording, reconciling and reporting on funding accounts for grants and contracts Experience forecasting and monitoring budgets Experience preparing financial reports and spreadsheets and identifying discrepancies Experience working with accounting programs and applying accounting principles is essential Experience supporting office/lab moves and renovations and troubleshooting equipment repairs Advanced proficiency with MS Office Suite, particularly MS Excel and proficiency with SAP systems, including Financial Information System (FIS), Human Resources Information System (HRIS), and Research Information System (RIS), or similar systems Well-developed interpersonal skills and excellent communication skills (written and oral) Strong numerical, accounting and analytical skills Ability to work in a high volume environment that requires multi-tasking on varied duties and to prioritize effectively and work under pressure Ability to explain detailed grant funding processes and provide recommendations/course of actions Excellent problem-solving ability, organizational and planning skills; and ability to work independently and as a part of a team Professionalism, accuracy, attention to detail, flexibility, tact, and ability to maintain confidentiality Ability to interpret and apply guidelines and procedures using independent judgement and analysis Ability to anticipate demands/pressures of assignments and adapt accordingly to meet critical deadlines Demonstrated initiative and resourcefulness To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Diligent Intuitive Meticulous Self-confident Closing Date: 10/21/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 10 -- $75,004 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $95,915. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Divisional HR Office Email: medhr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Payroll, Genetics, Microbiology, ERP, Finance, Research, Science, Technology Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Mississauga-Junior-Programmer-and-Digital-Designer-ON/606907717/": {"title": "Junior Programmer and Digital Designer Job Details", "description": "Junior Programmer and Digital Designer Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Junior Programmer and Digital Designer Date Posted: 10/13/2026 Req ID: 50508 Faculty/Division: UofT Mississauga Department: UTM: Institute for Management & Innovation Campus: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Position Number: 00053415 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: U of T Mississauga\u2014the second largest campus of Canada\u2019s top-ranked university and the only research university in Ontario\u2019s booming Peel Region\u2014is one of the world\u2019s great catalysts of human potential. Our employee community hums with the energy of 3,400 faculty, librarians and staff, who power our campus with curiosity, connection and care. We work together to spark life-changing research and innovation, make an indelible mark on the world by building equitable cities and societies, enable healthy lives, create a sustainable future and ignite entrepreneurship. Above all, we prioritize student success, and seek to give our 16,500 students the lift of a lifetime through learning and discovery. We love to open opportunities available nowhere else for our community to achieve their ambitions and make their unique contributions to Canada and the world. This work all comes together on a spectacularly green campus, alongside the Missinihe-ziibi (Trusting Creek or Credit River), where we seek to honour truth, reciprocity and reconciliation on the traditional land of the Huron-Wendat, Seneca and the Mississaugas of the Credit First Nation. We\u2019re thrilled to welcome those who want to learn more about us and to be part of what we do. Your opportunity: ICUBE is part of the Institute for Management & Innovation and is the home of Social Entrepreneurship and early-stage start-ups at the University of Toronto, providing expert support, resources and access to opportunities for entrepreneurial students and community members across all industries. ICUBE is looking for a creative Student Lead for the ICUBE Studio with a background in software development and experience working with start-up ventures. The ICUBE Studio intends to serve the prototyping and design needs of the ICUBE and other University of Toronto Entrepreneurship start-ups, while also providing UTM students with a professional work-integrated learning (WIL) experience while they are still enrolled in school. The successful candidate should have experience in project management and entrepreneurship, either by creating a new product or company or by having worked with a start-up venture. Your responsibilities will include: Analyzing user needs and business processes to create programming solutions Providing detailed analysis and recommendations on the suitability of major new technology and software systems Advising on best practices and strategies to maximize digital communication initiatives Training staff and faculty on the use of digital technologies Designing graphic elements for digital and online media Building and maintaining websites Troubleshooting issues uncovered by testing or user feedback Conceptualizing, organizing and executing event activities Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience Minimum three years related experience Experience with software design and development in a test-driven environment Experience with databases and object-relational mapping (ORM) frameworks (e.g. Hibernate) Experience with Illustrator, Photoshop, InDesign Experience working with WordPress and Shopify templates Experience with CRM software Demonstrated experience developing and producing a variety of graphic design and communications materials. Proficient in website development and maintenance, including knowledge of coding languages (e.g. C++, Java, JavaScript) and frameworks/systems (e.g. AngularJS, Git) Strong project management knowledge and skills Strong organizational skills, ability to multi-task and manage competing priorities Excellent communication skills, strong analytical ability and keen attention to detail Resourceful and a strong aptitude for troubleshooting Demonstrated ability to learn and innovate Demonstrated ability to work independently, as well as part of a team Assets (Nonessential): Experience with Agile development methodologies, an asset To be successful in this role you will be: Accountable Communicator Multi-tasker Organized Problem solver Team player Please note that one (1) position is available as a one-year term. Closing Date: 10/21/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 09 -- $70,633 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $90,329. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Information Technology (IT) Divisional HR Office Email: hrserv.utm@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Graphic Design, Testing, Project Manager, Sustainability, Developer, Creative, Technology, Energy Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Executive-Director%2C-Experiential-Learning-&-Professional-Development-ON/606910117/": {"title": "Executive Director, Experiential Learning & Professional Development", "description": "Executive Director, Experiential Learning & Professional Development Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Executive Director, Experiential Learning & Professional Development Date Posted: 10/08/2026 Req ID: 50495 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: ARTSC: Ofc of the Dean Campus : St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Faculty of Arts & Science is the heart of Canada\u2019s leading university and one of the most comprehensive and diverse academic divisions in the world. The strength of Arts & Science derives from our combined teaching and research excellence in the humanities, sciences and social sciences across 29 departments, seven colleges and 46 interdisciplinary centres, institutes and programs. We can only realize our mission with the dedication and excellence of engaged staff and faculty. The diversity of opportunities and perspectives within the Faculty reflect the local and global landscape and the need for curiosity, innovative thinking and collaboration. At Arts & Science, we take pride in our legacy of innovation and discovery that has changed the way we think about the world. POSITION OVERVIEW Working in coordination with the Dean, various Vice-Deans and Associate Deans (including but not limited to: Undergraduate, Graduate Education; Strategic Initiatives and Academic Planning, Research, Student Affairs, and Teaching & Learning) and reporting to the CAO, the Executive Director, Experiential Learning and Professional Development is responsible for strategic leadership in the planning, development, implementation, operation, successful management, and evaluation of the experiential learning, professional education, upskilling, and integrated academic program development in support of future-ready student outcomes for the Faculty of Arts & Science. The incumbent will oversee a team of full-time professionals who ensure that: programming focused on the Faculty of Arts and Science provides exemplary support to departments and programs in the development and delivery of programming focused on experiential learning, including undergraduate and graduate curricular experiential opportunities, research and international opportunities, and co-curricular career-engaged learning initiatives. the Faculty is a leading partner in the U of T Co-op program, leveraging the Arts & Science Internship Program (ASIP) and business and community relationships for student internships, while developing and expanding academic and departmental engagements with ASIP. the Faculty provides exemplary programming and support services to graduate students for learning, supports, and outreach aimed at promoting excellence in graduate professional development and academic success the Faculty provides flexible and future-ready programming innovations in support of the University\u2019s mission for career ready student success. The role of the Executive Director will focus on 5 critical areas: Program leadership, strategy and business development to grow and enhance experiential learning opportunities (including practica, community-engaged learning, organization-partnered projects, field placements, research and international opportunities, and co-curricular career-engaged learning) across all A&S departments and undergraduate & graduate programs, and, where appropriate, Colleges. Program leadership, strategy, and business development to grow and enhance the Arts & Science Internship Program, providing specialized professional development training and paid work-integrated learning opportunities to Arts & Science students, with a focus on preparing students for lifelong success in the labour market, and deepening relationships with local partners in the public, private and non-profit sectors. Program leadership and strategy in the development of graduate student success supports and programming. Leadership and management of growing and evolving teams, including developing optimal organizational structures which allow for coordination and alignment of activities between teams wherever possible, without duplication, and operation of growing units in relation to human resources, finance, space planning, facilities management and information technology; Serving as a senior representative of the Office of Experiential Learning and Outreach Support, the U of T Co-op Executive Committee, and the Office of Graduate Professional Development & Student Success to engage and build positive relations with community partners and employers, university partners, alumni, and current and prospective learners. The Executive Director is also responsible for developing and implementing strategies for marketing and communications related to their portfolio to attract and retain excellent students; ensure close connections between the Offices and academic departments; create a seamless integration of services with other services and education providers at UTSG, UTM and UTSC; and oversee the development of suitable experiential opportunities for students. The Executive Director promotes a team-based model of staffing whereby each member knows, respects and supports the work of their colleagues and the department as a whole. The Executive Director is responsible for overseeing the budget for the Office of Experiential Learning & Outreach Support, the Arts & Science Internship Program, and the Office of Graduate Professional Development & Student Success including revenue generation and developing evaluation measures to assess the effectiveness of the work of these offices. QUALIFICATIONS Education: Minimum post-graduate degree at a Masters level, with a PhD preferred, in an Arts and Science Discipline, with expertise designing and directing academically-linked experiential learning, programming and outreach opportunities, or related field or equivalent combination of education and experience. Education and experience should include a focus on experiential learning principles, academically-linked program planning and evaluation, resolving related issues in higher education, and leadership. Experience: A minimum of 8 years\u2019 experience of progressively senior administrative experience as a leader and manager of a mid-sized team; demonstrated experience in a role committed to excellence in meeting the needs of students, preferably in a post-secondary environment. Significant program management experience, and experience developing and executing a departmental strategic plan is required. Experience successfully leading and managing change in a complex setting that necessitates a dynamic and responsive action-oriented approach. Experience with and an understanding of the increasingly important role of employment services to students within the post-secondary setting is crucial. Extensive knowledge of educational services and public policy in the field of education in Canada and internationally. Extensive knowledge and experience implementing strategic partnerships and new business opportunities in a University setting. Must have the ability to articulate a vision and formulate action plans for the strong development of experiential learning and outreach support, and have a strong understanding of business and client development. Strong management experience in a unionized environment and managing a team with multiple areas of expertise. Demonstrated experience in transformative and innovative leadership and in successfully managing significant change initiatives. Skills: Demonstrated skills and interest in using technology in increase efficiencies. Must have strong analytical skills; experience with strategic budgeting, budget forecasting and financial analysis; adept with using critical analysis of date (including admissions, employment and survey data) to inform strategic decision-making. A creative and pragmatic, strategic thinker with strong implementation skills; proven marketing and networking talents. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in leading a diverse, professional team to achieve results and meet multiple stakeholder needs. Other: Must have high initiative, strong organizational and problem-solving skills, and be a strong leader who is nimble and able to embrace and manage change. Must be politically astute with the ability to undertake sensitive discussions and advocate for the portfolio. Highly developed skills in oral and written communication, including effective presentation skills for small and large audiences. Demonstrated negotiation and conflict resolution abilities are required. Consummate professional with an ability to exercise sound judgment, tact and diplomacy under stressful circumstances. Closing Date: 10/30/2026,11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 7 -- Hiring Zone: $151,028 - $176,200 -- Broadband Salary Range: $151,028 - $251,713 Job Category: Student Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Public Policy, Training, Program Manager, Intern, Learning, Government, Education, Management, Entry Level, Human Resources Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Teaching-Labs-Coordinator-ON/606908817/": {"title": "Teaching Labs Coordinator", "description": "Teaching Labs Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Teaching Labs Coordinator Date Posted: 10/09/2026 Req ID: 50496 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Division of Teaching Labs Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00059447 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Home to over 40 departments and institutes, the University of Toronto's Temerty Faculty of Medicine lies at the heart of the Toronto Academic Health Science Network and is a global leader in ground-breaking research and education, spanning clinical medicine, basic science and the rehabilitation sciences sectors. Your opportunity: The Division of Teaching Labs (DTL) supports the delivery of laboratory courses and practicals by providing laboratory infrastructure, experimental needs, and technical expertise to departments within the Temerty Faculty of Medicine. DTL focuses on providing sustainable, effective, and responsive service to the departments, and ensuring a positive, productive, and safe learning and work environment. We advance youth STEM initiatives through collaborative and in-house outreach and educational programming. As Teaching Labs Coordinator, you will play a key role in supporting teaching activities by coordinating laboratory operations, program administration, and health and safety compliance. You will assist with preparing and maintaining lab environments, supporting experimental work, and providing hands-on guidance to students and staff. You\u2019ll also bring strong organizational skills and attention to detail to administrative tasks, process improvements, and communications, including supporting the development and maintenance of standard operating procedures and safety documentation, helping to ensure the labs operate safely, efficiently, and effectively. Your responsibilities will include: Coordinating laboratory operations and experimental support, including preparing materials and equipment, assisting with experiments, modifying processes, reviewing procedures for feasibility and safety, and ensuring adherence to established procedures and standards Maintaining laboratory facilities, equipment, and inventory, including troubleshooting issues, restocking supplies, and ensuring proper cleaning, sterilization, and waste handling practices Supporting program administration and communications, including responding to enquiries, maintaining records and digital platforms, tracking student enrollment, and coordinating outreach and promotional activities Ensuring health, safety, and regulatory compliance, including delivering safety training, conducting inspections, monitoring adherence to standards, supporting biosafety documentation and permit requirements, and supporting risk assessments and mitigation planning Providing training, coordination, and guidance to staff and students, including recruiting and scheduling casual staff, delivering job-related training, and serving as a technical resource on lab procedures and equipment Essential Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s Degree or an acceptable combination of equivalent experience, preferably in biological science Minimum three (3) years of experience supporting teaching lab operations in a university environment Demonstrated experience setting up laboratory equipment and troubleshooting routine issues Demonstrated experience preparing routine samples for experiments Experience supporting experimental procedures and modifying lab processes, including reviewing processes for safety and feasibility in a teaching lab environment Experience providing administrative support and acting as a first point of contact Experience maintaining websites, databases, and digital platforms while supporting communications initiatives Experience coordinating staff, including recruitment, scheduling, and training Experience tracking and monitoring student registration or program participation Experience conducting lab inspections and delivering safety training Experience delivering training on experimental theory and protocols Experience developing, maintaining, or applying standard operating procedures and safety documentation Knowledge of health and safety regulations, laboratory standards, and compliance practices Proven ability to analyze workflows and implement process improvements Ability to orient students and staff to laboratory procedures and safe work practices Advanced proficiency with Office 365 Excellent written and verbal communication skills Highly organized with meticulous attention to detail Ability to prioritize tasks, manage competing deadlines, and work effectively in a fast-paced environment Demonstrated manual dexterity and precision in handling laboratory equipment To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Multi-tasker Organized Problem solver Team player Closing Date: 10/20/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 11 -- $79,640 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $101,845. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Research Administration & Teaching Divisional HR Office Email: medhr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Compliance, Laboratory, Teacher, Law, Rehabilitation, Legal, Science, Education, Healthcare Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Manager%2C-ISI-Office-&-Programs-ON/606911417/": {"title": "Manager, ISI Office & Programs Job Details", "description": "Manager, ISI Office & Programs Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Manager, ISI Office & Programs Date Posted: 10/09/2026 Req ID: 50511 Faculty/Division: VP - Research Department: Institutional Strategic Initiatives Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: No Description: About us The Vice-President, Research & Innovation (VPRI) portfolio supports the University of Toronto as a top public research university in the world. Our mission is to create the most supportive environment possible so that our researchers, innovators and learners can do what they do best \u2014 advance understanding and apply new knowledge. Our work supports, fosters and promotes the\u00a0research and innovation culture and activities of our faculty, staff and students, along with our\u00a0partner hospitals, funding sponsors, and partners in the public and private sector. The Institutional Strategic Initiatives (ISI) portfolio is dedicated to improving the university's capacity to seed, develop, and sustain large, cross-divisional, interdisciplinary, excellence-driven research initiatives. Working with university-wide and divisional units, the ISI portfolio provides support in areas such as research leadership, external partnerships, budget and finance, human resources, and proposal development. Your opportunity Reporting to the Executive Director, Strategic Initiatives, the Manager, ISI Office & Programs provides operational and program leadership for the ISI portfolio. Working through and alongside a team of staff, the Manager builds the systems, processes, tools and practices that enable a portfolio of complex interdisciplinary research initiatives to operate effectively, share knowledge and meet institutional requirements. This managerial role spans program and competition delivery, portfolio tracking and reporting, strategic communications, committee and governance support, digital and website oversight, workshops and communities of practice, and the development of operational guidance and agreements. The Manager serves as a key advisor to the Executive Director, translates strategic priorities into practical operational plans, and identifies opportunities to improve service, coordination, and consistency across the portfolio. The Manager oversees the day-to-day administrative and operational activities of the ISI Office, including workflow management, prioritization and troubleshooting, and develops and maintains the operational procedures, SOPs, guidance documents, templates and other tools that support this work. The Manager also leads the development and rollout of ISI programs and funding competitions, and establishes and maintains the portfolio trackers, dashboards and reporting processes used to collate reports and monitor key outcomes. The Manager drafts and negotiates agreements, and oversees the document and information management systems and practices that keep the portfolio\u2019s records and data organized and accessible In support of the portfolio\u2019s communications and governance needs, the Manager prepares and oversees reports, proposals, slide decks, memos and other communications, and provides strategic oversight of ISI websites and digital platforms. The Manager also supports ISI committees and governance processes \u2014 including meeting materials, coordination and follow-up \u2014 and plans and oversees workshops, communities of practice and other engagement activities. Essential Qualifications: (MINIMUM) Education: Post graduate degree (Master's or PhD) or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience: At least 5 years of relevant experience in strategic, financial, administrative and operational leadership, project management and business administration in a large research university or equivalent complex organization. Demonstrated experience leading cross-functional teams and managing a complex portfolio of programs and projects involving multiple stakeholders and competing priorities. Experience managing complex relationships with senior administrators, funders, partners and other stakeholders, preferably in a university environment or other large complex organization. Experience developing and implementing programs, funding competitions or other structured institutional processes. Experience developing operational procedures, SOPs, guidance documents, templates and process improvements. Experience developing portfolio tracking, reporting and evaluation approaches, including trackers or dashboards and qualitative and quantitative information. Experience overseeing digital platforms and information-management systems such as SharePoint or similar tools, as well as websites and digital communications. Experience preparing complex written and presentation materials for varied audiences, including reports, external funding proposals, presentations, briefing materials, memos and speaking notes. Experience supporting committees and governance processes, and planning workshops, meetings, communities of practice or training activities. Experience drafting, negotiating or administering agreements and contracts, and managing operational financial activities, procurement and vendor relationships. Experience supervising staff, including performance management and fostering an inclusive team environment; experience managing in a unionized environment. Skills: Superior written and verbal communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to synthesize complex information and communicate effectively. Advanced project and program management skills. Strong strategic thinking, judgement and creative problem-solving skills. Strong program development and evaluation skills. Strong organizational governance and committee-management skills, including an understanding of decision-making processes, reporting requirements and the preparation of materials for senior-level review and discussion. Strong research, writing, editing and presentation skills. Strong systems and information-management skills, including oversight of collaborative platforms, internal databases and reporting tools, with the ability to support data integrity, appropriate access, version control and alignment with institutional standards. Proficiency with digital tools and platforms such as Microsoft 365, SharePoint, website content-management systems and data analytics or visualization tools. Excellent ability to manage budgets, procurement processes, programs and vendor relationships. Demonstrated people leadership skills, including the ability to set expectations, develop staff, delegate effectively and foster a collaborative and accountable team environment. Other: High degree of collegiality; ability to work independently, as a team member, and across divisions and institutions. Ability to exercise tact, discretion, superior judgement and diplomacy, and to maintain confidentiality. Superior ability to foster a collaborative environment within the office and the broader community. Ability to exercise independent decision-making and sound judgement in a complex institutional environment. Ability to prioritize tasks and responsibilities, manage competing deadlines and work effectively under pressure. Strong attention to detail and the ability to source, assimilate and interpret significant amounts of information accurately and efficiently. Knowledge of organizational governance, policy development and decision-making processes within complex institutions. Familiarity with the university and research environment is essential. Closing Date: 10/21/2026,11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 4 -- Hiring Zone: $110,973 - $129,471 -- Broadband Salary Range: $110,973 - $184,957 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Project Manager, Performance Management, Program Manager, Procurement, Developer, Technology, Human Resources, Management, Operations Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Manager%2C-Summer-Accommodations-%28Term%29-ON/606907017/": {"title": "Manager, Summer Accommodations (Term) Job Details", "description": "Manager, Summer Accommodations (Term) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Manager, Summer Accommodations (Term) Date Posted: 10/09/2026 Req ID: 50509 Faculty/Division: VP-Facilities & Real Estate Department: S&E Student Residences Campus : St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: NOTE: Please note this is a one (1) year term position. The Student Residences team at Spaces & Experiences (S&E) oversees and operates undergraduate and graduate student housing for more than 2,200 students on the St. George campus. Our residences include Chestnut Residence, Oak House, Graduate House, and Knox Residence. We strive to offer a supportive and dynamic living-learning environment for students that fosters academic success, personal growth, and a strong sense of belonging. The Summer Accommodations portfolio is a significant, multi-property hospitality operation providing short-term stays at Chestnut Residence, Oak House, and Knox Residence between May and August each year. Operating under the \u201cStay at U of T\u201d brand, the portfolio delivers more than 40,000 room nights each summer to a diverse range of market segments including group, business, and leisure travelers. In addition to generating significant ancillary revenue, the operation provides an important opportunity to showcase the University\u2019s residences and deliver a high-quality guest experience to visitors from Canada and around the world. Reporting to the Dean of Residence & Director of Student Life, the Manager, Summer Accommodations provides primary leadership for the portfolio and is responsible for the overall planning, business development, and operations of the summer accommodations business. The Manager stewards the \u201cStay at U of T\u201d brand and contributes to the strategic direction of the portfolio, identifying opportunities to strengthen its market position, grow revenues, enhance the guest experience, and continuously improve the operation. The role is responsible for developing the annual operating budget, including revenue targets and related expenditures. The Manager leads the Summer Accommodations team and coordinates the many operational partners required to deliver a successful guest stay, including front desk, housekeeping, building operations, food services, and other stakeholders. The role oversees sales and business development across key market segments, develops and manages contracts for groups and other short-term stays, and monitors occupancy, revenue, and operational performance. The Manager also plays a visible role in the guest experience, building relationships with key clients and responding to escalated guest concerns and service issues to ensure that the portfolio consistently delivers on the standards and reputation of the \u201cStay at U of T\u201d brand. The Manager must be available to consult on or attend emergencies outside of normal office hours. Essential Qualifications: EDUCATION: Bachelor\u2019s degree in hospitality management, business administration, or other relevant discipline, or a similar combination of relevant education and experience. Graduate degree (i.e., MBA) considered an asset. EXPERIENCE: Seven (7) or more years of progressive experience in hotel, hospitality, short-term accommodations, conference services, or a comparable guest-service environment, including experience in a management or supervisory capacity. Demonstrated experience overseeing a hospitality or accommodations operation, including responsibility for staffing, service delivery, operational planning, and financial performance. Experience developing, managing, and monitoring operating budgets, revenues, expenses, and financial controls, with the ability to use financial and operational data to support business decisions. Experience in sales and business development within the hospitality or accommodations sector, including managing market segments, developing client relationships, and negotiating and administering group contracts. Experience managing guest relations and resolving escalated complaints and service issues promptly, effectively, and with sound judgment. Demonstrated experience coordinating complex, cross-functional operations and multiple internal and external stakeholders to deliver a seamless, high-quality guest experience. Experience using Opera Cloud or other property management systems, channel management platforms, and related hospitality technology to support reservations, inventory, occupancy, revenue, and guest services. Experience in a university, college, or student residence environment would be considered an asset. SKILLS: Strong operational and organizational skills, with the ability to translate strategic priorities into effective business plans, operating plans, service standards, and day-to-day practices. Strong business acumen, with the ability to identify revenue opportunities, understand market trends, monitor occupancy and revenue performance, and balance commercial objectives with guest experience and operational requirements. Demonstrated ability to lead, coach, and manage a team, fostering a positive, collaborative, and service-oriented work environment. Strong analytical skills, with the ability to gather, interpret, and synthesize operational, financial, sales, and guest experience data and use insights to inform decision-making and improve performance. Ability to evaluate the effectiveness of programs, services, and operational practices and implement improvements to enhance efficiency, revenue performance, and overall guest experience. Excellent interpersonal and relationship-management skills, with the ability to build productive relationships with internal and external partners and coordinate effectively across multiple operational functions. Strong customer service, judgment, and conflict-resolution skills, with a commitment to creating a welcoming, inclusive, and high-quality experience for all guests. Strong contract development and negotiation skills, with the ability to establish and manage agreements for group bookings and other short-term stays. Proactive and adaptable approach to identifying opportunities, responding to changing market conditions, and introducing new approaches to improve the competitiveness and effectiveness of the operation. Strong technology fluency and demonstrated ability to lead the effective use and configuration of hospitality technology to support business processes, optimize operational workflows, maintain data integrity, and enhance the guest experience. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with guests, clients, staff, senior leaders, and operational partners. Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, seasonal environment, managing competing priorities, deadlines, and operational issues with sound judgment and composure. Strong financial management skills, including the ability to implement and maintain appropriate financial controls, monitor performance against budget, and support accurate revenue and expense reporting. Closing Date: 10/23/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Ancillary Operations Schedule: Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 3 -- Hiring Zone: $97,336 - $113,558 -- Broadband Salary Range: $97,336 - $162,224 Job Category: Hospitality Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Front Desk, Relationship Manager, Housekeeping, MBA, Administrative, Customer Service, Hospitality, Management, Healthcare Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Area-Manager-ON/605420817/": {"title": "Area Manager Job Details", "description": "Area Manager Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Area Manager Date Posted: 10/14/2026 Req ID: 49915 Faculty/Division: Asst VP - Operations & Services Department: F.&S. Bldgs & Grounds -04 Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Area Manager, Caretaking is responsible for providing timely, efficient and effective caretaking services to assigned shifts of the St. George campus. Through supervisory of direct reports, oversees the provision of caretaking services (including but not limited to cleaning activities, response to campus community needs and customer concerns, service delivery schedules, waste and recycling collection and employee relations) on assigned shifts on a 24/7 basis. Responsible for interviewing, hiring and training new recruits at the hourly paid and supervisory staff levels, enforcing/maintaining health and safety standards within the department, responding to campus community needs/customer concerns, ensuring service delivery schedules, handling labour relations and attendance awareness issues, and operating within budget guidelines as directed, participate in the Caretaking Quality Assurance Program to support consistent service standards and performance. The responsibilites include but not limited to: Maintains all service schedules for assigned buildings. In consultation with supervisors, deploys available staff to effectively deliver core services and meet operational requirements. Makes appropriate adjustments to schedule in order to accommodate both planned and unplanned absences, replacements of employees on LTD and other long term leaves, etc. Resolves technical problems and staff-related issues that arise during department/project work on a timely basis, to ensure work can be completed with minimal delay. Keeps current on new procedures and work methods. Prepares reports on new methodology. Integrates new methods into current work design, ensuring health, safety and ergonomic concerns are addressed. Responsible for ensuring that workplace health and safety standards are maintained. Enforces WHMIS and OHSA regulations. Active member of Joint Health & Safety Committee. Review individual timesheets for all employees prepared by Supervisors. Approves timesheet input and submits bi-weekly to Payroll Services (PS) for processing. This process includes\u00a0submission of changes to previous pay resulting from unplanned events affecting pay (e.g. sick without pay, leave of absence without pay, etc.). Tracks and monitors supply purchases budget of approximately $300K - $400K per year. Monitors salary-related expenditures for indirect reports - approximately $2.5M - $4.0M per year. Makes recommendations to the Manager for budget reassignments throughout the year. In service delivery system (SAP), check status of work tickets, arrange requests with supervisors and service partners. Track and review financial records. Maintains both Key and Fob access control for in-house and contracted sites. Manages staff to ensure work tasks are completed on schedule and standards and policies are followed. Resolves informal complaints from unionized staff, in consultation with Human Resources and\u00a0Labour Relations. Qualifications Required: Education : High school graduation plus professional training required. Knowledge of hazardous chemicals related to cleaning, WHMIS regulations, Ontario Health & Safety Act. College diploma or undergraduate degree is considered an asset. Experience: Minimum of 5 years\u2019 experience managing a large, unionized workforce, preferably in a facility management setting (i.e. institutional caretaking operations and waste/recycling collection) or not-for-profit, or public service organization with responsibility for a budget of not less than $2M. Skills: Excellent organizational skills, including a demonstrated ability to work effectively under pressure of multiple demands, strict deadlines and frequently changing priorities. Good oral and written communication skills, including the ability to communicate effectively with a diverse workforce. Ability to motivate staff and demonstrate effective leadership. Good presentation skills preferred. Excellent computer skills including Microsoft Office Suite \u2013 Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint. Other: Ability to manage conflicting priorities and deadlines. Ability to create charts, graphs and reports from several software programs. Ability to analyze information and create comparable for work loading job assignments. Mathematical aptitude. Please Note: The regular hours of work will be Monday to Friday, from 4:00 p.m. to 12:00 a.m. Occasional day-shift work will be required to support training and development opportunities, attend meetings, and collaborate with the day team as needed. Closing Date: 10/28/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 2 -- Hiring Zone: $86,902 - $101,385 -- Broadband Salary Range: $86,902 - $144,835 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Manager, Quality Assurance, Payroll, QA, Employee Relations, Management, Technology, Finance, Quality, Human Resources Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Operating-Engineer-B-%283rd-Class%29-ON/604608217/": {"title": "Operating Engineer B (3rd Class) Job Details", "description": "Operating Engineer B (3rd Class) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Operating Engineer B (3rd Class) Date Posted: 10/16/2026 Req ID: 49554 Faculty/Division: Asst VP - Operations & Services Department: F.&S. Utilities -06 Campus : St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Under the direction of the Manager, Mechanical Operations and Maintenance and/or leadership of the Lead Hand Engineer, the incumbent is responsible for the operation and maintenance in the building(s) assigned where a Third (3rd) Class Operating Engineer Certificate is required either by law or due to the complexity of the operation and/or critical services provided for building environment and Faculty. \u00a0The engineer is responsible for the safe and economical operation and maintenance of all mechanical and associated equipment and services in their area of responsibility. Typical Duties: The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required and the extent of responsibility involved in this job; they in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated: regular rounds to check mechanical equipment and perform needed mechanical service; ensures continuous efficiency of all mechanical equipment services and faculty equipment; provides running maintenance by checking lube levels of compressors and adjustments to all equipment and controls serving areas such as computer rooms, laboratories, classrooms, offices, special faculty cold rooms/ warm rooms, etc.; answers and reacts promptly to all trouble calls or alarms from buildings, as well as from adjacent nearby buildings; reviews computer printouts and alarms and takes appropriate action; co-ordinates and/or assists outside contractors and University of Toronto Trades Services when work is performed during shift; recommends major repairs; housekeeping: \u00a0painting, sweeping floors, cleaning piping, boilers and equipment; responds to off duty calls to correct emergency situations and problems; and maintains daily log sheets on operating equipment and records all important events that occur during shift and communicates with relief shift engineer on event issues. Minimum Requirements: Education: High School graduate or equivalent combination of education and experience plus a Third (3rd) Class Operating Engineer Certification valid in the Province of Ontario. Experience: Minimum of one (1) year of experience as an operating engineer. Must have a good working knowledge of the operation and maintenance of mechanical equipment, including refrigeration, heating (e.g. boilers) and air handling systems, and ability to comprehend and apply environmental control principles. Must have: basic electrical knowledge and trouble-shooting skills, basic proficiency in standard office computer applications (e.g. Microsoft Word, Excel, Windows OS) and familiarity with computerized Building Automation Systems or other computerized control systems. Other: Must have: good diagnostic and record keeping skills, the ability to communicate effectively (both orally and written), strong customer service skills and the ability to work collaboratively with others. Building Environmental Systems Certificate an asset. Shift Details: Regular 8 hour shifts, 40 hours per week. Must be available day, afternoon and night shifts, including weekends and holidays NOTE : We are posting the position for 2 vacancies. This is a replacement position. Closing Date: 11/06/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: Unifor FT L2003 Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: $43.13/hr Job Category: Engineering / Technical Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Housekeeping, HVAC, Electrical, Engineer, Healthcare, Hospitality, Engineering, Operations Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Administrative-Coordinator%2C-Academic-Reviews-ON/607344817/": {"title": "Administrative Coordinator, Academic Reviews", "description": "Administrative Coordinator, Academic Reviews Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Administrative Coordinator, Academic Reviews Date Posted: 10/26/2026 Req ID: 50747 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Vice Dean, Strategy & Governance Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00060162 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Home to over 40 departments and institutes, the University of Toronto's Temerty Faculty of Medicine lies at the heart of the Toronto Academic Health Science Network and is a global leader in ground-breaking research and education, spanning clinical medicine, basic science and the rehabilitation sciences sectors. Your opportunity: As Administrative Coordinator, Academic Reviews, you will be responsible for coordinating cyclical reviews for units and programs across the faculty and serving as a key administrative support for the Associate Dean, Faculty and Academic Life and their broader portfolio. Working closely with the Manager, Governance and Academic Reviews, you will administer end-to-end academic review cycles, including liaising between departments and stakeholders, maintaining senior staff calendars, coordinating program assessment schedules and event logistics for both in-person and virtual formats. Your exemplary professionalim, and superior organizational and communication skills, will enable you to act as a trusted liaison between our leadership team and external partners, strengthening our governance frameworks for a leading medical school. Your responsibilities will include: Coordinating project timelines and milestones by developing task schedules in alignment with project goals Drafting, editing, and formatting correspondence, reports, and presentations ensuring high standards through careful proofreading and fact-checking Providing committee support, scheduling calendars and coordinating end-to-end travel logistics, including preparing itineraries, booking flights and accommodations Gathering and verifying documentation required for accreditation and program reviews to ensure full compliance with requirements Determining logistical details and activities for events and programming Analyzing processes and recommending changes for more efficient coordination of operations Essential Qualifications: Advanced College Diploma (3 years) or acceptable combination of equivalent experience Minimum five years related administrative experience, preferably in a University or hospital environment Experience supporting and coordinating accreditation and/or academic program reviews Demonstrated experience dealing with highly sensitive and confidential matters and providing administrative support to senior committees and leadership, including calendar management Experience coordinating multiple projects and time-sensitive priorities Experience serving as the first point of contact, screening enquiries, proactively coordinating conflicting schedules and coordinating frequent travel arrangements Experience independently drafting correspondence, reports and presentations, including on the behalf of senior leadership Experience reviewing existing processes and making recommendations for improvement and implementation Experience or exposure to implementing AI tools, automation, or emerging technologies to streamline administrative workflows and increase operational efficiency Advanced proficiency with M365, including experience with Sharepoint and MS Planner Professional demeanor with a strong customer service orientation and effective interpersonal skills Strong oral and written communication skills, superior attention to detail and the ability to concisely summarize information Superior organizational skills and the ability to deal effectively with multiple priorities and projects with conflicting deadlines Ability to adjust to changing priorities and interruptions and the ability to anticipate the needs of senior leadership nd flag questions or opportunities before issues arise Demonstrated ability to work independently, show initiative and exercise diplomacy and good judgment, and also the ability to work cooperatively and be an effective team member Proven effectiveness in relating to all levels of faculty, staff, learners and individuals external to the University Ability to maintain strict confidentiality Assets (Nonessential): Knowledge of the Temerty Faculty of Medicine, its hospital affiliations and partners Procificency with Microsoft Power Platform To be successful inthis role you will be: Articulate Communicator Diplomatic Organized Procedural Tactful Closing Date: 11/09/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 10 -- $75,004 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $95,915. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Divisional HR Office Email: medhr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Copy Editor, Proofreading, Rehabilitation, Administrative Assistant, Equity, Creative, Healthcare, Administrative, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Professor-Mechanical-Engineering-ON/607346417/": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "Assistant Professor - Mechanical Engineering Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant Professor - Mechanical Engineering Date Posted: 10/26/2026 Closing Date: 01/11/2027, 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50202 Job Category: Faculty - Tenure Stream (continuing) Faculty/Division: Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering Department: Department of Mechanical and Industrial Engineering Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes POSITION DESCRIPTION The Department of Mechanical & Industrial Engineering in the Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering at the University of Toronto invites applications for up to four full-time tenure stream positions in Mechanical Engineering. The appointments will be at the rank of Assistant Professor, with an anticipated start date as early as July 1, 2027. Broad areas of interest include, but are not limited, to computational and experimental fluid mechanics and heat transfer, solid mechanics, sustainable energy, robotics and automation, biomechanics and biomaterials, and the application of artificial intelligence and machine learning to all of the aforementioned. REQUIREMENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS Candidates must have earned a PhD degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related area by the time of appointment, or shortly thereafter, with a demonstrated record of excellence in research and teaching. We seek candidates whose research and teaching interests complement and enhance our existing departmental strengths . Registration as a Professional Engineer, or eligibility for registration, is preferred. Candidates must provide evidence of research excellence which can be demonstrated by a record of publications in top-ranked and field relevant journals or forthcoming publications meeting high international standards, the submitted research statement, presentations at significant conferences, awards and accolades, and strong endorsements from referees. Evidence of excellence in teaching will be provided through teaching accomplishments, the teaching dossier (with required materials outlined below) submitted as part of the application, as well as strong letters of reference. RESPONSIBILITIES The successful candidate will be expected to pursue innovative and independent research, and to establish an outstanding, competitive, and externally funded research program. In addition, the successful candidate will be assigned a teaching and service load. HIRING SALARY RANGE The expected salary range is CAD $140k-170k per annum, depending on experience. Negotiations beyond this salary range will be considered for exceptionally qualified candidates. ABOUT US Established in 1827, and located in vibrant downtown Toronto, the University of Toronto is Canada's largest university, recognized as a global leader in research and teaching. UofT's distinguished faculty, institutional record of groundbreaking scholarship and wealth of innovative academic opportunities attract outstanding students and academics from around the world. The Department of Mechanical & Industrial Engineering at the University of Toronto is home to the top mechanical and industrial engineering programs in Canada. We aim to foster a collegial world-class environment that excels in research, teaching and learning. APPLICATION PROCESS All applications materials, including recent reference letters, must be received by January 11, 2027. All qualified candidates are invited to apply online by clicking the link below. \u00a0Your CV and cover letter should be uploaded into the dedicated fields. Please combine additional application materials into one or two files in PDF/MSWord format. Applicants must submit the following materials: a cover letter; a current curriculum vitae; a research statement outlining current and future research interests; one recent publication; a teaching dossier which includes a teaching statement, sample course materials, and teaching evaluations if available; and the name and contact information of three references. The University of Toronto\u2019s recruiting tool will automatically solicit and collect letters of reference from each referee within 48 hours of an application being submitted. Applicants remain responsible for ensuring that referees submit recent letters (on letterhead, dated and signed) by the closing date. Submission guidelines and details on the automatic reference letter collection, including timelines, are available in the candidate FAQ . If you have any questions about this position, please contact Professor Markus Bussmann at mie.chair@utoronto.ca . All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Indigenous Substantiation The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for those candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information regarding the University's Indigenous Substantiation Process, please refer to: Indigenous Substantiation Website . Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Thermal Engineering, Industrial Engineer, Mechanical Engineer, Engineer, Engineering, Research Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Faculty Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Associate-ProfessorProfessor-Mechanical-Engineering-ON/607346517/": {"title": "Associate Professor/Professor", "description": "Associate Professor/Professor - Mechanical Engineering Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Associate Professor/Professor - Mechanical Engineering Date Posted: 10/26/2026 Closing Date: 01/11/2027, 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50203 Job Category: Faculty - Tenure Stream (continuing) Faculty/Division: Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering Department: Department of Mechanical and Industrial Engineering Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes POSITION DESCRIPTION The Department of Mechanical & Industrial Engineering in the Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering at the University of Toronto invites applications for up to four full-time tenure stream positions in Mechanical Engineering. The appointment will be at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor, with an anticipated start date as early as July 1, 2027. Broad areas of interest include, but are not limited to, computational and experimental fluid mechanics and heat transfer, solid mechanics, sustainable energy, robotics and automation, biomechanics and biomaterials, and the application of artificial intelligence and machine learning to all of the aforementioned. REQUIREMENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS Candidates must have earned a PhD degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related area, with a clearly demonstrated record of excellence in research and teaching. We seek candidates whose research and teaching interests complement and enhance our existing departmental strengths . Registration as a Professional Engineer, or eligibility for registration, is preferred. Candidates must provide evidence of research excellence which can be demonstrated by a record of sustained high-impact contributions and publications in top-ranked and field-relevant journals, the submitted research statement, presentations at significant conferences, awards and accolades, and other noteworthy activities that contribute to the visibility and prominence of the discipline, as well as strong endorsements from referees. Evidence of excellence in teaching will be provided through teaching accomplishments, the teaching dossier submitted as part of the application (with required materials outlined below), as well as strong letters of reference. RESPONSIBILITIES Candidates will have an established international reputation and will be expected to sustain and lead innovative and independent research, and to maintain an outstanding, competitive, and externally funded research program. In addition, the successful candidate will be assigned a teaching and service load. HIRING SALARY RANGE The rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The upper end of the salary range for this position exceeds $200,000 CAD per annum. Negotiations beyond this salary range will be considered for exceptionally qualified candidates. ABOUT US Established in 1827, and located in vibrant downtown Toronto, the University of Toronto is Canada's largest university, recognized as a global leader in research and teaching. U of T's distinguished faculty, institutional record of groundbreaking scholarship and wealth of innovative academic opportunities attract outstanding students and academics from around the world. The Department of Mechanical & Industrial Engineering at the University of Toronto is home to the top mechanical and industrial engineering programs in Canada. We aim to foster a collegial world-class environment that excels in research, teaching and learning. APPLICATION PROCESS All application materials, including recent reference letters must be received by January 11, 2027. All qualified candidates are invited to apply online by clicking the link below. Your CV and cover letter should be uploaded into the dedicated fields. Please combine additional application materials into one or two files in PDF/MSWord format. Applications must submit the following materials: a cover letter; a current curriculum vitae; a research statement outlining current and future research interests; one recent publication; a teaching dossier which includes a teaching statement, sample course materials, and teaching evaluations; and the name and contact information of three references. The University of Toronto\u2019s recruiting tool will automatically solicit and collect letters of reference from each referee within 48 hours of an application being submitted. Applicants remain responsible for ensuring that referees submit recent letters (on letterhead, dated and signed) by the closing date. Submission guidelines and details on the automatic reference letter collection, including timelines, are available in the candidate FAQ . If you have any questions about this position, please contact Professor Markus Bussmann at mie.chair@utoronto.ca . The University of Toronto has adopted the AAU Principles on Preventing Sexual Harassment in Academia , including the requirement that applicants release personnel information from prior employers regarding sexual misconduct. Full details and requirements can be found here . All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Indigenous Substantiation The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for those candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information regarding the University's Indigenous Substantiation Process, please refer to: Indigenous Substantiation Website . Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Thermal Engineering, Industrial Engineer, Mechanical Engineer, Sustainability, Engineer, Engineering, Energy Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Faculty Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Professor%2C-Teaching-Stream-Advanced-Manufacturing-&-Automation-ON/607346217/": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream", "description": "Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream - Advanced Manufacturing & Automation Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream - Advanced Manufacturing & Automation Date Posted: 10/26/2026 Closing Date: 12/07/2026, 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50204 Job Category: Faculty - Teaching Stream (continuing) Faculty/Division: Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering Department: Department of Mechanical and Industrial Engineering Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes POSITION DESCRIPTION The Department of Mechanical & Industrial Engineering (MIE) in the Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering at the University of Toronto invites applications for a full-time teaching stream position in Advanced Manufacturing & Automation. \u00a0The appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. REQUIREMENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS Applicants are required to have earned a Ph.D. in Engineering or a related field by the time of appointment or shortly thereafter.\u00a0 Alternatively, applicants are required to have\u00a0(i) at least a graduate degree in Engineering or a related field, with (ii) at least five years of industry and professional experience.\u00a0 Candidates must have a demonstrated record of excellence in teaching. We seek candidates with expertise suitable to teach courses in robotics and mechatronics, embedded and/or power systems, and/or advanced manufacturing and automation, and whose teaching interests complement and enhance our existing departmental strengths . \u00a0The successful candidate will teach introductory and advanced courses in these areas to undergraduate and graduate students in MIE and beyond. \u00a0Registration as a Professional Engineer, or eligibility for registration, is preferred. Candidates must have teaching experience in a degree-granting program, including lecture preparation and delivery, development of online material/lectures, and experience or interest in curriculum development. \u00a0Additionally, candidates must possess a demonstrated commitment to pedagogical inquiry and a demonstrated interest in teaching-related scholarly activities. Evidence of excellence in teaching and a commitment to pedagogical inquiry can be demonstrated through teaching accomplishments, awards and accolades, publications, presentations at relevant conferences, the teaching dossier submitted as part of the application (with required materials outlined below), and strong letters of reference. RESPONSIBILITIES The successful candidate will be assigned a teaching and service load. HIRING SALARY RANGE The salary range is $125,000 to $160,000 CAD per annum, depending on experience. \u00a0Negotiations beyond this salary range will be considered for exceptionally qualified candidates. ABOUT US Established in 1827, the University of Toronto is Canada's largest university, recognized as a global leader in research and teaching. UofT's distinguished faculty, institutional record of ground-breaking scholarship and wealth of innovative academic opportunities continually attract outstanding students and academics from around the world. The Department of Mechanical & Industrial Engineering at the University of Toronto is home to the top mechanical and industrial engineering programs in Canada. We aim to foster a welcoming world-class environment that excels at teaching, learning and research. APPLICATION PROCESS All application materials, including recent reference letters, must be received by December 7th, 2026. All qualified candidates are invited to apply online by clicking the link below. \u00a0Your CV and cover letter should be uploaded into the dedicated fields. \u00a0Please combine additional application materials into one or two files in PDF/MS Word format. \u00a0Applicants must submit the following materials: a cover letter; a current curriculum vitae; a complete teaching dossier, including a teaching statement, sample syllabi and course materials, and teaching evaluations; and the name and contact information of three references. At least one reference letter must primarily address the candidate\u2019s teaching. The University of Toronto\u2019s recruiting tool will automatically solicit and collect letters of reference from each referee within 48 hours of an application being submitted. \u00a0Applicants remain responsible for ensuring that references submit recent letters (on letterhead, dated and signed) by the closing date.\u00a0 Submission guidelines and details on the automatic reference letter collection, including timelines, are available in the candidate FAQ . If you have any questions about this position, please contact Prof. Markus Bussmann at mie.chair@utoronto.ca . All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Indigenous Substantiation The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for those candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information regarding the University's Indigenous Substantiation Process, please refer to: Indigenous Substantiation Website . Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Industrial Engineer, Power Systems, Curriculum Development, Engineer, Engineering, Education, Energy, Research Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Faculty Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Mississauga-Associate-ProfessorProfessor-Computer-Science-ON/607355617/": {"title": "Associate Professor/Professor", "description": "Associate Professor/Professor - Computer Science Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Associate Professor/Professor - Computer Science Date Posted: 10/26/2026 Closing Date: 12/15/2026, 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50132 Job Category: Faculty - Tenure Stream (continuing) Faculty/Division: University of Toronto Mississauga Department: Department of Mathematical and Computational Sciences Campus: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Existing Vacancy: Yes POSITION DESCRIPTION The Department of Mathematical and Computational Sciences at the University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) invites applications for one (1) full-time tenure stream appointment in the area of Computer Science. The appointment will be at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. This position is being advertised concurrently with the position for Assistant Professor in Computer Science (Req ID: 50131); however, only one appointment will be made. To be considered for this role and/or the Assistant Professor in Computer Science (Req ID: 50131) position, the candidate must submit a separate application for each posting. REQUIREMENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS Candidates must have earned a Ph.D. degree in Computer Science or a related area, with a clearly demonstrated record of excellence in research and teaching. Candidates must have an established international reputation. We seek exceptional candidates whose research and teaching interests complement and enhance our existing departmental strengths . Candidates must provide evidence of research excellence, as demonstrated by a record of sustained high impact contributions and publications in top-ranked and field-relevant journals or conferences; the submitted research statement; presentations at significant conferences; awards and accolades; other noteworthy activities that contribute to the visibility and prominence of the discipline; and strong endorsements from referees. Evidence of excellence in teaching will be demonstrated through teaching accomplishments, the teaching dossier, and strong letters of reference. Professional or lived experiences that enhance the ability to teach a diverse student body are highly valued. Equity, diversity and inclusion are essential to academic excellence as articulated in the University of Toronto\u2019s Statement on Equity, Diversity and Excellence. Candidates must demonstrate, in their application materials, an ability to foster diversity on campus and within the curriculum or discipline, and must show evidence of a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial environment. Examples of such evidence include: teaching that incorporates a focus on underrepresented communities; efforts undertaken to develop inclusive pedagogies, collaboration, and engagement with underrepresented communities; and mentoring of students from underrepresented groups. RESPONSIBILITIES The successful candidate will be assigned a teaching load and will teach in the undergraduate program at UTM and will also be a member of the tri-campus graduate Department of Computer Science at the University of Toronto . The successful candidate will be expected to pursue innovative and independent research at the highest international level; to establish an outstanding, competitive, and externally funded independent research program; to contribute to the enrichment of both undergraduate and graduate programs in the department; and will be assigned a sevice load and will participate in service and leadership within the academic community. HIRING SALARY RANGE The rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The salary range for this position exceeds $200,000 CAD per annum. ABOUT US The University of Toronto is an international leader in Computer Science research and education and offers the opportunity to teach, conduct research, and live in one of the most diverse metropolitan areas in the world. APPLICATION PROCESS All application materials, including recent signed reference letters, must be received by December 15, 2026. Application materials for the position must be submitted online through AcademicJobsOnline at https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/33018 . The required materials are: A current curriculum vitae A list of publications A research statement outlining current and future research interests A teaching dossier that includes a teaching statement, sample course syllabi, and course evaluations, and demonstrates a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion as outlined above Four to six (4-6) recent reference letters (on letterhead, dated and signed) uploaded to AcademicJobsOnline directly by the writers by the closing date. For inquiries, please contact our Chair\u2019s Assistant, Ryan Nguyen, at mcschairassist.utm@utoronto.ca . The University of Toronto has adopted the AAU Principles on Preventing Sexual Harassment in Academia , including the requirement that applicants release personnel information from prior employers regarding sexual misconduct. Full details and requirements can be found here. Caution: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T faculty job board. Please see the information above for the application instructions. Applications submitted via the U of T platform will NOT be considered for this position. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Indigenous Substantiation The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for those candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information regarding the University's Indigenous Substantiation Process, please refer to: Indigenous Substantiation Website . Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Computer Science, Equity, Academic, Drafting, Technology, Research, Finance, Education, Engineering Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Faculty Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Professor-Computer-Science-ON/607352617/": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "Assistant Professor - Computer Science Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant Professor - Computer Science Date Posted: 10/26/2026 Closing Date: 12/15/2026, 11:59PM ET Req ID: 49831 Job Category: Faculty - Tenure Stream (continuing) Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: Dept of Computer Science Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes POSITION DESCRIPTION The Department of Computer Science in the Faculty of Arts and Science at the University of Toronto invites applications for three (3) full-time tenure stream positions in the area of Computer Science. The appointments will be at the rank of Assistant Professor with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. REQUIREMENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS Candidates must have earned a PhD degree in Computer Science or a related area by the time of appointment, or shortly thereafter, with a demonstrated record of excellence in research and teaching. We seek applicants whose research and teaching interests complement and enhance our existing departmental strengths . Candidates must provide evidence of research excellence which can be demonstrated by a record of contributions and publications in top-ranked and field-relevant journals or conferences, or forthcoming publications meeting high international standards, the submitted research statement, presentations at significant conferences, awards and accolades, and strong endorsements by referees of top international stature. Candidates must demonstrate evidence in excellence in teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels through teaching accomplishments, and the teaching dossier, including a teaching statement (highlighting previous teaching experience including other teaching-related activities such as leading successful workshops or seminars, student mentorship, delivering conference presentations or posters, or experience as a teaching assistant or course instructor), sample course syllabi and materials (either of courses delivered by the applicants or planned for the future), teaching evaluations, or other evidence of superior performance in other teaching-related activities submitted as part of the application, as well as strong letters of reference. Professional or lived experiences that enhance the ability to teach a diverse student body are highly valued. RESPONSIBILITIES The University of Toronto is an international leader in Computer Science research and education . The successful candidates will be expected to pursue innovative and independent research at the highest international level; to establish an outstanding, competitive and externally funded independent research program; to contribute to the enrichment of both undergraduate and graduate programs in the department; and to participate in service and leadership within the academic community. The successful candidate will be assigned a teaching and service load. HIRING SALARY RANGE Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience and is competitive with our North American peers. The salary range for this position exceeds $200,000 CAD per annum. ABOUT US The University of Toronto offers the opportunity to teach, conduct research, and live in one of the most diverse metropolitan areas in the world. For more information about the Department of Computer Science see our website at https://www.cs.toronto.edu . APPLICATION PROCESS Application materials for the position must be submitted online through AcademicJobsOnline at https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32399 . The required materials are a current curriculum vitae; a list of publications; a research statement outlining current and future research interests; a teaching dossier that includes supporting materials mentioned above; and three to five (3\u20135) recent reference letters (on letterhead, dated, and signed) uploaded to AcademicJobsOnline directly by the writers by the closing date. Equity, diversity and inclusion are essential to academic excellence as articulated in the University of Toronto\u2019s Statement on Equity, Diversity and Excellence . We seek applicants who share these values and who demonstrate throughout the application materials their commitment and efforts to advance equity, diversity, inclusion and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment. All application materials, including recent signed reference letters, must be received by December 15, 2026. If you have any questions about the position, please contact recruit@cs.toronto.edu Caution: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T faculty job board. Please see the information above for the application instructions. Applications submitted via the U of T platform will NOT be considered for this position. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Computer Science, Equity, Drafting, CAD, Technology, Research, Finance, Engineering Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Faculty Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Professor-Computer-Science-ON/607352717/": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "Assistant Professor - Computer Science Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant Professor - Computer Science Date Posted: 10/26/2026 Closing Date: 12/15/2026, 11:59PM ET Req ID: 49406 Job Category: Faculty - Tenure Stream (continuing) Faculty/Division: University of Toronto Scarborough Department: University of Toronto Scarborough: Department of Computer and Mathematical Sciences Campus: University of Toronto Scarborough (UTSC) Existing Vacancy: Yes POSITION DESCRIPTION The Department of Computer and Mathematical Sciences at the University of Toronto Scarborough (UTSC) invites applications for three full-time tenure stream positions in any area of Computer Science. The appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. REQUIREMENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS Candidates must have earned a PhD degree in Computer Science or a related area by the time of appointment, or shortly thereafter, with a demonstrated record of excellence in research and teaching. We seek candidates whose research and teaching interests complement and enhance our existing departmental strengths . Candidates must provide evidence of research excellence which can be demonstrated through a record of publications in top-ranked and field-relevant journals or conferences, or forthcoming publications that meet high international standards; the submitted research statement; presentations at significant conferences; awards and accolades; and strong endorsements from referees of top international stature. Evidence of excellence in teaching will be demonstrated through teaching accomplishments, the teaching dossier (including the required materials outlined below, as well as evidence of superior performance in other teaching-related activities), and strong letters of reference. Other teaching-related activities can include performance as a teaching assistant or course instructor, experience leading successful workshops or seminars, student mentorship, or excellent conference presentations or posters. Professional or lived experiences that enhance the ability to teach a diverse student body are highly valued. Candidates must also show evidence of a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and to the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment, as demonstrated through the application materials. RESPONSIBILITIES The successful candidates will be expected to pursue innovative and independent research at the highest international level; and to establish an outstanding, competitive, and externally funded independent research program; to engage in undergraduate and graduate teaching and supervision and to participate in service and leadership within the academic community. In addition, the successful candidate will be assigned a teaching and service load. HIRING SALARY RANGE The salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The salary range for this position exceeds $200,000 CAD per annum. ABOUT US The University of Toronto offers the opportunity to teach, conduct research, and live in one of the most diverse metropolitan areas in the world. It is an international leader in Computer Science research and education. The successful candidate will also be a member of the tri-campus Graduate Department of Computer Science at the University of Toronto. The successful candidate will be expected to participate actively in the Graduate Department of Computer Science . APPLICATION PROCESS All application materials, including recent reference letters, must be received by December 15, 2026. All qualified candidates are invited to apply online through AcademicJobsOnline at https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32399 . Applicants must submit the following materials: a current curriculum vitae; a list of publications; a research statement outlining current and future research interests; a teaching dossier including a teaching statement, sample course materials, and teaching evaluations or evidence of superior performance in other teaching-related activities as listed above; and three to five (3-5) recent letters of reference uploaded to AcademicJobsOnline directly by the writers. Applicants remain responsible for ensuring that referees submit recent letters (on letterhead, dated and signed) by the closing date. If you have any questions about this position, please contact Jolyn Duan at jolyn.duan@utoronto.ca .For more information about our department, please see our website http://www.utsc.utoronto.ca/cms/ . Caution: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T faculty job board. Please see the information above for the application instructions. Applications submitted via the U of T platform will NOT be considered for this position. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Computer Science, Equity, Drafting, CAD, Technology, Research, Finance, Engineering Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Faculty Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Housing-Assistant-%28Term%29-ON/607356817/": {"title": "Housing Assistant (Term)", "description": "Housing Assistant (Term) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Housing Assistant (Term) Date Posted: 10/26/2026 Req ID: 50756 Faculty/Division: VP-Facilities & Real Estate Department: UNIVERSITY FAMILY HOUSING - CS Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00034538 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: University Family Housing is comprised of two 21 story residential towers and a unique stock of 83-century homes. The department provides housing to student families, faculty families and long-term residentialtenancies in two neighbourhoods on the St. George Campus to over 3000 adults and children, and provides on-site property management services, as well as educational and recreational programming for tenant families. Your opportunity: Under the direction of the Housing Administrator, the Housing Assistant is responsible for assisting the Administrator in maintaining a positive quality of student life in the Charles Street Student Family Residence. The primary responsibilities are to provide front-line customer service and to facilitate an open and easy flow of communication between all staff and contractors working at the residence. Other responsibilities include: entering, completing and monitoring electronic work order submissions, coordinating appliance deliveries; booking elevators and meeting rooms; storage and bicycle lockers; parking spaces for tenants and external parkers; reviewing contractor work schedules; closes tenant files; drafts various tenant letters; the collection and recording of rental payments, residence database maintenance; handling work orders; key control; mail distribution; answering routine residence queries and ordering office supplies. The Housing Assistant communicates with various departments and service providers on campus, such as Admissions & Eligibility, Campus Safety, Facilities & Services and Spaces & Experiences. The Assistant is responsible for appraising the Housing Administrator, Manager, Admissions & Housing Services and/or Assistant Director of any residence issues that may become a problem, as well as deals with day-to-day issues as part of the overall function of the position. Your responsibilities will include: Responding to enquiries within the defined scope of the role and redirecting as appropriate Troubleshooting and resolving routine maintenance requests and liaising with facilities or maintenance staff to facilitate resolution of building issues Informing contacts of maintenance work, service interruptions and other urgent notices Analyzing administrative processes and procedures, and recommending changes for improvement Applying established standards when respondingto emergencies Ordering supplies within established limits Serving as a resource to others by providing (non-supervisory) job-related guidance Essential Qualifications: Advanced College Diploma (3 years) or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum three (3) years\u2019 administrative experience in a customer service role, preferably in a residence environment. Intermediate proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Outlook). Must have strong written and verbal communication skills as well as excellent customer service skills. Must be tactful, professional and objective in dealing with residents. Good judgment, discretion and a pleasant and helpful attitude are essential. Must be organized, with strong ability to multitask and meet deadlines. Must possess the ability to work independently as well as in a team setting. Must display a willingness to take initiative in solving routine problems. Assets (Nonessential): Working knowledge of StarRez To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Multi-tasker Possess a positive attitude Problem solver Team player Please Note: This is a 9-month term. Closing Date: 11/03/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Ancillary Operations Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 07 -- $62,646 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $80,116. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Divisional HR Office Email: hruniversityoperations@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Equity, Database, Finance, Technology Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Program-Assistant-%2880-FTE%29-ON/607352417/": {"title": "Program Assistant (80% FTE)", "description": "Program Assistant (80% FTE) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Program Assistant (80% FTE) Date Posted: 10/26/2026 Req ID: 50688 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering Department: APSC Admin. Units Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00047962 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Faculty\u2019s Cross-Disciplinary Programs Office provides academic and administrative leadership to enhance cross-disciplinary educational services for U of T Engineering students. We seek to provide the foundation for success in academic and student life by providing guidance to undergraduate students in choosing minors, certificates while meeting their degree requirements. The Cross-Disciplinary Programs Office coordinates 10 minors, 17 certificates and several dedicated course offerings to support the various programs. Programs are available to all undergraduate engineering disciplines and recent data indicate that approximately 70% of graduating students are completing one or more of these programs as part of their degree. The CDP Office involves interaction with all Faculty departments, the Registrar\u2019s Office, and various departments and offices in the Faculty of Arts and Science and other partner faculties. Your opportunity: This position is an opportunity to work with students and faculty from all disciplines of engineering in a highly collaborative environment. Our leadership team provides an open, professional environment that fosters a culture built on respect, goal orientation, self-motivation, accountability, and teamwork. We believe in recognizing and valuing our employee\u2019s contributions to the advancement of the office\u2019s goals while promoting a strong commitment to work-life balance among our employees. Reporting to the Associate Director, the Program Assistant provides front-line assistance and program support to the Faculty\u2019s Minor and Certificate programs and other interdisciplinary courses and programs. The position is the front-line support for students interested in our minor and certificate programs and provides the necessary administrative assistance to keep the programs running smoothly. Your responsibilities will include: Providing detailed information to students on minor and certificate program and/or course requirements Acting as the first point of contact for general enquiries on our programs Responding to enquiries within the defined scope of the role and redirecting as appropriate Disseminating program information to current and potential students Liaising with students and faculty to coordinate program activities Updating and maintaining records on ACORN and Degree Explorer Serving as a resource to others by providing (non-supervisory) job-related guidance Assisting with data collection and reporting requirements Essential Qualifications: Advanced College Diploma (3 years) or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum two years of recent and relevant experience providing administrative support and front-line student services related to academic programs and processes in a university setting. Experience in an interdisciplinary university setting is preferred. Must have experience providing prospective and current post-secondary students tailored academic program and policy information based on their inquiries and needs. Knowledge of STEM disciplines. Experience working directly with faculty members and students in a detail-oriented and client services role. High level of proficiency with personal computers and appropriate software packages including Microsoft Office Suite Advanced level knowledge and experience with Quercus or similar student portal. Proficient with ROSI and Degree Explorer or similar student information system. Superior organizational, communication (oral and written) and interpersonal skills, with the proven ability to explain complex processes and procedures to a wide range of audiences. Demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment. Proven ability to accurately interpret, apply and communicate procedures and policies effectively with minimum oversight. Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively, work well under pressure, take initiative and set priorities and organize among multiple tasks and deadlines. Sound judgement, discretion, tact, and diplomacy, especially when handling sensitive and confidential matters. Strong customer service orientation and sensitivity to deal with the needs of students, staff, and faculty professionally. Ability to balance competing requirements of the position and delivering timely advice and service to students, faculty and staff with high accuracy and attention to detail. Assets (Nonessential): University degree. Knowledge of engineering undergraduate curriculum requirements. To be successfulin this role you will be: Approachable Communicator Organized Problem solver Team player Note: This position is a part-time position at 80% FTE. Closing Date: 11/03/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Part-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 08 at 80% FTE -- $53,217 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $68,055. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Administrative Assistant, Program Manager, Engineer, Equity, Part Time, Administrative, Management, Engineering, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Associate-ProfessorProfessor-Caribbean-Geographies-Caribbean-Ecologies-ON/607359017/": {"title": "Associate Professor/Professor", "description": "Associate Professor/Professor - Caribbean Geographies / Caribbean Ecologies Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Associate Professor/Professor - Caribbean Geographies / Caribbean Ecologies Date Posted: 10/26/2026 Closing Date: 01/11/2027, 11:59PM ET Req ID: 48728 Job Category: Faculty - Tenure Stream (continuing) Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: Department of Geography & Planning Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes POSITION DESCRIPTION The Department of Geography and Planning and the Centre for Caribbean Studies in the Faculty of Arts and Science at the University of Toronto invites applications for a full-time tenure stream position in the area of Caribbean ecological crises and ecological futures. This will be a joint appointment between the Department of Geography and Planning (51%) and the Centre for Caribbean Studies (49%). The appointment will be at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. The successful candidate will be eligible to be named the New College Professorship in Caribbean Studies for a three-year term, which is renewable following a favourable review. REQUIREMENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS Applicants must have earned a PhD degree in Caribbean Studies, Geography, Climate and Society, Political Ecology, Development Studies, or related areas including interdisciplinary fields. We seek candidates conducting interdisciplinary research on the broader nexus of Caribbean ecological crises and ecological futures and the intersecting areas of food, water, health, biodiversity and economy in the Caribbean while paying close attention to their impacts on the production of place and space. We also seek scholars who address the nexus between Caribbean ecological epistemologies and just environmental futures and whose research engages with critical Caribbean environmental issues. Candidates\u2019 research must be grounded within the Caribbean context. Experience and engagement with local communities in the Caribbean region will be an asset. Candidates must also clearly demonstrate a record of excellence in research and teaching in areas that complement and enhance existing strengths in both units and must have experience in research supervision. We seek applicants able to offer undergraduate and graduate courses that will serve the Caribbean Studies program as well as programs in Geography and Planning. We invite candidates whose application materials demonstrate past research, current projects and future plans that foreground the importance and urgency of environmental issues in the Caribbean and bring a level of intellectual curiosity, imagination and critical engagement that deepens our understanding of what's at stake. Candidates must provide evidence of research excellence, as demonstrated by a record of sustained high-impact contributions and publications in top-ranked and field-relevant venues, the submitted research statement, presentations at significant conferences, distinguished awards and accolades for innovative work, other noteworthy activities that contribute to the visibility and prominence of the discipline, and strong endorsement by referees of high international standing. Evidence of excellence in teaching will be demonstrated through the teaching accomplishments, the teaching dossier (including the required materials outlined below), as well as strong letters of reference. RESPONSIBILITIES Candidates will have an established international reputation and will be expected to sustain and lead innovative and independent research at the highest international level and to maintain an outstanding, competitive, and externally funded research program. In addition, the successful candidate will be assigned a teaching and service load. HIRING SALARY RANGE Rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The upper end of the salary range for this position exceeds $200,000 CAD per annum. ABOUT US The University of Toronto is home to one of the oldest and largest Geography program s in North America.\u00a0 Geographers at the University of Toronto are engaged in work at the center of many of today\u2019s most challenging issues and processes. Drawing on interdisciplinary approaches, and often working in partnership with communities and government, the program supports intellectual diversity and commitments to enhance, restore, and preserve our natural and social environments. The Centre for Caribbean Studies is the only program in Canada with degrees specifically dedicated to the study of the Caribbean and its people. The program consists of courses in Caribbean history, literature, and thought which deal with a wide range of issues including gender, religion, politics, culture, ethnicity, race, development, language, colonialism, environment and regional common markets. The appointment will be held at the University of Toronto campus in downtown Toronto (St. George campus). Toronto is a vibrant and cosmopolitan city, one of the most desirable cities in the world in which to work and live. All application materials, including recent reference letters, must be received by January 11, 2027. All qualified candidates are invited to apply online by clicking the link below. Your CV and cover letter should be uploaded into the dedicated fields. Please combine additional application materials into one or two files in PDF/MS Word format. Applicants must submit the following materials: a cover letter; a current curriculum vitae; a research statement outlining current and future research interests; one recent publication; a teaching dossier, including a teaching statement, sample course materials, and teaching evaluations; and the name and contact information of three references. Equity, diversity and inclusion are essential to academic excellence as articulated in University of Toronto's Statement on Equity, Diversity and Excellence . We seek candidates who share these values and who demonstrate throughout the application materials their commitment and efforts to advance equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment. The University of Toronto\u2019s recruiting tool will automatically solicit and collect letters of reference from each referee within 48 hours of an application being submitted. Applicants remain responsible for ensuring that references submit recent letters (on letterhead, dated and signed) by the closing date. Submission guidelines and details on the automatic reference letter collection, including timelines, are available in the candidate FAQs . If you have any questions about this position, please contact Professor Paul Hess, Chair, Department of Geography and Planning, jobs.geoplan@utoronto.ca . The University of Toronto has adopted the AAU Principles on Preventing Sexual Harassment in Academia , including the requirement that applicants release personnel information from prior employers regarding sexual misconduct. Full details and requirements can be found here . All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Indigenous Substantiation The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for those candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information regarding the University's Indigenous Substantiation Process, please refer to: Indigenous Substantiation Website . Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Equity, Academic, CAD, Drafting, Research, Finance, Education, Engineering Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Faculty Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Mississauga-Assistant-Professor-Computer-Science-ON/607355417/": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "Assistant Professor - Computer Science Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant Professor - Computer Science Date Posted: 10/26/2026 Closing Date: 12/15/2026, 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50131 Job Category: Faculty - Tenure Stream (continuing) Faculty/Division: University of Toronto Mississauga Department: Department of Mathematical and Computational Sciences Campus: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Existing Vacancy: Yes POSITION DESCRIPTION The Department of Mathematical and Computational Sciences at the University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) invites applications for one (1) full-time tenure stream appointment in the area of Computer Science. The appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor with an anticipated date of July 1, 2027. This position is being advertised concurrently with the position for Associate Professor/Professor in Computer Science (Req ID: 50132); however, only one appointment will be made. To be considered for this role and/or the Associate Professor/Professor in Computer Science (Req ID: 50132) position, the candidate must submit a separate application for each posting. REQUIREMENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS Candidates must have earned a Ph.D. degree in Computer Science or a related area by the time of appointment, or shortly thereafter, with a demonstrated record of excellence in research and teaching. We seek exceptional candidates whose research and teaching interests complement and enhance our existing departmental strengths . Candidates must provide evidence of research excellence which can be demonstrated through a record of publications in top-ranked and field-relevant journals or conferences, or forthcoming publications that meet high international standards; the submitted research statement; presentations at significant conferences; awards and accolades; and strong endorsements from referees. Candidates must demonstrate excellence in teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels through teaching accomplishments, and the teaching dossier, including a teaching statement highlighting previous experience that can include teaching-related activities such as leading successful workshops or seminars, student mentorship, delivering conference presentations or posters, or experience as a teaching assistant or course instructor.\u00a0 Excellence in teaching may also be demonstrated through materials such as sample course syllabi (either of courses delivered by the candidate or planned for the future), course evaluations, or other evidence of superior performance in teaching-related activities submitted as part of the application. Professional or lived experiences that enhance the ability to teach a diverse student body are highly valued. Equity, diversity and inclusion are essential to academic excellence as articulated in the University of Toronto\u2019s Statement on Equity, Diversity and Excellence . Candidates must demonstrate, in their application materials, an ability to foster diversity on campus and within the curriculum or discipline, and must show evidence of a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial environment. Examples of such evidence include: teaching that incorporates a focus on underrepresented communities; efforts undertaken to develop inclusive pedagogies, collaboration, and engagement with underrepresented communities; and mentoring of students from underrepresented groups. RESPONSIBILITIES The successful candidate will be assigned a teaching load and will teach in the undergraduate program at UTM and will also be a member of the tri-campus graduate Department of Computer Science at the University of Toronto. The successful candidate will be expected to pursue innovative and independent research at the highest international level; to establish an outstanding, competitive, and externally funded independent research program; to contribute to the enrichment of both undergraduate and graduate programs in the department; and will be assigned a service load and will participate in service and leadership within the academic community. HIRING SALARY RANGE The salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The salary range for this position exceeds $200,000 CAD per annum. ABOUT US The University of Toronto is an international leader in Computer Science research and education and offers the opportunity to teach, conduct research, and live in one of the most diverse metropolitan areas in the world. APPLICATION PROCESS All application materials, including recent signed reference letters, must be received by December 15, 2026 . Application materials for the position must be submitted online through AcademicJobsOnline at https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32399 . The required materials are: A current curriculum vitae A list of publications A research statement outlining current and future research interests A teaching dossier that includes a teaching statement, sample course syllabi, course evaluations or evidence of superior performance in teaching-related activities, and demonstrates a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion as outlined above Three to five (3-5) recent reference letters (on letterhead, dated and signed) uploaded to AcademicJobsOnline directly by the writers by the closing date. For inquiries, please contact our Chair\u2019s Assistant, Ryan Nguyen, at mcschairassist.utm@utoronto.ca . Caution: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T faculty job board. Please see the information above for the application instructions. Applications submitted via the U of T platform will NOT be considered for this position. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Indigenous Substantiation The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for those candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information regarding the University's Indigenous Substantiation Process, please refer to: Indigenous Substantiation Website . Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Computer Science, Equity, Drafting, CAD, Technology, Research, Finance, Engineering Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Faculty Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Manager%2C-Planning-&-Operations-ON/607364817/": {"title": "Manager, Planning & Operations Job Details", "description": "Manager, Planning & Operations Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Manager, Planning & Operations Date Posted: 10/26/2026 Req ID: 50758 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Office of the Faculty Comptroller & Chief Financial Officer Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About Us The Temerty Faculty of Medicine at the University of Toronto is at the centre of one of North America\u2019s largest biomedical research, education and clinical care networks. With 14 fully affiliated research-intensive hospitals \u2014 and dozens more community and clinical care sites \u2014 Temerty Medicine offers unparalleled opportunities in Canada\u2019s most dynamic city for our more than 9,000 faculty and staff and 7,000 learners at all levels. Your Opportunity As Manager, Planning and Operations, you will serve as strategic partner providing rotational leadership and operational support to designated departments across the Temerty Faculty of Medicine. Reporting to the Faculty Comptroller & Chief Financial Officer, you will help advance short- and long-term strategic planning, enhance operational efficiencies across academic, research, and administrative units, and ensure seamless continuity during department leadership transitions. Your ability to embrace new challenges as they emerge, coupled with your exceptional financial management and people leadership skills, will enable you to evaluate processes, navigate complex funding models and integrate financial planning with strategic objectives. By effectively leading teams through uncertainty, you will play a vital role in advancing our faculty\u2019s operational agility and collective impact. Essential Qualifications University degree, or an acceptable equivalent combination of education and experience in a relevant field A minimum of 5 years\u2019 senior administrative experience, preferably in a University or healthcare environment Strong financial acumen, including financial analysis, budgeting, and forecasting experience Experience developing high functioning teams, including a proven track record of success in leading and mentoring staff in a unionized environment Experience in research administration, including reviewing and negotiating research-related agreements Education program management experience in an academic environment, and knowledge of higher education curriculum and accreditation processes Experience in a student recruitment and admissions environment Familiarity with office renovation, capital projects and space management Experience scoping and managing projects and leading successful change Proven commitment to equity, diversity and inclusivity Proven leadership and management skills, including outstanding interpersonal, communication and presentation skills Superior planning and project management skills with a focus on executing and competing tasks under pressure and within tight deadlines Ability to maintain a broad perspective, and the ability to foster and maintain effective relationships with all levels of faculty, staff, learners, senior administrators and external stakeholders Strong technical skills, including knowledge of the University of Toronto\u2019s Administrative Management System (AMS) and a facility for working with project management tools and keep current with new and emerging technologies Advanced consulting skills, with the ability to work across the organization to influence decisions for a positive outcome Excellent conflict resolution skills with strong ability to exercise judgement, tact, discretion, and determination Assets Completion of a recognized professional accounting program (CMA, CGA, or CA) Closing Date: 11/16/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 4 -- Hiring Zone: $110,973 - $129,471 -- Broadband Salary Range: $110,973 - $184,957 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Operations Manager, Project Manager, Strategic Planning, Program Manager, Operations, Technology, Management, Strategy, Research Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Professor-Academic-General-Internist-ON/607303317/": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "Assistant Professor - Academic General Internist Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant Professor - Academic General Internist Date Posted: 10/21/2026 Closing Date: 11/25/2026 , 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50647 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Medicine Hospital Affiliation: University Health Network (UHN) & Sinai Health System (SHS) Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Department of Medicine, Temerty Faculty of Medicine at the University of Toronto and the Divisions of General Internal Medicine and Geriatrics of the University Health Network (UHN) and Sinai Health System (SHS) are seeking to recruit a Clinician Teacher, Internal Medicine, SHS. The successful candidate should have an interest in both inpatient and ambulatory general internal medicine. They will also be expected to participate in teaching activities at both the undergraduate and graduate medical education level. Candidates must currently hold or be eligible for a University of Toronto full-time clinical academic appointment at the rank of Assistant/Associate Professor\u00a0 or Professor and should fulfill the academic position description of a Clinician Teacher. Effective start date will be between July 2027, or sooner as mutually agreed upon. This Clinician Teacher (CT) position will be primarily based at Sinai Health and involve 75% clinical care, 20% scholarly activities and 5% administrative service. Clinical care is comprised of 24-26 weeks/year of clinical service, including: 6-10 weeks of Clinical Teaching Unit and 14-18 weeks of consults, hospital medicine inpatient service and ambulatory clinics, with informal clinical teaching while on service. Specifically, we are looking for someone with experience and expertise in Sinai\u2019s GIM obstetrical medicine service (consult and clinic), with potential for leadership in this area. Scholarly activities include formal teaching (40-50+ hours per year across multiple learner levels with an emphasis on sustained excellence in teaching at the undergraduate MD and postgraduate MD levels; as well as creative professional activities related to education, including curriculum development and novel approaches to teaching & education, with evidence of impact outside local settings). Please note that while CTs are assigned a primary site (SH); occasional secondary clinical work at a UHN site is encouraged. The mix of clinical and educational responsibilities will depend on the successful candidate\u2019s background and the needs of the Division. Competitive candidates will possess outstanding communication, teaching, organizational and interpersonal skills that enable them to work collaboratively with other physicians, learners, hospital staff and administrators. Candidates must have advanced academic training that is relevant to their position description (master\u2019s degree, doctoral degree or equivalent, see Table 2 on the Clinical Faculty Academic Appointments page for more details ). Candidates must also have a record of excellence in their area of interest. For applicants being considered for appointment as a Clinician Teacher, excellence will be assessed by the presence of scholarly contributions to teaching and education as evidenced by pedagogical innovation, curriculum development, experience in teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level, and teaching awards. Successful candidates must hold MD qualifications, be certified (or be eligible for certification) by the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada in General Internal Medicine, or hold international equivalent and be licensed (or be eligible for licensure) by the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario. Subspecialty certification in General Internal Medicine is preferred. Academic rank, salary and contractual arrangements will be commensurate with the qualifications and experience of the successful candidates. Compensation will be negotiated and within the usual income range for an academic general internist in the Province of Ontario (estimated range is $280,000-350,000 per year). Applications will be accepted until November 25, 2026 or until the position is filled. Interested individuals should send a copy of their letter of interest, curriculum vitae and the names and contact information for three references to: Jessica Liu MD FRCPC Division Head \u2013 General Internal Medicine and Geriatrics University Health Network and Sinai Health System Toronto General Hospital, 200 Elizabeth St. 14EN Room 216, Toronto, ON M5G 2C4 E-mail: care of samantha.johnson3@uhn.ca and jessica.liu@uhn.ca CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. For more information about the Department of Medicine at the University of Toronto, please visit our website at https://www.deptmedicine.utoronto.ca . The Department of Medicine\u2019s academic position descriptions can be viewed on this webpage: https://www.deptmedicine.utoronto.ca/academic-position- descriptions#AcademicPositionDescriptions . Information on Faculty academic appointments can be found here: https://deptmedicine.utoronto.ca/clinical-faculty-academic-appointments. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Curriculum Development, Geriatric, Academic, Internal Medicine, Physician, Education, Healthcare Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Service-Coordinator-ON/607312117/": {"title": "Service Coordinator", "description": "Service Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Service Coordinator Date Posted: 10/23/2026 Req ID: 50716 Faculty/Division: VP-Facilities & Real Estate Department: S&E Student Residences Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00039955 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Student Residences team at Spaces & Experiences (S&E) oversees and operates undergraduate and graduate student housing for more than 2,200 students on the St. George campus. Our residences include ChestnutResidence, Oak House, Graduate House, and Knox Residence. We strive to offer a supportive and dynamic living-learning environment for students that fosters academic success, personal growth, and a strong sense of belonging. Your opportunity: Reporting to the Manager, Residence Administration, the Service Coordinator is responsible for overseeing service desk operations at their assigned student residence(s). Responsibilities include greeting residents/guests and visitors, answering questions, transferring phone calls, distributing mail/parcels, monitoring building access, issuing keys and equipment, processing payments, and other administrative duties. The Service Coordinator is also responsible for training and scheduling other service desk staff, reviewing logs and audits, ordering supplies, and responding to routine email inquiries. Your responsibilities will include: Acting as the first point of contact for general enquiries Resolving minor complaints within the scope of the role and referring larger issues when appropriate Distributing routine welcome packages to students Providing guided tours of facilities Drafting internaland external communications Directing the activities of casual staff Coordinating staff schedule to ensure proper coverage Essential Qualifications: Advanced College Diploma (3 years) or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum three (3) years of administrative work experience in a post secondary environment, with at least one year working in a student residence environment. Intermediate computer skills with Microsoft 365 tools (e.g., Word, Excel, Outlook, Teams). Excellent customer service and interpersonal skills. Strong oral and written communication skills. Excellent attention to detail and organizational skills. Ability to multitask in a fast-paced environment. Good judgment, tact, and diplomacy. Excellent problem-solving skills. Assets (Nonessential): Proficiency with StarRez software system Experience with hotel/hospitality property management software. To be successful in this role you will be: Approachable Communicator Multi-tasker Problem solver Tactful Team player Please note: The shift for this position during the academic year (September to April) is Monday \u2013 Friday, 9:00am - 5:00pm The shift for this position during the summer term (May to August) is Tuesday \u2013 Saturday, 10:00am - 6:00pm Closing Date: 11/02/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 07 -- $62,646 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $80,116. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Divisional HR Office Email: hruniversityoperations@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Service Desk, Equity, Customer Service, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Systems-Administrator-Dev-Ops-ON/607321717/": {"title": "Systems Administrator", "description": "Systems Administrator - Dev Ops Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Systems Administrator - Dev Ops Date Posted: 10/23/2026 Req ID: 50608 Faculty/Division: Library Department: Scholars Portal Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00056470 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The University of Toronto Libraries (UTL) system is the largest academic library in Canada and is ranked in the top five among peer institutions in North America. The system comprises 40 libraries located across three university campuses: St.George, Mississauga, and Scarborough. This diverse and extensive network of college libraries, special collections, and specialized information centres plays a pivotal role in supporting the teaching, scholarly, and research needs of nearly 100,000 students enrolled in a wide array of graduate, professional, and undergraduate programs. The library system provides access to millions of resources in various formats, including electronic, print, audio-visual, data and geospatial materials. UTL also boasts impressive holdings of archival material and substantial digital collections, securely preserved in the libraries' data centre. The staff at UTL are integral to the academic and scholarly enterprise, working closely withfaculty and students to support their teaching, learning, and research requirements. They are subject matter experts; they are skilled in research data management, collections, statistics, GIS, metadata, digital preservation, scholarly communications, copyright, teaching, knowledge synthesis, open access and much more. Our work is grounded in our commitment to support equity, diversity, and inclusion. UTL continuously evolves to meet the changing academic priorities and pressures at the University and within the broader landscape of higher education. Your opportunity: Scholars Portal, a department of the University of Toronto Libraries, is the digital service arm of the Ontario Council of University Libraries (OCUL), delivering shared infrastructure, technology, and services that support Ontario\u2019s 21 university libraries. The Scholars Portal team of librarians, developers, and systems staff supports a broad portfolio of services spanning research and member services, data and geospatial services, digital collections, and digital preservation. Reporting to the Associate Director, the Systems Administrator \u2013 DevOps will play a key role in supporting Scholaris, Canada's national shared institutional repository service. The position will focus on maintaining and improving the infrastructure, deployment processes, and operational systems that support Scholaris, with an emphasis on automation, reliability, security, and performance. Working closely with developers, Systems team members, and other colleagues, the successful candidate will support application deployments, configuration management, CI/CD pipelines, monitoring, troubleshooting, and ongoing system maintenance. The role will also contribute to improving automation, streamlining operational processes, and supporting the continuous development and enhancement of Scholaris. As part of a collaborative technical team, the incumbent will help ensure that Scholaris remains a secure, reliable, and sustainable service that meets the evolving needs of the Canadian research community. Your responsibilities will include: Developing and programming network applications Customizing open source web applications Analyzing and installing networking equipment (Linux based servers and infrastructure services) Configuring system applications according to needs Troubleshooting complex computer system problems Creating complex and technical documentation and usersupport guides Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree (Computer Science, Information Technology or a related field) or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum 5 years' related experience Demonstrated experience administering and maintaining Linux-based systems (e.g., Ubuntu, Red Hat Enterprise Linux, or equivalent) Experience with configuration management and automation tools (e.g., Ansible, Chef, Puppet, or equivalent) Experience with CI/CD pipelines and deployment automation tools (e.g., Jenkins, GitLab CI, GitHub Actions, or equivalent) Proficiency in scripting and automation using Python, Bash, or similar languages Proficiency in scripting and automation using Python, Bash, or similar languagesExperience administering web servers and reverse proxies (e.g., Apache, Nginx, HAProxy, or equivalent) Familiarity with containerization and orchestration technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes, or equivalent) Familiarity with on-premises virtualization and infrastructure platforms (e.g., KVM, OpenStack, or equivalent) Experience with monitoring, logging, and troubleshooting tools used to support production services Knowledge of networking fundamentals, including TCP/IP, DNS, TLS, firewalls, and load balancing Understanding of secure systems administration practices, including patch management, access control, backup, and recovery Familiarity with databases and backend services (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL, MarkLogic, or equivalent) is an asset Strong analytical, problem-solving, and troubleshooting skills Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work independently and collaboratively with technical and non-technical colleagues Demonstrated commitment to the values of inclusivity, diversity, anti-racism, equity and accessibility Strong problem-solving and communication skills To be successful in this role you will be: Adaptable Communicator Goal oriented Organized Problem solver Team player Closing Date: 11/06/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Grant - Term Schedule: Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 14 -- $95,344 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $121,932. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Information Technology (IT) Divisional HR Office Email: utlhr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Audio Visual, Data Center, Open Source, System Administrator, Data Management, Creative, Technology, Data Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Program-Manager-ON/607311817/": {"title": "Program Manager Job Details", "description": "Program Manager Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Program Manager Date Posted: 10/23/2026 Req ID: 50717 Faculty/Division: UofT Scarborough Department: UTSC:Dept-Health & Society Campus: University of Toronto Scarborough (UTSC) Position Number: 00060187 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The University of Toronto Scarborough is a place of energy, enthusiasm and passion. Our commitment to inclusive excellence attracts the brightest learners, scholars and employees from around the globe. Our success has been made possible by the opportunity given to us by Indigenous hosts to operate on their territory, and we cherish our continuing partnerships with these communities. The University of Toronto Scarborough is an exciting campus with unlimited potential. Join us on our journey. The Department of Health and Society at the University of Toronto Scarborough consists of award-winning faculty who combine active and productive research programs with teaching innovation and excellence. Our department is home to a diverse community of interdisciplinary researchers, teachers, and students who ask cutting-edge questions about health, disability, illness, and disease locally and globally. The Department of Health and Society is dedicated to advancing critical change in health through interdisciplinary education, research excellence, and responsible community engagement. As a department, we aim to be a globally recognized community of scholars that fosters transformative critical research and education that tackles challenges to health in a complex society. This search aligns with the University\u2019s commitment to strategically and proactively promote diversity among our community members ( Statement on Equity, Diversity & Excellence ). Recognizing that Black, Indigenous, and other Racialized communities have experienced inequities that have developed historically and are ongoing, we strongly welcome and encourage candidates from those communities to apply. AgeTech LaunchPad is a purpose-built, university-embedded, and GTA-localized platform that addresses societal and systems-level challenges of population aging in a coordinated and practical way, enabling U of T faculty and trainees to collaboratively design, evaluate, and deploy pilot solutions across diverse community, home, and care environments. The Initiative leverages AGE-WELL, Canada\u2019s Technology and Aging Network that brings together researchers, older adults, caregivers, partner organizations and future leaders, to build sector relationships, establish international partnerships, develop bespoke training platforms, and make pathways for scaling successful interventions. Your opportunity: Working under the guidance of the Associate Director, the incumbent is responsible for planning, coordinating, and implementing all phases of assigned projects. This includes developing and adjusting project schedules to optimize timelines and ensure key milestones are met, as well as planning and organizing workflows for project teams. The incumbent builds and maintains strong relationships with stakeholders and strategic partners, reviews and assesses project requirements to support research objectives and timelines, and proactively identifies and communicates issues, risks, and roadblocks to project leaders. In addition, the incumbent monitors project progress and ensures that all assigned work is completed to established quality standards and project expectations. Your responsibilities will include: Planning and implementing project phases. Developing or modifying project schedules to expedite and/or compress the critical path to meet timelines. Planning and implementing workflow for a group. Building and strengthening relationships with stakeholders and partners of strategic importance. Reviewing and assessing requirements needed to meet project timelines. Informing project leaders of issues and roadblocks. Checking that assigned work completed meets expected standards. Analyzing draft funding proposals. Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum five (5) years relevant experience in project development and identifying, developing and executing strategies for research and development collaborations. Experience monitoring and assessing research impact. Experience with performance evaluation and benchmarking of initiatives or projects. Experience in working with older adults, caregivers, and other stakeholders involved in care and support of older adults. Familiarity with strategic partnerships and new business opportunities in a research and/or educational setting. Ability to compile and analyze data, prepare reports and other informational materials. Ability to support the translation of research technologies to industry partners. Proven analytical and problem solving skills and highly attentive to detail. Experience in aging population research. Solid project management experience including all aspects of project development and execution. Exceptional communication (oral and written) skills; Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to collaborate on initiatives with a wide variety of contacts both internal and external to the University. Excellent interpersonal skills and demonstrated ability to liaise, build and maintain relationships with a diverse range of internal and external stakeholders. Applicants are also expected to show evidence of a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment To be successful in this role you will be: Articulate Communicator Efficient Resourceful Responsible Team player Notes: This role is currently eligible for a hybrid work arrangement, pursuant to University policies and guidelines, including but not limited to the University of Toronto\u2019s Alternative Work Arrangements Guideline . This is a two (2) year TERM position. Closing Date: 11/12/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Grant - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 13 -- $89,794 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $114,832. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Divisional HR Office Email: humanresources.utsc@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Program Manager, R&D, Project Manager, Manager, Management, Research, Technology Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Mississauga-Operating-Engineer-Trainee-I-%28Term-Up-to-12-Months%29-ON/607324017/": {"title": "Operating Engineer Trainee I (Term", "description": "Operating Engineer Trainee I (Term - Up to 12 Months) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Operating Engineer Trainee I (Term - Up to 12 Months) Date Posted: 10/23/2026 Req ID: 50723 Faculty/Division: UofT Mississauga Department: UTM: Facilities, Management & Planning Campus: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The University of Toronto, Mississauga Campus (UTM) invites qualified candidates to apply for an Operating Engineer Trainee I position in the Facilities Management and Planning Department. The successful Trainee will be afforded the opportunity to gain valuable experience in the operation and maintenance of our boiler plant and the HVAC systems in various buildings in the Mississauga Campus. This experience can be used to achieve the requirements of a Fourth (4th) Class Operating Engineer Certification of Qualification through the Technical Standards and Safety Authority (TSSA). The term of this training program is up to 12 months. Upon successful completion of the program, if a vacancy for a full-time position is available, the Trainee may apply. This position is part of the UNIFOR, Local 2003 union and the successful candidate will be required to join this union. Qualifications Education: Grade 12 diploma (or equivalent and has successfully passed all TSSA exams for a Fourth (4th) Class Operating Engineer Certification for the Province of Ontario). Proof of passing these exams is required to be submitted with your application. Experience: Ability to demonstrate above-average mechanical aptitude. Basic electrical knowledge would be an asset. Other: Ability to communicate effectively in English both orally and in writing; be proficient in Microsoft Outlook email, Excel and Word and have basic keyboarding skills. Please note: There is no guarantee of a position upon successful completion of the Trainee Program. If a vacancy for a full-time Operating Engineer position is available, the Trainee may apply. Applicants must submit proof that both 4th Class Operating Engineer exams were passed with your online application Closing Date: 11/03/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: Unifor FT L2003 Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: Job Rate: $29.57/hour Job Category: Engineering / Technical Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Boiler Engineer, HVAC, Curriculum, Electrical, Engineer, Engineering, Operations, Education Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Mississauga-Senior-Energy-Engineer-ON/607303417/": {"title": "Senior Energy Engineer Job Details", "description": "Senior Energy Engineer Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Senior Energy Engineer Date Posted: 10/23/2026 Req ID: 50625 Faculty/Division: UofT Mississauga Department: UTM: Facilities, Management & Planning Campus: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: U of T Mississauga\u2014the second largest campus of Canada\u2019s top-ranked university and the only research university in Ontario\u2019s booming Peel Region\u2014is one of the world\u2019s great catalysts of human potential. Our employee community hums with the energy of 3,400 faculty, librarians and staff, who power our campus with curiosity, connection and care. We work together to spark life-changing research and innovation, make an indelible mark on the world by building equitable cities and societies, enable healthy lives, create a sustainable future and ignite entrepreneurship. Above all, we prioritize student success and seek to give our 16,500 students the lift of a lifetime through learning and discovery. We love to open opportunities available nowhere else for our community to achieve their ambitions and make their unique contributions to Canada and the world. This work all comes together on a spectacularly green campus, alongside the Missinihe-ziibi (Trusting Creek or Credit River), where we seek to honour truth, reciprocity and reconciliation on the traditional land of the Huron-Wendat, Seneca and the Mississaugas of the Credit First Nation. We\u2019re thrilled to welcome those who want to learn more about us and to be part of what we do. POSITION SUMMARY Reporting to the Associate Director, Sustainability and Energy Management, Facilities Management & Planning (FMP), the Senior Energy Engineer will lead energy efficiency, decarbonization, and climate action initiatives for facilities and the built environment at the University of Toronto, Mississauga (UTM), supporting the University's Climate Positive Plan and long-term greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions reduction targets. The Senior Energy Engineer will primarily be responsible for identifying, evaluating, and advancing energy conservation and decarbonization opportunities through engineering assessments, technical studies, recommissioning programs, and ongoing analysis of building and infrastructure performance. Responsibilities include quantifying energy and GHG reductions, developing technical proposals and business cases to support capital investments, coordinating the implementation of energy conservation measures, and establishing and maintaining systems to track energy consumption and performance. Through monitoring and targeting, and Measurement and Verification (M&V) protocols, the Senior Energy Engineer will evaluate and report on the effectiveness of implemented measures, identify opportunities for continuous improvement, establish performance benchmarks, and prepare regular progress reports to support the University's energy efficiency and Climate Positive objectives. In addition, the Senior Energy Engineer will contribute to the development of short- and long-term energy and decarbonization strategies, support funding and incentive applications, and serve as a technical resource to project teams undertaking capital developments, building renovations, infrastructure upgrades, and energy system modernization projects. The position will review proposed designs and technical solutions to support alignment with University energy performance standards and climate commitments. The Senior Energy Engineer will also support the development of awareness and engagement initiatives that promote energy conservation and sustainable building operations, collaborating with the Sustainability Office and campus stakeholders to encourage behavioural change and communicate progress toward institutional sustainability goals. EDUCATION: Degree in mechanical or electrical engineering; licensed professional engineer in the Province of Ontario(P.Eng). Certified Energy Manager (CEM), Certified Measurement and Verification Professional (CMVP), Certified Building Commissioning Professional (CBCP) by Association of Energy Engineers (AEE) is an asset. LEED accreditation preferred. EXPERIENCE: Minimum 5+ years of relevant work experience in the field of energy management within the commercial and institutional sectors with a proven track record. SKILLS: Proficiency in the use of standard office computer applications; expert level skill in utility database development and maintenance, invoice review for technical compliance. OTHER: Excellent oral and written communication skills, including the ability to write for publication and create and deliver presentations. \u00a0Highly developed interpersonal skills, including the ability to gain consensus. Excellent organizational, time management and project management skills. Demonstrated ability to work independently. Budget management skills. Closing Date: 11/05/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 4 -- Hiring Zone: $110,973 - $129,471 -- Broadband Salary Range: $110,973 - $184,957 Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Sustainability, Electrical Engineering, Electrical, Engineer, Energy, Engineering Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Lecturer-Assistant-Professor-Academic-Hospitalist-ON/607303617/": {"title": "Lecturer / Assistant Professor", "description": "Lecturer / Assistant Professor - Academic Hospitalist Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Lecturer / Assistant Professor - Academic Hospitalist Date Posted: 10/22/2026 Closing Date: 12/15/2026 , 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50702 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Medicine Hospital Affiliation: University Health Network Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Division of General Internal Medicine, Department of Medicine and University Health Network (UHN), and the Temerty Faculty of Medicine, Department of Medicine at the University of Toronto are seeking to recruit 1-3 Academic Clinicians to be based at Toronto General Hospital (TGH) and Toronto Western Hospital (TWH). Increasing patient volumes on the General Internal Medicine Clinical Teaching Units has necessitated the creation of a resident-independent team known at UHN/SHS as the Acute Inpatient Medicine, or AIM Team. This team is under the auspice of the Division of General Internal Medicine (GIM) & Geriatrics at UHN/SHS. The successful candidates must currently hold or be eligible for a full- time clinical academic appointment at the rank of Lecturer or Assistant Professor with a position description of Academic Clinician at the University of Toronto, with a start date of July 1, 2027. The Academic Clinician position has a 90% clinical care component, with 10% of time devoted to a combination of scholarly activities (teaching, quality improvement, and administrative service). The combined responsibilities will depend on the successful candidates\u2019 qualifications, experience, and the needs of the specific hospital site. The main clinical responsibilities of an AIM Academic Clinician include daytime inpatient Most Responsible Physician (MRP) work and nocturnist work at both TGH and TWH. As this program is expanding, there is the opportunity for additional service lines including non-MRP consult work, including consultations from the Emergency Department. In-house nocturnal clinical work is a requirement for this position (currently 12 - 16 nocturnal shifts per year for a 1.0 FTE).\u00a0 Including nocturnal work and weekends, total clinical work is in the range of 24-36 weeks per year as decided by the successful candidates, the Division Head of GIM & Geriatrics, and the AIM team leadership. The successful candidate will demonstrate flexibility and responsiveness across clinical sites and service lines. Responsibilities may encompass both consultative and MRP care for a variety of patients, including those receiving oncology, surgical, and nephrology care. As the AIM program continues to expand, team members will be expected to support the implementation of new service lines. The successful candidates must hold MD qualifications, be certified (or be eligible for certification) by the College of Family Physicians of Canada or the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada in Internal Medicine or hold international equivalent and be licensed (or be eligible for licensure) by the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario. The successful candidates will possess strong communication, organization and interpersonal skills.\u00a0 A strong interest and experience in hospitalist medicine would be an asset. Successful candidates will be appointed to the UHN Division of General Internal Medicine or the UHN Department of Family Community Medicine. Academic rank, salary and contractual arrangements will be commensurate with the qualifications and experience of the successful candidates. Compensation will be within the usual income range for an academic hospitalist in the Province of Ontario (estimated range is $300,000-$350,000 per year), achieved through a combination of fee for service and stipends for nocturnal call shifts. Applications will be accepted until December 15th or until the positions are filled. Interested individuals should submit their letter of intent, curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for three references to: Jessica Liu, MD MSc FRCPC Division Director \u2013 General Internal Medicine and Geriatrics University Health Network and Sinai Health System c/o Sharon Yun Toronto Western Hospital, 399 Bathurst St. 8EW Room 400, Toronto, ON M5T 2S8 Tel 416 603-5800 x 5965 Sharon.yun@uhn.ca CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. For more information about the Departments of Medicine and Family and Community Medicine at the University of Toronto, please visit our websites at www.deptmedicine.utoronto.ca . The Department of Medicine\u2019s academic position descriptions can be viewed here , under the position Academic Clinician. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Geriatric, Oncology, Internal Medicine, Emergency Medicine, Academic, Healthcare, Education Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Associate-Professor-Genitourinary-Pathologist-ON/607267117/": {"title": "Assistant/ Associate/ Professor", "description": "Assistant/ Associate/ Professor - Genitourinary Pathologist Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant/ Associate/ Professor - Genitourinary Pathologist Date Posted: 10/22/2026 Closing Date: 12/01/2026 , 11:59PM ET Open until Filled Req ID: 50684 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Lab. Medicine & Pathobiology Hospital Affiliation: Sunnybrook Health Science Centre Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Sunnybrook Health Sciences Centre, an academic teaching hospital fully affiliated with the University of Toronto, is seeking a permanent Genitourinary Pathologist to join the Division of Anatomic Pathology, Department of Laboratory Medicine and Molecular Diagnostics (LMMD), Precision Diagnostics and Therapeutics Program. The successful candidate should be eligible for an academic appointment at the rank of Assistant, Associate or full Professor in the Department of Laboratory Medicine at the University of Toronto. The start date will be September 1, 2027, or as mutually agreed on. We are seeking a physician who will foster excellence in Genitourinary pathology, education and research at the hospital. The qualified applicant shall hold a medical degree and relevant Fellowship from the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada or equivalent, a clinical fellowship in GU pathology and be eligible for medical licensure in the Province of Ontario.\u00a0 As a major cancer centre, the candidate will have clinical responsibilities in the area of Genitourinary pathology. Demonstrated ability in research with a record of publications and presentations would be an asset. Other duties include participating in on-call coverage, frozen sections and autopsy service. A fully accredited Anatomic Pathology residency program is in place and teaching of residents, fellows and medical students is expected. English is the primary language of work. The successful candidate should be eligible for an academic appointment in the Department of Laboratory Medicine and Pathobiology at the University of Toronto.\u00a0 Rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the uniform minimal level of compensation for laboratory physicians in the Province of Ontario ($418,000 per annum). Members of the Division of Anatomic Pathology at Sunnybrook will participate in teaching, research and quality improvement activities. The Division enjoys close and dynamic interactions with the other Divisions of the Department including hematopathology, molecular, transfusion medicine, microbiology and biochemistry. Interested individuals should submit a letter of application, a curriculum vitae, and the names and addresses of three referees to the Chair of the Search Committee: Dr Michelle Downes MD FRCPC Head, Division of Anatomic Pathology, Sunnybrook Health Sciences Centre 2075 Bayview Avenue, Room B2-04 Toronto, Ontario, M4N 3M5. Please send applications to michelle.downes@sunnybrook.ca Cc: lesley.nicholson@sunnybrook.ca The Search Committee will consider applications received by December 1, 2026 for shortlisting. \u00a0The position will remain open until filled. \u00a0Only short-listed applicants will be contacted. CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the UofT affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. As one of the largest departments of its kind, the Department of Laboratory Medicine and Pathobiology (LMP) has more than 450 faculty including basic scientists, pathologists, laboratory physicians and scientists. By combining research with clinical practice, we are uniquely positioned to translate new findings into reality. As a result, we are known as leaders in diagnosing and treating patients and populations, making an impact locally, nationally and internationally. For more information about the Department of Laboratory Medicine and Pathobiology, University of Toronto please visit our website at www.lmp.utoronto.ca . Sunnybrook Health Sciences Centre plays a leadership role in the Ontario Health Teams system and in caring for its North Toronto community and beyond through eleven comprehensive care programs: Holland Bone & Joint; Hurvitz Brain Sciences; Odette Cancer; Dan Women & Babies; Schulich Heart Centre; Tory Trauma; St. John\u2019s Rehabilitation; Precision Diagnostics and Therapeutics Program; Integrated Surgical; Veterans; and Integrated Community. Discovery is facilitated by the Sunnybrook Research Institute (SRI), one of the fastest growing hospital-based research enterprises in Canada with over 300 scientists in basic and applied research conducting >$100 million in research each year. \u00a0Of note, Laboratory Medicine forms a major pillar of the Sunnybrook strategic plan targeting personalized and precise treatment whereby predictive and therapeutic technologies are being utilized in physical and biological sciences to invent the future of healthcare. On the teaching front, Sunnybrook is committed to high quality inter-professional education and is the home of the University of Toronto Peters Boyd Academy for undergraduate medical education. \u00a0Sunnybrook also features postgraduate and fellowship training with an outstanding reputation for delivering rewarding educational experiences to more than 5,000 student learners from over thirty health disciplines, including 1,300 residents and fellows per year. To learn more about Sunnybrook, please visit our home page. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Pathology, Rehabilitation, Biochemistry, Microbiology, Healthcare, Science, Research Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Engineer-B-ON/607286117/": {"title": "Engineer B Job Details", "description": "Engineer B Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Engineer B Date Posted: 10/22/2026 Req ID: 50704 Faculty/Division: University of Toronto Scarborough Department: UTSC:FM-Power Plant Campus : University of Toronto Scarborough (UTSC) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About Us: The University of Toronto Scarborough is a place of energy, enthusiasm and passion. Our commitment to inclusive excellence attracts the brightest learners, scholars and employees from around the globe. Our success has been made possible by the opportunity given to us by our Indigenous hosts to operate on their territory, and we cherish our continuing partnerships with these communities. The University of Toronto Scarborough is an exciting campus with unlimited potential. Join us on our journey. As part of the Facilities Management department the Engineering Operations is responsible for the monitoring, operation and maintenance of building utility services. This group of Engineers are responsible for monitoring, control, maintenance and repair of the utilities distribution networks throughout the University of Toronto Scarborough to ensure a safe, secure and equitable environment for students, staff, faculty and visitors. This search aligns with the University\u2019s commitment to strategically and proactively promote diversity among our community members ( Statement on Equity, Diversity & Excellence ). Recognizing that Black, Indigenous, and other Racialized communities have experienced inequities that have developed historically and are ongoing, we strongly welcome and encourage candidates from those communities to apply. General Description of Class: Under the direction of the Assistant Director, Engineering and Physical Plant and/or the Lead Hand, Engineer, the incumbent is responsible for assisting in the shift operation of the Central Plant, district heating system, co-generation, heat recovery installation and other campus equipment governed by TSSA regulations. The shift engineer is responsible for the safe and economical operation and maintenance of all mechanical and associated equipment and services in their area of responsibility, including visiting campus buildings during emergency calls. Typical Duties: The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required and the extent of responsibility involved in this job; they in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated: Regular rounds to check mechanical equipment and perform needed mechanical service; Ensures continuous efficiency of all mechanical equipment services; Provides running maintenance by checking lube levels of compressors and adjustments to all equipment and controls; Answers and reacts promptly to all trouble calls or alarms from buildings, as well as from adjacent nearby buildings during off hour and weekend shifts; Reviews computer printouts and alarms and takes appropriate action; Co-ordinates and/or assists outside contractors and University of Toronto Trades Services when work is performed during shift; Housekeeping, painting, sweeping floors, cleaning piping, boilers and equipment; Responds to off duty calls to correct emergency situations and problems; Maintains daily log sheets on operating equipment and records all important events that occur during shift and communications with relief shift engineer on event issues: Minimum Requirements: Education: High School graduate or equivalent combination of education and experience, and a Third (3rd) Class Operating Engineer Certification valid in the Province of Ontario. Building Environmental Systems Certificate an asset. Experience: Minimum of one year of experience as an operating engineer. Must have a good working knowledge of the operation and maintenance of mechanical equipment, including refrigeration, heating (e.g., boilers) and air handling systems, and ability to comprehend and apply environmental control principles. Must have basic electrical knowledge and trouble-shooting skills, basic proficiency in standard office computer applications (e.g., Microsoft Word, Excel) and familiarity with computerized Building Automation Systems or other computerized control systems. Other: Must have good diagnostic and record keeping skills, the ability to communicate effectively (both orally and written), strong customer service skills and the ability to work collaboratively with others. Applicants are also expected to show evidence of a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment. Assets: Possession of a valid class \"G\" drivers licence is an asset. Work Schedule: Rotating 8-hour shifts, 40 hours/week. Must be available for day, afternoon, and night shifts (including weekends and statutory holidays). Closing Date: 11/02/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: Unifor FT L2003 Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: 04U - Job Rate: $43.13/hr Job Category: Engineering / Technical Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Power Plant Operator, Power Plant, Housekeeping, HVAC, Energy, Healthcare, Operations, Hospitality Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Mississauga-Shift-Engineer-%283rd-Class%29-ON/607272717/": {"title": "Shift Engineer (3rd Class) Job Details", "description": "Shift Engineer (3rd Class) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Shift Engineer (3rd Class) Date Posted: 10/22/2026 Req ID: 50676 Faculty/Division: UofT Mississauga Department: UTM: Facilities, Management & Planning Campus: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Under the direction of the Assistant Manager Utilities & Elevator Services, the incumbent is responsible for the safe and economical operation and maintenance of all Utilities equipment and associated services for all buildings on UTM campus. The incumbent is also responsible to the Chief Operating Engineer for operation of the Central Utilities Plant. Typical Duties The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required and the extent of responsibility involved in this job; they in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated: a.\u00a0 Regular rounds of mechanical equipment and Utilities services such as checking equipment temperatures and pressures, conducting water chemical treatment tests, changing filters, regenerating softeners and de-alkalized water equipment, etc.; b.\u00a0 Performance of running maintenance and minor repair, i.e. including packing of glands, changing of belts, strip down and minor repair to equipment including valves, steam traps, pressure reducing stations, control valves and other similar equipment. Providing emergency repairs to laboratory, classrooms and environmental rooms; c.\u00a0 Providing accurate details of routine monthly surveys and meter readings of equipment and facilities; d.\u00a0 Carrying out assigned inspection and preventative maintenance of all equipment, as per preventative maintenance work orders (i.e. Service Now); e.\u00a0 Keeping close check on the proper operation of all equipment in buildings under the Building Management System; f.\u00a0 Answering and responding promptly to all trouble calls or alarms during off hours and weekend shifts; g.\u00a0 Responding to calls from Campus Safety to correct emergency situations and problems on off shifts, weekends, and after hours; h.\u00a0 Obtaining assistance from outside contractors and other engineers as the situation dictates during off hours and weekends; assisting outside contractors when work is performed during shift; i.\u00a0 Coordinating shut down work required for repairing or restoring service with outside contractors; j.\u00a0 Maintaining daily log sheets on operating equipment, recording important breakdowns, malfunctions and events that occur during the shift; k.\u00a0 Operation and testing of fire alarm system, sprinkler system, fire pumps and emergency lighting; l.\u00a0 Maintaining adequate inventory of chemicals and spare parts; m.\u00a0 Advising the Assistant Manager or Lead Hands about problems which are considered to be outside of his/her scope of operation. Qualifications Education: High School graduate or equivalent combination of education and experience plus a Third (3rd) Class Operating Engineer Certification valid in the Province of Ontario. Building Environmental Systems Certificate an asset. Experience: Minimum of one (1) year experience as an operating engineer. Must have a good working knowledge of the operation and maintenance of mechanical equipment, including refrigeration, heating (e.g. boilers) and air handling systems, and ability to comprehend and apply environmental control principles.\u00a0 Must have: basic electrical knowledge and trouble-shooting skills, basic proficiency in standard office computer applications (e.g. Microsoft Word, Excel, Windows OS) and familiarity with computerized Building Automation Systems or other computerized control systems. Other: Must have: good diagnostic and record keeping skills, the ability to communicate effectively (both orally and written), strong customer service skills and the ability to work collaboratively with others. Hours of Work: This position is for a shift engineer who will rotate between night, afternoon and day shifts.\u00a0 Rotation includes weekdays and weekends.\u00a0 Night shift hours are 11:30 PM to 7:30 AM, afternoon shift hours are 3:30 PM to 11:30 PM and day shift hours are 7:30 AM to 3:30 PM. Closing Date: 11/02/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: Unifor FT L2003 Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: Job Rate - - $43.13/hour Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Chemical Research, Electrical, Engineer, Engineering, Night, Operations Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Manager%2C-AMSSAP-Platform-Administration-and-Support-ON/607265917/": {"title": "Manager, AMS/SAP Platform Administration and Support Job Details", "description": "Manager, AMS/SAP Platform Administration and Support Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Manager, AMS/SAP Platform Administration and Support Date Posted: 10/22/2026 Req ID: 50128 Faculty/Division: VP-People, Finance & Digital Services Department: AMS/SAP Platform Administration and Support Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Reporting to the Associate Director, AMS/SAP, the incumbent manages a collaborative and highly skilled team responsible for the technical design, administration, security, operations, and continuous evolution of the University's SAP technical ecosystem. They provide leadership for the enterprise SAP platform, encompassing on-premises licenses and cloud-based SAP subscription technologies, SAP integration processes, supporting technology platforms, and the growing portfolio of third-party enterprise applications and services that extend and integrate with the University's SAP landscape. The incumbent collaborates closely with other EASI teams and the University\u2019s SAP-based application primary stakeholders to investigate, advise, and assist in formulating, advancing and maximizing the value of UofT\u2019s investment in SAP technology. The position will take a lead role in the value exploration of SAP-related technology, identifying opportunities to accelerate business innovation, gain efficiencies and transform mission-critical systems, and will inform EASI leadership and principal stakeholders on these opportunities. They will advise on and contribute to the University\u2019s SAP technical strategy and roadmap by researching, recommending and optimizing its enterprise SAP platform services and capabilities. The incumbent is responsible for ensuring the SAP technical environment is resilient, scalable, secure, and aligned with institutional standards, and business priorities. They oversee the planning, design, implementation, optimization, and lifecycle management of SAP platform services while ensuring the technical foundation supports reliable operations, future modernization initiatives, and evolving business capabilities. The incumbent will also work closely with ITS Information Security, SAP, other vendors, and specialists at peer universities to research, design, build and execute a sustainable technical environment, ensuring the University\u2019s SAP platform supports enterprise-level solutions that meet or exceed the standards, policies and security requirements of the University and technology best practices. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: EDUCATION: Undergraduate degree in a quantitative discipline (e.g., computer science, applied mathematics, engineering, statistics) or relevant combination of education and experience. EXPERIENCE: Minimum ten (10) years\u2019 related experience in a complex enterprise-level environment as a technical and project lead, designing, delivering and supporting institution-wide SAP solutions and their technology platforms which includes a minimum five (5) years of hands-on SAP BASIS administration, SAP Configuration and ABAP development experience. Strong experience with Microsoft Azure cloud, SAP solutions design, SAP Agile methodology and project planning, streamlining operational processes, and technical leadership. Experience in using DevOps and Agile methodologies. Experience leading complex and diverse, multi-stakeholder projects. Experience in negotiating sensitive and complex agreements. Experience in team building, training, mentoring, and managing highly technical staff. Experience negotiating with service providers, establishing and monitoring service level agreements. SKILLS: Strong experience and hands-on administration and troubleshooting of the SAP Platform resources including but not limited to: SAP Configuration, SAP BASIS Administration, SAP Solution Manager, SAP Integration Suite and PI, SAP Security, SAP Single Sign-On, SAP HANA, S4/HANA, SAP Fiori, SAP Enterprise Portal, SAP Content Server, SAP Business Technology Platform, DB2. Azure Cloud Administration. Strong skills with technical solutions design, system planning, development and design, networking and computer infrastructure, capacity management, disaster recovery planning, changeover planning for complex and critical enterprise applications. Highly adept at conducting research into technical or project-related products and issues, to continually improve solutions and processes as technology changes. Exceptional business acumen, and ability to liaise with and gain agreement from a broad range of internal and external stakeholders. Strong writing, communication, presentation and interpersonal skills with the ability to produce high quality, comprehensive communications materials and articulate complex ideas to both technical and non-technical audiences. Strong team and technical leadership skills. Demonstrated skills to simultaneously lead multiple complex projects in ambiguous situations, with multiple interruption and conflicting deadlines. Superior organizational skills in planning, project management and task coordination. Excellent hands-on knowledge of systems analysis, specifications techniques, process streamlining and implementation strategies, including DevOps concepts and strategies. Thorough knowledge of software development frameworks and models. Ability to work both independently and in a team-oriented, collaborative environment. Adept at conforming to shifting priorities, demands and timelines. Strong ability to elicit cooperation and collaboration from a wide variety of sources, including upper management, stakeholders, and other departments. Excellent conflict resolution skills with strong ability to exercise judgement, tact, discretion and determination. Adept at quickly learning, understanding, and applying new technologies and process frameworks. SAP Solution Architecture Certification preferred. OTHER: Exceptional leadership and teamwork skills with the ability to work and deliver under pressure. High degree of political acuity and judgement - must be able to collaborate, influence and cooperate with team members, technical specialists, and divisional stakeholders at various levels, in a manner that facilitates cooperation and consensus building. Must be able to deal calmly and effectively with a variety of people. Ability to abstract institutionally focused business problems in order to support the development of new and more efficient solutions. Strong functional knowledge of the University\u2019s business domain. Ability to work independently with a high degree of initiative, discretion, and tact. Strong analytical skills with the ability to take business requirements and abstract them into models and concepts. Proven people and relationship manager with the ability to build an exceptional and dedicated team, and a strong communicator who will establish regular and consistent communications with EASI leadership, ITS partners and divisional stakeholders advising on projects, technology, performance, and opportunities. Excellent decision-making skills. Ability to interpret University policy with regards to maintenance and access of information. Ability to keep abreast of current issues in relevant technology and up to date with best practices. Ability to identify the need to arrange for the provision of education in the use of supported products. Closing Date: 11/06/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 4 -- Hiring Zone: $110,973 - $129,471 -- Broadband Salary Range: $110,973 - $184,957 Job Category: Information Technology (IT) Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Cloud, Relationship Manager, SAP, Solution Architect, ERP, Technology, Customer Service Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Information-Services-Representative-ON/607269417/": {"title": "Information Services Representative Job Details", "description": "Information Services Representative Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Information Services Representative Date Posted: 10/22/2026 Req ID: 50700 Faculty/Division: VP & Provost Department: Hart House Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00060140 Existing Vacancy: No About us: Hart House is a centre for experiential education outside the classroom at the University of Toronto. Since it opened in 1919, Hart House functions as a place where students, faculty, staff, alumni and members of the broader community connect with each other and the world. Through an array of co-curricular programming in the arts, dialogue and wellness, Hart House works with local and international partners to foster community and to create innovative learning opportunities for students. Hart House operates from a historic facility on the St. George campus, as well as a 150-acre farm in Caledon, Ontario, offering a wide range of services through a social enterprise model that generates revenue to support its student-focused programming on all three University of Toronto campuses. The Information Services Desk is a dynamic focal point within Hart House where administrative functions related to a wide range of services and sales \u2013 e.g., registration for classes, memberships and other service offerings for Hart House, ticket sales for Hart House Theatre, reservations for the Hart House Fitness Centre \u2013 as well as providing general information about Hart House and the university, are performed. The Information Services Desk provides our diverse community an open door, welcoming them to enjoy a multitude of activities and services at Hart House. Your opportunity: The Information Services Representative is directly supervised by the Manager, Information & Customer Service and plays a role in supporting the Information Services team. The incumbent will work in close collaboration with the Information Services Associates and Fitness, Wellness and Recreation team to this end with a focus on the facilitation of strong customer service at service points within the building. They will also be responsible to support and provide guidance to non-appointed staff. The incumbent will act as the first point of contact for general inquiries and will be providing routine and detailed information on programs and events. They will direct information to visitors on eligibility requirements, procedures, and policies for Hart House facilities. The incumbent will be responsible for collating and organizing materials, maintaining emergency contact lists, booking rooms, ensuring responsiveness to inquiries, and maintaining daily reports. They will also handle incoming and outgoing mail and deliveries and liaise with facilities or caretaking staff to address any building issues. This role will be responsible for following rules and procedural instructions when opening and/or closing the Information Services Desk. Your responsibilities will include: Acting as the first point of contact for general inquiries, providing routine information on programs, events, and eligibility requirements Applying established standards when responding to emergencies and redirecting inquiries as appropriate Booking rooms and arranging accommodations, ensuring efficient and appropriate use of spaces Resolving minor complaints within the scope of the role and referring larger issues to the appropriate channels Checking eligibility of students to access the facility and maintaining control over the distribution of access to designated University spaces Supporting the Information Services team in providing information on programs and services to internal and external contacts Assisting with registrations, maintaining databases, generating reports, conducting regular checks and balancing financial transactions against sales Serving as a resource to others by providing (non-supervisory) administrative guidance Essential Qualifications: High School Diploma or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum of two years of experience in customer service Minimum of one year experience in a high-volume, multi-service customer service environment involving cash/point-of-sale transactions, scheduling/reservations, and in person conflict resolution Demonstrated experience with providing job-related guidance to others Demonstrated experience de-escalating conflict with members of the public, including handling complaints, denying access/service when policy requires it, and managing frustrated or distressed patrons Excellent personal and human relation skills Computer skills required: Microsoft Office Suite. Keyboarding skills. Familiarity with or ability to quickly learn Fusion software to maintain membership database and online registrations is essential Must be able to work collaboratively and professionally as part of a team while also being capable to work independently when required An energetic individual who enjoys the challenge of work in a dynamic environment Excellent customer service, interpersonal skills, good judgment and initiative Strong sales orientation Accuracy along with the ability to multi-task is essential Demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion in all work responsibilities and in collaborative workplace practices Fluent in written and spoken English Ability to work under pressure First Aid/CPR Training is required and will be provided Assets (Nonessential): Experience with Fusion and/or Audience View a notable asset Experience with POS equipment Experience in a higher education context is preferred Fluency in second or more languages would be an asset Experience or knowledge in fitness, health or recreation promotion Knowledge and experience of for the University of Toronto and/or Hart House programs and services To be successful in this role you will be: Accountable Adaptable Patient Possess a positive attitude Self-directed Team player Notes: Hours of work: Tuesday through Saturday from 2:45 PM to 11:00 PM A cover letter is required with your application. Closing Date: 10/30/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 04 -- $52,327 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $66,919. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Divisional HR Office Email: cahrs.hr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Customer Service Representative, Facilities, Equity, Database, Customer Service, Operations, Finance, Technology Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Manager%2C-Core-Research-Operations-ON/607266117/": {"title": "Manager, Core Research Operations Job Details", "description": "Manager, Core Research Operations Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Manager, Core Research Operations Date Posted: 10/22/2026 Req ID: 50699 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Ofc Vice Dean, Research & Health Sci Edu Campus : St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About Us Home to over 40 departments and institutes, the University of Toronto's Temerty Faculty of Medicine lies at the heart of the Toronto Academic Health Science Network and is a global leader in ground-breaking research and education, spanning clinical medicine, basic science and the rehabilitation sciences sectors. Your Opportunity The Office of the Vice Dean, Research, Innovation & Health Science Education (VDRIHSE) oversees all research undertaken for the Temerty Faculty of Medicine and coordinates with its counterparts at the affiliated hospital research institutes for clinical research. This includes grant proposal development, administering internal funding allocations, collecting and reporting on research productivity metrics, and managing core research facilities. As Manager, Core Research Operations, you will support all aspects of research operational management, development, and administration for the core facilities within the VDRIHSE. Reporting to the Director and working closely with the core facility academic leads, you will drive initiatives to maximize research funding opportunities for sustainability, oversee daily unit operations, and supervise technical and research operations teams while ensuring that core facilities spaces are appropriately allocated for maximum operational efficiency. Additionally, you will shape the future of the core units by creating short- and long-term strategic plans and launching continuous improvement initiatives that drive service excellence and financial sustainability. This includes partnering with peer facilities (Division of Comparative Medicine) and associated TAHSN-wide core service delivery units to uncover new funding streams and champion opportunities for strategic partnership and service consolidation. Qualifications PhD degree in a relevant scientific discipline or an acceptable equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum of five (5) years related experience in a research administration and operations role in a University or hospital research institute. Demonstrated experience overseeing research operations, including financial management, resource allocation and human resources management. Prior research managerial experience in a basic research institute required, along with experience supporting core research facilities. Experience managing and reporting on research funds including infrastructure grants. Experience leading, and supervising high-functioning teams, with a strong preference for candidates who have successfully led staff and interpreted collective agreements within a unionized environment using established HR policies and procedures. Experience supporting end-to-end grant lifecycles, from pre-award proposal development for multi-site grants to post-award milestone and financial reporting for major federal, provincial and institutional awards. Experience overseeing facility health and safety programs, including preparing and coordinating biosafety permit applications. Advanced proficiency with M365. Proven leadership and management skills, including excellent interpersonal, communication and presentation skills. Excellent problem-solving ability, organizational and planning skills. Ability to maintain a broad perspective and foster effective relationships with all levels of faculty, staff, students, senior administration and external constituents. Ability to work in a collaborative and collegial manner, with an appreciation for the challenges and opportunities of working within a large, decentralized institution. Ability to train, coach, and motivate staff to work collaboratively toward the goals of the office. Ability to work independently and as part of a team, with a high level of initiative and resourcefulness, including the ability to manage deadlines and prioritize work. Ability to maintain confidentiality. Knowledge of chemical and biological hazards related to research. Assets: Knowledge and experience using the University\u2019s Administrative Management System Closing Date: 11/05/2026,11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Grant - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 4 -- Hiring Zone: $110,973 - $129,471 -- Broadband Salary Range: $110,973 - $184,957 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Operations Manager, Medical Research, Clinical Research, HR, Operations, Healthcare, Research, Human Resources Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Project-Manager%2C-Finance-Initiatives-ON/607260017/": {"title": "Project Manager, Finance Initiatives Job Details", "description": "Project Manager, Finance Initiatives Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Project Manager, Finance Initiatives Date Posted: 10/22/2026 Req ID: 50690 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Office of the CAO Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00055694 Description: About Us The Temerty Faculty of Medicine at the University of Toronto is at the centre of one of North America\u2019s largest biomedical research, education and clinical care networks. With 14 fully affiliated research-intensive hospitals \u2014 and dozens more community and clinical care sites \u2014 Temerty Medicine offers unparalleled opportunities in Canada\u2019s most dynamic city for our more than 9,000 faculty and staff and 7,000 learners at all levels. Your Opportunity As Project Manager, Finance Initiatives, you will serve as a strategic partner to the Dean\u2019s Executive team, leading project management and financial analysis for the Temerty Faculty of Medicine\u2019s Budget Model Review and implementation planning. Reporting to the Chief Administrative Officer, and working closely with the Office of the Chief Financial Officer and Comptroller, you will evaluate the current budget framework, analyze revenue and cost drivers, develop scenarios and impact analyses, and present clear financial briefings that translate complex data into actionable insights for Faculty leadership. Your proven ability to evaluate processes, identify and articulate vulnerabilities and obstacles, and collaborate with key partners to deliver quality business solutions will help us enhance our operational agility and innovation. Essential Qualifications University degree, and/or acceptable equivalent combination of education and experience in financial accounting Minimum four (4) years\u2019 experience of progressively senior accounting, financial analysis and budgeting experience Proven experience with business intelligence tools, data analytics and data visualizations Experience conducting financial research, producing reports and presenting on findings Experience presenting complex financial data to senior leadership, including experience facilitating and steering governance committees toward actionable outcomes Extensive experience managing complex and multi-stakeholder financial projects, including leading, organizing and tracking the outcomes of projects Significant communications experience with demonstrated success in implementing an integrated communications strategy Extensive experience with university budgeting and fund accounting Significant experience with administrative management systems (FIS, HRIS and RIS) Strong technical skills, including advanced proficiency with MS Power BI and MS Excel, and a facility for working with project management tools and keep current with new and emerging technologies Proven commitment to equity, diversity and inclusivity Must be an articulate and effective communicator, both verbal and written Must possess excellent interpersonal and diplomacy skills, and the ability to build collaborative relationships at all levels with proven ability to exhibit tact and diplomacy in sensitive situations Advanced consulting skills, with the ability to work across the organization to influence decisions for a positive outcome Strong business acumen and negotiation skills; ability to deal with senior University leaders in a manner which facilitates cooperation and consensus building Strong organization skills with the ability to effectively prioritize and execute tasks in a high-pressure environment Highly detail oriented with proven analytical and conceptual thinking skills Ability to work under pressure with shifting priorities; high degree of political acuity and judgment Ability to lead and assemble working groups and committees to discuss and assess projects that require input from many stakeholders and provide leadership to guide and oversee their efforts Must be able to conduct thorough research, concisely summarize information and provide a rationale for action Demonstrated ability to plan and execute complex projects and manage conflicting priorities while working toward tight deadlines Ability to take the initiative and respond to change Closing Date: 11/12/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 3 -- Hiring Zone: $97,336 - $113,558 -- Broadband Salary Range: $97,336 - $162,224 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Recruiter: Dinuka Perera Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Project Manager, Business Intelligence, Equity, HRIS, Technology, Research, Finance, Human Resources Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Research-Officer-ON/607268717/": {"title": "Research Officer Job Details", "description": "Research Officer Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Research Officer Date Posted: 10/22/2026 Req ID: 50701 Faculty/Division: UofT Scarborough Department: UTSC:Dept-Psychology Campus: University of Toronto Scarborough (UTSC) Position Number: 00060160 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The University of Toronto Scarborough is a place of energy, enthusiasm and passion. Our commitment to inclusive excellence attracts the brightest learners, scholars and employees from around the globe. Our success has been made possible by the opportunity given to us by Indigenous hosts to operate on their territory, and we cherish our continuing partnerships with these communities. The University of Toronto Scarborough is an exciting campus with unlimited potential. Join us on our journey. The Department of Psychology at the University of Toronto Scarborough is a vibrant, research and teaching intensive department. In addition to providing students with deep grounding in one or more disciplinary traditions, the Department also fosters research at all levels. Its commitment to socially engaged, leading edge research and direct engagement with its community is reflected not only through its curriculum but also in the creative and innovative projects undertaken by faculty and often providing research opportunities for graduate and undergraduate students. Working alongside faculty, a team of dedicated staff members provide administrative services and support the daily operation of a department that is committed to promoting equity, diversity and inclusion to help create a truly rich and engaging student experience. Your opportunity: The Department of Psychological Clinical Science is home to a world-class MA/PhD program in Clinical Psychology that integrates rigorous scientific research with clinical training. The Clinical Neurosciences Laboratory, led by Dr. Anthony C. Ruocco, brings together clinical psychology and neuroscience to advance understanding of mental health, inform suicide prevention, and improve assessment and intervention. The research combines psychological assessment, cognitive testing, and magnetic resonance imaging of the brain to investigate questions with meaningful implications for individuals, families, and communities. As the Research Officer, you will play a key role in supporting the successful delivery of research studies by fostering and maintaining positive relationships with project partners such as research assistants, graduate students, MRI staff, and referral partners. You will provide general orientation on study procedures, and will support the consistency and effective study operations. You will monitor and track research activities, accurately record and organize experimental data and results, and maintain the integrity and confidentiality of research records. Working closely with the Principal Investigator, you will support participant engagement and longitudinal follow-up activities, and coordinate daily study operations, including participant scheduling, preparation of consent forms, distribution and collection of surveys and questionnaires, and verification of financial transactions. In addition, you will exercise sound judgment in addressing routine issues, safeguarding sensitive and confidential information, and escalating concerns or matters requiring input or approval to the Principal Investigator. Strong organizational skills, meticulous attention to detail, and a compassionate and sensitive approach will be essential in working with participants who will contribute to research focused on improving suicide prevention. Your responsibilities will include: Fostering positive relationships with project partners Tracking and monitoring research activities Informing Principal Investigator of concerns or setbacks Collecting experimental data, verifying results and passing on findings Recording and tabulating experiment results Scheduling study participants Disseminating and collecting research surveys and questionnaires Handling sensitive and/or confidential information Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in psychology, neuroscience, or a related field. Minimum two years of related experience supporting and coordinating studies involving human participants Experience working with people experiencing mental health challenges Experience coordinating and formatting research data into reports, maintaining accurate records within a database and conducting data quality checks Demonstrated experience and understanding of informed consent, participant confidentiality, and secure handling of sensitive research information Experience tracking study financial information and coordinating process for participant compensation Proficiency with Microsoft Excel, Word, Outlook. Advanced proficiency with databases (i.e. REDCap) used to collect, track and compile research data, including participant registration, electronic consent forms, surveys and questionnaires, longitudinal data collection, participant study data and reporting. Strong organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to coordinate multiple activities, manage competing deadlines, and maintain accuracy. Excellent interpersonal skills, discretion, and a respectful, sensitive approach to working with people from diverse backgrounds. Demonstrated ability to work independently, resolve routine problems, follow established protocols, and recognize when consultation or escalation is required Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, graduate students, research assistants, and clinical and imaging partners and provide general orientation with respect to study procedures Must be willing to travel and work on the St. George campus to support participants with their MRI scanning appointments. Will be required to work some Saturdays (approximately once per month). Applicants are expected to show evidence of a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment. Assets (Nonessential): Experience preparing participants regarding safety screening prior to MRI scanning To be successful in this role you will be: Approachable Communicator Meticulous Organized Problem solver Resourceful Tactful NOTE: This is a two (2) years TERM position. Closing Date: 11/08/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Grant - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 07 -- $62,646 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $80,116. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Research Administration & Teaching Divisional HR Office Email: humanresources.utsc@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Counseling, Medical Research, Clinical Research, Research Scientist, Healthcare, Research, Science Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Recruitment-Process-Coordinator-ON/607264017/": {"title": "Recruitment Process Coordinator", "description": "Recruitment Process Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Recruitment Process Coordinator Date Posted: 10/22/2026 Req ID: 50605 Faculty/Division: University of Toronto Co-op Department: University of Toronto Co-op Campus: Tri-Campus Position Number: 00056267 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The University of Toronto, Canada\u2019s top-ranked university, is a place of energy, enthusiasm, and passion. Our commitment to inclusive excellence attracts the brightest learners, scholars, and employees from around the globe. Our success has been made possible by the opportunity given to us by our Indigenous hosts to operate on their territory, and we cherish our continuing partnerships with these communities. The University of Toronto has committed to an expansion of experiential learning opportunities for students, to enhance both the student learning experience and the University\u2019s ability to support broader community and societal needs. Each of U of T\u2019s three campuses are directing significant resources and energy into expanding experiential learning, particularly work integrated learning (WIL) programming such as co-op and internships. Our goal is to ensure our graduates remain amongst the most employable in the world. The Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering\u2019s Professional Experience Year (PEY) Co-op, the Faculty of Art & Science\u2019s Arts & Science Internship Program (ASIP), the University of Toronto Scarborough\u2019s Arts & Science Co-op and Management Co-op programs and the new UTM Co-op Internship program facilitate co-op and internship opportunities for more than 3,500 students from over 150 academic programs annually. These programs allow students to apply their academic learning in a real-world context, build valuable professional networks and skills, and explore career options. The five programs have formed a unique collaborative partnership called the Tri-Campus Co-op Partnership (TCP) that amplifies the strengths of the five programs, provides a seamless recruiting experience for employers, and expand the depth and breadth of work term opportunities available to TCP co-op and internship students. The mandate of the U of T Co-op Hub team remains tri-campus in scope, ensuring that all activities and initiatives serve the equal benefit of the entire U of T Co-op community. The team is linked administratively to the Scarborough campus, however, currently travels and works at all three campuses. This search aligns with the University\u2019s commitment to strategically and proactively promote diversity among our community members ( Statement on Equity, Diversity & Excellence ). Recognizing that Black, Indigenous, and other Racialized communities have experienced inequities that have developed historically and are ongoing, we strongly welcome and encourage candidates from those communities to apply. Your opportunity: Working under the direction of the Manager, Operations & Shared Services, the incumbent is part of the U of T Co-op Operations Hub which centrally supports the co-op student hiring process for all of the TCP co-op programs. The Recruitment Process Coordinator provides logistical support to our employer partners as they move through the co-op hiring process and is an important part of the employer\u2019s client support team along with their external relations colleagues. Providing excellence in customer service, the incumbent ensures that the employer\u2019s experience is seamless and positive, helping to make U of T every employer\u2019s destination of choice when choosing where to recruit co-op students. The Recruitment Process Coordinator will be responsible for overseeing the logistics of the hiring process for their assigned employers and ensuring that their corresponding external relations colleagues are well-informed on key strategic and partnership matters. The incumbent will vet and approve the co-op postings submitted by employers, ensure they are posted in a timely manner for co-op students to apply to in our shared system, alert the employer when and how student applications can be reviewed, arrange interviews, coordinate offers and complete all documentation needed in our shared system. In essence, the incumbent will be responsible for all communication and steps to encourage and facilitate the employers\u2019 posting(s) to efficiently move through the process to the ultimate outcome, a co-op student being hired. Together with their Operations Hub colleagues, the incumbent will monitor shared inboxes, respond to inquiries within their scope and triage other inquiries to teams across TCP. This includes monitoring inquiries from prospective employers and quickly distributing them to the appropriate external relations colleagues for expedient follow up. Working together with colleagues from five different programs and with many employers to support, the incumbent will thrive in a collaborative, team-oriented and fast-paced environment with a lot of moving parts. The incumbent will have very strong attention to detail and use their time management skills to work efficiently to keep all their tasks well-coordinated, organized and communicated. As a team player, the incumbent will support their other Operations Hub and TCP colleagues during peak periods to ensure that everyone is supported and processes flow efficiently. Your responsibilities will include: Providing detailed information on processes, policies, and procedures Liaising with contacts to ensure consistent administration procedures are followed Strengthening relationships with stakeholders and partners of strategic importance Acting as the first point of contact for program-related enquiries Creating and updating job postings in the database Coordinating interview schedules Updating and maintaining records Keeping well-informed on University programs, policies and procedures Essential Qualifications: Advanced College Diploma (3 years) or acceptable combination of equivalent experience Minimum of three (3) years of recent and related experience in a client-facing customer service role in an administrative setting and records and database administration Demonstrated experience working with a database and/or customer relationship management software, including data manipulation and reporting skills; advanced skills in Microsoft Excel required Very strong sense of customer service including delivering on time, friendly and supportive service to external partners and internal stakeholders Proven regard for stakeholder experience Excellent written and verbal communication skills Must be able to stay organized, multi-task, prioritize and meet deadlines while exercising accuracy and keen attention-to-detail Very strong time management skills Ability to work under time constraints and workload pressures while maintaining sound judgment, tact, diplomacy, discretion, confidentiality and professionalism when dealing with employer partners, staff, students, faculty and leadership Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite as well as the ability to adapt to and learn new technologies Demonstrated ability to coordinate efficient administrative processes and to maintain electronic filing systems Ability to work well in a team environment and maintain productive and respectful working relationships with all stakeholders Demonstrated behavior that indicates personal commitment to innovation, teamwork, flexibility, initiative, and integrity Applicants are expected to show evidence of a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment Assets (Nonessential): Experience working in a postsecondary environment Previous experience working in co-operative education departments or career services Experience with Symplicity\u2019s CSM platforms Experience working with Salesforce To be successful in this role you will be: Courteous Efficient Meticulous Organized Responsible Team player Notes: This role is currently eligible for a hybrid work arrangement, pursuant to University policies and guidelines, including but not limited to the University of Toronto\u2019s Alternative Work Arrangements Guideline . Closing Date: 11/01/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 09 -- $70,633 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $90,329. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Divisional HR Office Email: humanresources.utsc@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: CRM, Intern, Relationship Manager, DBA, Database, Technology, Entry Level, Customer Service Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Mississauga-Building-Engineer-%283rd-Class%29-ON/607263917/": {"title": "Building Engineer (3rd Class) Job Details", "description": "Building Engineer (3rd Class) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Building Engineer (3rd Class) Date Posted: 10/22/2026 Req ID: 50677 Faculty/Division: UofT Mississauga Department: UTM: Facilities, Management & Planning Campus: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Under the direction of the Assistant Manager Utilities & Elevator Services, the incumbent is responsible for the safe and economical operation and maintenance of all Utilities equipment and associated services for all buildings on the UTM campus.\u00a0 The incumbent is also responsible to the Chief Operating Engineer for operation of the Central Utilities Plant. Typical Duties The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required and the extent of responsibility\u00a0involved in this job; they in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated: a.\u00a0 Regular rounds of mechanical equipment and Utilities services such as: checking equipment temperatures and pressures, conducting water chemical treatment tests, changing filters, regenerating softeners and de-alkalized water equipment, etc.; b.\u00a0 Performance of running maintenance and minor repair, i.e. including packing of glands,\u00a0changing of belts, strip down and minor repair to equipment including valves, steam traps, pressure reducing stations, control valves and other similar equipment. Providing emergency repairs to laboratory, classrooms and environmental rooms; c.\u00a0 Providing accurate details of routine monthly surveys and meter readings of equipment and facilities; d.\u00a0 Carrying out assigned inspection and preventative maintenance of all equipment, as per preventative maintenance work orders (i.e., Service Now); e.\u00a0 Keeping close check on the proper operation of all equipment in buildings under the Building Management System; f.\u00a0 Answering and responding promptly to all trouble calls or alarms during off hours and weekend shifts; g.\u00a0 Responding to calls from Campus Safety to correct emergency situations and problems on off shifts, weekends, and after hours; h.\u00a0 Obtaining assistance from outside contractors and other engineers as the situation dictates during off hours and weekends; assisting outside contractors when work is performed during shift; i.\u00a0 Coordinating shut down work required for repairing or restoring service with outside contractors; j.\u00a0 Maintaining daily log sheets on operating equipment, recording important breakdowns, malfunctions and events that occur during the shift; k.\u00a0 Operation and testing of fire alarm system, sprinkler system, fire pumps and emergency lighting; l.\u00a0 Maintaining adequate inventory of chemicals and spare parts; m.\u00a0 Advising the Assistant Manager or Lead Hands about problems which are considered to be outside of his/her scope of operation. Qualifications Education: High School graduate or equivalent combination of education and experience plus a Third\u00a0(3rd) Class Operating Engineer Certification valid in the Province of Ontario. Building Environmental\u00a0Systems Certificate an asset. Experience: Minimum of one (1) year experience as an operating engineer. Must have a good\u00a0working knowledge of the operation and maintenance of mechanical equipment, including refrigeration,\u00a0heating (e.g. boilers) and air handling systems, and ability to comprehend and apply environmental\u00a0control principles.\u00a0 Must have: basic electrical knowledge and trouble-shooting skills, basic proficiency in\u00a0standard office computer applications (e.g. Microsoft Word, Excel, Windows OS) and familiarity with\u00a0computerized Building Automation Systems or other computerized control systems. Other: Must have: good diagnostic and record keeping skills, the ability to communicate effectively\u00a0(both orally and written), strong customer service skills and the ability to work collaboratively with\u00a0others. Hours of Work: The successful candidate will mostly carry out duties on a day shift, Monday to Friday, from 7:30 AM to 4 PM, with possible coverage for afternoon and /or night shifts on weekdays and/or weekends. Closing Date: 10/30/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: Unifor FT L2003 Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: Job Rate - - $43.13/hour Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Chemical Research, Electrical, Engineer, Inspector, HVAC, Engineering, Quality, Operations Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Dental-Assistant-ON/607289517/": {"title": "Dental Assistant", "description": "Dental Assistant Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Dental Assistant Date Posted: 10/26/2026 Req ID: 50623 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Dentistry Department: Faculty of Dentistry Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00032454 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Exciting new advances and global challenges are radically reshaping the field of dentistry. Our vision at the Faculty of Dentistry at the University of Toronto is to not just address and respond to these changes \u2013 but to thoughtfully and conscientiously shape the field of the future. With our robust and comprehensive educational training programs (DDS, MSc, PhD degrees, IDAPP and other specialty programs), our emphasis on community outreach and care, and our internationally known and interdisciplinary research mission, the Faculty of Dentistry at the University of Toronto continues to earn its reputation as one of the top dental schools in North America. Throughout more than 150 years of dental education -- the oldest, largest and most comprehensive training program in Canada -- we have striven to graduate the highest quality of students while providing the public the highest standards of care. We are driving by our vision to improve health by advancing dentistry through inspired leadership, innovation, and excellence in education, research and practice. Your opportunity: Under the general supervision of the manager, the incumbent provides dental assistant and administrative services to the undergraduate and graduate students, academic and administrative staff and performs all aspects of dental assisting as defined by the ODAA for regularly scheduled and special programs. The incumbent follows through with proper protocol for infection control in all aspects of clinical work, provides administrative services as directed for patients, both in person and on the telephone, accesses and enters data in order to retrieve patient information and book appointments , and assists in special assignments and other duties that are Faculty-related. Please note this is for a term position in our Undergraduate Clinics until the end of June 2027. Your responsibilities will include: Assisting faculty, dental students and technicians during treatment procedures Updating and maintaining database records Responding to enquiries within the defined scope of the role and redirecting as appropriate Applying established standards when cleaning, sanitizing and/orsterilizing facilities Applying established standards when administering biological and/or medical imaging Providing safety training and ensuring compliance to occupational safety precautions Following rules and procedural processrelated to Personal Health Information Protection Act (PHIPA) Essential Qualifications: Graduation from an accredited Dental Assistant program, Certified Dental Assistant (CDA) and current member of the ODAA,including HARP. Must also have current CPR. Minimum two years of experience in the dental field, encompassing all aspects of dentistry. Experience using all dental related materials and products (e.g. amalgams, impression materials, eugenols, disinfectants, put and fissure sealants, vinyl polysiloxanes, etc.). Highly developed organizational, time management, and communication skills and excellent interpersonal and problem-solving skills. Strong computer skills with experience in Microsoft Office. Capability to work in all facets relating to dentistry (e.g. mixing all materials). Ability to work quickly and accurately. Manual dexterity. Ability to work in close association and cooperation with others as part of a team. Demonstrated ability to exercise tact, discretion, good judgement, and initiative. Demonstrated ability to clearly and accurately convey information. Ability to prioritize tasks and multi-task; demonstrated punctuality, work dependability. Ability to act with sensitivity and empathy when responding to diverse groups of individuals. Assets (Nonessential): Familiarly with Axium To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Cooperative Courteous Efficient Multi-tasker Organized Please note this is for a term position in our Undergraduate Clinics until the end of June 2027. Closing Date: 11/04/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 06 -- $59,000 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $75,450. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Health & Wellbeing Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Infection Control, Equity, Information Security, Dental, Healthcare, Finance, Technology, Research Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Service-and-Technology-Delivery-Lead-ON/603172317/": {"title": "Service and Technology Delivery Lead Job Details", "description": "Service and Technology Delivery Lead Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Service and Technology Delivery Lead Date Posted: 10/20/2026 Req ID: 48436 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering Department: APSC Admin. Units Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering is a world-renowned community of researchers and students dedicated to solving some of the world's most pressing challenges through collaborative and multidisciplinary research and experiential education. Through rigorous technical training, and unparalleled extracurricular and professional experience opportunities, we prepare the next generation of engineering leaders and change makers to unlock the future's boundless potential. The Faculty IT Office works together to support a dedicated and diverse group of academic and administrative professionals who exemplify excellence in their fields. Your opportunity: Reporting to the Manager, Client Services, the Client Technology and Service Delivery Lead is responsible for ensuring effective and efficient client technology services through the planning, implementation, and continuous improvement of end-user computing and collaboration environments. The incumbent provides technical leadership and operational oversight for client services, guiding technical staff, resolving complex issues, and driving service maturity through workflow optimization, performance monitoring, and process improvement. Working closely with stakeholders, the role leads initiatives to enhance service delivery, optimize the use of enterprise platforms, and support teaching, research, and administrative functions across the Faculty. Your responsibilities will include: Leading and continuously improving technology service delivery by designing efficient workflows, establishing service standards, implementing system and service enhancements, and evaluating technologies and tools that enhance efficiency, reliability, user experience, and operational effectiveness. Providing technical leadership and guidance to support staff, including coordinating work, resolving escalations, and ensuring consistency in service delivery Monitoring and analyzing service performance, including defining key performance indicators and using data to inform improvements Supporting and optimizing endpoint and client technology environments, including deployment, configuration, and lifecycle management Troubleshooting complex technical issues and acting as an escalation point for system and service-related problems Leading and supporting initiatives and projects related to client technology services, including planning, coordination, and reporting Developing and maintaining documentation, training materials, and knowledge resources to support staff and end-users Supporting audio-visual and collaboration technologies through evaluation, troubleshooting, and continuous improvement of systems Essential Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in computer science, Information Technology, or acceptable combination of equivalent experience Minimum five (5) years of recent and related experience in a large, multi-unit and complex IT environment overseeing Tier 2/3 support and technical teams, with a strong client service orientation Minimum three (3) years of experience providing technical leadership to staff across a diverse range of end-user and enterprise computing environments, with experience in areas including BYOD strategies, print services, networking, and remote desktop technologies Demonstrated experience and strong understanding in endpoint and mobile device management across Windows and macOS platforms, including hardware and software management, device configuration, policy enforcement, and lifecycle support, using enterprise management platforms (e.g., Microsoft Intune, Quest KACE, or similar), with responsibility for software licensing, encryption, endpoint backup, anti-malware, and overall endpoint security management Demonstrated experience and strong understanding of Active Directory, Microsoft Entra ID, and endpoint identity management concepts, including Group Policy, security groups, authentication, and hybrid identity environments Demonstrated experience with endpoint deployment, including automation, scripting, or software packaging techniques. This extends to mobile device management, including configuration, policy enforcement, and lifecycle support of mobile devices. Proven hands-on IT Service Management (ITSM) implementation and administration experience with ServiceNow or an equivalent platform, including Change Management and Knowledge Management process design, implementation, and continuous improvement Demonstrated expert technical writing skills, including development of knowledge articles, technical documentation, standards, and operational procedures Demonstrated experience supporting audio-visual and collaboration technologies through evaluation, implementation, and ongoing optimization of systems, including coordination with external vendors for technology-enhanced spaces Demonstrated experience leveraging enterprise platforms to improve service delivery, automate workflows, enhance reporting, and drive process improvement. (e.g., Microsoft 365 tools such as SharePoint, Teams, Power BI, Power Automate or similar) Demonstrated experience analyzing service delivery performance and implementing process improvements Demonstrated ability to build relationships and communicate effectively with bothtechnical and non-technical stakeholders Strong time management and prioritization skills, with the ability to manage competing demands and shifting priorities High attention to detail and commitment to delivering consistent, high-quality service Strong analytical, problem-solving, and organizational skills Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Assets (Nonessential): Experience with data management and visualization toolsets such as Power BI considered a strong asset Expert/advanced Excel reporting and data mining capabilities are considered a very strong asset Proven aptitude for IT architecture and formulation of best practices in system design, implementation, administration and troubleshooting Familiarity with University policies and practices related to information technology and information security Proven aptitude for risk and security implementation in an operations environment Technical certifications related to endpoint management, cloud platforms, or service management (e.g., Microsoft Certified, PMP, ITIL) would be considered strong assets To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Meticulous Multi-tasker Organized Problem solver Resourceful Closing Date: 11/04/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Personnel Subarea: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 16 -- $107,502 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $137,476. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Information Technology (IT) Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Cloud, Audio Visual, Business Process, Data Mining, Technical Writer, Technology, Creative, Management Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Data-Specialist-&-Academic-HR-Coordinator-ON/607220817/": {"title": "Data Specialist & Academic HR Coordinator", "description": "Data Specialist & Academic HR Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Data Specialist & Academic HR Coordinator Date Posted: 10/21/2026 Req ID: 50624 Faculty/Division: University of Toronto Scarborough Department: UTSC:Human Resource Services Campus: University of Toronto Scarborough (UTSC) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: ABOUT US The University of Toronto Scarborough is a place of energy, enthusiasm and passion. Our commitment to inclusive excellence attracts the brightest learners, scholars and employees from around the globe. Our success has been made possible by the opportunity given to us by Indigenous hosts to operate on their territory, and we cherish our continuing partnerships with these communities. The University of Toronto Scarborough is an exciting campus with unlimited potential. Join us on our journey. Human Resource Services aims to enhance the University\u2019s mission by fostering a healthy, collaborative and equitable work environment that will attract, develop and retain the best qualified talent to support the campus's strategic vision of inspiring inclusive excellence. We are strategic partners and trusted advisors to the campus leadership, staff and faculty and are committed to providing excellent quality service in a diverse, safe and welcoming environment at the University of Toronto Scarborough. This search aligns with the University\u2019s commitment to strategically and proactively promote diversity among our community members ( Statement on Equity, Diversity & Excellence ). Recognizing that Black, Indigenous, and other Racialized communities have experienced inequities that have developed historically and are ongoing, we strongly welcome and encourage candidates from those communities to apply. YOUR OPPORTUNITY Under the general direction of the Lead, Data Analysis/Senior Data Specialist & Senior Academic HR Coordinator, this position is responsible for conducting research, undertaking special projects, maintaining and improving various internal processes and databases to ensure data integrity, and preparing and analyzing a variety of reports required for the HR and Dean\u2019s offices, UTSC Campus, and the University. The incumbent will work on a wide range of special HR projects, the specifics of which will vary, but which will build on a solid understanding of HR principles and practices, sound technical knowledge including expertise with HRIS and HRIS reporting and sound knowledge of U of T policies. Projects will require research and the gathering and analysis of a variety of different types of data needed to provide information and answers to questions posed by senior Campus and University decision makers. The incumbent will have a general knowledge and understanding of the University\u2019s collective agreement provisions and HR policies and procedures. The incumbent advises on academic HR policies and procedures relating to research and study leave credits and timing, salary administration, and retirement options to ensure compliance with University policies, and coordinates a variety of annual campus-wide activities, such as salary increases and research and study leaves. The incumbent is responsible for the management and integrity of employment and career data on all academic staff under general direction of the Lead. This includes ensuring that academic records on HRIS are accurate and up-to-date; tracking and monitoring the career progression and leave entitlements for tenure stream and teaching stream faculty; ensuring that any contractual conditions are cleared; provision of regular and ad hoc data reports and analyses to the Executive Director of Human Resources and the Vice-Dean Faculty Affairs, Equity and Success. The incumbent is responsible for the documentation and monitoring of cases pertaining to, for example, faculty and instructor sick leaves, accommodations, and LTD statuses. The incumbent will provide analysis and input to decisions for HR related activities across the UTSC campus. The incumbent provides, develops and maintains a comprehensive understanding of immigration requirements relating to the recruitment of foreign academics, liaising with the HR Immigration Officers on an as-needed basis.\u00a0 The incumbent reviews documentation prepared by departments prior to sending to HR Immigration Officers to ensure compliance with HRSDC\u2019s regulations. ESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: University degree in a relevant discipline and course work in the Human Resources field and statistics data leading to the completion of the CHRP designation or equivalent combination of education and experience. EXPERIENCE: Minimum of three (3) years of related experience, preferably in a university setting. Significant experience with databases and systems and compiling and analyzing complex human resources information. Proven successful experience gathering data, developing measurement tools, building analytics and experience with project management. Related experience in human resource with an emphasis on collective agreement and employment policy interpretation and application; experience with compensation and recruitment methodology and practices; understanding of HRIS & payroll processes and sound knowledge of human resources best practices and employment related legislation. SKILLS: Proficiency in word processing and spreadsheet application, preferably in a PC environment. Expertise in SAP and HRIS is essential. Superior knowledge of Microsoft Excel, Word and PowerPoint. Effective written and oral communication skills and superior problem-solving skills. OTHER: Must possess strong communication skills, both verbal and written; facilitation and interpersonal skills; and detail oriented. Demonstrated analytical and problem-solving skills. Ability to work effectively with multiple and conflicting priorities and the ability to maintain strict standards of confidentiality. Must be a team player and committed to service excellence. Superior analytical skills. Ability to synthesize a range of information and data from a variety of sources and to reconcile conflicting information in order to reach a conclusion, report accurately on an issue and to solve problems. Ability to independently prioritize tasks to meet deadlines and deal with multiple and conflicting demands. Ability to make sound recommendations based on research and data rather than staged agendas of individual parties. Applicants are expected to show evidence of a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment. ASSETS: Experience in data and statistics. Working experience with appointed academic staff, CUPE 3902, Unit 1, Unit 3 & Unit 5 Collective Agreements. NOTES This is a TERM position ending April 2028. This role is currently eligible for a hybrid work arrangement, pursuant to University policies and guidelines, including but not limited to University of Toronto\u2019s Alternative Work Arrangements Guideline . Closing Date: 11/03/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 2 -- Hiring Zone: $86,902 - $101,385 -- Broadband Salary Range: $86,902 - $144,835 Job Category: People, Finance & Digital Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Payroll, Data Analyst, HR, HRIS, Finance, Data, Human Resources, Research Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Research-Associate-%28Limited-Term%29-ON/607240617/": {"title": "Research Associate (Limited Term)", "description": "Research Associate (Limited Term) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Research Associate (Limited Term) Date Posted: 10/21/2026 Req ID: 50613 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Kinesiology & Physical Education Department: Faculty of Kinesiology & Physical Education Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Faculty of Kinesiology and Physical Education is looking to hire an experience, independent and motivated research associate to conduct a critical, comparative analysis between FIFA 2026 (World Cup of football) and LA28 (Olympic Summer Games) to assess questions and issues of migration, mobility, border control, legitimacy and international politics. The project will combine a mix of policy and document analysis and investigate the roles of international sports organizations (such as FIFA and the International Olympic Committee) in navigating international participation and national immigration and border policies. Education: PhD in Social Sciences or relevant field Experience: 3-5 years of post-PhD research experience. Experience conducting research in post-secondary environments, particularly within Canada. Strong understanding of the global sports and political landscape. Demonstrated experience researching sports mega-events and their social and political implications. Other: Experience with qualitative research methodologies, including data collection and analysis. Demonstrated ability to conceptualize and apply social and political theory to the study of global football and sports mega-events. Position Start Date: Expected start date is December 1, 2026; however, the start date is negotiable Position End Date: December 1, 2027 with possibility of renewal Method of Application: Resume and cover letter to be emailed to: Dr. Simon Darnell (simon.darnell@utoronto.ca) Closing Date: 10/30/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Research Associate Appointment Type : Grant - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: R01 - Research Associate (Limited Term): $55,661 - $104,364 Job Category: Research Administration & Teaching Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Research Associate, Research Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Service-Worker-Caretaking-%28Overnight%29-ON/607226817/": {"title": "Service Worker Caretaking (Overnight) Job Details", "description": "Service Worker Caretaking (Overnight) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Service Worker Caretaking (Overnight) Date Posted: 10/21/2026 Req ID: 50650 Faculty/Division: VP & Provost Department: Hart House Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes About Us \u2013 Hart House Hart House is a centre for experiential education outside the classroom at the University of\u202fToronto. Since it opened in 1919, Hart House functions as a place where students, faculty, staff,\u202falumni and members of the broader community connect with each other and the world. Through\u202fan array of co-curricular programming in the arts, dialogue and wellness, Hart House works with\u202flocal and international partners to foster community and to create innovative learning\u202fopportunities for students. Hart House operates from a historic facility on the St. George campus,\u202fas well as a 150-acre farm in Caledon, Ontario, offering a wide range of services through a social\u202fenterprise model that generates revenue to support its student-focused programming on all three\u202fUniversity of Toronto campuses. General Description of Class Under general supervision works according to detailed procedures in cleaning and custodial duties, may assist in other maintenance duties. Typical Duties The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required, and the extent of responsibility involved in this position. \u00a0They in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated. Flexibility of the employee to perform a wide variety of functions is necessary in successfully fulfilling the requirements of this position. \u00a0The degree to which each employee performs each of the following tasks listed below will vary according to where and when the employee is scheduled to work. a) \u00a0 \u00a0cleans and dusts furniture, floors, hallways, stairways and ledges, using authorized and appropriate materials and equipment including heavy duty electric buffers, automatic floor machines, large dust mops, \u00a0vacuum cleaners , carpet cleaning equipment and other cleaning equipment; b) \u00a0 \u00a0reconditions floors as required; including stripping, refinishing, scrubbing, spray buffing, buffing, sealing and other related floor care duties; c) \u00a0 \u00a0regularly cleans washrooms, including sinks, walls and partitions, toilets, urinals, mirrors, floors, metal fixtures, plumbing fixtures and faucets; d) \u00a0 \u00a0collects litter from floors and waste/compost from receptacles, empties into janitor cart, removes garbage/recycling \u00a0from buildings and deposits into waste bins or compactors; e) \u00a0 \u00a0cleans carpets as required; removes spots/stains from surfaces as required; f) \u00a0 \u00a0washes windows and walls including partition glass; g) \u00a0 \u00a0moves and resets furniture when necessary in order to complete work; h) \u00a0 \u00a0makes beds for residence guests in residence operations when necessary; i) \u00a0 \u00a0cleans blackboards, whiteboards and other writing surfaces as directed; replenishes supplies as required; j) \u00a0 \u00a0replenishes paper towels, toilet paper, hand soap and sanitizers to receptacles within washrooms \u00a0 \u00a0 and utility kitchens and other areas as required; k) \u00a0 \u00a0changes light bulbs and cleans fixtures as required; l) \u00a0 \u00a0clears exterior entrance ways of buildings of debris and garbage; m) \u00a0 \u00a0cleans exterior entrance pads and podiums using power washing equipment; n) \u00a0 \u00a0assists in snow removal when necessary; o) \u00a0 \u00a0may periodically assist with set ups for special events and exams; p) \u00a0 \u00a0cleans escalators and elevator interior and exterior; q) \u00a0 \u00a0locks and unlocks doors as directed; and r) \u00a0 \u00a0other related duties as required. Minimum Requirements for Selection Education: Completion of tenth grade or equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience: One year of related work experience is desirable. Other: Physical ability to perform duties described and to use indicated equipment. Ability to communicate effectively in English (oral and written). Notes: This is a term position for 6 months from January 2027 to July 2027. Hours of work: Sunday through Thursday from 11:00 PM to 7:30 AM. Working hours include weekends (including long weekends), evenings, and holidays. Closing Date: 10/29/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: CUPE F/T L3261 Appointment Type : Budget - Term. This is a term position for 6 months from January 2027 to July 2027. Schedule: Full-Time. Hours of work are Sunday through Thursday from 11:00 PM to 7:30 AM. Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: Job Rate: $25.96/hr Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Event Planning, Facilities, Hospitality, Operations Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Special-Projects-Officer-ON/607226517/": {"title": "Special Projects Officer Job Details", "description": "Special Projects Officer Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Special Projects Officer Date Posted: 10/21/2026 Req ID: 50648 Faculty/Division: School of Graduate Studies Department: School of Graduate Studies Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Working under general direction of the Assistant Dean, School of Graduate Studies, the Special Projects Officer is responsible for identifying issues, advising on strategy options, recommending solutions, implementing project plans, and responding to the objectives and priorities of the Office of the Vice- Provost, Graduate Research and Education. Working closely with the Assistant Dean, School of Graduate Studies, other members of the Decanal Team (Dean, Vice-Deans), as well as other senior university administrators, the Special Projects Officer is responsible for project management and implementation to ensure the work of the Vice-Provost's Office can be carried out efficiently and effectively. Such project management and implementation includes: (a) providing strategic advice on policy matters and other issues, such as academic administrator searches and review committees, (b) advising on draft policies and proposals, (c) undertaking detailed research on a wide variety of issues and topics, (d) following-up on decisions made by the members of the portfolio and the portfolio's various committees, (e) developing draft communications such as remarks, presentations, and correspondence, and (f) ensuring ongoing maintenance of the highest level of pro-activity and service for the portfolio of the Office of the Vice- Provost, Graduate Research and Education. The Special Projects Officer will coordinate, assist with and advance projects, initiatives and daily activities within the Office of the Vice-Provost, Graduate Research and Education that require knowledge of confidential information about Faculty staffing, priorities, and new academic directions. \u00a0The role of the Special Projects Officer will continue to evolve and the individual must be willing to respond to the given priorities of the day and be willing to work cooperatively in a challenging and dynamic environment. About Us: The School of Graduate Studies (SGS) promotes University-wide inclusive excellence in graduate education, research and professional training to ensure high standards across the various academic divisions, as well as supporting postdoctoral fellows. SGS defines and administers University-wide regulations for graduate education. We share responsibility for graduate education with graduate units and divisions and operates through a system of collegial governance, consultation, and decanal leadership. SGS also provides expertise and advice; reviews the design and delivery of programs; develops performance standards; supports access, equitable inclusion, fairness, and ethical conduct in graduate education; organizes services and financial assistance to graduate students; encourages a close and positive relationship between research and graduate instruction, and represents the cause of graduate education at the University of Toronto and in the broader academic and general community. Qualifications Required: I. \u00a0 \u00a0EDUCATION: University degree required, post graduate degree (Master's or PhD) an asset, or equivalent in education and experience. II. \u00a0 \u00a0EXPERIENCE: Minimum four (4) years\u2019 experience in a University setting in progressively senior positions. Extensive experience with the University, knowledge of university policies and procedures, and an understanding of the university\u2019s organizational structure, including its governance. Experience leading complex and multi-stakeholder projects. \u00a0Knowledge about media (including traditional, new and social media), protocol, diplomacy and an excellent understanding of the University\u2019s mission and intersection with the broader community. III. \u00a0 \u00a0SKILLS: Strong quantitative and qualitative data literacy skills. Advanced computer skills in Microsoft Office (must be able to set up templates and macros in Word and Excel, set up Excel spreadsheets and graphics, and prepare sophisticated PowerPoint presentations), and scheduling software. Familiarity with Microsoft Sharepoint an asset. \u00a0Web design skills such as content management software and Wordpress preferred. \u00a0Familiarity with Acrobat and other Adobe software an asset. IV. \u00a0 \u00a0OTHER: Strong research, writing, communication, presentation and interpersonal skills; high degree of political acuity and judgment; ability to deal with senior University Officers in a manner which facilitates cooperation and consensus building; ability to work independently with a high degree of initiative, discretion, and tact; ability to work under pressure; superior organizational skills in planning, project management and task coordination; flexibility and problem solver orientation; and strong leadership capabilities. Closing Date: 11/10/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 3 -- Hiring Zone: $97,336 - $113,558 -- Broadband Salary Range: $97,336 - $162,224 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Project Manager, Web Design, Sharepoint, Developer, Technology, Creative, Research Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-Maternal-Fetal-Medicine-Physician-ON/607243417/": {"title": "Assistant/ Associate/ Full Professor", "description": "Assistant/ Associate/ Full Professor - Maternal Fetal Medicine Physician Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant/ Associate/ Full Professor - Maternal Fetal Medicine Physician Date Posted: 10/22/2026 Closing Date: 11/25/2026 , 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50640 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Obstetrics&Gynaecology Hospital Affiliation: Unity Health Toronto - St. Michael's Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at St. Michael\u2019s Hospital, in partnership with the University of Toronto Faculty of Medicine, Department of Obstetrics & Gynecology, is currently recruiting one (1) full-time academic physician with subspecialist CERTIFICATION in MATERNAL FETAL MEDICINE (MFM ). The successful candidate will have an academic position description of Clinician Teacher or Clinician Educator and must be eligible for a full-time clinical academic appointment at the rank of Assistant, Associate or Full Professor at the University of Toronto. Effective start date is July 1, 2027 or shortly thereafter. In alignment with our strategic vision, preferred areas of clinical and research focus include high risk pregnancy, ultrasound, maternity care for critically ill, complex and vulnerable patients, and MFM community outreach. This is an exciting opportunity to join a busy, professionally rewarding group clinical practice with other dedicated healthcare professionals in an attractive and expanding hospital facility with a progressive Administration. The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is part of the Women\u2019s and Children\u2019s Health Program at Unity Health Toronto, St. Michael\u2019s Hospital.\u00a0 We are committed to patient-centered multidisciplinary care, an integrated approach to community health, and excellence in education and research. St. Michael\u2019s boasts nationally and internationally recognized programs in multiple sclerosis, cystic fibrosis, bleeding disorders, diabetes, HIV, addiction, renal transplant, and intensive care (complex medical and surgical, trauma, neurosurgery, and cardiac and cardiovascular). Our perinatal addictions program could present a further opportunity for the successful candidate. St. Michael\u2019s wealth of resources includes the Li Ka Shing Institute for Knowledge Translation, the MAP Centre for Urban Health Solutions; HUB Health Research Solutions; the Centre for Research in Inner City Health (CRICH); the Institute for Biomedical Engineering, Science and Technology: Evaluation Centre for Complex Health Interventions, the Centre for Global Health Research, the Allan Waters Family Simulation Centre and the Centre for Faculty Development. These represent extensive opportunities for collaboration in urban health research, education and knowledge translation. The St. Michael\u2019s Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is fully affiliated with the University of Toronto and provides learning experiences for fellows, obstetrics and gynecology residents, family practice residents, interns, medical students, and students of nursing and midwifery. The SMH Ultrasound unit is responsible for obstetric ultrasound training for all U of T Ob/Gyn residents and MFM Fellows. The department is proud to maintain award-winning research activities and a strong continuous quality improvement program. The successful candidate will join our team of 19 faculty members: 7 MIGS fellowship-trained surgeons, 7 core obstetrician-gynecologists, 1 uro-gynecologist, and 4 maternal fetal medicine subspecialists. We provide comprehensive care to the broad community, aiming to perform approximately 3,000 deliveries per year. We work collaboratively with Family Medicine and Midwifery. We are fully supported by a level 2C neonatal intensive care unit, which will soon be moving to new state-of-the-art clinical space in the recently completed Peter Gilgan Tower. Plans are underway for expansion of the labour and birth unit into the current NICU space. The current 4 MFM subspecialists work collaboratively to provide an array of services, including High-Risk Pregnancy Clinics, Obstetric Ultrasound, Amniocentesis, Prenatal Diagnosis, Diabetes in Pregnancy Clinic, in-patient and outpatient consultations, Labour and Birth coverage. \u201cMFM of the week\u201d coverage and MFM community outreach services to Humber River Hospital and Southlake Regional Health Centre. Fetal echocardiography is offered by a Pediatric Cardiologist two mornings weekly and consultative services in the Medical Complications of Pregnancy Clinic by an internist are provided once weekly. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to the department\u2019s educational responsibilities and clinical and research activities. In joining the SMH MFM division, the successful candidate will commit to taking part in the SMH MFM outreach programs in our surrounding community hospitals. When establishing the successful candidate\u2019s clinical and academic schedules, we will strive for an equitable distribution of clinical and academic resources both within and outside of Unity Health Toronto. Qualified applicants must hold an MD degree must be licensed or eligible for medical licensure with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario and must be certified or eligible for certification in the subspeciality of Maternal Fetal Medicine by the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada. The position requires an individual who has additional training or equivalent experience in care of high-risk pregnancies in vulnerable patient populations, as well as a record of demonstrated excellence in clinical care and scholarship in this area. The successful candidate will have a strong record of relevant research accomplishment. The successful applicant will have an active staff appointment, be eligible for alternate funding plan (AFP) payments and joining the department practice plan. MFM administrative roles, including that of Division Head, Maternal Fetal Medicine, may be built into the position. This would depend on the candidate\u2019s level of expertise, years of training, academic ranking and administrative qualifications. Estimated remuneration will be in the range of $300,000 - $350,000 as per Ministry of Health OHIP (Ontario Health Insurance Plan) billings with additional remuneration from the practice plan for academic work related to teaching, research output and administrative activities. The posted University Position Description is Clinician Teacher, Clinician Educator or Clinician Investigator, to be tailored to the candidate\u2019s career goals, qualifications and prior accomplishments. A clinician investigator would be contingent on obtaining the funding required to support this. If the successful candidate wishes to lead a program of grant-funded research, then graduate-level training commensurate with specific research interests is strongly desired. Academic interests are expected to broadly align with the strategic vision of the department, the hospital and Unity Health Toronto. We invite you to join our dynamic team. Inquiries may be directed to Dr. Filomena Meffe, Chief Department of Obstetrics & Gynaecology at 416-864-5384 Fillomena.Meffe@unityhealth.to or Dr. Tatiana Freire-Lizama, Interim Head Maternal Fetal Medicine Tatiana.Freire-Lizama@unityhealth.to Applications will be accepted until November 25, 2026 or until the position is filled. Interested candidates are requested to reply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae and contact information of three referees to: Dr. Filomena Meffe c/o Janet Forrest \u2013 Administrative Assistant St. Michael\u2019s Hospital 30 Bond Street 15-018b Cardinal Carter Toronto ON M5B 1W8 Email: Janet.Forrest@unityhealth.to CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Obstetrics, Gynecology, ICU, Pediatric, Ultrasound, Healthcare Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-WIIH-Research-Officer-ON/606241617/": {"title": "WIIH Research Officer Job Details", "description": "WIIH Research Officer Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb WIIH Research Officer Date Posted: 10/19/2026 Req ID: 50257 Faculty/Division: Dalla Lana School of Public Health Department: Dalla Lana School of Public Health Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00059962 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Dalla Lana School of Public Health is a Faculty of the University of Toronto that originated as one of the Schools of Hygiene begun by the Rockefeller Foundation in 1927. The School, which played a critical role in the COVID-19 pandemic response, went through a dramatic renaissance after the 2003 SARS crisis and it is now the largest public health school in Canada, with more than 850 faculty, 1,000 students, and research and training partnerships with institutions throughout Toronto and the world. With $76 million in research funding per year, including more than $31.5 million held at DLSPH, the School contributes to improving population health and health policy and health systems through discoveries and innovation in data science and AI, maternal, child and reproductive health, climate change [response], implementation and improvement sciences, preventable disease through vaccines and prevention through [and] wellness such as with diabetes, comparative health policy, sustainable and equitable health systems, global and Indigenous health, among many other areas. Your opportunity: At the Waakebiness Institute for Indigenous Health, researchers and educators fromacross the University of Toronto work with community partners and Indigenous peoples to address the complex factors that underlie disparities in health between Indigenous and non-Indigenous people. The Institute is engaged in research, educationand service initiatives to overcome health challenges and evaluate interventions to prevent disease and improve health. Its scholars study health policy and administration to improve the delivery and quality of Indigenous health care, and educate Indigenous and non-Indigenous students, so that each year more Canadians and citizens of the world can recognize, reduce and eliminate health inequities. As Research Officer, you will work closely with the Principal Investigator and project partners to support the successful coordination and delivery of research activities. You will foster positive relationships with project partners, coordinate meetings and project materials, support data management and analysis, and prepare reports and other materialsfor knowledge translation. Your strong organizational, communication, and research skills will allow you to effectively manage multiple priorities and contribute to the progress of research projects. Your responsibilities will include: Supporting research initiatives through literature reviews, data collection, database maintenance, data analysis, and quantitative research coding Coordinating project meetings, including scheduling, preparing agendasand materials, recording action items, and following up on outstanding items Fostering positive relationships with project partners and liaising with contacts to facilitate outreach opportunities Supporting the Principal Investigator by identifying and communicating project concerns, setbacks, and progress Analyzing, organizing, and formatting research data for presentations, reports, and other project materials Drafting progress reports and knowledge translation materialsfor review by the project lead Generating reports, disseminating information, and responding to project-related enquiries within the defined scope of the role Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in a relevant discipline, or an acceptable equivalent combination of education and experience Minimum two (2) years of relevant research experience, preferably in a public health environment Experience conducting literature reviews, collecting and analyzing research data, and maintaining research databases Knowledge of Indigenous cultural safety and lived experience of indigenous knowledges Experience with quantitative research data and coding Experience coordinating meetings, preparing materials, documenting action items, and following up on project activities Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and relevant research and data management tools Must possess a solid understanding of Indigenous affairs, health, and cultural traditional knowledges Strong organizational, communication, interpersonal, and relationship-building skills Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines Demonstrated ability to work independently, exercise judgment, and contribute effectively as part of a team Ability to respond to enquiries within the defined scope of the role and redirect enquiries as appropriate Excellent time managementand problem-solving skills with the ability to meet conflicting priorities and balance multiple projects Demonstrates initiative and possesses a strong commitment to research work with a strong commitment to accuracy and attention to detail Client-services oriented with demonstrated listening and critical thinking skills with the ability to learn new skills Ability to maintain a broad perspective; ability to foster and maintain effective relationships with all levels To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Goal oriented Intuitive Organized Problem solver This is a 2-year, part-time (45% FTE) term position. Closing Date: 10/27/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Part-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 07 -- $27,106,65. with an annual step progression to a maximum of $34,665.75. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Recruiter: Dinuka Perera Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Data Management, Public Health, Data Analyst, Part Time, Data, Healthcare, Research Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Professor%2C-Teaching-Stream-CLTA-Geographic-Data-Science-ON/607187317/": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream", "description": "Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream - CLTA - Geographic Data Science Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream - CLTA - Geographic Data Science Date Posted: 10/21/2026 Closing Date: 12/10/2026, 11:59PM ET Req ID: 49017 Job Category: Faculty - Contractually Limited Term Appointment Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: Dept of Geography Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes POSITION DESCRIPTION The Department of Geography & Planning in the Faculty of Arts & Science at the University of Toronto (St. George campus) invites applications for a three-year full-time contractually limited term appointment (CLTA) in Geographic Data Science. The appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream, with an anticipated start date of January 1, 2027. REQUIREMENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS Applicants must have earned a PhD degree in physical or human geography or a closely aligned discipline with a pedagogy/teaching focus in Geographic Data Science by the time of appointment, or shortly thereafter, with a demonstrated record of excellence in teaching. We welcome applications from candidates with an interest in the applications of Geographic Data Science in fields such as transportation, planning, or environmental geography, among others. We seek candidates whose teaching interests complement our existing departmental strengths. Candidates must demonstrate teaching expertise in a degree-granting program at the undergraduate level, including lecture preparation and delivery, curriculum development, and development of online material/lectures in geographic data science, including courses on geographic information systems (GIS), spatial analysis, and computer mapping applications. Additionally, candidates must possess a demonstrated commitment to excellent pedagogical inquiry and a demonstrated interest in teaching-related scholarly activities. Evidence of excellence in teaching and a commitment to excellent pedagogical inquiry will be provided by teaching awards and accolades; presentations at significant, discipline-relevant conferences; and in a teaching dossier which includes teaching accomplishments; a statement of teaching philosophy; sample course syllabi related to the teaching of Geographic Data Science and/or GIS; teaching evaluations; and strong letters of reference. RESPONSIBILITIES The successful candidate will be assigned a teaching and service load. \u00a0Teaching may include introductory, intermediate, and advanced Geographic Data Science/GIS courses, a capstone Geographic Data Science/GIS course, and a graduate-level GIS course for non-specialists. HIRING SALARY RANGE The salary range is $115,000 to $145,000 CAD per annum, depending on experience. Negotiations beyond this salary range will be considered for exceptionally qualified candidates. ABOUT US The University of Toronto is a tri-campus, research-intensive institution. This appointment is at the St. George campus, which is located in the heart of Toronto and offers the opportunity to conduct research, teach and live in one of the most diverse cities in the world. The University also offers opportunities to work in a wide range of collaborative programs and centres of research. For more information on working at the University of Toronto, please visit https://www.utoronto.ca/research-innovation/working-at-uoft . For more information about the Department of Geography & Planning, please visit our home page: http://geography.utoronto.ca/ . APPLICATION PROCESS All application materials, including recent reference letters, must be received by December 10, 2026 . All qualified candidates are invited to apply online by clicking the link below. Your CV and cover letter should be uploaded into the dedicated fields. Please combine additional application materials into one or two files in PDF/MS Word format. Applicants must submit the following materials: a cover letter; a current curriculum vitae; a complete teaching dossier which includes a teaching statement, sample syllabi and course materials; and teaching evaluations The name and contact information of three references. At least one reference letter must primarily address the candidate\u2019s teaching. The University of Toronto\u2019s recruiting tool will automatically solicit and collect letters of reference from each referee within 48 hours of an application being submitted. Applicants remain responsible for ensuring that references submit recent letters (on letterhead, dated and signed) by the closing date. Submission guidelines and details on the automatic reference letter collection, including timelines, are available in the candidate FAQ . If you have any questions about this position, please contact Professor Paul Hess at chair.geoplan@utoronto.ca . All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: GIS, Geology, Information Systems, Drafting, Database, Technology, Engineering Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Faculty Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Coordinator%2C-Student-Athlete-Academic-Support-ON/607185817/": {"title": "Coordinator, Student-Athlete Academic Support", "description": "Coordinator, Student-Athlete Academic Support Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Coordinator, Student-Athlete Academic Support Date Posted: 10/20/2026 Req ID: 50602 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Kinesiology & Physl Ed. Department: Faculty of Kinesiology & Physl Ed Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00041740 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The University of Toronto's Faculty of Kinesiology and Physical Education is globally recognized for developing and advancing knowledge about the interactions of physical activity and health through outstanding undergraduate and graduate education programs, cutting-edge research and the delivery of sport, recreation and high performance athletic opportunities for students, staff, faculty and community members across the 3 campuses. In achieving this vision, the Faculty is guided by values of integrity, respect, equity and diversity. For more information, please visit kpe.utoronto.ca Your opportunity: Reporting to the Director, Interuniversity and High Performance Athletics and under the general supervision of the Assistant Manager, Student-Athlete Services, the incumbent provides a wide range of academic success support services, activities and guidance to interuniversity and high performance student-athletes. Working in a diverse, fast-paced, energetic team environment, the incumbent will be detail oriented and deliver accurate, effective, and efficient support while projecting a welcoming, positive and professional image for the Varsity Blues program at the University of Toronto. This position collaborates closely with interuniversity coaches, registrars, and on-campus student support staff to promote the well-being, inclusion, holistic development, and academic success of student athletes, empowering them to thrive both within and beyond sport. Your responsibilities will include: Delivering and promoting student-athlete service programs, opportunities and/or initiatives, including academic success, accessibility, health and wellness consulting, career training and transition support programs. Liaising with student-athletes, team leaders, athletic and academic staff to foster collaboration, advance service delivery and ensure consistent administration procedures are followed. Verifying athlete eligibility in relation to University, OUA and USports rules and regulations. Developing program materials and resources for student-athletes, including editing content for brochures, newsletters, websites and handbooks. Determining activities and logistical details for student-athlete service programming that will enrich the student-athlete experience and facilitate success. This will also include coordinating the schedule for student-athlete service programs. Directing the activities of casual staff and submit time sheets for data processing. Creating and updating students records and processing academic conflict letters maintaining confidentiality of information. Keeping well-informed about student service programs across all three campuses and providing informed advice and guidance on athletic eligibility, as well as the integration and enhancement of student-athlete services. Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree, preferably in Kinesiology or acceptable combination of equivalent experience Minimum two years experience in student-athletes services, University sport programming or equivalent experience in a University or similar academic setting Minimum two years experience developing program materials and resource for student-athletes A solid understanding of Ontario University Athletics (OUA) and U SPORTS eligibility rules required Familiarity with University of Toronto academic rules, regulations, and student support resources on all 3 campuses Excellent verbal and written communication skills Skilled in establishing and maintaining effective working relationships with a diverse group of students and University colleagues Knowledge in the practical application of student development theory and academic learning strategies Good problem solving, multi tasking and organization skills Demonstrated initiative and motivation and ability to maintain confidentiality in a fast-paced diverse environment Assets (Nonessential): Ontario College of Teachers certification is an asset. To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Cooperative Organized Self-directed Team player Closing Date: 10/28/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time - evening and weekend work will be required Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 09 -- $70,633 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $90,329. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Divisional HR Office Email: kpe.hr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Academic, Intern, Consulting, Equity, Education, Entry Level, Technology, Finance, Research Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Manager%2C-Academic-Programs-ON/607211817/": {"title": "Manager, Academic Programs Job Details", "description": "Manager, Academic Programs Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Manager, Academic Programs Date Posted: 10/20/2026 Req ID: 50513 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Rehabilitation Sciences Sector Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Home to over 40 departments and institutes, the University of Toronto's Temerty Faculty of Medicine lies at the heart of the Toronto Academic Health Science Network and is a global leader in ground-breaking research and education, spanning clinical medicine, basic science and the rehabilitation sciences sectors. Your opportunity: The Rehabilitation Sciences Sector (RSS) in the Temerty Faculty of Medicine is a world leader in the delivery of rehabilitation sciences health professional programs and research. The RSS is comprised of four essential departments: Department of Occupational Science and Occupational Therapy (OSOT), Department of Physical Therapy (PT), Rehabilitation Sciences Institute (RSI), and the Department of Speech-Language Pathology (SLP). As Manager, Academic Programs, you will play a principal role in overseeing academic programs and services across our newly integrated Sector. Working closely with RSS Chairs and senior administrative leaders, you will develop plans, establish business processes and lead complex projects related to educational programs and student placements, electives, experiential learning, and community-based service learnings. Your record of building and mentoring collaborative teams, ensuring the delivery of integrated and effective student experiences and leading the process of continuous improvement of our programs\u2019 curriculum service design and delivery will help us enhance our Sector\u2019s efficiency, effectiveness and operational agility. Essential Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Business, Student Affairs, Education or related field to the discipline or equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum five (5) years of related administrative experience in a university, medical school, teaching hospital or comparable environment Knowledge and experience supporting clinical education programs and clinical training opportunities Experience with education program management and student placements in an academic environment Demonstrated knowledge and experience with curriculum development and processes Experience managing projects and leading successful change, including developing strategies, implementing initiatives and establishing best practices Experience managing, leading and mentoring staff, preferably in a unionized environment A well-developed financial acumen, including financial analysis and budgeting Strong understanding of principles of equity; experience working with under-represented groups and supporting inclusion initiatives Knowledge of collective agreement interpretation and administration Advanced proficiency in MS Office Suite, learning management systems and educational technology systems (Quercus, POWER, Slate, ROSI), content management systems and survey tools Strong ability to build and maintaining effective working relationships and partnerships with internal and external stakeholders Highly developed verbal and written communication and presentation skills Excellent interpersonal skills with a strong ability to foster and maintain effective relationships with both internal and external stakeholders Extensive knowledge of accreditation processes and program procedures for reviews and audits. Strong team-building skills and a collaborative and consultative leadership style; excellent analytical skills and creative problem-solving ability Excellent organizational, analytical, and critical thinking skills Demonstrated ability to seek innovative and creative solutions with a personal commitment to excellence Responsive and high degree of flexibility Strong attention to detail and manage competing priorities within a complex environment Please note this is a term positions through September 1, 2028. Closing Date: 11/10/2026,11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 2 -- Hiring Zone: $86,902 - $101,385 -- Broadband Salary Range: $86,902 - $144,835 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Therapy, Rehabilitation, Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, Academic, Healthcare, Education Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Indigenous-Community-Engagement-Manager-ON/607173417/": {"title": "Indigenous Community Engagement Manager Job Details", "description": "Indigenous Community Engagement Manager Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Indigenous Community Engagement Manager Date Posted: 10/20/2026 Req ID: 50598 Faculty/Division: VP & Provost Department: Office of Indigenous Initiatives Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: No Description: Please note that short-listed candidates may be asked to participate in an Indigenous substantiation process. Indigenous Substantiation | Indigenous University of Toronto About us: The Office of Indigenous Initiatives was established in response to the U of T\u2019s Truth and Reconciliation Commission Steering Committee\u2019s final report, Answering The Call: Wecheehetowin. The Office\u2019s mandate is to support and guide the U of T community as it continues to work towards reconciliation. Efforts are directed towards listening, coordinating, advising, and collaborating with academic and non-academic communities in addressing the Calls to Action. The Office intersects with areas such as teaching and learning, student experience, Faculty and staff recruitment and engagement, and community-based research. The Office also conducts a regular environmental scan, produces a report to establish the impact and progress of Indigenous Initiatives on campus, and manages the activities of the Council of Indigenous Initiatives and the Elder\u2019s Circle. Your opportunity: Reporting to the Executive Director, Indigenous Initiatives, the Indigenous Community Engagement Manager is responsible for providing a high level of confidential operational and administrative support to the Office and Executive Director in the implementation, administration, and management of the Indigenous Substantiation Framework including but not limited to processing substantiation requests and updating the portal. The Manager will socialize and promote the Indigenous Substantiation Framework across the University to faculty, students, librarians and staff, including senior leadership and will liaise with Indigenous communities and governing bodies outside the university. The incumbent is responsible for strengthening the internal University Indigenous community by creating opportunities for connection, networking, and engagement throughout the year. The Manager will develop and coordinate gatherings, events, and networking initiatives that bring together community members, foster relationships, and encourage collaboration. The Manager will create and manage an Indigenous Affinity Group for Indigenous employees across the University. The goal of the Affinity Group is to create a strong, connected community for Indigenous employees that seeks to meet the distinct needs of the group. The incumbent works in a complex environment that requires a high degree of sensitivity, responsiveness, and a need to maintain absolute confidentiality. The incumbent represents the University on relevant committees inside and outside the University community, providing assistance, information, outreach, resources and referrals. Essential Qualifications: (MINIMUM) EDUCATION: University degree in a related field or an equivalent combination of education and experience. EXPERIENCE: Minimum three to five years of related experience. Experience working in Indigenous (First Nations, M\u00e9tis, or Inuit) communities and demonstrated experience developing community engagement initiatives. Professional experience in and understanding of complex issues related to equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility. Demonstrated experience with successful event planning for large and small in-person and hybrid events. Experience working within a post-secondary context is strongly preferred. SKILLS: Experience and computer proficiency in a PC environment, including standard office computer applications (e.g. Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, etc.). Acrobat and familiarity with Microsoft SharePoint an asset. OTHER: Professional writing and/or editing skills. Superior written and oral communication skills. Excellent interpersonal and facilitation skills. Ability to develop and deliver effective presentations. Demonstrated ability to communicate and work effectively with diverse constituencies and communities in a team environment. Demonstrated abilities to multi-task, trouble shoot and problem solve. Excellent organizational skills. Ability to be innovative and work independently. Demonstrated ability to relate to students, staff, and faculty that builds trust and confidence. Ability to work under pressure and to meet deadlines. Closing Date: 11/02/2026,11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 1 -- Hiring Zone: $79,707 - $92,992 -- Broadband Salary Range: $79,707 - $132,843 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Administrative Assistant, Event Planning, Developer, Equity, Hospitality, Administrative, Research, Technology, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Financial-Officer-%28Term%29-ON/607174217/": {"title": "Financial Officer (Term) Job Details", "description": "Financial Officer (Term) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Financial Officer (Term) Date Posted: 10/20/2026 Req ID: 50618 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: Department of History Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Faculty of Arts & Science is the heart of Canada\u2019s leading university and one of the most comprehensive and diverse academic divisions in the world. The strength of Arts & Science derives from our combined teaching and research excellence in the humanities, sciences and social sciences across 29 departments, seven colleges and 46 interdisciplinary centres, institutes and programs. We can only realize our mission with the dedication and excellence of engaged staff and faculty. The diversity of opportunities and perspectives within the Faculty reflect the local and global landscape and the need for curiosity, innovative thinking and collaboration. At Arts & Science, we take pride in our legacy of innovation and discovery that has changed the way we think about the world. The Department of History is one of the largest history departments in North America and is internationally renowned. The University of Toronto's Department of History is recognized as one of the leading history departments in North America and ranks among the world's top programs in the discipline. The department offers exciting opportunities to interpret the past and examine its significance through research, education and life-long learning. It provides an opportunity for individuals interested in being active in local, national and international research and public affairs to bring unique perspective to important events. Your opportunity: Reporting to the Department Manager, the Financial Officer is the primary resource for faculty and staff in the administration of the department's research grants. The incumbent ensures compliance with University policies, the Guideto Financial Management (GTFM), and applicable sponsor requirements through the review and processing of a broad range of financial transactions. The incumbent also administers payroll for a variety of employee groups, including the review, verification,processing, and reconciliation of payroll transactions to ensure accuracy and compliance with University policies and procedures. Your responsibilities will include: Forecasting and planning financial activities incorporating budgets with multiple sources of revenue and/or recoveries Monitoring, recording, reconciling and/or reporting on funding accounts for grants and contracts Analyzing information to identify spending trends and recommendcost saving measures Processing financial and payroll transactions Verifying that HRIS transactions are processed according to applicable policies, procedures, collective agreements, and applicable legislated requirements Applyingthe University Guide to Financial Management and other applicable policies, agency and regulatory requirements Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience in Business Administration, Finance or Accounting. Minimum three years of recent and relevant experience in financial administration with experience in payroll and financial reporting, preferably in an academic environment. Experience in financial administration of research grants. Experience monitoring funds and making recommendations on expenditures. Demonstrated knowledge of financial management procedures and policies pertaining to funding agencies, expense reimbursement, procurement, etc. Experience processing financial and payroll transactions in SAP-based system. Experience with reconciliations and identifying and resolving discrepancies. Experience providing cost-saving recommendations, and implementing plans and process improvements. Advanced proficiency with MS Office Suite, financial information systems (FIS) and human resources information systems (HRIS). Excellent communications skills, both written and verbal. Strong interpersonal skills, including the ability to exercise good judgment in dealing with faculty, and staff and can work in a team environment. Excellent attention to detail and accuracy, and solid organizational and problem-solving skills. Demonstrated ability to meet deadlines and manage competing priorities. Ability to work independently and as a member of a team. Assets (Nonessential): Experience providing financial administration and payroll support in a unionized environment. To be successful in this role you will be: Insightful Meticulous Organized Problem solver Team player This recruitment is to fill one full time 6 month term position. Closing Date: 10/28/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 11 -- $79,640 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $101,845. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Finance/Budget/Planning/Audit Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: HRIS, Payroll, Compliance, Public Policy, Information Systems, Human Resources, Finance, Legal, Government, Technology Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Innovations-and-Partnerships-Officer-ON/607207017/": {"title": "Innovations and Partnerships Officer Job Details", "description": "Innovations and Partnerships Officer Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Innovations and Partnerships Officer Date Posted: 10/20/2026 Req ID: 50604 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Lab. Medicine & Pathobiology Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00060056 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Home to over 40 departments and institutes, the University of Toronto's Temerty Faculty of Medicine lies at the heart of the Toronto Academic Health Science Network and is a global leader in ground-breaking research and education, spanning clinical medicine, basic science and the rehabilitation sciences sectors. Your opportunity: The Department of Laboratory Medicine and Pathobiology (LMP) occupies a unique position at the interface between basic biomedical science and clinical practice. We are an assembly of over 400 investigators, scientists, and clinicians, who educate and mentor trainees pursuing undergraduate, graduate, and postgraduate medical studies, engaged in investigating disease mechanisms and patterns and translating new knowledge and discoveries into improved health outcomes for patients and populations. Situated in LMP, the Temerty Centre for Artificial Intelligence Research and Education in Medicine (T-CAIREM), an interdepartmental centre, serves as a focal point for collaboration between computer scientists, healthcare providers, trainees, medical basic science researchers and industry to advance health through machine learning. The mission of the Centre is to advance research, education, knowledge dissemination and digital infrastructure in the field of AI in medicine. T-CAIREM aims to be a global leader in facilitating high quality, accessible educational offerings and researchcollaborations at the intersection of AI and health. T-CAIREM seeks to build capacity to reflect the emerging role of AI in healthcare professions and to build strategic partnerships to implement new solutions that can transform practice. As theInnovations and Partnerships Officer, you will play an important role in advancing T-CAIREM\u2019s financial sustainability through commercialization and business development activities across its research and education portfolio in AI in medicine. You will identify grant, government, and industry funding opportunities, develop strategic partnerships, and help move initiatives toward implementation and commercialization. Working with inventors, researchers, and external partners, you will develop intellectual property protection plans, assist with commercialization agreements and negotiation-related matters, and contribute to diverse and sustainable revenue streams that support T-CAIREM\u2019s mission and continued impact. Your responsibilities will include: Conducting detailed analysis and evaluation of new products and/or technology to determine commercialization potential Writing grant and investment proposals and solicitation documentation for proof of concept, product development, and commercialization activities Supporting commercialization agreements and informing researchers and staff on issues surrounding negotiations Developing intellectual property plans and ensuring agreements align with University standards and guidelines Developing business development strategies, conducting market research and analysis, and pursuing new business, funding, partnership, and growth opportunities Identifying and developing research and innovation partnerships and fostering collaboration between academic and industry partners Advising inventors on product development and providing researchers with information on commercialization matters Forecasting, planning, and monitoring complex budgets and producing complex statistical and/or financial reports Essential Qualifications: Master's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum six (6) years of experience supporting commercialization and business development activities Demonstrated experience conducting detailed analysis and evaluation of new products and/or technology to determine commercialization potential Experience writing grant and investment proposals to secure proof of concept and product development funding Demonstrated experience supporting commercialization agreements and informing researchers and staff on issues surrounding negotiations Experience developing intellectual property protection plans Demonstrated experience developing research and industry partnerships and identifying new business, funding, or collaboration opportunities Experience conducting market research and analysis and implementing sales and marketing plans to support revenue-generating activities Experience analyzing commercialization metrics and preparing reports using Excel and business intelligence tools such as Power BI or Tableau Experience advising inventors on product development and commercialization Experience forecasting, planning, and monitoring complex budgets and producing complex statistical and/or financial reports Understanding of the AI and digital health innovation ecosystem, including commercialization considerations for AI-enabled medical technologies Strong proficiency with Microsoft Office and experience using customer relationship management (CRM) systems, such as Salesforce, HubSpot, or Microsoft Dynamics, to manage partnership pipelines, stakeholder engagement, and business development activities Ability to convey highly complex, technical, and confidential information Strong analytical skills and ability to communicate negotiation-related information clearly Effective relationship-management, collaboration, and conflict-resolution skills Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail To be successful in this role you will be: Diplomatic Discerning Entrepreneurial Persuasive Proactive This is a term position of 3 years. Closing Date: 10/29/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 19 -- $128,706 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $164,586. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Divisional HR Office Email: medhr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Rehabilitation, CRM, Product Development, Relationship Manager, Market Research, Healthcare, Technology, Research, Marketing, Customer Service Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Housing-Assistant-ON/607201417/": {"title": "Housing Assistant", "description": "Housing Assistant Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Housing Assistant Date Posted: 10/20/2026 Req ID: 50626 Faculty/Division: VP-Facilities & Real Estate Department: UNIVERSITY FAMILY HOUSING - CS Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00053282 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: University Family Housing is comprised of two 21 story residential towers and a unique stock of 83-century homes. The department provides housing to student families, faculty families and long-term residentialtenancies in two neighbourhoods on the St. George Campus to over 3000 adults and children, and provides on-site property management services, as well as educational and recreational programming for tenant families. Your opportunity: Under the direction of the Housing Administrator, the Housing Assistant is responsible for assisting the Administrator in maintaining a positive quality of student life in the Charles Street Student Family Residence. The primary responsibilities are to provide front-line customer service and to facilitate an open and easy flow of communication between all staff and contractors working at the residence. Other responsibilities include: entering, completing and monitoring electronic work order submissions, coordinating appliance deliveries; booking elevators and meeting rooms; storage and bicycle lockers; parking spaces for tenants and external parkers; reviewing contractor work schedules; closes tenant files; drafts various tenant letters; the collection and recording of rental payments, residence database maintenance; handling work orders; key control; mail distribution; answering routine residence queries and ordering office supplies. The Housing Assistant communicates with various departments and service providers on campus, such as Admissions & Eligibility, Campus Safety, Facilities & Services and Spaces & Experiences. The Assistant is responsible for appraising the Housing Administrator, Manager, Admissions & Housing Services and/or Assistant Director of any residence issues that may become a problem, as well as deals with day-to-day issues as part of the overall function of the position. Your responsibilities will include: Responding to enquiries within the defined scope of the role and redirecting as appropriate Troubleshooting and resolving routine maintenance requests and liaising with facilities or maintenance staff to facilitate resolution of building issues Informing contacts of maintenance work, service interruptions and other urgent notices Analyzing administrative processes and procedures, and recommending changes for improvement Applying established standards when respondingto emergencies Ordering supplies within established limits Serving as a resource to others by providing (non-supervisory) job-related guidance Essential Qualifications: Advanced College Diploma (3 years) or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum three (3) years' administrative experience in a customer service role, preferably in a residence environment. Intermediate proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Outlook). Must have strong written and verbal communication skills as well as excellent customer service skills. Must be tactful, professional and objective in dealing with residents. Good judgment, discretion and a pleasant and helpful attitude are essential. Must be organized, with strong ability to multitask and meet deadlines. Must possess the ability to work independently as well as in a team setting. Must display a willingness to take initiative in solving routine problems. Assets (Nonessential): Working knowledge of StarRez To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Multi-tasker Possess a positive attitude Problem solver Team player Closing Date: 10/29/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Ancillary Operations Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 07 -- $62,646 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $80,116. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Divisional HR Office Email: hruniversityoperations@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Equity, Database, Finance, Technology Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Co-op-Coordinator-ON/607206217/": {"title": "Co-op Coordinator", "description": "Co-op Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Co-op Coordinator Date Posted: 10/20/2026 Req ID: 50629 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering Department: FASE: Engineering Career Centre Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00045307 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Engineering Career Centre (ECC) connects University of Toronto students with meaningful professional experiences that provide a solid foundation for successful careers and life-long learning. In addition to hosting a wide range of professional development workshops, events and services throughout the year, the ECC team runs a work-integrated learning program that connects engineering students with a wide range of industry opportunities. As passionate and career-driven academic professionals, the ECC team seeks to nurture students and provide a comfortable transition from academic to professional life. Your opportunity: The Engineering Career Centre is the second largest operation of its kind in Ontario, offering extensive support to University of Toronto students seeking experiential learning opportunities. The ECC is undergoing rapid expansion in both team growth and program evolution. The EngineeringCareer Centre prides itself as an open, professional environment that fosters a culture built on respect, goal orientation, self-motivation, accountability, and teamwork. The leadership team believes in recognizing and valuing our employees\u2019 contributions to the advancement of the department\u2019s goals while promoting a strong commitment to work-life balance among our employees. The ECC team is credited with executing a highly successful work integrated learning program that connects engineering students with meaningful work terms of up to 16 months in length. Under the general direction of the Director, Employer Relations, the Co-op Coordinator will participate in business development activities and support student work-integrated learning during a Professional Experience Year (PEY) work term recruitment cycle. The Employer Relations team plays a valuable role in facilitating interactions between student job-seekers and hiring managers to solidify and grow existing relationships with PEY employers. Your responsibilities will include: Implementing plans that support the development of work-integrated learning opportunities for students. Advising students on work related recruitment processes and practices. Building and strengthening relationships with stakeholders and partners of strategic importance by engaging in day-to-day communication, and actively seeking networking and relationship-building opportunities. Probing forinformation from employers to establish activities that best meet student learning needs. Evaluating job prospects in alignment with student academic goals. Promoting programs at recruitment events Analyzing job descriptions and recommending changes to employer Conducting work term site visits and writing reports on site visit findings. Reviewing performance evaluations and providing feedback to both the employer and the student. Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum five years of recent and related experience in employer relations for an experiential learning program, preferably for a co-operative education or internship program in a post-secondary environment. Minimum two years of experience working directly with industry partners to facilitate co-op or other work-integrated learning placements through complete recruitment and work-termcycles. Demonstrated success developing and growing employer partnerships that result in newco-op, internship, or experiential learning opportunities through proactive outreach,engagement, and relationship building. Relevant experience analyzing co-op employment and employer engagement data toidentify gaps in sector representation and inform strategies for developing employerpartnerships, particularly within underrepresented and emerging industries. Experience interpreting and applying relevant academic, employment, and programpolicies to assess opportunities, provide recommendations, and ensure compliance in anexperiential learning environment. Strong computer skills and working knowledge of MS Outlook, Word, Excel, Access, PowerPoint; web editing software, relational databases, and the Internet research tools Must have excellent negotiation and conflict resolution skills Highly developed sense of accountability, initiative, judgement, tact, diplomacy, andprofessionalism. Results-orientation with high attention to detail and accuracy. Strong organizational and time-management skills with the proven ability to prioritize and meet multiple competing deadlines. Highly developed presentation, verbal, and written communication skills. Strong client service orientation and relationship management skills. Demonstrated ability to work effectively independently, with direction, and within a team environment. Ability to travel within the GTA and surrounding area with appropriate transportation. A passion and commitment to the University and its students, and ability to bring energy and creativity to the role. Demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment. Assets (Nonessential): Graduate degree or educational background in Engineering, Human Resources or Business Valid driver\u2019s license and access to a vehicle are assets Goal oriented and comfortable working in a target-based environment. Experience working with Customer Relationship Management (CRM) tools. Ability to work effectively with a wide variety of people at different levels of the University and with external stakeholders. To be successful in this role you will be: Accountable Achievement oriented Communicator Diplomatic Proactive Resilient Tactful Closing Date: 10/29/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 12 -- $84,564 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $108,145. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: CRM, Relationship Manager, Internet Research, Engineer, Equity, Technology, Customer Service, Research, Engineering, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Veterinary-Technologist-III-ON/607151417/": {"title": "Veterinary Technologist III Job Details", "description": "Veterinary Technologist III Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Veterinary Technologist III Date Posted: 10/19/2026 Req ID: 50609 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Div of Comparative Med. Campus : St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: General Description of Class Under general direction performs laboratory animal care and performs technical procedures requiring advanced training, experience and expertise on a regular basis. Typical Duties: The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required and the extent of responsibility involved in this job. They in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated. Flexibility of the employee to perform a wide variety of functions is necessary in successfully fulfilling the requirements of this position. The degree to which each employee performs each of the following tasks listed below will vary according to where and when the employee is scheduled to work. (a) participates in project specific work as requested by investigators or managerial staff; (b) assists in training of staff in technical procedures related to their expertise; (c) performs multiple technical or surgical procedures at an advanced level of training; (d) performs duties in the Level 3 containment area; (e) wears personal protective equipment as appropriate; (f) performs the duties of a Veterinary Technologist II and; (g) other related duties as required. Minimum Requirements for Selection Education: Graduate of a veterinary technician/technology diploma program or related university degree in biological/animal/veterinary sciences or equivalent. Experience: Three years of related experience with a minimum of two years as a Veterinary Technologist. Other: Being a Registered Laboratory Animal Technician through the Canadian Association for Laboratory Animal Science is considered an asset. Physically capable of performing the required duties, including lifting up to 50 lbs. No history of animal-related allergies. Must be willing to participate in the University Health and Safety program, which includes the requirement to undergo an immunization program depending on the work environment. Ability to communicate effectively in English (oral and written). Ability to take direction and work independently. May be required to be in possession of a valid Provincial Class \"G\" driver's license. Ability to work weekends and holidays as required. Closing Date: 10/28/2026,11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: CUPE F/T L3261 Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: Job Rate: $35.41/hr Job Category: Engineering / Technical Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Veterinarian, Veterinary Technician, Laboratory, Engineer, Veterinary, Science, Engineering Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Staff-Research-Scientist-%28AI-for-Self-Driving-Labs%2C-2-year-Term%29-ON/607133617/": {"title": "Staff Research Scientist (AI for Self-Driving Labs, 2-year Term)", "description": "Staff Research Scientist (AI for Self-Driving Labs, 2-year Term) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Staff Research Scientist (AI for Self-Driving Labs, 2-year Term) Date Posted: 10/19/2026 Req ID: 50600 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: Acceleration Consortium Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Description: T he Acceleration Consortium (AC), based at the University of Toronto (U of T), is a global community of academia, industry, and government working to accelerate the discovery and development of advanced materials and molecules. The AC develops self-driving laboratories (SDLs), autonomous research platforms that integrate artificial intelligence, robotics, automation, and advanced computing to dramatically reduce the time and cost of scientific discovery. AC Staff Research Scientists are highly skilled, experienced, and independent researchers that develop the AI and automation technologies required to build robust and scalable self-driving labs, manage these SDLs, and design and implement collaborative research programs that leverage the SDLs to accelerate discovery. \u00a0Staff Scientists will advance SDL technologies and apply them to challenges in areas such as clean energy, sustainability, healthcare, and advanced manufacturing. The Acceleration Consortium (AC) promotes inclusive research environment and supports the EDI priorities of the unit. The Acceleration Consortium received a $200M Canadian First Research Excellence Grant for seven years to develop self-driving labs for chemistry and materials, the largest ever grant to a Canadian University. This grant will provide the Acceleration Consortium with seven years of funding to execute its vision. The AC operates and continuously develops seven SDLs as core facilities: SDL0 - A central AI and automation lab to advance the robotics and AI tools used in SDLs SDL1 - Inorganic solid-state materials for advanced materials and energy SDL2 - Organic small molecules for sustainability and health SDL3 - Medicinal chemistry for improving small molecule drug candidates SDL4 - Polymers for materials science and biological applications SDL5 - Formulations for pharmaceuticals, consumer products, and coatings SDL6 - Human organ mimicry with organoids / organ-on-a-chip SDL7 - Synthetic scale-up of materials and molecules (University of British Colombia partner lab) This posted position is for a role within SDL0: AI & Automation. Experience in one or more of the following is desired: Close collaboration with experimental scientists, achieving scientific objectives with AI-driven systems. Agentic and sequential decision-making for autonomous experimentation, including active learning and optimal experimental design. Generative and probabilistic modeling, including uncertainty estimation, risk-aware prediction, and data-efficient learning. Applied machine learning on real-world experimental or industrial data, including multivariate time-series and noisy, sparse, or incomplete datasets. Orchestration and control of self-driving laboratories, including experimental workflow automation, instrument integration, and real-time data processing. Staff Research Scientists will work with a diverse team of leading experts at U of T, including Faculty and Staff Scientists in and associated with SDL0 such as: Al\u00e1n Aspuru-Guzik, Anatole von Lilienfeld, Kourosh Darvish, Florian Shkurti, Chris Sutton, Willi Gottstein, and more. Moreover, the Staff Scientists will work collectively, sharing knowledge among each other (spanning all AC labs), local and global AC faculty, and the many trainees that work in these labs. This role will report to the Academic Director and Executive Director of the Acceleration Consortium. The components and duties of the work can include: SDL and Automation Development Working with the AC community, including faculty and partners to determine the required capabilities of the SDLs to be built. Developing the plans for SDLs that will meet user requirements and designing novel instruments for automated material synthesis and characterization. Developing customized hardware and Python software packages to build SDLs. Selection, procurement, and installation of the equipment required for SDLs. Research Direction Working with the AC community, develop research programs that leverage the AC\u2019s SDLs and support the research objectives of AC faculty and industry partners. Using SDLs to synthesize and characterize large quantities of candidate molecules, calibrating theoretical models with experimental data, predicting promising candidates with computational tools and machine learning algorithms, and elucidating structure-property relationships of emerging molecules, polymers, solid-state materials, formulations, etc. Tasks include: Implementing research and development projects of AC\u2019s industry partners when implemented in AC labs Developing plans supporting research collaborations and estimating financial resources required for programs and/or projects. Working with Product Managers to ensure research outcomes meet partner requirements. Promoting AC\u2019s research capacity, including delivering presentations at conferences. Collaboration in preparing and submitting research proposals to granting agencies and progress reporting. Preparing manuscripts for submission to peer review publications/journals and stewarding them through the process. Other Supporting consulting services related to the application of SDLs for materials discovery for the AC\u2019s partners. Support research-focused events such as Annual Symposium. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Education \u2013 Ph.D. in Computational Chemistry, Software Engineering, Physics, Chemistry, Materials Science, Biology, or equivalent. Experience 1 to 5 years of experience (inclusive of PhD and/or post-graduate work) in research and development, preferably with significant experience in AI for self-driving labs. Experience in AI for science. Experience in the development of AI tools for self-driving labs. Experience working closely with a Principal Investigator or as a Principal Investigator or as Project Director with responsibilities of managing, developingand executing a major research project in the area of AI and automation, including AI utilization in experimental planning, and workflow establishment forseamless integration of experiments and simulations. Strong experience and expert knowledge of AI and automation. Experience working with industry partners and on industry led research anddevelopment projects. Strong experience presenting research at academic conferences. Demonstrated record of academic and/or research excellence. Skills Expert Skills Python, LATEX, Git, Microsoft Office. Strong and effective communicator in oral and written English. Collegial in working with team members and collaborators. Ability to work independently. Other Must have a strong publication record. Demonstrated success in writing and preparing manuscripts, presentations, reports, briefs, and scientific abstracts and manuscripts for peer-reviewed journals. Applications are being reviewed on a rolling basis. Please apply ASAP and do not wait for the listed job closing date. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Please refer to our website for some general information about benefits. Closing Date: 11/21/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Research Associate Appointment Type : Grant - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: R01 -- Research Associates (Limited Term):  $55,661 - $104,364, salary will be assessed based on skills and experience Job Category: Research Administration & Teaching Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: R&D Engineer, Research Scientist, Environmental Engineering, Chemistry, Software Engineer, Engineering, Science Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-LecturerAssistantAssociate-Professor-Forensic-Psychiatrist-ON/607139617/": {"title": "Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor", "description": "Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor - Forensic Psychiatrist Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor - Forensic Psychiatrist Date Posted: 10/19/2026 Closing Date: 11/26/2026 , 11:59PM ET, Open Until Filled Req ID: 50592 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Psychiatry Hospital Affiliation: Centre for Addiction & Mental Health Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Description: Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor - Forensic Psychiatrist The Department of Psychiatry, Faculty of Medicine at the University of Toronto and the Department of Psychiatry of The Centre for Addiction and Mental Health (CAMH), are seeking to recruit two psychiatrists \u2013 Forensic Psychiatry Division, to provide clinical care in the inpatient and outpatient program as part of the Forensic Division, Complex Care and Recovery Program. There are teaching opportunities with undergraduate and post graduate students, forensic psychiatry subspecialty residents and fellows, as well as potential opportunities for engagement in creative professional activities. The successful candidate must be eligible for a full-time clinical academic appointment at the rank of Lecturer, Assistant or Associate Professor in the Department of Psychiatry, at the University of Toronto. The effective start date is January 1, 2027 , or a mutually agreeable date thereafter. The Centre for Addiction and Mental Health (CAMH) is Canada\u2019s largest mental health teaching hospital and one of the world\u2019s leading research centres in its field. CAMH is fully affiliated with the University of Toronto and is a Pan America Health Organization/World Health Organization Collaborating Centre. With a dedicated staff of more than 4,000 physicians, clinicians, researchers, educators and support staff, CAMH offers outstanding clinical care to more than 37,000 patients each year and over 118 inpatient and outpatient clinical programs. The organization conducts ground-breaking research through its 11 research centres and provides expert training to over 13,000 health care professionals and scientists. In addition, CAMH delivers education programs to over 40,000 healthcare professionals each year and advocates on public policy issues at all levels of government. The successful candidate must hold an MD degree, must be Board certified or Board Eligible in Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada Specialty, and must be eligible for medical licensure with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario.\u00a0 As a full-time staff member at CAMH, the candidate will provide on-call services as part of their clinical responsibilities. Remuneration is in accordance with the compensation of a psychiatrist in the province of Ontario.\u00a0\u00a0 Estimated remuneration will be in the range of $300,000 - $400,968 per annum, commensurate with academic rank, qualifications and experience.\u00a0 All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply by November 15, 2026. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Should you be interested in this opportunity, please forward a one-page statement of interest, curriculum vitae and the names and contact information of three referees via email to: Dr. Treena Wilkie Chief of Forensic Services and the Deputy Physician-in-Chief, Medical Affairs and Practice; Centre for Addiction and Mental Health; 1001 Queen Street West, Unit 3-4, Toronto, ON M6J 1H4. The Centre for Addiction and Mental Health treena.wilkie@camh.ca About the Forensic Psychiatry Division The Forensic Service at CAMH is a growing and vibrant clinical program of over 190 inpatient beds, court and community programs, a sexual behaviors program and a correction-based mental health service.\u00a0 We have strong research involvement in multiple areas including correctional mental health, sexual behaviors, neurobiology of aggression, risk and secure recovery.\u00a0 The successful candidate will join a collegial team of over 25 psychiatrists and will provide exemplary team-based psychiatric care for people with acute or persisting mental illness, including concurrent substance use disorders. The ideal candidate will have exemplary clinical skills and experience working with an interdisciplinary team, and be dedicated to high quality patient-centered care. For more information on the University of Toronto, Department of Psychiatry, please visit http://www.psychiatry.utoronto.ca . For more information about Centre for Addiction and Mental Health (CAMH), please visit https://www.camh.ca/ . CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Counseling, Behavioral Health, Substance Abuse, Public Policy, Healthcare, Government, Legal Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Senior-Development-Officer-%28TERM%29-ON/607129617/": {"title": "Senior Development Officer (TERM) Job Details", "description": "Senior Development Officer (TERM) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Senior Development Officer (TERM) Date Posted: 10/19/2026 Req ID: 50464 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Nursing Department: Lawrence Bloomberg Faculty of Nursing Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00054404 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Lawrence Bloomberg Faculty of Nursing at the University of Toronto is Canada\u2019s top faculty of nursing and ranked among the top nursing faculties in the world. Recognized as a global leader in ground-breaking research and education, the Faculty has produced more than 13,000 nursing leaders in clinical, research, educational and administrative roles over the past century. Our faculty members, students, staff, and alumni make up a vibrant community rich with impact. At Bloomberg Nursing, we thrive on the challenge to create better outcomes in health care \u2013 locally, nationally, and across the globe. As we continue to advocate for the communities and people who are under-served by our health caresystems, you will find us at the forefront of research and education that makes a difference. Your opportunity: The Lawrence Bloomberg Faculty of Nursing\u2019s Advancement Office is critical to this success. As leading advancement professionals, we are committed to excellence and take pride in connecting alumni, volunteers, and donors to impactful Faculty initiatives. Through our work, we play a tangible role in advancing the future of nursing and health care. As part of the collaborative and performance driven Advancement Office, the Senior Development Officer will work under the general direction of the Director of Advancement. As Senior Development Officer, you will contribute to Annual and Leadership Giving, Major Gift and Gift Planning fundraising initiatives across the Faculty. In this role, you will collaborate with colleagues in the Advancement Office, across the Faculty, and throughout the Division of University Advancement to develop meaningful relationships, increase donors\u2019 engagement with the Faculty, and solicit donations that will advance the priorities of the Faculty and strengthen the Faculty\u2019s donor pipeline. Your responsibilitieswill include: Assessing needs and contributing to the development and implementation of plans for prospect identification, cultivation, solicitation and recognition Determining the appropriate involvement of members of the university community and volunteers in the cultivation, solicitation and recognition process Meeting face-to-face with current and potential donors to discuss giving interests and opportunities Identifying, evaluating and recommending the necessary steps to bring the prospect closer to making a major financial commitment to the University Developing tailored fundraising initiatives that support strategic initiatives Developing marketing/communications strategies that support fundraising campaigns and programs Developing and implementing plans to support donor management and stewardship strategies and/or activities Writing briefing notes, solicitation plans and call reports to track donor interaction Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum of five (5) years\u2019 experience in a non-profit development office. Experience with leadership annual giving and/or major gift fundraising experience in a post-secondary environment preferred. Demonstrated experience managing a portfolio of donor relationships, including one-on-one donor identification, cultivation, solicitation and stewardship. Proven track record of soliciting and bringing prospects closer to a financial commitment. Passion for individual giving fundraising techniques, including face to face solicitation and tailored philanthropic strategies. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills (both oral and written), with an ability to engage and influence a wide range of community members and build long-term relationships. Ability to work productively and effectively with individuals of affluence and influence. Proven ability to motivate others (volunteers, team members, donors, etc.). Strong team player who values collaboration. Demonstrated proposal and presentation skills. Evidence of leadership, initiative, tact, diplomacy, attention to detail and creativity. Possess a high level of integrity, donor confidentiality and discretion with sensitive information, tasks and relationships. Ability to handle multiple competing priorities and excel in a results-oriented environment by meeting established personal and team goals. Strong computer skills including demonstrated proficiency with Microsoft 365 and donor databases. To be successful in this role you will be: Achievement oriented Articulate Communicator Diplomatic Persuasive Proactive Resourceful Team player Closing Date: 10/27/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 15 -- $101,242 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $129,471. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Divisional HR Office Email: pfhr@utoronto.ca Note: This is a TERM position for six (6) months. Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Marketing Communications, Communications, Fundraising, Medical Research, Marketing, Nonprofit, Research, Healthcare Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Intermediate-Financial-Analyst-ON/607154217/": {"title": "Intermediate Financial Analyst Job Details", "description": "Intermediate Financial Analyst Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Intermediate Financial Analyst Date Posted: 10/19/2026 Req ID: 50611 Faculty/Division: VP-People, Finance & Digital Services Department: Capital Accounting Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00000171 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Financial Services is a department within the Vice President - People, Finance and Digital Services portfolio which supports the academic goals and objectives of the University through excellent financial management, and effective and appropriate use of all financial resources (operating, research, trust and capital funds). The University\u2019s decentralized management model places financial management responsibility within every division of the University as well as within Financial Services. The major long-term priority for the office includes: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0to meet legislative, regulatory and reporting requirements for financial activities; \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0to direct and manage key activities with the external financial community on behalf of the University (e.g. banking, treasury); \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0to efficiently and effectively deliver core services to divisions that are provided centrally by Financial Services Your Opportunity: The Financial Services Department (FSD) provides financial expertise to the University\u2019s community. Comprised of a group of accounting professionals, the FSD office is focused on financial reporting and the University Guide to Financial Management policy compliance. As the Intermediate Financial Analyst, you will perform a broad range of duties including financial reporting, analysis and financial management. You will foster strong working relationships with stakeholders and leverage your analytical skills to synthesize information, uncover trends, and deliver insights to optimize internal processes and improve decision-making. Your Responsibilities will include: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Overseeing the financial management of budgets that include strategic planning, analysis and forecasting. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Overseeing, analyzing and forecasting revenue-generating activities. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Advising staff on accounting practices and University financial policies and procedures. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Interpreting and applying policies and procedures when making independent decisions. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Making recommendations on budget allocations involving multiple sources of revenue and recoveries \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Forecasting and planning financial activities incorporating budgets with multiple sources of revenue and/or recoveries. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Transferring funds and expenditures within the context of an overall plan. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Implementing plans and process improvements for financial administration activities. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Monitoring, recording, reconciling and/or reporting on funding accounts for grants and contracts. Identifying and resolving individual financial discrepancies. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Applying the University Guide to Financial Management and other applicable policies, agency and regulatory requirements. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Acting as a first point of contact for internal and external auditors. Providing detailed information regarding the auditors' final report. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Performing complex financial data modeling and analysis. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Conducting financial research and analysis. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Identifying and analyzing data discrepancies and taking necessary actions to correct errors. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Handling sensitive and/or confidential information. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Keeping well-informed on changes to policies, procedures, collective agreements, and applicable legislated requirements. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Reviewing asset purchase expenses and determines proper accounting treatment according to the University financial policies and Canadian Accounting Standards. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Reconciling conference fund accounts \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Preparing government reports such as Statistics Canada report and Council of Ontario Finance Officers Financial report Essential Qualifications: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Bachelor's Degree with focus in accounting, advanced standing in a recognized accounting program or equivalent combination of education and experience \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Minimum five years\u2019 related financial experience in accounting, modeling, analysis, and financial reporting, in a University or similar public sector environment. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Experience in capital project management and knowledge of construction industry. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Hands-on experience in preparing financial statements. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Skilled in maintaining complex financial models. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Proven ability to conduct financial research and present findings effectively. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Demonstrated success in introducing innovative solutions and processes to improve efficiencies in financial management. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Successful track record of providing support and consultation to various stakeholders. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Advanced proficiency with MS Office Suite, including expert knowledge of MS Excel and Financial Information System (FIS). \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Strong written and oral communication skills. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Demonstrated ability to apply knowledge of accounting principles. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Highly attentive to detail and accuracy. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Demonstrated ability to organize and execute complex projects and manage conflicting priorities within established timelines. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Ability to work independently as well as a collaborative team member in a multi-stakeholder environment. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Ability to exercise sound judgment, respect matters of a sensitive nature, and maintain confidentiality. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Strong organizational skills NOTE:\u00a0 This position is 70% on site. Closing Date: 11/02/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time NOTE:\u00a0 This position is 70% on site. Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 15 -- $101,242 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $129,471. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Finance/Budget/Planning/Audit Divisional HR Office Email: cahrs.hr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Financial Analyst, Compliance, Construction, Data Modeler, Project Manager, Finance, Legal, Engineering, Data, Technology Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Customer-Experience-Representative-ON/607155417/": {"title": "Customer Experience Representative Job Details", "description": "Customer Experience Representative Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Customer Experience Representative Date Posted: October 19, 2026 Req ID: 50607 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Kinesiology and Physl Ed. Department: Faculty of Kinesiology and Physl Ed. Campus: St. George (downtown) campus Position Number: 38585 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The University of Toronto\u2019s Faculty of Kinesiology and Physical Education is globally recognized for developing and advancing knowledge about the interactions of physical activity and health through outstanding undergraduate and graduate education programs, cutting-edge research and the delivery of sport, recreation and high performance athletic opportunities for students, staff, faculty and community members across the three campuses. In achieving this vision, the Faculty is guided by values of integrity, respect, equity and diversity https://kpe.utoronto.ca/. Your opportunity: Reporting to the Manager, Active Healthy Living Centre, the Customer Experience Representative is responsible for working cooperatively, in a team environment to deliver a high level of customer service to all current and potential members of the athletic centre. The incumbent\u2019s role is to project a positive, welcoming, and professional image at all times, representing the Faculty in an inclusive manner and to provide fast, efficient, and friendly customer service. Must have the ability to work evenings, weekends and weekdays. Your responsibilities will include: Using Fusion recreation management software system for membership sales, program registratrions, towel and locker sales and other transactions Providing detailed information on program and/or course eligibility requirements, procedures, policies and deadlines Troubleshooting and resolving routine issues Disseminating information Applying established standards when responding to emergencies Serving as a resource to others by providing (non-supervisory) job-related guidance Essential Qualifications: Advanced College Diploma (3 years) or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum three years experience working in a front-desk customer service focused role in an athletic facility Minimum one year processing transactions on Fusion recreation management software, including Point of Sale, registrations, scheduling and reporting Experience working with the public ina high volume, fast-paced environment Proficiency with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, Publisher) and AdobeAcrobat is required Strong interpersonal skills Ability to exercise tact, diplomacy and discretion Strong conflict resolution skills Displays good judgement Strong customer service focus Strong knowledge of the Faculty\u2019s Intramural, Intercollegiate, Instruction, Junior Blues, and Camp U of T programs and procedures To be successful in this role you will be: Approachable Communicator Intuitive Multi-tasker Organized Problem solver Team player Closing Date: October 28, 2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - continuing Schedule: Full-time, Monday to Friday, 6:45am-2:30pm Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 07 -- $62,646. with an annual step progression to a maximum of $80,116. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay\u00a0Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Athletics Divisional HR Office Email: kpe.hr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Customer Service Representative, Front Desk, Facilities, Equity, Customer Service, Administrative, Operations, Research, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Program-Coordinator-ON/607138517/": {"title": "Program Coordinator", "description": "Program Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Program Coordinator Date Posted: 10/19/2026 Req ID: 50603 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Anesthesiology & Pain Medicine Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00052975 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Home to over 40 departments and institutes, the University of Toronto's Temerty Faculty of Medicine lies at the heart of the Toronto Academic Health Science Network and is a global leader in ground-breaking research and education, spanning clinical medicine, basic science and the rehabilitation sciences sectors. Your opportunity: The Department of Anesthesiology & Pain Medicine is a hub of excellence, innovation, and very high in academic productivity. We are the leading department of anesthesia in the country, and amongst the leading departments in the world. We are an assembly of over 640 members; faculty and trainees combined who are dedicated to providing outstanding clinical care for every patient across the city and the province and to constantly improving care through relentless innovation. We are advancing medical education to better support our community of learners, including patients, students, residents, fellows and faculty. As Program Coordinator, Anesthesia Residency Program, you will work collaboratively to support our residency education programs. Drawing upon your excellent communication skills and keen attention to detail, you will serve as a central facilitator, frequently liaising with trainees and faculty to provide program administrative support for over 100 residents. Your strong organizational skills and technical proficiency, and adeptness at working with online course materials, assessments and evaluations are key to the successful delivery. Your responsibilities will include: Responding to enquiries and providing detailed information to students and residents on program and/or course requirements Ensuring hospital administrators follow medical education requirements, guidelines, and procedures Checking program, application, and Royal College training requirements and supporting documentation for accuracy and completeness Coordinating program, course, examination, interview, and meeting schedules and activities Drafting routine correspondence and updating records and web content Maintaining course, program, and student information in student information systems and databases Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience Minimum two years of program coordination and student services experience in a university or teaching hospital environment Demonstrated experience coordinating education program administration and ensuring program requirements, guidelines, and procedures are adhered to Demonstrated experience coordinating examination timetables, program schedules, and related program activities Demonstrated experience checking, verifying, and maintaining the accuracy and completeness of program, application, and student records and documentation Experience providing front-line support to students, residents, faculty, academic leaders, committees, and other stakeholders Experience coordinating meetings and committee support, including schedules, agendas, materials, minutes, and follow-up items Experience supporting events and implementing virtual meeting platforms Experience drafting correspondence, maintaining databases, and generating reports Advanced proficiency with MS Office Suite, student information systems, learning management systems, videoconferencing platforms, and related administrative technologies Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with tact, diplomacy, and the ability to respond to enquiries with clarity and professionalism Strong organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines, and adapt to changing demands Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently and collaboratively Assets (Nonessential): Experience with medical education curriculum processes Experience working with POWER, Elentra, Quercus, MEDSIS, OATS To be successful in this role you will be: Adaptable Communicator Proactive Problem solver This is a term position until June 2028. Closing Date: 10/27/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 09 -- $70,633 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $90,329. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Divisional HR Office Email: medhr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Rehabilitation, Information Systems, Anesthesia, Administrative Assistant, Program Manager, Healthcare, Technology, Administrative, Management Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Director%2C-Strategy%2C-Operations-&-Compliance-ON/607149617/": {"title": "Director, Strategy, Operations & Compliance", "description": "Director, Strategy, Operations & Compliance Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Director, Strategy, Operations & Compliance Date Posted: 10/19/2026 Req ID: 50610 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Emerging & Pandemic Infections Consortum Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00060161 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Description: About Us: Home to over 40 departments and institutes, the University of Toronto's Temerty Faculty of Medicine lies at the heart of the Toronto Academic Health Science Network and is a global leader in ground-breaking research and education, spanning clinical medicine, basic science and the rehabilitation sciences sectors. Your Opportunity: The Office of the Vice Dean, Research, Innovation & Health Science Education oversees all research undertaken for the Temerty Faculty of Medicine and coordinates with its counterparts at the affiliated hospital research institutes for clinical research. This includes grant proposal development, administering internal funding allocations, collecting and reporting on research productivity metrics, and managing core research facilities. The Toronto High Containment Facility (THCF) has expanded its physical operations and level of service extensively since the onset of the COVID-19 pandemic. With the support of federal and provincial governments, new space and infrastructure will launch in 2027, including emerging Biobank and Viral Core platforms, to support a larger client base in infectious disease research. The facility is also a platform for delivering the Emerging Pathogens and Infectious Disease Consortium (EPIC) programming and commitments, which fosters collaboration, partnership, and integration of research and expertise across the University, affiliated hospital research institutes and industry partners. As the Director, Strategy, Operations and Compliance, you will provide strategic, operational, and programmatic leadership to support the expanded mandate of the Toronto High Containment Facility and its associated institutional initiatives, including EPIC. Working closely with the Vice Dean, Academic Directors, and institutional partners, you will oversee strategic planning, facility operations, regulatory compliance, financial management, and partnership development. Your leadership will contribute to the successful launch of the expanded facility, strengthen collaboration across the infectious disease research community, and support the long-term sustainability of its programs. Essential Qualifications PhD in molecular or cellular biology, infectious disease, immunology, or an acceptable combination of education and experience Minimum ten (10) years of experience in strategic planning, operational management, and implementation of complex research programs or initiatives within an academic, research, or healthcare environment Detailed knowledge of Canadian regulations governing biological agents and biocontainment laboratories, including regulatory and compliance requirements for biosafety level 3 facilities Demonstrated experience liaising with government and institutional regulatory bodies to meet compliance and regulatory requirements for commissioning and decommissioning high containment facilities Experience with the operations and maintenance of complex infrastructure and equipment supporting high-containment research facilities Experience planning and implementing research infrastructure projects, including facility development, expansion, or upgrades Demonstrated experience developing and managing strategic partnerships and collaborative research initiatives involving academic institutions, hospitals, government, and industry partners Experience developing financial sustainability strategies for research facilities, including identifying external funding opportunities, revenue sources, and service growth opportunities Demonstrated experience in financial management, including budget development and oversight, financial forecasting, resource allocation, and financial reporting Demonstrated experience managing staff, including recruitment, performance management, staff development, and organizational planning Experience supporting organizational governance and developing and implementing policies, procedures, and operational processes for research programs or facilities Experience coordinating research and infrastructure funding proposals involving institutional and external research partners, reporting on progress to funding agencies Demonstrated experience managing communications and external engagement activities for research programs or initiatives Strong research and analytical skills, including the ability to assess opportunities across scientific and technical disciplines Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to synthesize complex information and present clear recommendations to senior leadership and external stakeholders Strong negotiation, diplomacy, and consensus-building skills, with the ability to navigate complex stakeholder interests and resolve competing priorities Excellent judgment, tact, and discretion in handling sensitive and confidential matters and making decisions on complex operational and strategic issues Assets (Nonessential) Experience in a senior administrative role within a university or similarly complex research organization Closing Date: 10/28/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Appointment Type : Grant - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 6 -- Hiring Zone: $137,645 - $160,585 -- Broadband Salary Range: $137,645 - $229,410 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Divisional HR Office Email: medhr@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Operations Manager, Rehabilitation, Immunology, EMR, Compliance, Operations, Healthcare, Legal Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-Anesthesiology-&-Pain-Medicine-Unity-Health-ON/607092717/": {"title": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor", "description": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor | Anesthesiology & Pain Medicine | Unity Health Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Assistant / Associate / Full Professor | Anesthesiology & Pain Medicine | Unity Health Date Posted: 10/15/2026 Closing Date: 11/30/2026 , 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50559 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Anesthesiology & Pain Medicine Hospital Affiliation: Unity Health Toronto - St. Michael's Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Department of Anesthesiology & Pain Medicine, Temerty Faculty of Medicine at the University of Toronto, and Unity Health Toronto - St. Michael\u2019s Hospital are seeking an academic anesthesiologist to fulfill a strategic role within the Department of Anesthesia at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. The anticipated start date will be July 1, 2027, or one which is mutually agreed upon. The successful candidate will provide anesthetic care throughout the hospital programs including supervision and teaching of students, residents, and fellows. On-call services will be provided in rotation. Participation in formal in-house and University teaching programs, as well as hospital administrative duties, will be expected. Academic opportunities for research and teaching are available. Academic time is assigned according to an objective assessment of requirements. The incumbent will have major clinical responsibilities and in addition to their own academic activities, will facilitate the research, teaching, and education by others. Teaching may be done concurrently with clinical care and/or in organized educational programs. Strategic needs currently include, among others, cardiovascular anesthesia and cardiovascular critical care, interventional pain, obstetric anesthesia, and educational leadership. The successful candidate must have a medical degree, postgraduate fellowship training, Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada certification in Anesthesia, or international equivalent, and be eligible for licensure with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario. The successful candidate must have proven clinical skills at a high level, evidence of demonstrated excellence in research and/or education and/or quality improvement, and a commitment to teaching students, residents, and fellows. Scholarly excellence will be assessed using University of Toronto, Temerty Faculty of Medicine guidelines. St. Michael\u2019s Hospital is part of Unity Health Toronto, which includes Providence, St. Joseph\u2019s, and St. Michael\u2019s. St. Michael\u2019s is one of Canada\u2019s leading academic health sciences centres and is fully affiliated with the University of Toronto. Located in downtown Toronto, it provides secondary, tertiary, and quaternary care services for Toronto, southern Ontario, and beyond. The Hospital is organized in a programmatic fashion with an emphasis on Heart & Vascular Disease, Trauma and Neurosurgery, Neuromusculoskeletal Disorders, Oncology, Specialized Services, Inner City Health, and Diabetes Comprehensive Care. The Hospital services more than 77,000 patients annually in our emergency department, 520,000 ambulatory visits, and over 25,000 inpatients, with more than 450 inpatient beds and 25 operating rooms. The Department of Anesthesia at St. Michael\u2019s is known for its clinical excellence and dedication to quality improvement, research, and education. A new patient care tower opened in 2020 that includes modernized operating rooms and critical care areas. Compensation for clinical activities and academic rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience and within the usual range for an academic anesthetist in the Province of Ontario ($350,000 \u2013 550,000 per annum). Applications will be accepted until November 30, 2026, or until the position is filled. Applicants should submit a letter of interest, a copy of their curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information of three referees to: Dr. Nick Lo Interim Chief, Department of Anesthesia Unity Health Toronto - St. Michael\u2019s Hospital, Toronto Nick.Lo@unityhealth.to For more information about the Department of Anesthesia at the University of Toronto, please visit our website at http://www.anesthesia.utoronto.ca/ CAUTION: This ad is \u201cposted only\u201d to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above\u00a0for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position . Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Anesthesia, ICU, Medical, Patient Care, Medical Technologist, Healthcare Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Senior-Manager%2C-Information-Security-ON/607109817/": {"title": "Senior Manager, Information Security Job Details", "description": "Senior Manager, Information Security Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Senior Manager, Information Security Date Posted: 10/16/2026 Req ID: 50591 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: Information and Instructional Technology Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00055831 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About Us The Faculty of Arts & Science is the heart of Canada\u2019s leading university and one of the world's most comprehensive and diverse academic divisions. The strength of Arts & Science derives from our combined teaching and research excellence in the humanities, sciences and social sciences across 29 departments, seven colleges and 46 interdisciplinary centres, institutes and programs. We can only realize our mission with the dedication and excellence of engaged staff and faculty. The faculty\u2019s diversity of opportunities and perspectives reflects the local and global landscape and the need for curiosity, innovative thinking, and collaboration. At Arts & Science, we take pride in our legacy of innovation and discovery that has changed how we think about the world. The Faculty\u2019s divisional IT team, Information & Instructional Technology (IIT) provides divisional IT services and support across the Faculty including day to day computing and infrastructure fulfillment as well as data centre and public web services and application development. Working collaboratively with central University IT and local departmental IT teams, IIT supports teaching, research, and administrative operations through secure, reliable, and modern technology solutions. Your Opportunity Reporting to the Executive Director, Information & Instructional Technology, and with a dotted-line relationship to the University's Chief Information Security & Digital Trust Officer (CISDTO), the Senior Manager, Information Security provides strategic and operational leadership for the Faculty's information security and IT risk management programs. The Senior Manager, Information Security is responsible for developing, implementing, and advancing a coordinated, division-wide approach to information security and technology risk. Working collaboratively with institutional security leadership, divisional IT, and departmental IT teams, the incumbent strengthens the Faculty's security posture while supporting the diverse needs of teaching, research, and administration. The role combines strategic planning, security program development, risk assessment and program management, technical expertise, incident coordination, and stakeholder engagement. It also supports the responsible adoption of emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence, automation, and cloud services, in alignment with University policies, standards, and governance requirements. As a member of the Faculty's IT leadership team, the Senior Manager, Information Security fosters a proactive, collaborative, and risk-aware security culture while balancing security requirements with academic and operational priorities. Key Responsibilities Information Security Strategy and Risk Management Lead the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of divisional information security and IT risk management programs. Establish security priorities, assess vulnerabilities, identify risks, and recommend appropriate controls and remediation strategies. Support the adoption and implementation of University information security policies, standards, governance requirements, and industry best practices. Develop security reporting, risk assessments, performance measures, and recommendations to support informed leadership decisions. Advise on security and risk considerations associated with emerging technologies, including AI, automation, cloud platforms, and digital innovation. Security Operations and Incident Management Coordinate divisional security incident response, investigations, escalation, and remediation in collaboration with institutional security teams and departmental IT. Support security assessments, technical investigations, vulnerability management, and risk reduction initiatives. Collaborate with functional IT Managers and teams to strengthen operational resilience, security controls, and business continuity readiness. Review proposed technology solutions and projects to identify security risks and recommend appropriate safeguards. Leadership and Program Delivery Lead and manage assigned security personnel, resources, priorities, projects, and operational activities. Develop and oversee security initiatives, including planning, budgeting, procurement, vendor management, implementation, and performance reporting. Collaboration, Governance and Security Awareness Build strong working relationships with Faculty leadership, departmental IT teams, institutional security teams, and other stakeholders. Promote a consistent and collaborative approach to information security and risk management across the Faculty. Provide expert security advice to academic and administrative units on technology initiatives, risk mitigation, and compliance requirements. Support security awareness, education, and engagement initiatives for faculty, staff, and students. Required Qualifications Education University degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Information Technology, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. Graduate degree and professional certifications such as CISSP, CISM, CISA, CRISC, PMP, or equivalent are considered assets. Experience Information Security and Risk Management Minimum eight (8) years of progressively responsible experience in information technology, with significant experience in information security, IT risk management, and security program development. Demonstrated experience developing, implementing, and improving information security policies, standards, controls, and risk management practices. Strong experience assessing security risks across enterprise technology environments, including endpoints, servers, networks, cloud services, applications, vendor solutions and identity systems. Experience coordinating security incidents, investigations, vulnerability assessments, and remediation activities. Experience with security monitoring, threat detection, defense-in-depth strategies, and security assessment tools. Experience supporting compliance reviews, security audits, and the implementation of security governance requirements. Technology and Infrastructure Minimum eight (8) years of experience in an IT operations, infrastructure, or technology support environment. Strong understanding of enterprise IT architecture, networking, cloud platforms, infrastructure security, and business-critical applications. Experience with Microsoft enterprise technologies, including Azure, Microsoft Entra ID, and associated security and identity management capabilities. Knowledge of change management, configuration management, and technology lifecycle practices. Familiarity with the security and governance considerations associated with artificial intelligence, automation, and emerging technologies. Leadership and Management Minimum eight (8) years of experience in a formal people management or technology leadership role. Demonstrated success leading and mentoring technical teams, managing competing priorities, and delivering complex initiatives. Experience with project and program management, financial planning, budgeting, procurement, vendor management, and contract oversight. Proven ability to collaborate with diverse stakeholders and influence outcomes across decentralized or complex organizational environments. Skills and Competencies Strong strategic thinking, leadership, organizational, and decision-making abilities. Excellent interpersonal, relationship management, and communication skills. Ability to translate complex technical and security issues into clear, practical recommendations for senior leadership and non-technical stakeholders. Strong analytical, problem-solving, risk assessment, and incident management capabilities. Ability to manage multiple priorities, respond effectively to urgent issues, and exercise sound judgment under pressure. Strong commitment to collaboration, confidentiality, professionalism, and service excellence. Ability to navigate complex organizational structures, build consensus, and escalate issues appropriately. Demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity, and inclusion. Additional Assets Experience working in a large, decentralized organization, preferably within higher education or a research-intensive environment. Familiarity with IT Service Management and ITIL practices, including platforms such as ServiceNow. Familiarity with AI security governance, cloud security assessments, and enterprise technology risk management. LEAN, Six Sigma, or related process improvement experience. Other Requirements Availability to respond to critical security incidents outside regular working hours, when required. Ability to manage sensitive and confidential information with discretion and integrity. Closing Date: 11/06/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 5 -- Hiring Zone: $125,319 - $146,206 -- Broadband Salary Range: $125,319  - $208,864 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Information Security, Cloud, Information Technology, IT Manager, Risk Management, Technology, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Service-Worker-Caretaking-ON/607120217/": {"title": "Service Worker Caretaking Job Details", "description": "Service Worker Caretaking Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Service Worker Caretaking Date Posted: 10/16/2026 Req ID: 50401 Faculty/Division: New College Department: New College Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Under general supervision works according to detailed procedures in cleaning and custodial duties, may assist in other maintenance duties. Typical Duties The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required, and the extent of responsibility involved in this position.\u00a0 They in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated. Flexibility of the employee to perform a wide variety of functions is necessary in successfully fulfilling the requirements of this position.\u00a0 The degree to which each employee performs each of the following tasks listed below will vary according to where and when the employee is scheduled to work. a) cleans and dusts furniture, floors, hallways, stairways and ledges, using authorized and appropriate materials and equipment including heavy duty electric buffers, automatic floor machines, large dust mops,\u00a0 vacuum cleaners , carpet cleaning equipment and other cleaning equipment; b) reconditions floors as required; including stripping, refinishing, scrubbing, spray buffing, buffing, sealing and other related floor care duties; c) regularly cleans washrooms, including sinks, walls and partitions, toilets, urinals, mirrors, floors, metal fixtures, plumbing fixtures and faucets; d) collects litter from floors and waste/compost from receptacles, empties into janitor cart, removes garbage/recycling\u00a0 from buildings and deposits into waste bins or compactors; e) cleans carpets as required; removes spots/stains from surfaces as required; f) washes windows and walls including partition glass; g) moves and resets furniture when necessary in order to complete work; h) makes beds for residence guests in residence operations when necessary; i) cleans blackboards, whiteboards and other writing surfaces as directed; replenishes supplies as required; j) replenishes paper towels, toilet paper, hand soap and sanitizers to receptacles within washrooms and utility kitchens and other areas as required; k) changes light bulbs and cleans fixtures as required; l) clears exterior entrance ways of buildings of debris and garbage; m) cleans exterior entrance pads and podiums using power washing equipment; n) assists in snow removal when necessary; o) may periodically assist with set ups for special events and exams; p) cleans escalators and elevator interior and exterior; q) locks and unlocks doors as directed; and r) other related duties as required. Minimum Requirements for Selection Education:\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Completion of tenth grade or equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience:\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 One (1) year of related work experience is desirable. Other: Physical ability to perform duties described and to use indicated equipment. Ability to communicate effectively in English (oral and written). Note: There is one (1) full-time position available. The hours of work for this onsite position are Wednesday to Sunday, 8:00am to 4:30pm. Closing Date: 10/27/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: CUPE F/T L3261 Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: Job Rate: $25.96/hr Job Category: Hospitality Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Event Planning, Equity, Hospitality, Finance Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Program-Administrator%2C-Strategic-Initiatives-%28TERM%29-ON/607121717/": {"title": "Program Administrator, Strategic Initiatives (TERM) Job Details", "description": "Program Administrator, Strategic Initiatives (TERM) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Program Administrator, Strategic Initiatives (TERM) Date Posted: 10/16/2026 Req ID: 50597 Faculty/Division: Henry N.R. Jackman Faculty of Law Department: Henry N.R. Jackman Faculty of Law Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00059634 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Henry N.R. Jackman Faculty of Law is one of the oldest professional faculties at the University of Toronto. Today, it is one of the world's great law schools. The Faculty's rich academic programs are complemented by its many legal clinics and public interest programs. Jackman Law is housed in the elegant, state-of-the-art Jackman Law Building, alongside two historic buildings, Flavelle House and Falconer Hall, on the St. George Campus in downtown Toronto. Your opportunity: Jackman Law is undertaking a range of strategic initiatives designed to advance the Faculty's priorities and strengthen its academic programs, student experience and broader engagement. This is an exciting opportunity to join a collaborative team and contribute to the development and implementation of high-impact initiatives across the Faculty. Under the general direction of the Head of Strategy and Transformation & Senior Advisor to the Dean, the Program Administrator, Strategic Initiatives will provide project, program and administrative leadership for a diverse portfolio of strategic priorities. The incumbent will coordinate projects from planning through implementation, support the development and delivery of new and evolving programs, build strong relationships with internal and external partners, and help ensure initiatives are delivered effectively, thoughtfully and on schedule. Your responsibilities will include: Planning and implementing project phases for programs and strategic initiatives. Coordinating meeting schedules, agendas, materials, deadlines, action and follow-up items for the Head of Strategy and Transformation & Senior Advisor to the Dean. Implementing plans and process improvements for Faculty program activities and initiatives. Fostering cooperative working relationships with a wide variety of internal and external contacts, such as faculty, staff, students, and partners. Drafting internal and external communications in support of strategic priorities and initiatives. Conceptualizing, organizing and executing event and programming activities. Supporting funding opportunities by drafting funding applications. Monitoring accounts for a project and/or program. Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum five years of relevant experience in program administration, project coordination, or strategic initiatives, preferably within a higher education or similarly complex organization Demonstrated experience coordinating multiple projects or initiatives, including establishing work plans, managing timelines and deliverables, coordinating stakeholders, and identifying and resolving issues. Experience supporting the development, implementation and administration of programs, services or strategic initiatives. Demonstrated experience interpreting and applying policies, procedures and guidelines and exercise sound judgment in determining appropriate courses of action. Experience researching and analyzing information, processes or programs and developing recommendations for improvement. Experience providing executive support to a senior leader, including managing meeting schedules, agendas, materials, deadlines, action and follow-up items, and arranging travel. Experience developing effective working relationships with a wide range of internal and external stakeholders. Experience planning and coordinating events involving multiple stakeholders. Demonstrated experience drafting, editing and proofreading high-quality communications, reports, correspondence and other materials for internal and external audiences. Experience coordinating promotional, outreach or communications activities across print and/or digital channels. Experience gathering and analyzing data and preparing reports and other information to support planning and decision-making. Experience supporting funding applications, including researching opportunities, gathering information, preparing application materials and monitoring deadlines. Experience with project or program financial administration, including monitoring budgets/accounts, processing expenses and ensuring appropriate approvals. Demonstrated ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines while maintaining a high degree of accuracy and attention to detail. Excellent organizational, project management and problem-solving skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong interpersonal skills and demonstrated ability to work collaboratively and effectively with colleagues and stakeholders at different levels of an organization. Demonstrated discretion and judgment in handling confidential, complex and sensitive information. Strong computer skills and demonstrated ability to learn and use relevant administrative, communications and data-management systems. Assets (Nonessential): Experience working in a university, professional school or other complex academic environment. Knowledge and understanding of the legal community and profession. To be successful in this role you will be: Achievement oriented Adaptable Collaborative Diplomatic Discerning Organized Proactive Resourceful Closing Date: 10/27/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 13 -- $89,794 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $114,832. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Divisional HR Office Email: pfhr@utoronto.ca NOTE : This posting is for a one year term opportunity with the possibility of an extension Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Data Management, Project Manager, Writing, Copy Editor, Proofreading, Data, Technology, Creative Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Machinist-Journeyperson-%28Millwright%29-Temp-ON/606399617/": {"title": "Machinist Journeyperson (Millwright) -Temp Job Details", "description": "Machinist Journeyperson (Millwright) -Temp Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Machinist Journeyperson (Millwright) -Temp Date Posted: 10/26/2026 Req ID: 50301 Faculty/Division: VP-Facilities & Real Estate Department: VP-Facilities & Real Estate Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Under general supervision, the incumbent performs a variety of millwright work in the area of responsibility. Typical Duties The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required and the extent of responsibility involved in this job. They in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated: Must ensure that you work ethically, safely, doing exceptionally high quality of workmanship. Must be able to read and interpret technical drawings, orthographic, pictorial and schematic. Must be able to use a variety of measuring tools, hand tools and power tools. Millwrights frequently lift and move heavy, awkward equipment. Rigging and hoisting abilities are a must. Maintaining prime movers, including all related attachments such as gears, belt pulleys and sheaves or chain sprockets, including the maintenance or replacement of bearings and bearing housings. Maintenance and rebuilding of pumps, motors and fans including gas turbines including all associated equipment. Maintenance of Hydraulic and Pneumatic systems and equipment. Must be able to arc weld. Other related duties as required. Minimum Requirements Education : High school graduate. Must hold a valid Ontario Industrial Mechanic Millwright Certificate of Qualification (Red Seal); working knowledge of the Occupational Health andSafety Act as it pertains to Trade Regulations (industrial & construction), and WHMIS. Experience : Experience working with machines, tools and equipment associated with a Millwright duties, competent in welding and fabricating skills. Must have mechanical and mathematical aptitude to calculate dimensions and tolerances. Demonstrated proficiency with Microsoft Outlook; Computer knowledge of Microsoft Excel and Word is preferred. Other : Ability to prepare sketches and read and interpret drawings, schematics and specifications; Must have physical ability to perform duties as described; strong problem-solving and customer service skills; tact, diplomacy and discretion; good communication skills (verbal and written) and a demonstrated ability to work in a team environment; ability to keep up-to-date with changing technology and techniques that are congruent to the trade. Please note : This is a temporary opportunity lasting approximately 1 year. This role will be posted until filled. Closing Date: 11/20/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: Lock/MachT L353 Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: $45.10 per hour Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Hydraulics, Temporary, Engineering, Contract Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}, "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Manager%2C-Accounts-Payable-ON/604982317/": {"title": "Manager, Accounts Payable Job Details", "description": "Manager, Accounts Payable Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Manager, Accounts Payable Date Posted: 08/06/2026 Req ID: 49750 Faculty/Division: VP-Facilities & Real Estate Department: FRE Financial Strategy and Services Department Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About Us: Facilities and Real Estate Division (FRE) serves the University of Toronto\u2019s three campuses and is responsible for ensuring that the University\u2019s physical infrastructure reflects the scale, ambition, and global standing of its academic enterprise. The division plays a central role in aligning campus infrastructure, capital investment, and real estate strategy with the University\u2019s academic priorities and long-term sustainability. FRE manages several key portfolios, including Facilities and Services, University Planning Design & Construction, Spaces & Experiences and Real Estate Partnerships. We strive to provide efficient and effective services that support the University's mission, values and commitments. The FRE Financial Strategy and Services Department works closely with its portfolio departments, as well as internal and external stakeholders, to manage FRE's financial resources, enhance operational efficiency, and improve financial management capacity. The department ensures compliance, provides strategic advice, enhances support for the decision-making process, manages risks, optimizes financial processes, adopts new technologies, improves existing systems, and promotes best practices. Your Opportunity: This position is responsible for overseeing the accounts payable function for the division by managing a team of AP specialists to perform AP related day-to-day operations. This role\u2019s core duties include ensuring the accurate and timely processing of invoices, maintaining vendor relationships, and ensure PO documentation is compliant with established policies and implementing best practices to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of the AP process. The AP Manager will play a critical role in maintaining financial accuracy and compliance with division and institution policies and directives. The AP Manager will support compliance and audit activities, provide AP related analysis and recommendations, oversee team staff\u2019s training and development, and contribute to system development, administration and maintenance. Required Qualifications: EDUCATION: A University degree in Finance, Accounting, Business Administration, or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Professional accounting designation required (e.g. CGA, CPA, CMA, CA). EXPERIENCE: Minimum of six (6) years of accounting experience in an accounts payable supervisory role, preferably in higher education or large public sector organization. Knowledge of SAP or the University's Administrative Management System (AMS) is required. Experience with document control and process implementation. SKILLS: Advanced proficiency with spreadsheet and word-processing software. Proficient in Excel formulas, Vlookup, Pivot Table and conditional formatting etc. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Strong working knowledge of customer service principles and practices, ability to perform with minimum supervision and make decisions independently. Ability to multi-task, effectively prioritize workload, meet hard and fast deadline. Must possess strong analytical skills. Detail-oriented with multiple tasks, information organization. OTHER: Demonstrated ability to prioritize multiple tasks and projects with sensitive deadlines. Superior planning and organizational skills. Demonstrated high level of service to a large group of stakeholders. Closing Date: 11/09/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 3 -- Hiring Zone: $97,336 - $113,558 -- Broadband Salary Range: $97,336 - $162,224 Job Category: Finance/Budget/Planning/Audit Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a\u00a0culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively\u00a0address and serve the interests of our global community. We\u00a0strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples,\u00a0Black and racialized persons, women, persons with\u00a0disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities.\u00a0We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to\u00a0equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse\u00a0perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to\u00a0strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Indigenous Substantiation Process The University of Toronto has implemented a process to substantiate Indigenous Membership/Citizenship/Enrolment for candidates who identify as Indigenous. For more information about this process, please refer to the Indigenous Substantiation Website . Job Segment: Accounts Payable, Document Control, ERP, Accounting, CPA, Finance, Administrative, Technology Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"}}, "rows": {"https:/